uish the group that claimed responsibility for an attack on a Kenyan mall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/world/africa/kenya-somali-militants-attacked.html', 'snippet': 'The Kenyan military led an African Union operation against the Shabab in southern Somalia on Thursday in an effort to vanquish the group that claimed responsibility for an attack on a Kenyan mall.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The Kenyan military led an African Union operation against Islamist militants in southern Somalia on Thursday in an effort to vanquish the group that claimed responsibility for a terrorist attack last month in a Kenyan mall that killed more than 60 people. In a statement on Thursday, Kenya said it had “conducted a major aerial offensive” on a militant training camp run by the group, the Shabab, in the Dinsoor region of Somalia, possibly killing as many as 300 militants and destroying the site. The casualty estimate could not be independently confirmed. Kenya said that the training camp had been used by Shabab “operatives” who had “infiltrated” Kenya, and that it was where those who carried out the mall attack had “received their training.” A spokesman for the African Union peacekeeping mission said the attack was part of the force’s broader campaign against the Shabab. A Shabab spokesman denied that any of its camps had been attacked, Reuters reported. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenya: Somali Militants Attacked', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenya: Somali Militants Attacked', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kron, Josh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Somalia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nairobi, Kenya, Westgate Mall Shootings (2013)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T00:59:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Kron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc65338c-6422-53ad-bcc4-a5922705740f', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc65338c-6422-53ad-bcc4-a5922705740f'}, {'abstract': 'Money, politics and success on the field divide two soccer teams (and their fans) in the Catalan capital.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/sports/soccer/the-invisible-team-barcelonas-little-brother-espanyol.html', 'snippet': 'Money, politics and success on the field divide two soccer teams (and their fans) in the Catalan capital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BARCELONA, Spain — Every day, Javier Aguirre sits in his office and reads four all-sports newspapers. And every day, he finds himself furious as he turns page after page (after page after page).', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/sports/espanyola/espanyola-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/01/sports/espanyola/espanyola-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/sports/espanyola/espanyola-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 