ization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/504e35bf-c199-5e16-b2de-89ef5cdbf465', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/504e35bf-c199-5e16-b2de-89ef5cdbf465'}, {'abstract': 'The latest casualty of the Senate Republican filibuster is Patricia Ann Millett, a highly qualified judicial nominee.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/opinion/the-politics-of-petulance.html', 'snippet': 'The latest casualty of the Senate Republican filibuster is Patricia Ann Millett, a highly qualified judicial nominee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senate Republicans on Thursday again refused to allow the nomination of a highly qualified judicial nominee to come up for a full vote. Their use of the filibuster is by now all too familiar, and the latest casualty is Patricia Ann Millett, whom President Obama nominated in June, along with two other people, to the United States Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Politics of Petulance', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Politics of Petulance', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Millett, Patricia A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appeals Courts (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on the Judiciary', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T01:12:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/626e16bd-7f00-5521-9cbc-c469b2061b01', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/626e16bd-7f00-5521-9cbc-c469b2061b01'}, {'abstract': 'Days after a federal judge blocked a Texas law that threatened to shut down many of the state’s abortion clinics, an appeals court said the rule should take effect while the case goes forward.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/us/most-of-law-on-abortion-is-reinstated-in-texas.html', 'snippet': 'Days after a federal judge blocked a Texas law that threatened to shut down many of the state’s abortion clinics, an appeals court said the rule should take effect while the case goes forward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Only three days after a federal judge blocked a new Texas law that threatened to shut down many of the state’s abortion clinics, the United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit, in New Orleans, reversed the decision, saying the rule should take effect while the case is argued in the months to come.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Reversal, Court Allows Texas Law on Abortion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Reversal, Court Allows Texas Law On Abortion', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckholm, Erik', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeakel, Lee', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abbott, Gregory W (1957- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T01:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_d