nk': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legislatures and Parliaments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samanci, Gulay', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice and Development Party (Turkey)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Republican People's Party (Turkey)", 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dalbudak, Nurcan', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T01:25:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Arango and Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arango', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c94faa2-bd5d-57fa-b2dd-076d7f308731', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c94faa2-bd5d-57fa-b2dd-076d7f308731'}, {'abstract': 'A thrift-store painting is now worth well over half a million dollars, thanks to the imprimatur of Banksy.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/10/31/banksy-altered-painting-brings-615000-at-auction/', 'snippet': 'A thrift-store painting is now worth well over half a million dollars, thanks to the imprimatur of Banksy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A thrift-store painting is now worth well over half a million dollars, thanks to the imprimatur of Banksy. “The Banality of the Banality of Evil,” a landscape that he doctored by adding a Nazi military figure, his own signature and a certificate of authenticity, sold for $615,000 in a charity auction that ended on Thursday evening. The money was to benefit Housing Works, which anonymously received the painting in its Gramercy shop and put it up for sale online on Tuesday. The auction attracted 138 bids, from a minimum starting offer of $74,000, with the price jumping by several hundred thousand dollars in the final moments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Banksy-Altered Painting Brings $615,000 at Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Banksy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T01:28:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melena Ryzik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melena', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ryzik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e509c029-1486-5e35-862d-25a60c475296', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e509c029-1486-5e35-862d-25a60c475296'}, {'abstract': 'An obsession with exports is coming at a high cost for other euro countries and its own economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/opinion/why-germany-needs-to-bolster-domestic-demand.html', 'snippet': 'An obsession with exports is coming at a high cost for other euro countries and its own economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Treasury Department’s semiannual report on the international economy and exchange rates usually makes for boring reading. But the latest edition, released this week, broke from that tradition by offering some blunt and much-needed perspective about the German economy: Its heavy reliance on exports is hurting weaker European countries that share the euro. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany’s Blind Spot', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany’s Blind Spot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T01:29:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e9857bf-4bd2-56e1-b55e-6356adc8729f', 'word_count': 361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e9857bf-4bd2-56e1-b55e-6356adc8729f'}, {'abstract': 'An amendment that would allow state judges to stay on the bench to age 80 deserves a yes vote. Four others should be approved, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/opinion/new-yorks-constitutional-amendments.html', 'snippet': 'An amendment that would allow state judges to stay on the bench to age 80 deserves a yes vote. Four others should be approved, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New York State voters will decide on Tuesday on six amendments to the highly detailed State Constitution. In earlier editorials, we argued that the amendment to expand casino gambling in the state should be rejected. An amendment that would allow state judges to stay on the bench to age 80 deserves a yes vote. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Constitutional Amendments', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York’s Constitutional Amendments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitutional Amendments', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T01:29:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a72a6c2-f4ba-5b11-8a6a-232ca730367a', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a72a6c2-f4ba-5b11-8a6a-232ca730367a'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court was unwise to block necessary changes ordered by Judge Shira Scheindlin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/opinion/a-bad-ruling-on-stop-and-frisk.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court was unwise to block necessary changes ordered by Judge Shira Scheindlin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit was unwise to put a stay on the necessary remedies Judge Shira Scheindlin of Federal District Court in Manhattan ordered in August in response to the civil rights violations of New York City’s stop-and-frisk policy. And it overreached in taking the extraordinary step of removing Judge Scheindlin from the long-running litigation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bad Ruling on Stop-and-Frisk', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bad Ruling on Stop-and-Frisk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': '