, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Politician From Germany Meets Snowden', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snowden, Edward J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merkel, Angela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strobele, Hans-Christian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mascolo, Georg', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T03:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89da09aa-e958-5f59-97bd-2ddce34fe14c', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89da09aa-e958-5f59-97bd-2ddce34fe14c'}, {'abstract': '“The Pervert’s Guide to Ideology” is the second critical analysis of what values the movies are really imparting, by the philosopher Slavoj Zizek.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/movies/the-perverts-guide-to-ideology.html', 'snippet': '“The Pervert’s Guide to Ideology” is the second critical analysis of what values the movies are really imparting, by the philosopher Slavoj Zizek.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Pervert’s Guide to Ideology,” Sophie Fiennes’s second collaboration with the public intellectual Slavoj Zizek, sets out a daunting task. Titling a film that way, even tongue in cheek, recalls the Monty Python sketch about summarizing Proust, only with an even broader remit.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag