rents-intervene-to-help-a-bullied-child/', 'snippet': 'Has your child been bullied, and how did you, as a parent, handle the situation?', 'lead_paragraph': 'From Michael Winerip at Booming:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Should Parents Intervene to Help a Bullied Child?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winerip, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T16:12:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e41b6b5-2494-544f-8b48-73efa2308dd2', 'word_count': 190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e41b6b5-2494-544f-8b48-73efa2308dd2'}, {'abstract': 'The epic Douglas firs that rule the Oregon woods grow from something small and inconceivable. So does a song.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/the-seeds-of-song/', 'snippet': 'The epic Douglas firs that rule the Oregon woods grow from something small and inconceivable. So does a song.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Up here, you know the Douglas fir rules the woods. It’s the tree among trees, reaching heights over 400 feet and these Oregon hills and mountains are full of their kind. As a kid I recall wandering up through the western coast range by truck, a rickety old Ford Bronco my buddy’s uncle let us use since it had a winch on account of nine times out of ten we’d get stuck up to the knee in some sloppy earth up there from the rains.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tale of the Seed and the Song', 'kicker': 'Measure for Measure', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blitzen Trapper (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T16:15:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Earley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Earley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c6130f1-6202-52db-96a6-072639d2569c', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c6130f1-6202-52db-96a6-072639d2569c'}, {'abstract': 'Sotheby’s will auction paintings, furniture and other works that belonged to Ralph O. Esmerian, the former chairman of the American Folk Art Museum, who is now imprisoned for financial fraud.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/folk-art-collection-from-imprisoned-former-museum-chairman-going-to-auction/', 'snippet': 'Sotheby’s will auction paintings, furniture and other works that belonged to Ralph O. Esmerian, the former chairman of the American Folk Art Museum, who is now imprisoned for financial fraud.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than 200 watercolors, pieces of furniture, carvings, weather vanes and other valuable items that were once destined for the American Folk Art Museum\xa0are being auctioned at Sotheby’s on Jan. 25. The collection, estimated to be worth between $6.4 million and $9.5 million, belonged to the museum’s former chairman\xa0Ralph O. Esmerian, who once owned\xa0 the jewelry retailer Fred Leighton and who is currently serving a six-year sentence for a series of financial frauds totaling $210 million.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Folk Art Collection From Imprisoned Former Museum Chairman Going to Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Auction Is Set for Folk Art Of Jailed Ex-Museum Chief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Esmerian, Ralph O', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T16:20:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c7acb2f-2fbd-5c14-94b2-f407abb74904', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c7acb2f-2fbd-5c14-94b2-f407abb74904'}, {'abstract': 'Tips, examples and a quiz to help students think about what the opening lines of an essay or article must do — and how to use what they learn to make their own writing stronger.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/skills-practice-writing-effective-openings/', 'snippet': 'Tips, examples and a quiz to help students think about what the opening lines of an essay or article must do — and how to use what they learn to make their own writing stronger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Let’s cut to the chase for the peyote-eating optimists out there: as long as LeBron James, Derrick Rose, Kevin Durant, James Harden and any team coached by Gregg Popovich walk the wood planks of the N.B.A., a championship banner will not swing at Madison Square Garden or Barclays Center.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 