'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/calendar-coming-events-in-london-washington-and-thailand/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘Georgians Revealed: Life, Style and the Making of Modern Britain,’ London\xa0The Victorian and Elizabethan periods may be well known, but many quintessentially “polite” things thought of as British — taking tea, theatergoing and a fascination with gardening — originated in Georgian England. “Georgians Revealed,” from Nov. 8 to March 11 at the British Library, explores the roots of popular culture and “the revolution in everyday life” that took place between 1714 and 1830, through artwork, rare books and everyday objects, like the first fashion magazines. (Above, a circa 1714 portrait of George I.) Talks about culinary history, poetry and the emerging middle class; guided walking tours; and a night of “Vice and Virtue” with live music and performances, and food and drink, are highlights.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/travel/03CALENDAR1/03CALENDAR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/travel/03CALENDAR1/03CALENDAR1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 726}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/travel/03CALENDAR1/03CALENDAR1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/travel/03CALENDAR1/03CALENDAR1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 660, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non