evices on flights, airlines will need to provide the power for smartphones and tablets.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/in-flight-devices-yes-but-what-about-the-power/', 'snippet': 'After the F.A.A’s approval of the use of electronic devices on flights, airlines will need to provide the power for smartphones and tablets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:44 p.m. | With the Federal Aviation Administration’s decision to allow passengers to use portable electronic devices throughout flights, the next question from fliers will most likely be, “So, where’s the power outlet?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In-Flight Devices, Yes. But What About the Power?', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Aviation Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JetBlue Airways Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Airlines', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Airways Group Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T18:30:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c