g mayoral candidates, is often cast as a threat to the real estate industry, but he has won over some skeptics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every month, Leonard Steinberg, a leading broker at Douglas Elliman who has been responsible for more than $2 billion in residential real estate transactions, largely in downtown Manhattan, publishes something called The Luxury Letter. The report combines various listings — for $9 million duplexes in Chelsea, for a $44.9 million “loft mansion” in TriBeCa — with Mr. Steinberg’s insights on the high-end property market and the city more generally. Titled “Mayoral Issues: A Tale of Two Cities?” the October editor’s note recommended that the city’s presumptive next leader, Bill de Blasio, devise a “worst tenants” list, and cautioned those who criticize Michael R. Bloomberg that a mayor’s role is to be “effective C.E.O. of the city, not ‘best friend.’\xa0”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1262, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/nyregion/03BIGCITY1_SPAN/03BIGCITY1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Surprise Ally for the Rich', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Surprise Ally for the Rich', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T21:20:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ginia Bellafante', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ginia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bellafante', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8354c8d3-acb7-5478-88ed-c99b6aa68018', 'word_count': 865, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8354c8d3-acb7-5478-88ed-c99b6aa68018'}, {'abstract': 'Naomi Watts and Nicole Kidman are portraying the Princess of Wales and the Princess of Monaco, respectively, in a pair of upcoming biopics. Here’s how the four ladies’ stories stack up.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/01/chart-the-parallel-lives-of-princess-di-princess-grace-and-the-b-f-f-actresses-playing-them-in-the-movies/', 'snippet': 'Naomi Watts and Nicole Kidman are portraying the Princess of Wales and the Princess of Monaco, respectively, in a pair of upcoming biopics. Here’s how the four ladies’ stories stack up.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two new films are coming out about the not-so-fairy-tale lives of Diana, Princess of Wales (played by Naomi Watts), and Grace, Princess of Monaco (Nicole Kidman). Both were universally adored before dying in mysterious auto accidents. Their biopics appear to be star vehicles for the B.F.F. actresses — and the chattering class is abuzz, because both movies are so tiara-twistingly bad as to inspire outrage and bewilderment. Are they propaganda campaigns to bring down parasitic Western monarchies as we know them? You be the judge.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '54', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Parallel Lives of Princess Di, Princess Grace and the B.F.F. Actresses Playing Them in the Movies', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Entertainment: Royal Smackdown', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Family', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Diana, Princess of Wales', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kidman, Nicole', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watts, Naomi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-01T21:21:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cintra Wilson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cintra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wilson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_