of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d2925bd-d932-5fcd-b73a-e6c40f23b19d', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d2925bd-d932-5fcd-b73a-e6c40f23b19d'}, {'abstract': 'A federal appeals court has dealt a grievous blow to the reproductive health and rights of Texas women.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/opinion/a-bad-reversal-on-the-texas-abortion-law.html', 'snippet': 'A federal appeals court has dealt a grievous blow to the reproductive health and rights of Texas women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A three-judge panel of the United States Court of Appeals for the Fifth Circuit has dealt a grievous blow to the reproductive health and rights of Texas women. On Thursday, the court allowed Texas, pending the court’s final resolution of the case, to enforce a provision in the state’s new abortion law that requires doctors who perform the procedure to have admitting privileges at a nearby hospital. As a result, a third of the state’s 36 licensed abortion clinics have stopped providing abortions. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bad Reversal on the Texas Abortion Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Bad Reversal on the Texas Abortion Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T02:26:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/55d4a5f4-9693-571c-8ddc-a5212e7a689f', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55d4a5f4-9693-571c-8ddc-a5212e7a689f'}, {'abstract': 'Noam Bramson has the skills and vision needed to run the county well.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/opinion/for-county-executive-in-westchester.html', 'snippet': 'Noam Bramson has the skills and vision needed to run the county well.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the race for Westchester County executive, the incumbent, Rob Astorino, a Republican, pledges to continue cutting taxes and spending and to spur business. The Democratic challenger, Noam Bramson, the mayor of New Rochelle, says he will protect the social safety net while promoting “smart growth” development and greater cooperation among the county’s local governments. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For County Executive in Westchester', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For County Executive in Westchester', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Astorino, Rob', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bramson, Noam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, County Executives', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endorsements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T02:30:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e212d48b-681c-5475-9606-1825ee64c312', 'word_count': 242, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e212d48b-681c-5475-9606-1825ee64c312'}, {'abstract': 'After creating disorder in his country, Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki suddenly wants more American help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/opinion/can-iraq-be-saved.html', 'snippet': 'After creating disorder in his country, Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki suddenly wants more American help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With Iraq wracked by the worst violence in three years, Prime Minister Nuri Kamal al-Maliki was in Washington this week looking for military aid and other help. This was quite a turnabout, since he had essentially forced American troops to leave in 2011. Since then, the pressures in Iraq have grown, and Mr. Maliki bears much responsibility for the current turmoil.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Iraq Be Saved?', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Iraq Be Saved?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maliki, Nuri Kamal al-', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA IN MESOPOTAMIA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State of Iraq and Syria', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T02:30:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/df20e0b5-1e04-5912-8eb1-0506aab0d110', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df20e0b5-1e04-5912-8eb1-0506aab0d110'}, {'abstract': 'Tips for talking to your employer about a mini-sabbatical to do something you have always dreamed of doing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/your-money/planning-for-a-needed-break-from-work.html', 'snippet': 'Tips for talking to your employer about a mini-sabbatical to do something you have always dreamed of doing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOSEPH BUBMAN took six months off his job as a management consultant two years ago to work with a charity in Kenya and Guatemala. It was something he had dreamed of doing and he spent almost a year planning it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/02/business/Shortcuts/Shortcuts-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}]