ccess signing up for health insurance under the Affordable Care Act has been elusive for some and a dream come true for others. It often depends on geography.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/affordable-care-act/2013/11/02/health-exchange-a-one-month-checkup/', 'snippet': 'Success signing up for health insurance under the Affordable Care Act has been elusive for some and a dream come true for others. It often depends on geography.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Affordable Care Act’s goal of providing health insurance for all Americans grew more complicated when governors of more than 30 statesopted not to create their own health care exchanges. That left the federal government responsible for enrolling a much larger portion of the population than it had expected, which is at least part of the reason for the troubled rollout of HealthCare.gov. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Health Exchange: A One-Month Checkup', 'kicker': 'In Practice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T04:41:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8c05885-e390-5454-bf50-f8bfc593e6f3', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8c05885-e390-5454-bf50-f8bfc593e6f3'}, {'abstract': 'After 18 years in prison, Sundhe Moses was paroled. His case is part of a broad investigation into Louis Scarcella, a retired detective suspected of using questionable tactics and evidence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/nyregion/100000002531340/a-verdict-revisited-for-iffy-evidence.html', 'snippet': 'After 18 years in prison, Sundhe Moses was paroled. His case is part of a broad investigation into Louis Scarcella, a retired detective suspected of using questionable tactics and evidence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After 18 years in prison, Sundhe Moses was paroled. His case is part of a broad investigation into Louis Scarcella, a retired detective suspected of using questionable tactics and evidence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/nyregion/video-scarcella-moses/video-scarcella-moses-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/01/nyregion/video-scarcella-moses/video-scarcella-moses-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/nyregion/video-scarcella-moses/video-scarcella-moses-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/01/nyregion/video-scarcella-moses/video-scarcella-moses-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/nyregion/video-scarcella-moses/video-scarcella-moses-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Case Amid Doubts on Evidence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T04:50:26+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'Mona El-Naggar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mona', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'El-Naggar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/c7ae7683-0480-521a-b690-2004f53c3ab9', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/c7ae7683-0480-521a-b690-2004f53c3ab9'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) PROMISED LAND (2012) Matt Damon, above, plays a corporate predator and staunch defender of his company’s cause — fracking, the contentious drilling technique for natural gas — who arrives in a small farming town with the belief that he is offering local landowners a lifeline. Some, hearing the amounts being offered for drilling rights, are eager to sign up. But troubles arise when an old-timer (Hal Holbrook) starts asking questions about what fracking will do to the water supply, the livestock and the land itself. Then an environmental activist (John Krasinski) appears on the scene. The movie “has a point to make, and it does so in a way that is both honorable and disappointing,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times about this film, directed by Gus Van Sant and written by Mr. Damon and Mr. Krasinski. “It admirably tries to represent both sides of the fracking debate, even though its allegiance is clearly to the antifracking position. There is nothing wrong with such advocacy, except that in this case it means that the movie veers away from its strengths, ending in a welter of convenient (and dubious) plot twists and puffed-up speeches.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday'