'By Perry Garfinkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garfinkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0601c47c-abaa-54b9-9668-b07312dd7df4', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0601c47c-abaa-54b9-9668-b07312dd7df4'}, {'abstract': 'Stoke City goalkeeper Asmir Begovic scored a goal 12 seconds into the match on Saturday when the wind grabbed a clearing pass.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/sports/soccer/a-goalkeepers-revenge-stoke-citys-begovic-scores-goal.html', 'snippet': 'Stoke City goalkeeper Asmir Begovic scored a goal 12 seconds into the match on Saturday when the wind grabbed a clearing pass.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is one thing to score a goal only 14 seconds into a game. But it is quite another when that goal scorer turns out to be a goalkeeper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Goalkeeper’s Revenge: Stoke City’s Begovic Scores Goal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stoke City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:20:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Bell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a291676-0ff9-5fed-8b19-b41d7fbac479', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a291676-0ff9-5fed-8b19-b41d7fbac479'}, {'abstract': 'My prejudices against conservatives were just as uncompromising as the prejudices I’d often projected onto them.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/i-want-to-be-friends-with-republicans/', 'snippet': 'My prejudices against conservatives were just as uncompromising as the prejudices I’d often projected onto them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trouble started the night Jeff, one of the guys I drink and talk about God with, announced that he’d been summoned to court for the Zimmerman trial jury pool. We’d kept politics out of our Wednesday night meetings, which are held on my back porch, the six of us seated at an old dining room table propped next to my broken hot tub (Florida short-sale homes come standard with broken hot tubs). Instead of Bible Study, we call it our Tavern Ministry, and while we were often drunk halfway through, a churchlike decorum had always held sway. Once the case came up, though, decorum collapsed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'I Want to Be Friends With Republicans', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David James Poissant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'James', 'lastname': 'Poissant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91ca35e4-736d-5e10-a070-f6664d18b041', 'word_count': 1133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91ca35e4-736d-5e10-a070-f6664d18b041'}, {'abstract': 'While forgery is an economic crime, it may not always be an artistic or aesthetic one.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/in-praise-of-art-forgeries.html', 'snippet': 'While forgery is an economic crime, it may not always be an artistic or aesthetic one.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN Queens, a guy working in his garage churned out “Pollocks” and “Rothkos” that fooled the experts, sold for millions of dollars and helped destroy the Knoedler & Company gallery, as we learned in recent months. In China, thousands of artisans have forged the country’s artistic treasures, both ancient and modern, according to a report in The New York Times.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 414}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 706, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1412, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03SUBFORGERY/03SUBFORGERY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of Art Forgeries', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Praise of Art Forgeries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knoedler & Co', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Blake Gopnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Blake', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gopnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/61d4f5db-eb8b-56d7-b28e-d21ec3b82e03', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61d4f5db-eb8b-56d7-b28e-d21ec3b82e03'}, {'abstract': 'Once the envy of others, the U.S. is more likely to be scrutinized these days.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/friedman-calling-america-hello-hello-hello-hello.html', 'snippet': 'Once the envy of others, the U.S. is more likely to be scrutinized these days.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SINGAPORE — HAVING lived and worked abroad for many years, I’m sensitive to the changing ways that foreigners look at America. Over the years, I’ve seen an America that was respected, hated, feared and loved. But traveling around China and Singapore last week, I was confronted repeatedly with an attitude toward America that I’ve never heard before: “What’s up with you guys?”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/thomas-l-friedman/thomas-l-friedman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Calling America: Hello? Hello? Hello? Hello?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker'