ionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/poverty-in-america-is-mainstream/', 'snippet': 'Contrary to popular belief, the percentage of the population that directly encounters poverty is exceedingly high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few topics in American society have more myths and stereotypes surrounding them than poverty, misconceptions that distort both our politics and our domestic policy making.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poverty in America Is Mainstream', 'kicker': 'The Great Divide', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poverty in America Is Mainstream', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:30:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mark R. Rank', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Rank', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/27b632d8-58c7-5c0f-8987-79d3d2a19d2b', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27b632d8-58c7-5c0f-8987-79d3d2a19d2b'}, {'abstract': 'On average, black players are born in nicer neighborhoods than other black men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/in-the-nba-zip-code-matters.html', 'snippet': 'On average, black players are born in nicer neighborhoods than other black men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AS the N.B.A. season gets under way, there is no doubt that the league’s best player is 6-foot-8 LeBron James, of the Miami Heat. Mr. James was born poor to a 16-year-old single mother in Akron, Ohio. The conventional wisdom is that his background is typical for an N.B.A. player. A majority of Americans, Google consumer survey data show, think that the N.B.A. is composed mostly of men like Mr. James. But it isn’t.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-articleLarge-v3.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-articleLarge-v3.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-jumbo-v3.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-thumbStandard-v4.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/opinion/contributor-davidowitz/contributor-davidowitz-thumbLarge-v4.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the N.B.A., ZIP Code Matters', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In the N.B.A., ZIP Code Matters', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:31:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Stephens-Davidowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens-Davidowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7174b0d3-1de1-552b-a92e-8d6bcbd76419', 'word_count': 1261, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7174b0d3-1de1-552b-a92e-8d6bcbd76419'}, {'abstract': 'A new book focuses on the half-dozen Texas and Oklahoma energy companies behind the surging growth of hydraulic fracturing for oil and gas in the last two decades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/business/the-frackers-and-the-birth-of-an-energy-boom.html', 'snippet': 'A new book focuses on the half-dozen Texas and Oklahoma energy companies behind the surging growth of hydraulic fracturing for oil and gas in the last two decades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One could argue that, except for the Internet, the most important technological advance of the last two decades has been hydraulic fracturing, widely known as fracking. Practically overnight, it seems, this drilling technique has produced so much oil and gas beneath American soil that we are at the brink of something once thought unattainable: true energy independence. And its repercussions, for geopolitics, the environment and other areas, are only now being grasped.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 832}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 739, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1477, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-SHELF/03-SHELF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Frackers’ and the Birth of an Energy Boom', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Birth of an Energy Boom', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zuckerman, Gregory', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydraulic Fracturing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chesapeake Energy Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClendon, Aubrey K', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shale', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:37:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bryan Burrough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bryan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burrough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/93abed3f-34f8-58e8-82be-d90d9160d4fa', 'word_count': 788, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93abed3f-34f8-58e8-82be-d90d9160d4fa'}, {'abstract': 'In Newtown, Conn., the suffering is made raw again as the anniversary of the shooting nears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/that-dreadful-day-in-december.html', 'snippet': 'In Newtown, Conn., the suffering is made raw again as the anniversary of the shooting nears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWTOWN, Conn. — “Every day in this first year is a very difficult journey,” said Mark Barden, whose 7-year-old son Daniel was one of the 20 schoolchildren slain last December here in the Sandy Hook shooting massacre. “And with the anniversary of the tragedy coming up, it seems to be getting more difficult.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'That Dreadful Day in December', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'That Dreadful Day in December', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Newtown, Conn, Shooting (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newtown (Conn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/15069f02-bd4e-52f1-8ad4-35b05d566e8c', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15069f02-bd4e-52f1-8ad4-35b05d566e8c'}, {'abstract': 'Some plans with inadequate coverage policies will be canceled, but consumers will not be left out in the cold.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/insurance-policies-not-worth-keeping.html', 'snippet': 'Some plans with inadequate coverage policies will be canceled, but consumers will not be left out in the cold.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congressional Republicans have stoked consumer fears and confusion with charges that the health care reform law is causing insurers to cancel existing policies and will force many people to pay substantially higher premiums next year for coverage they don’t want. That, they say, violates President Obama’s pledge that if you like the insurance you have, you can keep it. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insurance Policies Not Worth Keeping', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Policies Not Worth Keeping', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/36b0b40f-7e3e-5f73-9d22-ea384817c45b', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36b0b40f-7e3e-5f73-9d22-ea384817c45b'}, {'abstract': 'Hawaii is on the verge of allowing same-sex marriage, yet its path to equality hasn’t always been strewn with leis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/the-aloha-spirit-for-everyone.html', 'snippet': 'Hawaii is on the verge of allowing same-sex marriage, yet its path to equality hasn’t always been strewn with leis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEWTOWN, Conn. — Hawaii is on the brink of becoming the 15th state to allow same-sex couples to marry. The victory, once it comes, will have a special resonance. This is the state whose Supreme Court in 1993 first opened the door to marriage equality by declaring marriage a basic civil right, setting off a reactionary scramble that led to the federal Defense of Marriage Act, a legal bulwark against gay couples that the United States Supreme Court has partly demolished.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 1199, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sunday-review/03editorialSUB/03editorialSUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Aloha Spirit, for Everyone', 'kicker': 'Editorial | Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Aloha Spirit, for Everyone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downes, Lawrence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/690e5283-94da-5fd3-9814-4f0f102d4876', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/690e5283-94da-5fd3-9814-4f0f102d4876'}, {'abstract': 'California has imposed $16 million in penalties and fines in a case demonstrating the importance of state laws requiring the disclosure of political donations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/a-victory-against-dark-money.html', 'snippet': 'California has imposed $16 million in penalties and fines in a case demonstrating the importance of state laws requiring the disclosure of political donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A group of wealthy donors wanted to give millions to two right-wing California political campaigns last year, but didn’t want anyone to know their identities. They came up with a scheme that any money-launderer would be proud of, funneling the cash through a convoluted series of independent spending groups that were allowed to collect unlimited dollars. By the time the donations had been used to buy advertising, the original money trail had been erased.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Victory Against Dark Money', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Victory Against Dark Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Americans for Responsible Leadership', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Center to Protect Patient Rights', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Americans for Job Security', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, Charles G', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Koch, David H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fair Political Practices Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:56:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a13e2b7e-14fa-5b4d-ba6c-ea141224e04e', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a13e2b7e-14fa-5b4d-ba6c-ea141224e04e'}, {'abstract': 'With Congress deadlocked, state legislatures have begun placing restrictions on the collection of personal data.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/opinion/sunday/states-take-on-privacy.html', 'snippet': 'With Congress deadlocked, state legislatures have begun placing restrictions on the collection of personal data.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tired of waiting for Congress to pass comprehensive privacy legislation, state lawmakers are taking matters into their own hands, and not a moment too soon. Legislatures across the country have enacted laws to regulate the kinds of information that companies and law enforcement agencies can collect about individuals and how it can be done. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'States Take on Privacy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'States Take On Privacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'State Legislatures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T18:56:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c78fcb34-55b2-5a08-86df-2cb437005108', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c78fcb34-55b2-5a08-86df-2cb437005108'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Harris said that after her mother was killed at their home in Queens, she knew that she had to be strong for her son, who was born two months later.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/nyregion/a-teenagers-course-altered-by-motherhood.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Harris said that after her mother was killed at their home in Queens, she knew that she had to be strong for her son, who was born two months later.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the third trimester of her pregnancy, Daniel Harris, then 16, struggled to comfortably sleep through the night. So she was awake just after 4 a.m., when the sound of screaming became audible. She thought a next-door neighbor was responsible for the commotion, until her frightened younger sister went to her bedroom and a sick realization hit. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/02/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/02/nyregion/neediest/neediest-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'c