eLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/sunday-review/03SUBEXPOSURES01/03SUBEXPOSURES01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/sunday-review/03SUBEXPOSURES01/03SUBEXPOSURES01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/sunday-review/03SUBEXPOSURES01/03SUBEXPOSURES01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/01/sunday-review/03SUBEXPOSURES01/03SUBEXPOSURES01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/01/sunday-review/03SUBEXPOSURES01/03SUBEXPOSURES01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eloquent Empty Spaces', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eloquent Empty Spaces', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Urban Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T19:22:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Saville', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Saville', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c461bda-baab-5f43-a426-5f9ea956af45', 'word_count': 186, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c461bda-baab-5f43-a426-5f9ea956af45'}, {'abstract': 'Readers comment on my Sunday column that aims to show why, in human terms, health care reform like Obamacare is so needed.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/the-human-face-of-our-health-care-mess/', 'snippet': 'Readers comment on my Sunday column that aims to show why, in human terms, health care reform like Obamacare is so needed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Republicans have been focusing on the messiness of the Obamacare rollout, and that’s perfectly legitimate. It has been very messy. Some liberals think they shouldn’t acknowledge the problems, because that just gives the critics more talking points. I disagree: The rollout has been a disaster, and President Obama was misleading when he said everyone could keep their existing insurance. Let’s not disguise the truth.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Human Face of Our Health Care Mess', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:12:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2162bf7-1b9a-5bea-8cd3-e05f4e491c49', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2162bf7-1b9a-5bea-8cd3-e05f4e491c49'}, {'abstract': 'Chuck Leavell, 61, of the Mother Nature Network, also plays piano for the Rolling Stones. His office reflects his work with both the environment and his music — and his love of family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/business/in-touch-with-nature-and-with-rock-n-roll.html', 'snippet': 'Chuck Leavell, 61, of the Mother Nature Network, also plays piano for the Rolling Stones. His office reflects his work with both the environment and his music — and his love of family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WOODEN WONDERS My business partner, Joel Babbit, picked out the furniture, including the desk in my office. I was really pleased with his choice. Wood gives us so much, including beautiful furniture. And let’s not forget that wood is a renewable resource. The instrument that has given me so much joy and a great career, the piano, is also made of wood, as are so many other musical instruments.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 705, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1411, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-WORKSPACE1SUB/03-WORKSPACE1SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Touch With Nature, and With Rock ’n’ Roll', 'kicker': 'Workspace', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Touch With Nature, and With Rock ’n’ Roll', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewine, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mother Nature Network', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leavell, Chuck', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wood and Wood Products', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rolling Stones', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:14:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Edward Lewine', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Edward', 'lastname': 'Lewine', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/32a74d1d-ce41-596c-b05b-59ed3e0013c4', 'word_count': 652, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32a74d1d-ce41-596c-b05b-59ed3e0013c4'}, {'abstract': 'Three other people were injured when a Ford Expedition jumped a curb at an intersection and plowed into a group of pedestrians.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/nyregion/boy-9-is-killed-by-suv-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Three other people were injured when a Ford Expedition jumped a curb at an intersection and plowed into a group of pedestrians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 9-year-old boy was killed and three other people were hurt when a sport utility vehicle jumped the curb at an intersection in Fort Greene, Brooklyn,\xa0on Saturday, the authorities said.\xa0', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boy, 9, Is Killed by S.U.V. in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boy, 9, Is Killed by S.U.V. in Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c10215d1-302a-5a0f-a07a-d513688d74fd', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c10215d1-302a-5a0f-a07a-d513688d74fd'}, {'abstract': 'Secret Compass fell during the Juvenile Fillies race and was euthanized after sustaining a lateral condylar fracture with dislocation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/sports/filly-sustains-fatal-injury-at-breeders-cup.html', 'snippet': 'Secret Compass fell during the Juvenile Fillies race and was euthanized after sustaining a lateral condylar fracture with dislocation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ARCADIA, Calif. — The second day of the Breeders’ Cup off to a tragic start when Secret Compass fell during the Juvenile Fillies race, dismounting her rider, John Velazquez. The filly sustained a lateral condylar fracture with dislocation and was euthanized.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/03cup1/03cup1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 588, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/03cup1/03cup1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 588, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/03cup1/03cup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/03cup1/03cup1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/03cup1/03cup1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Filly Sustains Fatal Injury at Breeders’ Cup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Filly Sustains Fatal Injury at Breeders’ Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Breeders' Cup (Horse Races)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:18:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d65b954-c4fe-5a57-aa60-37398d6178d3', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d65b954-c4fe-5a57-aa60-37398d6178d3'}, {'abstract': 'Germany does a bad, bad thing.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/sin-and-unsinn/', 'snippet': 'Germany does a bad, bad thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Continuing on my German theme: Matt O’Brien catches something that I’d missed — and it’s really, really bad. I’ve mentioned before that the European Commission’s estimates of the structural rate of unemployment in troubled economies are disastrously misleading. Its model (pdf) just isn’t designed to cope with sustained slumps that put some countries into near- or actual deflation, where the downward stickiness of nominal wages becomes a crucial issue. What the model does in such cases is interpret the failure of these countries to experience accelerating deflation as a rise in the structural rate of unemployment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sin and Unsinn', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:35:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5b3d3d8-566c-536a-a9a7-4bf599e28f91', 'word_count': 345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5b3d3d8-566c-536a-a9a7-4bf599e28f91'}, {'abstract': 'New devices for keeping tabs on small children use GPS, Wi-Fi and other location-tracking technology and can be linked to apps on a parent’s phone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/technology/if-a-young-child-wanders-technology-can-follow.html', 'snippet': 'New devices for keeping tabs on small children use GPS, Wi-Fi and other location-tracking technology and can be linked to apps on a parent’s phone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most parents have experienced that feeling of fear when a young child wanders off at the playground or disappears during a trip to the supermarket. New technology, in the form of voice watches and miniature sensing devices, is aimed at thwarting such distress by keeping track of children who are too young to carry a smartphone. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 486, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 486}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1660, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/03-NOVEL3/03-NOVEL3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'If a Young Child Wanders, Technology Can Follow', 'kicker': 'Novelties', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If a Young Child Wanders, Technology Can Follow', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wonder Technology Solutions AB', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Filip Technologies', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Positioning System', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wireless Communications', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:37:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Eisenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eisenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cd28eb5-8d90-5951-8eb0-d7111fd8a23d', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cd28eb5-8d90-5951-8eb0-d7111fd8a23d'}, {'abstract': 'This chart looks ahead to the rest of the season and indicates what kind of fantasy matchup a player will have.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/sports/football/2013-fantasy-football-matchup-analysis-WRs.html', 'snippet': 'This chart looks ahead to the rest of the season and indicates what kind of fantasy matchup a player will have.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This chart looks ahead to the rest of the season and indicates what kind of fantasy matchup a player will have.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fantasy Football: 2013 Matchup Analysis, Wide Receiver', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fantasy Sports', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T20:53:31+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/6a307978-74cc-5e88-8fad-30c2cc4ade99', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/6a307978-74cc-5e88-8fad-30c2cc4ade99'}, {'abstract': 'Gary Vaynerchuk, a social media marketer, pounces on any trend — tweeted or otherwise — in his quest to sell, sell, sell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/technology/riding-the-hashtag-in-social-media-marketing.html', 'snippet': 'Gary Vaynerchuk, a social media marketer, pounces on any trend — tweeted or otherwise — in his quest to sell, sell, sell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About once a week, Gary Vaynerchuk posts a Twitter message that reads, “Is there anything I can do for you?” He means it literally. He is inviting his roughly one million followers to send requests for any kind of help or favor. And if you respond, he will try to punch you in the face.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/business/Vaynerchuk-slide-JUEH/Vaynerchuk-slide-JUEH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/business/Vaynerchuk-slide-JUEH/Vaynerchuk-slide-JUEH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit'