and off the California coast, presenting a rare opportunity for local scientists to study one of the world’s most elusive and awe-inspiring big fish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/OARFISH-1/OARFISH-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Oarfish Offer Chance to Study an Elusive Animal Long Thought a Monster', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oarfish Offer Chance to Study an Elusive Animal Long Thought a Monster', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quenqua, Douglas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marine Biology', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T21:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Environment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ab88128-5b90-5aca-9743-9c8af654510a', 'word_count': 1101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ab88128-5b90-5aca-9743-9c8af654510a'}, {'abstract': 'Two reporters for Radio France Internationale had been interviewing a leader with a separatist group in Mali’s unstable desert north. Their bodies were found with their throats slit.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/world/africa/two-french-journalists-are-kidnapped-and-killed-by-gunmen-in-mali.html', 'snippet': 'Two reporters for Radio France Internationale had been interviewing a leader with a separatist group in Mali’s unstable desert north. Their bodies were found with their throats slit.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — Two French journalists were kidnapped and killed in northern Mali on Saturday, the French Foreign Ministry said, underscoring the continuing instability of a region retaken from fighters linked to Al Qaeda only eight months ago. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two French Journalists Are Kidnapped and Killed by Gunmen in Mali', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two French Journalists Are Kidnapped and Killed by Gunmen in Mali', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Radio France Internationale', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dupont, Ghislaine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verlon, Claude', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T21:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c4a6c77-7c44-5558-a3a3-f2db81958032', 'word_count': 603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c4a6c77-7c44-5558-a3a3-f2db81958032'}, {'abstract': 'Topics on this week’s talk shows include the technical problems with President Obama’s health care law, the scope of surveillance by the National Security Agency, and new demands by some Republican lawmakers for more information about the attack on an American mission in Benghazi, Libya.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/sunday-breakfast-menu-nov-3/', 'snippet': 'Topics on this week’s talk shows include the technical problems with President Obama’s health care law, the scope of surveillance by the National Security Agency, and new demands by some Republican lawmakers for more information about the attack o...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Technical problems that continue to complicate President Obama’s signature health care law and reports of high-level espionage on both enemies and allies have made for a tumultuous week in the White House. Also, some Republicans are threatening to block the administration’s nominees for federal posts until the survivors of the 2012 attack on the American mission in Benghazi, Libya, appear before Congress. Supporters on both sides of each issue will hash it out on the Sunday news shows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, Nov. 3', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T21:47:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/35243ae6-dd16-5b7b-a7b3-50bd408ee398', 'word_count': 532, 'uri': 'nyt://article/35243ae6-dd16-5b7b-a7b3-50bd408ee398'}, {'abstract': 'Surprising parallels, none of them good.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/france-1930-germany-2013/', 'snippet': 'Surprising parallels, none of them good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Did France cause the Great Depression? It sounds a bit like a joke (Billy Crystal in Moscow, 1989: “I was raised thinking you were the enemy; you were raised thinking I was the enemy. We were both wrong: it’s the French”) But it’s the actual title of a very good paper by Doug Irwin, who points out that France, with its undervalued currency, soaked up a huge proportion of the world’s gold reserves in 1930-31, and suggests that France was responsible for about half the global deflation that took place over that period.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'France 1930, Germany 2013', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T22:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4346d5e3-d26f-5b71-ab66-c41264554838', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4346d5e3-d26f-5b71-ab66-c41264554838'}, {'abstract': 'In which Andy Kravis and Victor Barocas knock over the fruit cart.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/02/stolen-produce/', 'snippet': 'In which Andy Kravis and Victor Barocas knock over the fruit cart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greetings all! I’m filling in for Deb for the day, which is just long enough to rave about this Sunday puzzle from Andy Kravis and Victor Barocas. Fair warning first: there are spoilers below.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stolen Produce', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T22:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Gaffney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gaffney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ece467f-14bd-5b7b-b4e7-056d6a6adbb2', 'word_count': 825, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ece467f-14bd-5b7b-b4e7-056d6a6adbb2'}, {'abstract': 'G-Team Novy Bor won the open section at the European Club Cup’s tournament despite its lack of big-name talent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/crosswords/chess/little-noticed-czech-team-snares-a-european-title.html', 'snippet': 'G-Team Novy Bor won the open section at the European Club Cup’s tournament despite its lack of big-name talent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Czech team with few top-ranked players on its roster was the surprise winner of the European Club Cup open division title last week in Rhodes, Greece. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Little-Noticed Czech Team Snares a European Title', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Little-Noticed Czech Team Snares a European Title', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClain, Dylan Loeb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Navara, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Topalov, Veselin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caruana, Fabiano', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grischuk, Alexander', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karjakin, Sergey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Svidler, Peter', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rhodes (Greece)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Laznicka, Viktor', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wojtaszek, Radoslaw', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'G-Team Novy Bor', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Socar', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-02T22:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/164cb39d-797a-58d4-b46e-9d68cf92c7ab', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/164cb39d-797a-58d4-b46e-9d68cf92c7ab'}, {'abstract': 'The mayoral race in Detroit is riddled with complications, among them the presence of an emergency manager running the city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/us/politics/in-detroit-mayors-race-is-one-piece-of-a-puzzle.html', 'snippet': 'The mayoral race in Detroit is riddled with complications, among them the presence of an emergency manager running the city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — If people along the streets of this city seem less than consumed by the prospect of choosing a new mayor on Tuesday, perhaps it is the barrage of distractions: the governor who has been testifying in a courthouse here about Detroit’s descent into bankruptcy; the appointed emergency manager who has brought in his own team to run City Hall; the long list of questions about the fate of this city’s artwork, its streetlights, its tens of thousands of empty buildings. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/JP-DETROIT-1/JP-DETROIT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/us/JP-DETROIT-1/JP-DETROIT-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/JP-DETROIT-1/JP-DETROIT-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/us/JP-DETROIT-1/JP-DETROIT-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1293, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'le