stablished the prize in September to encourage visual and video artists, photographers and poets to create new works that focus on social justice.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/first-winner-named-in-madonnas-art-for-freedom-project/', 'snippet': 'Madonna and Vice established the prize in September to encourage visual and video artists, photographers and poets to create new works that focus on social justice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Madonna announced on Sunday the first winner in the Art for Freedom online competition that she and Vice, the multimedia company, have established to encourage visual and video artists, photographers and poets to create works that focus on social justice. Madonna has also expanded her partnerships in the project to include the social website Tumblr.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'First Winner Named in Madonna’s ‘Art for Freedom’ Project', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Winner Named In Madonna’s Art Project', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Madonna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Vice (Magazine)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mazatlan (Mexico)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T16:43:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b059d90-0fe2-5a14-8d06-0bd907e5593d', 'word_count': 228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b059d90-0fe2-5a14-8d06-0bd907e5593d'}, {'abstract': 'Buzunesh Deba and Tigist Tufa built a huge lead before Priscah Jeptoo ran them down, taking the lead around Mile 24 to win by 49 seconds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/sports/jeptoo-trailing-for-miles-rallies-to-win-womens-race.html', 'snippet': 'Buzunesh Deba and Tigist Tufa built a huge lead before Priscah Jeptoo ran them down, taking the lead around Mile 24 to win by 49 seconds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Priscah Jeptoo of Kenya sprinted on the last leg to win the New York City Marathon women’s race on Sunday and take the World Marathon Majors series title.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/MARATHONBLOG14/MARATHONBLOG14-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/MARATHONBLOG14/MARATHONBLOG14-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/MARATHONBLOG14/MARATHONBLOG14-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/MARATHONBLOG14/MARATHONBLOG14-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/MARATHONBLOG14/MARATHONBLOG14-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/sports/MARATHONBLOG14/MARATHONBLOG14-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'cred