lifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/124191b3-00ff-5827-8e46-c3d637b80720', 'word_count': 1099, 'uri': 'nyt://article/124191b3-00ff-5827-8e46-c3d637b80720'}, {'abstract': 'Eamon Morrissey performs in “Maeve’s House,” a one-man show about the writer Maeve Brennan at the Irish Arts Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/theater/reviews/maeves-house-at-the-irish-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'Eamon Morrissey performs in “Maeve’s House,” a one-man show about the writer Maeve Brennan at the Irish Arts Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Celtic oral tradition merges with snapshots of old Manhattan — and old Dublin — in Eamon Morrissey’s engrossing one-man show “Maeve’s House,” at the Irish Arts Center. The woman of the title is Maeve Brennan, the Irish writer whose short stories and Talk of the Town items, often written under the nom de plume “the Long-Winded Lady,” filled pages at The New Yorker for about 30 years, beginning in 1949. Mr. Morrissey’s play recites passages from some of her work and recalls his family’s links with Brennan as well. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/theater/04maeve/04maeve-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 599, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/theater/04maeve/04maeve-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 599, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/theater/04maeve/04maeve-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'l