None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Elections Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T21:57:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fcac4a0-8721-550a-b779-58d5754fbd9b', 'word_count': 287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fcac4a0-8721-550a-b779-58d5754fbd9b'}, {'abstract': 'The web series “city.ballet.,” produced and conceived by the actress and City Ballet board member Sarah Jessica Parker, explores different facets of the company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/arts/dance/cityballet-web-series-shows-human-side-of-dancers.html', 'snippet': 'The web series “city.ballet.,” produced and conceived by the actress and City Ballet board member Sarah Jessica Parker, explores different facets of the company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it really take to be a dancer in New York City Ballet? In “city.ballet.,” a new web series to be released on Monday by AOL On Originals, key ingredients are strength, grit, talent and perseverance. Having a life outside ballet is not a bad idea. And when all else fails, reach for the wine. After a recent performance of “Swan Lake,” the principal dancer Teresa Reichlen confesses, she “kind of had two dinners, half a bottle of wine and” — she adds with a sheepish smile — “a margarita, and that’s it. That’s it!” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Short Peeks Backstage at New York City Ballet', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Short Peeks Backstage At New York City Ballet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Sarah Jessica', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AOL On Originals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T21:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a87cd62-2c9a-5091-88d3-348f5e1feca1', 'word_count': 774, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a87cd62-2c9a-5091-88d3-348f5e1feca1'}, {'abstract': 'A tribute to an extremely optimistic song, in my opinion, by John Lieb.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/03/camp-classic/', 'snippet': 'A tribute to an extremely optimistic song, in my opinion, by John Lieb.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — The Monday through Thursday puzzles this week appeared last Saturday at the Arlington Puzzle Festival in Arlington, Va. A report on the 2012 festival is posted here and the 2013 results should be posted soon.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Camp Classic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T22:00:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byl