e', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/chacha/chacha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/chacha/chacha-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/chacha/chacha-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Details Emerge About Tainted Gallery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gallery Faces Another Forgery Complaint', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Knoedler & Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forgery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Masaccio, Anthony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perenyi, Ken', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Freedman, Ann', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T22:38:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3e22d060-43da-52b3-9ce3-a55135909ae1', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3e22d060-43da-52b3-9ce3-a55135909ae1'}, {'abstract': 'Works by Matisse, Picasso and Chagall are said to be among a collection of 1,500 pieces of art found in Munich, according to BBC News and the German magazine Focus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/arts/design/art-found-in-germany-linked-to-nazi-looting.html', 'snippet': 'Works by Matisse, Picasso and Chagall are said to be among a collection of 1,500 pieces of art found in Munich, according to BBC News and the German magazine Focus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Works by Matisse, Picasso and Chagall are said to be among a collection of 1,500 pieces of art found in Munich, according to BBC News and the German magazine Focus. The works were reportedly confiscated by the Nazis during the 1930s and ’40s and, if confirmed as genuine, would be among the largest recoveries of looted art with a possible value over $1.3 billion. The stockpile was discovered by chance in 2011, when tax investigators obtained a warrant to search the home of Cornelius Gurlitt, the son of the art dealer Hildebrand Gurlitt. There are international warrants out for at least 200 pieces in the collection, which is being stored in a secured warehouse in Munich. It is unclear why the discovery was not publicly reported until now. The United States Holocaust Memorial Museum estimates that the Nazis seized about 16,000 works of art in all, according to BBC News.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Found in Germany Linked to Nazi Looting', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Found in Germany Linked to Nazi Looting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T22:41:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/87489878-6e3c-5cd3-8aa3-0f2fd5c1c3a5', 'word_count': 150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87489878-6e3c-5cd3-8aa3-0f2fd5c1c3a5'}, {'abstract': 'Diana Nyad, the 64-year-old whose quest to swim from Cuba to Florida captivated the world, has struck a deal to write a memoir.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/books/distance-swimmer-has-a-book-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Diana Nyad, the 64-year-old whose quest to swim from Cuba to Florida captivated the world, has struck a deal to write a memoir.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diana Nyad, the 64-year-old whose quest to swim from Cuba to Florida captivated the world, has struck a deal to write a memoir. Knopf, the publisher of Sheryl Sandberg, Alice Munro and Nathan Englander, acquired the memoir, calling it a book “about her life in and out of the water.” Jordan Pavlin, executive editor at Knopf, will edit the book.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/arts-2/arts-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 795, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/arts-2/arts-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 795}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/arts-2/arts-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/arts-2/arts-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1000, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': 