 “Trophy Wife” both receiving full-season orders. “Super Fun Night,” which stars Rebel Wilson, received an additional order of only four episodes, setting the show up to be replaced at some point later in the season. Another new comedy, “Back in the Game” starring James Caan, did not receive an additional episode order, leaving its future in doubt after its initial 13-episode order is completed. The vote of confidence for “Trophy Wife” was something of a surprise, considering its ratings have been the lowest out of the four shows through the early part of the season. The other three have been on fairly equal ground in terms of viewership, but none could be qualified as hits. “The Goldbergs” has averaged 6.1 million total viewers; “Super Fun Night” 6.4 million; “Back in the Game” 6.7 million; “Trophy Wife” has averaged 4.7 million.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Extends the Lives of Some New Sitcoms', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'ABC Extends the Lives Of Some New Sitcoms', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-03T22:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/e3dd67be-2422-5e1d-bab5-9b3b244499d6', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e3dd67be-2422-5e1d-bab5-9b3b244499d6'}, {'abstract': 'Three residential buildings under construction in Manhattan are so tall that they will be instant landmarks. And apa