-playhouse.html', 'snippet': 'The theater in New Hope, Pa., has announced that Robyn Goodman will be the theater’s new executive producer and that Alexander Fraser will be the new producing director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bucks County Playhouse in New Hope, Pa., has announced that Robyn Goodman will be the theater’s new executive producer and that Alexander Fraser will be the new producing director. They will assume their roles in January, after the departure of Jed Bernstein, who is set to become the next president of Lincoln Center. Ms. Goodman is the lead producer of “Rodgers & Hammerstein’s Cinderella” on Broadway. She was also the producer of the Broadway runs of “Avenue Q” and “In the Heights.” Mr. Fraser’s recent credits include serving as an associate producer on the Chicago staging of “Kinky Boots” and the Broadway production of “The Normal Heart.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Leaders for Bucks County Playhouse', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Leaders For Playhouse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bucks County (Pa)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodman, Robyn', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bucks County Playhouse', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T00:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/12b9d691-7abf-5701-bb13-bb0d5bf367c9', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12b9d691-7abf-5701-bb13-bb0d5bf367c9'}, {'abstract': 'Discussing money in the doctor’s office is good medicine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/opinion/doctor-first-tell-me-what-it-costs.html', 'snippet': 'Discussing money in the doctor’s office is good medicine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURHAM, N.C. — IF an antibiotic would cure your infection, your doctor would probably still warn you about the chance of sun sensitivity before prescribing the pill. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Doctor, First Tell Me What It Costs', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Doctor, First Tell Me What It Costs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Avastin (Drug)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T00:16:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter A. Ubel, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Ubel', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5caae38-c304-5efb-8cf3-f4d994b39091', 'word_count': 481, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5caae38-c304-5efb-8cf3-f4d994b39091'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Wess was not the first flutist in jazz, but his deft flute solos enjoyed a prominent platform: the front row of the Basie ensemble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/arts/music/frank-wess-91-flutist-for-the-basie-band-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Wess was not the first flutist in jazz, but his deft flute solos enjoyed a prominent platform: the front row of the Basie ensemble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Frank Wess, who helped popularize the flute as a jazz instrument in the 1950s and ’60s with the Count Basie Orchestra, where he was also a standout saxophone soloist, died on Wednesday in Manhattan. He was 91.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 474, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 474}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 808, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1616, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/arts/wess-obit/wess-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Frank Wess, 91, Saxophonist and Flutist With the Basie Band, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Frank Wess, 91, Flutist for the Basie Band', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wess, Frank', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Count Basie Orchestra', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Basie, Count', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T00:25:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/adafb8f7-57ce-5788-a41f-2b1321ba5282', 'word_count': 734, 'uri': 'nyt://article/adafb8f7-57ce-5788-a41f-2b1321ba5282'}, {'abstract': 'If you think a tax on soft drinks will help fight obesity, think what a tax on corruption could do for our economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/opinion/mexicos-soda-pop-ploy.html', 'snippet': 'If you think a tax on soft drinks will help fight obesity, think what a tax on corruption could do for our economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My first job out of college, in 1983, was working for Coca-Cola. The training, which lasted a month, was the same for everyone: all day in a truck, making deliveries, mostly to rural areas. We would leave before dawn and return as the sun was setting. We delivered soft drinks to churches and whorehouses. We went to places that didn’t appear on any map, where there were no roads beyond the tracks left by trucks like ours. We went where the government didn’t go, where there were no hospitals, no schools and sometimes even no running water.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 687, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/03/opinion/03toscanaart/03toscanaart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': "Mexico's Soda Pop Ploy", 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico’s Soda-Tax Gimmick', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Toscana, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soft Drinks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sales and Excise Taxes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T00:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Toscana', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Toscana', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1464d2a-13ff-5b34-9f34-4dbe1f49380e', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1464d2a-13ff-5b34-9f34-4dbe1f49380e'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Hallett, former president of Time and Sports Illustrated, has joined Playbill Inc. as its publisher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/business/media/Bruce-Halletta-new-publisher-for-playbill.html', 'snippet': 'Bruce Hallett, former president of Time and Sports Illustrated, has joined Playbill Inc. as its publisher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems as if Bruce Hallett will work only for magazines with instantly identifiable covers.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/playbill/playbill-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 927, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/business/playbill/playbill-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 927}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/playbill/playbill-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 664, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/playbill/playbill-superJumbo.jpg', 'heigh