ealth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Romney Sees Christie as Potential G.O.P. Savior in ’16', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Romney Sees Christie as Potential G.O.P. Savior in ’16', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGeehan, Patrick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Meet the Press (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Halperin, Mark', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Heilemann, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T02:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Patrick McGeehan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGeehan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e414f3e8-a8ff-5ea4-978a-2e363b26b2bd', 'word_count': 230, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e414f3e8-a8ff-5ea4-978a-2e363b26b2bd'}, {'abstract': 'They are beggaring their neighbors, and the world, by running big trade surpluses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/opinion/krugman-those-depressing-germans.html', 'snippet': 'They are beggaring their neighbors, and the world, by running big trade surpluses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'German officials are furious at America, and not just because of the business about Angela Merkel’s cellphone. What has them enraged now is one (long) paragraph in a U.S. Treasury report on foreign economic and currency policies. In that paragraph Treasury argues that Germany’s huge surplus on current account — a broad measure of the trade balance — is harmful, creating “a deflationary bias for the euro area, as well as for the world economy.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Those Depressing Germans', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Those Depressing Germans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T02:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/882c1d68-049b-5390-9b0a-478d2aa04f70', 'word_count': 781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/882c1d68-049b-5390-9b0a-478d2aa04f70'}, {'abstract': 'Federal subsidies will pay the entire monthly cost of some plans being offered in the online marketplaces, a surprising figure that has not gotten much attention, in part because the zero-premium plans come with serious trade-offs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/business/under-health-care-act-millions-eligible-for-free-policies.html', 'snippet': 'Federal subsidies will pay the entire monthly cost of some plans being offered in the online marketplaces, a surprising figure that has not gotten much attention, in part because the zero-premium plans come with serious trade-offs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Millions of people could qualify for federal subsidies that will pay the entire monthly cost of some health care plans being offered in the online marketplaces set up under President Obama’s health care law, a surprising figure that has not garnered much attention, in part because the zero-premium plans come with serious trade-offs.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'sourc