reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c5fc14-03d8-52b5-acd6-2fd93a107468', 'word_count': 1195, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c5fc14-03d8-52b5-acd6-2fd93a107468'}, {'abstract': 'When the Supreme Court revisits the blurry boundary between church and state it should ensure government neutrality toward all religions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/opinion/a-prayer-in-the-town-hall.html', 'snippet': 'When the Supreme Court revisits the blurry boundary between church and state it should ensure government neutrality toward all religions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The wall between church and state is one of the most powerful and enduring images in American law, but as a metaphor it fails to capture the complicated and porous relationship most Americans have to the expression of religion in public life. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Prayer in the Town Hall', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Prayer in the Town Hall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece (NY)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prayers and Prayer Books', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'First Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T02:13:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/73c78fd5-e586-5035-b5fd-d785a3623d19', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73c78fd5-e586-5035-b5fd-d785a3623d19'}, {'abstract': 'The Colorado Avalanche, who are off to an N.H.L.-best start, were jolted out of their reverie Wednesday by the arrest of goaltender Semyon Varlamov in connection with an assault on his girlfriend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/sports/hockey/arrest-of-the-avalanches-goalie-casts-a-shadow-on-a-promising-season.html', 'snippet': 'The Colorado Avalanche, who are off to an N.H.L.-best start, were jolted out of their reverie Wednesday by the arrest of goaltender Semyon Varlamov in connection with an assault on his girlfriend.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — During their drive to Pepsi Center, there was much shimmering ground for two Colorado Avalanche fans to cover: the poise and production of the team’s 18-year-old rookie forward, Nathan MacKinnon; the inspired play of the defense; the mad genius of the first-year coach, Patrick Roy. And yet, as Keith Martin and his son-in-law drove to the Avalanche’s game here Saturday night against the Montreal Canadiens, they spoke mostly of the dark cloud shadowing the team’s resurgence.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/sports/avalanche1/avalanche1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 504, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/sports/avalanche1/avalanche1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 504}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/sports/avalanche1/avalanche1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank':