ivil-military relations in the country and its relationship with India.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/what-will-a-new-army-chief-mean-for-pakistan-and-the-neighborhood/', 'snippet': 'The choice for the new army chief in Pakistan will affect the civil-military relations in the country and its relationship with India.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since it was announced last month that Pakistan’s army chief, Gen. Ashfaq Parvez Kayani, would be retiring, Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif has kept the country dangling on his choice, creating a new parlor game for the chattering classes in the process. General Kayani has been characteristically mum, except for an unusual press release that said he was leaving the office on Nov. 29, without closing out other options, even as he accepted the concurrent role of chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1509, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/asia/04-kayani-IndiaInk/04-kayani-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Will a New Army Chief Mean for Pakistan and the Neighborhood?', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kayani, Ashfaq Parvez', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Inter-Services Intelligence', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T12:35:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shuja Nawaz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shuja', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nawaz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e73f024-cae4-5853-9875-e8e46bb60522', 'word_count': 1475, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e73f024-cae4-5853-9875-e8e46bb60522'}, {'abstract': 'Though it has a bookish name, the new lodging caters to more than the R.I.S.D. and Brown crowd.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/accommodations-in-providence-a-hipster-hotel-in-a-former-brothel/', 'snippet': 'Though it has a bookish name, the new lodging caters to more than the R.I.S.D. and Brown crowd.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was only a matter of time before Providence, R.I., long a petri dish for eggheads, design wunderkinds and culinary aspirants, would get its very own vintage-y, self-consciously cool hotel. The Dean, 52 rooms housed in a historic building from 1911 that was once a brothel, reflects the state’s bookish and somewhat gritty impulses toward homegrown authenticity. The lodging’s original mosaic tile flooring is intact, as is the old-timey brick facade, and rooms are furnished mostly with flea market finds. While the hotel’s name is an ode to the area’s academic community — it’s close to R.I.S.D. and Brown University — its arrival signals Providence’s continued cultural renaissance outside campus gates.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Providence, a Hipster Hotel in a Former Brothel', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Head of the Class', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providence (RI)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T13:00:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Hawgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hawgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8c57cda-604f-5d06-98b8-80caae984801', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8c57cda-604f-5d06-98b8-80caae984801'}, {'abstract': 'The multiple-choice responses provided did not offer readers the chance to express support for commentaries that questioned the official Chinese view of events.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/in-poll-many-chinese-angry-at-perceived-u-s-media-bias/', 'snippet': 'The multiple-choice responses provided did not offer readers the chance to express support for commentaries that questioned the official Chinese view of events.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lawyers might call it a leading question, one that would possibly be ruled out of order in a court of law: “How do you feel about the American media repeatedly putting out malicious views of China?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/04SINO-USMEDIA01/04SINO-USMEDIA01-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 222, 'width': 391, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/04SINO-USMEDIA01/04SINO-USMEDIA01-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 222, 'width': 391, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/world/04SINO-USMEDIA01/04SINO-USMEDIA01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': '