raska', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burger, Warren E', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Robert E', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stephens, Linda', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Galloway, Susan', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T14:26:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/431b3bdd-875d-5816-b99e-e8e4ae474350', 'word_count': 963, 'uri': 'nyt://article/431b3bdd-875d-5816-b99e-e8e4ae474350'}, {'abstract': 'The elections were seen as a test of an accord brokered by the European Union that aimed to overcome ethnic enmities in Kosovo and the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/world/europe/violence-mars-election-in-kosovo.html', 'snippet': 'The elections were seen as a test of an accord brokered by the European Union that aimed to overcome ethnic enmities in Kosovo and the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The future of a landmark power-sharing agreement between Serbs and ethnic Albanians in Kosovo was called into doubt on Monday after local elections in Kosovo over the weekend were blighted by violence and intimidation by people suspected of being Serbian hard-liners.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Violence Mars Election in Kosovo', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Accord Tested\r\nAmid Violence\r\nIn Kosovo Vote', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kosovo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Serbia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T14:39:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Bilefsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bilefsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d60c65e0-40f0-5587-87dd-c247f809eff5', 'word_count': 617, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d60c65e0-40f0-5587-87dd-c247f809eff5'}, {'abstract': 'On not learning from experience.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/a-tale-of-two-fed-presidents/', 'snippet': 'On not learning from experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Props to Jeffrey Lacker, the president of the Richmond Fed, for admitting that he has been wrong so far about inflation. Indeed he has: Lacker has been warning about inflationary dangers for more than five years. Still, given the behavior of so many interest rate and inflation hawks in this Lesser Depression — the norm seems to be never even acknowledging the wrong predictions, or trying to rewrite what they said in the past — Lacker’s frank confession of error is refreshing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Tale of Two Fed Presidents', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T14:53:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4faa36b4-fe73-5b2d-bd62-89099dc43b55', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4faa36b4-fe73-5b2d-bd62-89099dc43b55'}, {'abstract': 'Video of Egypt’s deposed president, Mohamed Morsi, in court was broadcast on state television and widely shared online.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/egyptian-television-shows-morsi-in-court/', 'snippet': 'Video of Egypt’s deposed president, Mohamed Morsi, in court was broadcast on state television and widely shared online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 5:38 p.m. | As my colleagues David Kirkpatrick and Mayy el-Sheikh report, Egypt’s deposed president, Mohamed Morsi, appeared in court on Monday to face charges of inciting the murder of protesters, his first public appearance since his removal from office in July.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reaction on the Streets and Online as Morsi Appears in Court', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morsi, Mohamed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T14:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb187728-9470-5cf6-b37f-c8b32ec88706', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb187728-9470-5cf6-b37f-c8b32ec88706'}, {'abstract': 'But for full-time workers, especially those 35 or older, the gender gap in wages remains pronounced.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/in-part-time-jobs-women-outearn-men/', 'snippet': 'But for full-time workers, especially those 35 or older, the gender gap in wages remains pronounced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The oft-lamented gender wage gap disappears and actually reverses when only part-time workers are considered, according to a new data release from the Bureau of Labor Statistics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Part-Time Jobs, Women Outearn Men', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f3c9560-8afe-5d61-a291-9d01f9ded760', 'word_count': 334, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f3c9560-8afe-5d61-a291-9d01f9ded760'}, {'abstract': 'Men’s Wearhouse refused to allow Jos. A. Bank confidential access to its books, possible ending the battle to combine two of the country’s biggest retailers of men’s suits.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/mens-wearhouse-rejects-jos-a-bank-again/', 'snippet': 'Men’s Wearhouse refused to allow Jos. A. Bank confidential access to its books, possible ending the battle to combine two of the country’s biggest retailers of men’s suits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Men’s Wearhouse again rebuffed a $2.3 billion takeover bid by Jos. A. Bank on Monday, refusing to allow the rival retailer confidential access to its books. The move may be the last salvo in the battle to combine two of the country’s biggest retailers of men’s suits.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/dealbook/dbpix-suits/dbpix-wearhouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/business/dealbook/dbpix-suits/dbpix-wearhouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/dealbook/dbpix-suits/dbpix-wearhouse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/dealbook/dbpix-suits/dbpix-wearhouse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/business/dealbook/dbpix-suits/dbpix-wearhouse-thumb