], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6831dcd6-ac88-5314-aa87-c84c32511d05', 'word_count': 775, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6831dcd6-ac88-5314-aa87-c84c32511d05'}, {'abstract': 'The leader of Pussy Riot has gone missing in the Russian prison system.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/where-is-nadya/', 'snippet': 'The leader of Pussy Riot has gone missing in the Russian prison system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Soon after she arrived in a penal colony in Mordovia in late 2012, Nadezhda (Nadya) Tolokonnikova, the leader of the protest punk group Pussy Riot, asked for a copy of Anatoly Marchenko’s “My Testimony,” an exhaustive accounting of the life of Soviet political prisoners. Marchenko spent 15 of his 48 years in Soviet prisons, including a number in Mordovlag (an acronym for Mordovian camps), the part of the gulag where Tolokonnikova was serving her two-year sentence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Is Nadya of Pussy Riot?', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cold War Era', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorbachev, Mikhail S', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pussy Riot', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations',