ie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thomas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c86401d-cb0c-52ea-ba9b-ec51b61c2f6e', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c86401d-cb0c-52ea-ba9b-ec51b61c2f6e'}, {'abstract': 'Kewsong Lee, who had been at Warburg for more than two decades, will hold the new position of deputy chief investment officer for corporate private equity at Carlyle.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/high-level-executive-switches-to-carlyle-from-warburg-pincus/', 'snippet': 'Kewsong Lee, who had been at Warburg for more than two decades, will hold the new position of deputy chief investment officer for corporate private equity at Carlyle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group has hired Kewsong Lee away from his post as managing director at Warburg Pincus, an unusually high-level transition within private equity’s executive ranks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High-Level Executive Switches to Carlyle From Warburg Pincus', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wooing an Executive', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T17:26:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Abrams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Abrams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8019233b-6a9e-5555-85f1-5c1ba35c1def', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8019233b-6a9e-5555-85f1-5c1ba35c1def'}, {'abstract': 'With its new price range, Twitter is worth as much as $14 billion. A calculator offers a way for investors to decide if that is too high or just right.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/weigh-in-on-twitters-i-p-o-value/', 'snippet': 'With its new price range, Twitter is worth as much as $14 billion. A calculator offers a way for investors to decide if that is too high or just right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twitter is increasing the price for its upcoming initial public offering by as much as a third. The social network is now looking to raise $23 to $25 a share, according to a filing on Monday with the Securities and Exchange Commission.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weigh In on Twitter’s I.P.O. Value', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Calculators', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Reuters Group PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T17:28:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aeff9e9a-8c9a-5f40-8672-e9d0f2493140', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aeff9e9a-8c9a-5f40-8672-e9d0f2493140'}, {'abstract': 'Lina Lapelyte’s “Have a Good Day!” will make its American premiere at the festival in January.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/lithuanian-opera-rounds-out-prototype-festival-lineup/', 'snippet': 'Lina Lapelyte’s “Have a Good Day!” will make its American premiere at the festival in January.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The “Prototype: Opera/Theater/Now” festival of avant-garde chamber opera and musical theater has added one stage production — the American premiere of “Have a Good Day!” by the Lithuanian composer Lina Lapelyte — as well as two concerts to the schedule it announced in July. It has also set the dates for the individual productions.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lithuanian Opera Rounds Out Prototype Festival Lineup', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lithuanian Opera At Prototype Festival', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T17:30:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b833e444-23fe-5ac7-8e85-0ef7fa6fbdcc', 'word_count': 299, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b833e444-23fe-5ac7-8e85-0ef7fa6fbdcc'}, {'abstract': 'How an (unwise) aversion to arbitrariness can drive rapid social change.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/casinos-pot-and-the-quest-for-consistency/', 'snippet': 'How an (unwise) aversion to arbitrariness can drive rapid social change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column on “pot and jackpots” — that is, the march toward marijuana legalization and the spread of casino gambling — tried to widen the usual culture-war frame to encompass not just bedroom-and-altar hot buttons, but the way the broader logic of “consenting adults” is working itself out in other areas of American life. One point I didn’t get to, though, is the extent to which both of these issues, pot and gambling, illustrate what one might call the rationalizing impulse in modern American politics, which seeks perfect fairness and consistency at the expense of compromises rooted in the accidents of history, and which makes it hard for conservatives to defend older, inherently-arbitrary arrangements even when they make practical sense.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Casinos, Pot and the Quest For Consistency', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Casinos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gambling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marijuana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Native Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlantic City (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nevada', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T17:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96e7a733-b936-5395-a708-8589c90e13c0', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96e7a733-b936-5395-a708-8589c90e13c0'}, {'abstract': 'The actress looked casual and cozy at Los Angeles International Airport yesterday.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/the-look-rosie-huntington-whiteleys-jet-set-chic/', 'snippet': 'The actress looked casual and cozy at Los Angeles International Airport yesterday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Girl: The actress was travel-ready in a star-print cardigan, oversize shades and fedora at Los Angeles International Airport yesterday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosie Huntington-Whiteley’s Jet-Set Chic', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models (Professional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huntington-Whiteley, Rosie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T17:30:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b09fb8b0-af91-55ed-a4df-494ae6a63b83', 'word_count': 43, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b09fb8b0-af91-55ed-a4df-494ae6a63b83'}, {'abstract': 'Did Medicare deny you coverage because you were a patient “on observation status”? Tell us about it.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/appealing-observation-status-to-medicare/', 'snippet': 'Did Medicare deny you coverage because you were a patient “on observation status”? Tell us about it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A question for readers: Have you filed an appeal with Medicare after it would not cover nursing home care or prescription drugs following hospitalization — because you were on observation status? We’d like to know about it. Please leave a comment. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Appealing Observation Status to Medicare', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T17:41:55+0000', 'document_type': 'ar