 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a224698-d520-5ac4-94fa-bdb2ef2f1c7d', 'word_count': 493, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a224698-d520-5ac4-94fa-bdb2ef2f1c7d'}, {'abstract': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/weekend-gun-report-november-1-3-2013/', 'snippet': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday morning, Paul Ciancia, 23, walked into Los Angeles International Airport with a legally purchased .223-caliber assault rifle and five 30-round magazines and\xa0opened fire on a T.S.A. security checkpoint, killing 39-year-old Gerardo Hernandez, a father of two who had screened passengers there for three years, and wounding four others—two additional T.S.A. agents and two passengers. The rampage was halted when he was shot in the mouth and the leg by authorities. The next day, federal prosecutors charged him with murder.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Gun Report: November 1-3, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T21:30:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8f951b4-a2c1-59d3-98c7-438d4515ac8e', 'word_count': 2721, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8f951b4-a2c1-59d3-98c7-438d4515ac8e'}, {'abstract': '“American Masters: Jimi Hendrix — Hear My Train a Comin’” is a documentary about the guitarist whose death in 1970 at the age of 27 cemented his legendary status.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/arts/television/revisiting-jimi-hendrix-on-pbss-american-masters.html', 'snippet': '“American Masters: Jimi Hendrix — Hear My Train a Comin’” is a documentary about the guitarist whose death in 1970 at the age of 27 cemented his legendary status.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For some in the dismayingly large club of rock stars who died too young, it’s easy to imagine an alternate future in which fate or bad judgment does not intervene and they live to a ripe old age. John Lennon becomes a patron of the arts and fends off repeated requests that he run for office. Cass Elliot does a stint on “The View.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Talent Whose Light Was Bright but Brief', 'kicker': 'Television Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Talent Whose Light Was Bright but Brief', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendrix, Jimi', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T21:38:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e10b180-3647-5992-b2fd-549983bf9c0d', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e10b180-3647-5992-b2fd-549983bf9c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Genetic testing of 44 herbal supplements from a dozen companies found that only two companies used completely authentic ingredients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/05/health/Testing-Supplements.html', 'snippet': 'Genetic testing of 44 herbal supplements from a dozen companies found that only two companies used completely authentic ingredients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Genetic testing of 44 herbal supplements from a dozen companies found that only two companies used completely authentic ingredients.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/science/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/science/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 309}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/science/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/science/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT/1105-HERBAL-FOR-FRONT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 309, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Testing Supplements', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dietary Supplements and Herbal Remedies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T21:39:25+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Health', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/e95fc00d-ec84-5c2b-990d-03ddc68c8d22', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/e95fc00d-ec84-5c2b-990d-03ddc68c8d22'}, {'abstract': 'The festival, which has become the alt-classical world’s main showcase, will offer 11 concerts, with new works by several young composers.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/raft-of-new-works-scheduled-for-ecstatic-music-festival/', 'snippet': 'The festival, which has become the alt-classical world’s main showcase, will offer 11 concerts, with new works by several young composers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ecstatic Music Festival, which has quickly become the alt-classical world’s main showcase, will offer 11 concerts during its fourth season, which opens Jan. 31 and runs through March 29. As in past years, the concerts, which are assembled by the composer Judd Greenstein, are double or triple bills in which ensembles (many led by composers) perform separate sets and also join forces, either on new collaborative works or improvisations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Raft of New Works Scheduled for Ecstatic Music Festival', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ecstatic Music Festival', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T21:39:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/476b15fe-60ec-5c9c-9aad-bbd65904568c', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/476b15fe-60ec-5c9c-9aad-bbd65904568c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Sparks discusses his work, including how he builds stories that will work for both page and screen.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/the-read-around-nicholas-sparks/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Sparks discusses his work, including how he builds stories that will work for both page and screen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Read Around,” a new weekly video feature, authors discuss the when, where and how behind their latest books. Below, Nicholas Sparks talks about his novel “The Longest Ride” and how he approaches building a story that will work for both page and screen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Read Around: Nicholas Sparks', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sparks, Nicholas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-04T21:41:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06ab754d-dd59-577c-8e5e-3346607194b2', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06ab754d-dd59-577c-8e5e-3346607194b2'}, {'abstract': 'How often did you apologize to your boss, your friends or your family last week?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/04/being-a-working-mother-means-always-having-to-say-youre-sorry/', 'snippet': 'How often did you apologize to your boss, your friends or your family last week?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sorry!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '