that still makes me laugh.” The actor Bruce Dern, after appearing alongside the Duke in the 1972 western “The Cowboys,” correctly boasted that he was “the only actor who ever killed John Wayne.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Secrets of a Game Show Writer', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T01:00:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Levinson Wilk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'Levinson', 'lastname': 'Wilk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a0c7d91c-3412-525b-9a8e-d30e91e087f6', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a0c7d91c-3412-525b-9a8e-d30e91e087f6'}, {'abstract': 'Charlie Crist, a former Republican who was Florida’s governor from 2007 to 2011, formally announced that he would run for the job again, this time as a Democrat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/us/politics/crist-former-florida-governor-tosses-hat-in-ring-again.html', 'snippet': 'Charlie Crist, a former Republican who was Florida’s governor from 2007 to 2011, formally announced that he would run for the job again, this time as a Democrat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ST. PETERSBURG — Hopscotching from one Democratic touchstone to the next — education, voting rights, the environment and bipartisanship — former Gov. Charlie Crist of Florida announced Monday that he would run for the job once again, this time as a Democrat.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/us/CRIST-1/CRIST-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crist, Former Florida Governor, Tosses Hat in Ring Again', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Florida’s Ex-Governor Tosses Hat in Ring Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crist, Charlie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T01:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lance Speere and Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lance', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Speere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/768c15c1-6a49-523a-b37f-08a94a63eb42', 'word_count': 771, 'uri': 'nyt://article/768c15c1-6a49-523a-b37f-08a94a63eb42'}, {'abstract': 'A short film celebrates Alfred Russel Wallace, who is co-credited with discovering the theory of natural selection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/opinion/the-animated-life-of-ar-wallace.html', 'snippet': 'A short film celebrates Alfred Russel Wallace, who is co-credited with discovering the theory of natural selection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although Alfred Russel Wallace made one of the most important scientific discoveries in history, he’s been all but forgotten. A contemporary of Charles Darwin, Wallace was the other guy to discover natural selection – the evolutionary process whereby better adapted organisms are more likely to survive and pass on their traits than less adapted ones. Although two people discovered this theory, evolution by natural selection is virtually synonymous with Darwin. This is partly due to the lasting fame of Darwin’s opus, “On the Origin of Species,” but some argue it is also due to Wallace’s extraordinary modesty – he lauded Darwin’s work and humbly downplayed his own contributions. In 1889 he even wrote a book in support of evolution titled “Darwinism.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/opinion/video-opd