ue': 'Wheeler, Thomas E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sohn, Gigi B', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Communications Commission', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T01:36:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wyatt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wyatt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/342cd673-f6b5-5aeb-a2b9-76dea1951ea1', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/342cd673-f6b5-5aeb-a2b9-76dea1951ea1'}, {'abstract': 'An ill-advised visit to Cairo undercuts earlier efforts to rebuke generals and promote democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/opinion/mr-kerry-fumbles-in-egypt.html', 'snippet': 'An ill-advised visit to Cairo undercuts earlier efforts to rebuke generals and promote democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secretary of State John Kerry’s trip to Egypt, included in his Middle East itinerary at the last minute, served only to add to the confusion over the Obama administration’s policy toward this critically important Arab nation. Mr. Kerry was the highest-ranking American official to visit Cairo since Mohamed Morsi, the country’s first democratically elected president, was deposed in July. Mr. Kerry seemed to go further than necessary or prudent to make common cause with the authoritarian generals who led the coup and are now running the country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mr. Kerry Fumbles in Egypt', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Kerry Fumbles in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None},