 years, the Roman Catholic Diocese of Brooklyn and the nonprofit group running Christ the King High School in Queens have acted as one, managing the twin hurdles of declining enrollments and shrinking revenues with a joint aim of fostering parochial education.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/DIOCESE/DIOCESE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brooklyn Diocese Sues One of Its High Schools in Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diocese of Brooklyn Sues One of Its Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christ the King High School', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Charter Schools', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T01:43:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Al Baker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Al', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f22a06b-d53a-507c-9e31-4c15a4b14c69', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f22a06b-d53a-507c-9e31-4c15a4b14c69'}, {'abstract': 'A Senate vote shows support for fair treatment of gay, bisexual and transgender workers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/opinion/toward-ending-workplace-discrimination.html', 'snippet': 'A Senate vote shows support for fair treatment of gay, bisexual and transgender workers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An overdue measure to outlaw employment discrimination based on sexual orientation and gender identity cleared a procedural hurdle on Monday night in the Senate. The move is one step toward putting into federal law a basic principle most Americans support: Job applicants and employees should be judged on their professional credentials and the caliber of their work, and not be held back because of who they are.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page':