kipedia entries came to be incorporated into his speeches with no attribution, faced charges of direct plagiarism on Monday night.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Rand Paul Faces New Charges of Plagiarism', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Senator Paul Faces New Charges of Plagiarism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plagiarism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Rand', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BuzzFeed Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wikipedia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Week, The (Magazine)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Dan', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kentucky', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T04:33:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/545b2051-9c99-5d67-8324-0aa692ddb421', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/545b2051-9c99-5d67-8324-0aa692ddb421'}, {'abstract': 'The Mets formally announced that their radio games are moving to WOR-AM in a five-year deal with the news and talk station’s owner, Clear Channel Media and Entertainment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/sports/baseball/mets-games-move-to-wor-am.html', 'snippet': 'The Mets formally announced that their radio games are moving to WOR-AM in a five-year deal with the news and talk station’s owner, Clear Channel Media and Entertainment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mets formally announced that their radio games are moving to WOR-AM (710) in a five-year deal with the news and talk station’s owner, Clear Channel Media and Entertainment. The announcement did not say if Howie Rose, who has called Mets games since 1996, and Josh Lewin, who joined the Mets’ broadcast team in 2012, will be moving to WOR from WFAN, AM and FM, which had carried the games since 1987. In a statement, the Mets said: "Now that our agreement is official, WOR is in discussions regarding announcers.” ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mets Games Move to WOR-AM', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mets Games to WOR', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WOR-AM', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rose, Howie', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radio', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clear Channel Communications Inc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T04:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c6cb58f-6d9b-5294-8da9-f8ecb6ecb7a9', 'word_count': 122, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c6cb58f-6d9b-5294-8da9-f8ecb6ecb7a9'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama told supporters on Monday that he was committed to fixing the problems of the health exchange website that have prevented enrollment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/us/politics/obama-to-campaign-to-ensure-health-laws-success.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama told supporters on Monday that he was committed to fixing the problems of the health exchange website that have prevented enrollment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — On the fifth anniversary of his election, President Obama told a rally of grass-roots supporters on Monday evening that “I’ve got one more campaign in me” — to make sure his signature health care law works.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama to Campaign to Ensure Health Law’s Success', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organizing for Action', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T04:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jackie Calmes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jackie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Calmes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/02758717-9cbd-5c97-b963-82b62de48859', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02758717-9cbd-5c97-b963-82b62de48859'}, {'abstract': 'At a sale of paintings, drawings and sculptures from the estate of Jan Krugier, a Geneva-based dealer, many expensive works did not sell at all, or went far below expectations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/arts/despite-picassos-bidding-is-sluggish-at-christies.html', 'snippet': 'At a sale of paintings, drawings and sculptures from the estate of Jan Krugier, a Geneva-based dealer, many expensive works did not sell at all, or went far below expectations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The highly anticipated fall auction season got off to a surprisingly gloomy start on Monday night at Christie’s, which held a special sale of paintings, drawings and sculptures from the estate of Jan Krugier, the Geneva-based dealer who died in 2008. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 783, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 783}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 785, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1569, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard