ed to know in New York for Tuesday: mayoral decision day, fall-appropriate weather and a 19th century election surprisingly free of “ruffianism.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 12:10 p.m. | It’s finally here — Election Day.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 1919, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05nytoday/05nytoday-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York Today: To the Polls', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T10:57:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Correal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Correal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13af26d4-55a8-5e0b-8db2-b3a4bf3c9655', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13af26d4-55a8-5e0b-8db2-b3a4bf3c9655'}, {'abstract': 'Throughout the day, Times journalists will be filing dispatches from around the country, with a particular focus on New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/its-election-day/', 'snippet': 'Throughout the day, Times journalists will be filing dispatches from around the country, with a particular focus on New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Today is Election Day across the nation, as voters in many states go to the polls to choose local and state officials. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Election Day', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T11:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/391c486a-bffd-5261-9b45-34d15a754ec8', 'word_count': 189, 'uri': 'nyt://article/391c486a-bffd-5261-9b45-34d15a754ec8'}, {'abstract': 'Three recipes for broccoli from chefs who know what they’re talking about (they have children).', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/broccoli-gone-wild/', 'snippet': 'Three recipes for broccoli from chefs who know what they’re talking about (they have children).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks ago, while researching Michael Moss’s cover story about broccoli’s image problem, I learned about the Kitchen Community, a Colorado-based\xa0nonprofit that has put up, in low-income neighborhoods, billboards with simple recipes to encourage people to cook. Cool idea, except that the broccoli recipe struck me as wrong: “Olive oil & salt, 350° oven, 1 hour.” Broccoli is a favorite in my house. During the week, I boil the florets in two inches of water, drain and add butter and salt. Sometimes, if I’ve had enough sleep, I go wild and sauté it after parboiling — this adds char and brings out sweetness. My husband can steam it with scientific precision. None of these methods take an hour; maybe 15 minutes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broccoli Gone Wild', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Broccoli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Gabrielle', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moss, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Telepan, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waxman, Jonathan (1950- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T11:00:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lia Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/123f95ff-43b3-5d79-b817-3d7a9b8cdcaf', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/123f95ff-43b3-5d79-b817-3d7a9b8cdcaf'}, {'abstract': 'The often lucrative short-term rentals facilitated by Airbnb are often in violation of New York City zoning law or of tenants’ leases.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/daily-report-in-new-york-airbnb-offers-extra-income-but-questionable-legality/', 'snippet': 'The often lucrative short-term rentals facilitated by Airbnb are often in violation of New York City zoning law or of tenants’ leases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Airbnb is a service adored by some, despised by others, and most commonly known as a place to rent out your apartment while you are out of town for a few days, Elizabeth A. Harris reports. But doing so is often illegal in New York City, one reason the company has locked horns with the New York State attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-superJumbo-v3.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/30/technology/bits-daily-report/bits-daily-report-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS