-bb50-50cf-ad5d-5920cf352ad0', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33e5a18c-bb50-50cf-ad5d-5920cf352ad0'}, {'abstract': 'To watch the health insurance sign-up process last month in Louisville, a city of 600,000, was to get a glimpse of how the rollout of the exchanges was supposed to work from coast to coast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/affordable-care-act/2013/11/05/in-kentucky-a-glimpse-of-health-insurance-help/', 'snippet': 'To watch the health insurance sign-up process last month in Louisville, a city of 600,000, was to get a glimpse of how the rollout of the exchanges was supposed to work from coast to coast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOUISVILLE, Ky. – Jennifer Albrecht lost her job after being given a diagnosis of multiple sclerosis last year – a turn of events that her husband, Hugh, described as feeling like “a building fell on us.” She stretches out her medicine because she cannot afford the refills, suffering worse flare-ups as a result. But last month, after seeking the help of a “kynector” – one of Kentucky’s counselors certified to help people sign up for insurance under the federal health care law – Ms. Albrecht found she qualified for Medicaid. Her coverage will take effect at the beginning of 2014. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Kentucky, a Glimpse of Health Insurance Help', 'kicker': 'In Practice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T13:30:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d55b3ba3-3ed6-5566-b078-6a01f6ba2ae2', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d55b3ba3-3ed6-5566-b078-6a01f6ba2ae2'}, {'abstract': 'Keep on eavesdropping, America, because as long as you do Israelis will know you’re still helping police the world.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/spies-r-us/', 'snippet': 'Keep on eavesdropping, America, because as long as you do Israelis will know you’re still helping police the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A solid majority of Americans say it is “unacceptable for the United States to monitor the phones of allied leaders,” according to a recent poll by the Pew Research Center. But Israelis aren’t so fussed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spies R Us', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wiretapping and Other Eavesdropping Devices and Methods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T13:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shmuel Rosner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shmuel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a357a13-2620-5896-bc57-bb7fce11100f', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a357a13-2620-5896-bc57-bb7fce11100f'}, {'abstract': 'A man who fired a weapon Monday night in the Garden State Plaza mall, sending thousands running, shot and killed himself early Tuesday morn