 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87d7d9d8-ef4c-51b0-b7af-3651abaa86a0', 'word_count': 624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87d7d9d8-ef4c-51b0-b7af-3651abaa86a0'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/the-gun-report-november-5-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Guns are now allowed in public libraries in Seattle, thanks to\xa0a state supreme court ruling holding that\xa0cities have no right to ban guns in public places such as parks and libraries. The board of the library system said it did not have a choice but to remove its longstanding ban on firearms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 5, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T15:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90e0cfcd-f2f9-5993-9f4a-6c530866ed89', 'word_count': 1381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90e0cfcd-f2f9-5993-9f4a-6c530866ed89'}, {'abstract': 'The New York Herald Tribune front page coverage of Cosmonaut Valentina Tereshkova’s journey into space.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/1963-first-woman-in-space/', 'snippet': 'The New York Herald Tribune front page coverage of Cosmonaut Valentina Tereshkova’s journey into space.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Hello Hawk, hello Hawk, this is Seagull”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1963: First Woman in Space', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Moscow (Russia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T15:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Barthelemy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barthelemy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0e31f69-341e-5850-b225-d57e4376b15c', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0e31f69-341e-5850-b225-d57e4376b15c'}, {'abstract': 'Here is a sampling of some of the interesting races and ballot initiatives the National Desk will be following throughout the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/national-races-were-watching-today/', 'snippet': 'Here is a sampling of some of the interesting races and ballot initiatives the National Desk will be following throughout the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Virginia, Kenneth T. Cuccinelli II, the Republican candidate, and Terry McAuliffe, a Democrat, are running for governor of a state that had once been a Republican stronghold. Mr. McAuliffe, who has been slightly ahead in the polls, was joined by President Obama at a rally on Sunday. And Mr. Cuccinelli has been winding down his campaign with a whirlwind of events, campaigning alongside a roster of Republican governors and presidential hopefuls.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/us/liveblog-va2/liveblog-va2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'National Races We’re Watching Today', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T15:37:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce7556c0-3077-59f6-9ab4-bcbd24d4551f', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce7556c0-3077-59f6-9ab4-bcbd24d4551f'}, {'abstract': 'The dismissal of the manager, Troy Carter, occurred days before the scheduled release of the singer’s new album. Mr. Carter had managed Lady Gaga since 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/business/media/lady-gaga-said-to-fire-her-manager.html', 'snippet': 'The dismissal of the manager, Troy Carter, occurred days before the scheduled release of the singer’s new album. Mr. Carter had managed Lady Gaga since 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lady Gaga has fired her manager, Troy Carter, just days before the release of her new album, according to three people with direct knowledge of the news who were not authorized to speak about it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lady Gaga Said to Fire Her Manager', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lady Gaga Is Said to Have Fired Manager', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interscope Records', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Troy (1972- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T15:42:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7392277c-a70f-504d-8984-f63184f3e368', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7392277c-a70f-504d-8984-f63184f3e368'}, {'abstract': 'With Election Day finally here, Mr. Lhota, who has trailed well behind his Democratic opponent, did not appear eager to engage in conversation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/new-york-lhota-has-little-to-say-as-he-casts-ballot/', 'snippet': 'With Election Day finally here, Mr. Lhota, who has trailed well behind his Democratic opponent, did not appear eager to engage in conversation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If voting for himself for mayor felt climactic for Joseph J. Lhota, he did not revel in the moment on Tuesday morning.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York: Lhota Has Little to Say as He Casts Ballot', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T15:55:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/632d265f-69cb-533f-ae0e-f23e5b5a3067', 'word_count': 291, 'uri': 'nyt://article/632d265f-69cb-533f-ae0e-f23e5b5a3067'}, {'abstract': 'The Taiwanese computer maker said Tuesday that its chief executive, J.T. Wang, had resigned, citing an inability to come to grips with a downturn in the PC business.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/acers-chief-resigns-amid-slump-in-pc-sales/', 'snippet': 'The Taiwanese computer maker said Tuesday that its chief executive, J.T. Wang, had resigned, citing an inability to come to grips with a downturn in the PC business.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL —\xa0Acer, the Taiwanese computer maker, said Tuesday that its chief executive, J.T. Wang, had resigned, citing an inability to come to grips with a downturn in the PC business.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':