artlingly pleasant anomaly in the normally intimidating 11-million-person megacity of São Paulo. On a quaint square across from a tiny 112-year-old church, a bar called Frangó (frangobar.com.br) offers worn wooden tables in cozy nooks, an astonishing 500-label beer list and a celebrated version of the popular Brazilian chicken croquettes called coxinhas. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/travel/10-frugal-span/10-frugal-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rio and São Paulo, Go North', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Rio and São Paulo, Go North', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kugel, Seth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sao Paulo (Brazil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T17:56:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Kugel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kugel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/65d7da03-bbe7-5cfc-9f81-7df0993ec978', 'word_count': 1119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65d7da03-bbe7-5cfc-9f81-7df0993ec978'}, {'abstract': 'The race for governor in swing state Virginia has boiled down to a street fight for voter turnout Tuesday, with the rest of the country watching ahead of Congressional midterm elections next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/virginia-a-street-fight-for-turnout/', 'snippet': 'The race for governor in swing state Virginia has boiled down to a street fight for voter turnout Tuesday, with the rest of the country watching ahead of Congressional midterm elections next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Terry McAuliffe, the Democratic candidate for governor, just shrugged when one commuter declined to shake his hand at a Metro station. “Can’t get ’em all,” he said, more amused than disappointed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 644, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1289, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/nyregion/05va-1/05va-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia: A Street Fight for Turnout', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T17:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Maguire', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Maguire', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8fc31af-8e09-5179-b600-caf7c8711336', 'word_count': 594, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8fc31af-8e09-5179-b600-caf7c8711336'}, {'abstract': 'The death of the prisoner, a 22-year-old man who had leukemia, prompted accusations of medical malpractice by Palestinian leaders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/world/middleeast/palestinian-inmate-with-cancer-dies-in-israeli-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'The death of the prisoner, a 22-year-old man who had leukemia, prompted accusations of medical malpractice by Palestinian leaders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GAZA — A Palestinian prisoner with cancer died in an Israeli hospital on Tuesday, prompting accusations of medical malpractice by Palestinian leaders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Palestinian Inmate With Cancer Dies in Israeli Hospital', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Israel: Improper Treatment Alleged in Prisoner’s Death', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Akram, Fares', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T17:58:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Fares Akram', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Fares', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Akram', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdb91cc3-833a-5422-8275-709248cc2c0d', 'word_count': 210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdb91cc3-833a-5422-8275-709248cc2c0d'}, {'abstract': 'Marvel Comics is expanding its superhero stable to include a teenage Muslim girl as a lead character.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/books/marvel-comics-introducing-a-muslim-girl-superhero.html', 'snippet': 'Marvel Comics is expanding its superhero stable to include a teenage Muslim girl as a lead character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With most superheroes, when you take away the colorful costume, mask and cape, what you find underneath is a white man. But not always. In February, as part of a continuing effort to diversify its offerings, Marvel Comics will begin a series whose lead character, Kamala Khan, is a teenage Muslim girl living in Jersey City.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 685}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 897, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1794, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/marvel-image/marvel-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mighty, Muslim and Leaping Off the Page', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'She’s Mighty, Muslim and Leaping Off the Page', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gustines, George Gene', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marvel Comics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, G Willow', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:03:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Gene Gustines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'Gene', 'lastname': 'Gustines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d9d5a6c-9b4f-5473-92ef-191b5add4d14', 'word_count': 802, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d9d5a6c-9b4f-5473-92ef-191b5add4d14'}, {'abstract': 'Our daughters (8 and 10) think we already are married. We had a commitment ceremony almost 20 years ago. When we head to City Hall to “make it legal,” wouldn’t it just confuse them if we ask them to come along?', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/should-our-daughters-come-to-our-gay-wedding/', 'snippet': 'Our daughters (8 and 10) think we already are married. We had a commitment ceremony almost 20 years ago. When we head to City Hall to “make it legal,” wouldn’t it just confuse them if we ask them to come along?', 'lead_paragraph': 'One morning when I was making breakfast before school, my second-grade daughter, fresh off her school’s diversity unit on homosexuality, decided it was time I had a lesson in gay rights. First, she said, you should never use the word “gay” in a negative way, as in “That’s so gay!” Very interesting, I said, plotting to push a little deeper into this intriguing topic. So what is “gay,” I asked? Gay is when two boys like each other, and lesbian is when two girls like each other, she explained. Did she know anyone who was gay or lesbian, I asked? “I’m pretty sure I’m a lesbian because all my friends are girls,” she declared. Did she know anyone else? “Well, Larry only plays with boys, so he must be gay.” Anyone else? Nope.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Should Our Daughters Come to Our (Gay) Wedding?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:04:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Peyser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peyser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f30078d3-1437-519f-988b-0543e1ec2b30', 'word_count': 614, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f30078d3-1437-519f-988b-0543e1ec2b30'}, {'abstract': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/in-our-pages-november-6/', 'snippet': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': '1938 Plot to Kill King of Siam Found', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Our Pages: November 6', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History (Academic Subject)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Thailand', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:06:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a935f4b7-7198-563b-afbf-047330a2248c', 'word_count': 205, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a935f4b7-7198-563b-afbf-047330a2248c'}, {'abstract': '“Amaluna,” which opened in Montreal in April 2012, is inspired by “The Tempest,” and directed by Ms. Paulus, who won a Tony for directing this year’s “Pippin” revival.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/diane-pauluss-cirque-du-soleil-show-headed-to-new-york/', 'snippet': '“Amaluna,” which opened in Montreal in April 2012, is inspired by “The Tempest,” and directed by Ms. Paulus, who won a Tony for directing this year’s “Pippin” revival.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cirque du Soleil has discovered that one way to wow New Yorkers — that is, beyond the company’s usual blend of daring acrobatics and high-gloss artistry — is to come to town with productions staged by major directors. Last year, Cirque brought “Totem,” staged at Citi Field by Robert Lepage, the Canadian director whose production of Wagner’s “Ring” at the Metropolitan Opera has been the subject of debate among opera aficionados in recent years, and who also directed “Ka,” the Cirque spectacular in which an acrobat fell to her death in June.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 784}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 1002, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-cirque/05artsbeat-cirque-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diane Paulus’s Cirque du Soleil Show Headed to New York', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulus, Diane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cirque du Soleil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citi Field (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:07:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b033b54-3935-52e4-b01c-e872503af771', 'word_count': 229, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b033b54-3935-52e4-b01c-e872503af771'}, {'abstract': 'Bart Chilton said he would leave the Commodity Futures Trading Commission on the same day it voted for one of his favored proposals, a plan to limit speculation in commodities trading.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/in-surprise-exit-bart-chilton-to-depart-futures-commission/', 'snippet': 'Bart Chilton said he would leave the Commodity Futures Trading Commission on the same day it voted for one of his favored proposals, a plan to limit speculation in commodities trading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 8:10 p.m. | Bart Chilton, the outspoken regulator whose colorful commentary on financial risk taking positioned him as a fierce critic of the industry he helped oversee, announced on Tuesday that he was leaving his post at the Commodity Futures Trading Commission. The move is the latest sign that Wall Street’s scrappiest regulatory agency is poised for a makeover.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/SPECULATION-01/SPECULATION-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/business/SPECULATION-01/SPECULATION-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}},