Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:14:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Protess and Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Protess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a750600-42cd-5996-96fa-bcaec88a7e6d', 'word_count': 1109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a750600-42cd-5996-96fa-bcaec88a7e6d'}, {'abstract': 'New Yorkers will probably elect de Blasio, even though they have been warned not to do this by Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/its-election-day-why-is-no-one-panicking/', 'snippet': 'New Yorkers will probably elect de Blasio, even though they have been warned not to do this by Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Election Day! A day for fresh starts and new directions, though probably not in New Jersey, which looks set to re-elect its Republican governor, Chris Christie, by an overwhelming margin over the Democrat, Barbara Buono. Just how overwhelming is the big question, and the answer may well affect how much Mr. Christie will intrude into the lives of non-Jersey Americans in the next presidential race.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'It’s Election Day. Why Is No One Panicking?', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lhota, Joseph J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87a43629-e42b-5b74-8234-f39783dfd2fa', 'word_count': 371, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87a43629-e42b-5b74-8234-f39783dfd2fa'}, {'abstract': 'In Brownsville, Brooklyn, some voters said their views of the Police Department’s stop-and-frisk strategy influenced their opinions of the candidates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/new-york-stop-and-frisk-crosses-into-the-ballot-box/', 'snippet': 'In Brownsville, Brooklyn, some voters said their views of the Police Department’s stop-and-frisk strategy influenced their opinions of the candidates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just after 7 a.m. on Tuesday, Darrian Smith, 48, a custodian at Public School 150 in Brownsville, Brooklyn, was sweeping the grounds outside the school, which also serves as a polling place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York: Stop-and-Frisk Crosses into the Ballot Box', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17ccc1f4-e8ce-5df3-8b31-d43a5ac96e2e', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17ccc1f4-e8ce-5df3-8b31-d43a5ac96e2e'}, {'abstract': 'Sandwiched between the Ace Hotel and Powell’s City of Books, it features nine trendy food and retail outlets and has been endorsed by Carrie Brownstein, the city’s unofficial mayor.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/on-the-verge-in-portland-a-new-shopping-center-thats-so-portland-it-hurts/', 'snippet': 'Sandwiched between the Ace Hotel and Powell’s City of Books, it features nine trendy food and retail outlets and has been endorsed by Carrie Brownstein, the city’s unofficial mayor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An unexpected location in Portland, Ore., has evolved into a gleaming retail destination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On the Verge | In Portland, a New Shopping Center That’s So Portland It Hurts', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Portland (Ore)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Portlandia (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:21:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Borel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e472c13-1e69-51f9-b376-668a1f91a4a4', 'word_count': 214, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e472c13-1e69-51f9-b376-668a1f91a4a4'}, {'abstract': 'A new recording of a Civil War classic gives us a picture into 19th century American culture.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/listen-to-the-mockingbird/', 'snippet': 'A new recording of a Civil War classic gives us a picture into 19th century American culture.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The tune, so recognizable, was composed by an African-American street musician named Richard Milburn in 1855, about whom too little is known. The words were written by “Alice Hawthorne,” the nom de plume of a lyricist whose real name was Septimus Winner. (Why would anyone refuse to use such a name?)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/04/25/opinion/opinionator-pog-disunion/opinionator-pog-disunion-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Listen to the Mockingbird’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:22:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Widmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Widmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a3507f6-4eb7-531b-948f-22a16e5866d6', 'word_count': 844, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a3507f6-4eb7-531b-948f-22a16e5866d6'}, {'abstract': 'City and campaign officials reported that turnout so far has been low, despite the opportunity to choose a new mayor for the first time in 12 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/new-york-as-expected-not-very-many-voters-at-the-polls/', 'snippet': 'City and campaign officials reported that turnout so far has been low, despite the opportunity to choose a new mayor for the first time in 12 years.', 'lead_paragraph': ' By early Tuesday afternoon, election officials and both mayoral campaigns said turnout at the city’s 1,200 polling places was low to moderate, at most.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York: As Expected, Not Very Many Voters at the Polls', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:25:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09f65461-a474-5a10-8a5e-86ce66d4838b', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09f65461-a474-5a10-8a5e-86ce66d4838b'}, {'abstract': 'Brentwood Associates, based in Los Angeles, bought the men’s shoemaker from Goldner Hawn Johnson & Morrison, based in Minneapolis, for about $180 million.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/allen-edmonds-changes-private-equity-hands/', 'snippet': 'Brentwood Associates, based in Los Angeles, bought the men’s shoemaker from Goldner Hawn Johnson & Morrison, based in Minneapolis, for about $180 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The private equity firm Brentwood Asso