he “Africa Rising” narrative: The total number of people living in extreme poverty has increased.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/world/africa/behind-those-fast-growth-rates-rising-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'There is a disquieting reality behind the “Africa Rising” narrative: The total number of people living in extreme poverty has increased.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DAKAR, Senegal — It was his first post-election news conference, at a luxurious villa high above the Congo River, and the president of the Democratic Republic of Congo was in a combative mood. How dare the reporters question his country’s progress, he argued: just look at our sizzling growth rate — double, even triple, the rates of those pitiful laggards in the West.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind Those Fast Growth Rates, Rising Inequality', 'kicker': 'Letter From Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFRICA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kabila, Joseph', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:32:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/869ae706-403a-5e18-bbd2-ed03f95dfa6f', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/869ae706-403a-5e18-bbd2-ed03f95dfa6f'}, {'abstract': 'The increase of 139,000 subscribers was certainly helped by CBS’s dispute with Time Warner Cable. In Latin America, growth slowed significantly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/business/media/directv-reports-gain-in-us-subscribers.html', 'snippet': 'The increase of 139,000 subscribers was certainly helped by CBS’s dispute with Time Warner Cable. In Latin America, growth slowed significantly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DirecTV surprised Wall Street on Tuesday by reporting a gain of 139,000 television subscribers in the United States in the third quarter of the year, a sharply higher rise than analysts had expected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'DirecTV Reports Gain in U.S. Subscribers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DirecTV', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latin America', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Cable Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T18:37:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeef21d9-03fd-5135-8153-e2408f1363d6', 'word_count': 440, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeef21d9-03fd-5135-8153-e2408f1363d6'}, {'abstract': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission is seeking to expand the types of commodities future contracts subject to trading limits.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/proposed-rule-limits-size-of-commodities-traders-positions/', 'snippet': 'The Commodity Futures Trading Commission is seeking to expand the types of commodities future contracts subject to trading limits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1979, Nelson Bunker Hunt and William Hunt famously bought up as much silver as they could in the commodities market. By the time they were done, the brothers had acquired more than a third of the world’s supply of silver, sending the price of the precious metal soaring. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-speculation1/dbpix-speculation1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-speculation1/dbpix-speculation1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-speculation1/dbpix-speculation1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-speculation1/dbpix-speculation1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-speculation1/dbpix-speculation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-speculation1/dbpix-speculation1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-specula