elling a scrum of reporters, “Yes, I have smoked crack cocaine.”', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/i-have-smoked-crack-cocaine-torontos-mayor-admits-on-camera/', 'snippet': 'Toronto Mayor Rob Ford stunned constituents and his own staff on Tuesday by telling a scrum of reporters, “Yes, I have smoked crack cocaine.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Updated, 5:34 p.m. | After dodging questions for months about video evidence said to show him using drugs, Mayor Rob Ford of Toronto stunned constituents and his own staff on Tuesday by telling a scrum of reporters, “Yes, I have smoked crack cocaine.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘I Have Smoked Crack Cocaine,’ Toronto’s Mayor Admits on Camera', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Robert B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T19:37:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d4e4d48e-3921-51d1-9925-0e515fe82ff8', 'word_count': 641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d4e4d48e-3921-51d1-9925-0e515fe82ff8'}, {'abstract': 'While the M23 rebels of Congo send signals of peace, the photographer Pete Muller, who has been documenting the conflict, will continue his work there exploring notions of masculinity.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/a-congolese-rebellion-routed-a-photographers-work-continues/', 'snippet': 'While the M23 rebels of Congo send signals of peace, the photographer Pete Muller, who has been documenting the conflict, will continue his work there exploring notions of masculinity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The column of soldiers marched uphill single file, slowly but deliberately making its way to the town of Bunagana, on the border between the Democratic Republic of Congo and Uganda. Pete Muller trekked alongside them to photograph the moment when Congolese soldiers liberated the town from the control of the M23 rebel group, part of a rapid advance by government forces that pushed the group out of areas it held in its year-and-a-half long insurrection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Congolese Rebellion Routed, a Photographer’s Work Continues', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T19:38:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/28204c6e-670f-522f-b01b-f63fc80adcba', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28204c6e-670f-522f-b01b-f63fc80adcba'}, {'abstract': 'An app from Audiovox works with a remote wireless shutter release to frame larger or more distant shots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/technology/personaltech/review-audiovox-shutterball-remote-shutter-release.html', 'snippet': 'An app from Audiovox works with a remote wireless shutter release to frame larger or more distant shots.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It appears that selfies — those self-portraits of you and your arm — are here to stay, even gaining mention in the Oxford Dictionaries.', '