ny and will show “the real Martin, a man hounded and set upon by all comers in the 12 months before he died.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The television and radio host Tavis Smiley will write a book about the Rev. Dr. Martin Luther King Jr., Mr. Smiley’s publisher said, exploring the attacks on Dr. King’s “character, ideology, and political tactics and how they shaped both the year leading up to his death in 1968 and his lasting legacy.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tavis Smiley to Write Book on Martin Luther King Jr.’s Final Days', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Martin Luther Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ritz, David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smiley, Tavis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hachette Book Group', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'LITTLE BROWN & CO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T20:33:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d2fd192-e513-592a-9ee4-1c7d22c13153', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d2fd192-e513-592a-9ee4-1c7d22c13153'}, {'abstract': 'Sophie de Oliveira Barata makes bedazzled legs and reptilian arms — not your everyday prosthetic limbs. Here are some interesting tidbits about her work.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/the-art-of-the-prothesis/', 'snippet': 'Sophie de Oliveira Barata makes bedazzled legs and reptilian arms — not your everyday prosthetic limbs. Here are some interesting tidbits about her work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The people who ask Sophie de Oliveira Barata to make their prosthetic limbs — Nadav Kander photographed several of them for this past weekend’s health issue — want hands and legs that are not only functional but also personally expressive in some way. She produces her bespoke creations, like the snake-arm seen above, out of her London-based Alternative Limb Project. The pictures made us curious to know more about de Oliveira Barata’s enterprise, so she sent us some interesting facts about her work making prostheses:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 819, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1638, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/04/magazine/04-snake-arm/04-snake-arm-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art of the Prosthesis', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T20:37:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Staff', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Staff'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34eadfc9-e125-5cea-a120-c0a127296b34', 'word_count': 200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34eadfc9-e125-5cea-a120-c0a127296b34'}, {'abstract': 'Endo’s deal for Paladin Labs of Canada will involve creating a new holding company based in Ireland to house both firms. The move should significantly reduce Endo’s tax rate.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/the-tax-motive-in-endo-healths-deal/', 'snippet': 'Endo’s deal for Paladin Labs of Canada will involve creating a new holding company based in Ireland to house both firms. The move should significantly reduce Endo’s tax rate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Greed is seeping into the art of mergers and acquisitions. Endo Health Solutions is the latest buyer to receive a warm welcome for a sensible acquisition with notable savings. Its market value jumped almost as much as the $1.6 billion price of its purchase, Paladin Labs. But the deal also involves a huge tax dodge, and investors aren’t factoring in enough risk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Tax Motive in Endo Health’s Deal', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Elan Corporation PLC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations',