yt://article/c6643790-3cbc-5b83-8818-aacf87e10899'}, {'abstract': 'The media company’s revenues surpassed Wall Street expectations, but profits were down in part because of the cost of starting two new channels.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/business/media/tv-investments-drag-on-21st-century-fox-profits.html', 'snippet': 'The media company’s revenues surpassed Wall Street expectations, but profits were down in part because of the cost of starting two new channels.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Investments in new cable channels were a drag on 21st Century Fox’s third-quarter profits, but total revenues still surpassed analysts’ expectations. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Profits at 21st Century Fox Hampered by TV Investments ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Profits at 21st Century Fox Hampered by TV Investments', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '21st Century Fox', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'News Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:34:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c1c02d2-b524-5d5c-a565-093f4e405568', 'word_count': 482, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c1c02d2-b524-5d5c-a565-093f4e405568'}, {'abstract': 'Ib Andersen’s presentation of “Cinderella” for Ballet Arizona proves touching, funny and musical.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/arts/dance/cinderella-tries-the-fit-with-ballet-arizona.html', 'snippet': 'Ib Andersen’s presentation of “Cinderella” for Ballet Arizona proves touching, funny and musical.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Few careers in ballet have shown a more remarkable trajectory than that of Ib Andersen. I remember him in 1979 in Copenhagen as a young star of the Royal Danish Ballet (he had been the youngest principal in its history), shining in several of the mid-19th-century classics by the Danish master August Bournonville. A year later Mr. Andersen was a principal of New York City Ballet, where he created roles in new ballets by George Balanchine and Jerome Robbins. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 694, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1388, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06BALLETAZ/06BALLETAZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Putting Up With Evil, Then Getting a Princely Hand', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Putting Up With Evil, Then Getting a Princely Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cinderella (Ballet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet Arizona', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Andersen, Ib', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:36:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd4f648d-6141-59a9-a035-823f3bb96d4b', 'word_count': 1087, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd4f648d-6141-59a9-a035-823f3bb96d4b'}, {'abstract': '“The Stone Roses: Made of Stone” looks at a British band with a future that went unfulfilled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/movies/the-brief-season-of-the-stone-roses.html', 'snippet': '“The Stone Roses: Made of Stone” looks at a British band with a future that went unfulfilled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most of the guys are in their 50s now, and 50 isn’t old for rock stars anymore. But most rock stars have not messed things up as thoroughly as the Stone Roses did roughly 20 years ago. One minute their debut album was being acclaimed as among the greatest ever; the next they were embroiled in a legal battle that delayed their follow-up album for five years. It flopped, and the group broke up.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/stonespan/stonespan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Blooming, Languishing, Reviving', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Stone Roses: Made of Stone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stone Roses (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Ian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meadows, Shane', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:37:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/aa56868c-4afb-54f4-af7a-3d6e9981ec51', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aa56868c-4afb-54f4-af7a-3d6e9981ec51'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Smith will retire from the New York Philharmonic at the end of this season after 36 years with the orchestra.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/philip-smith-philharmonics-principal-trumpet-to-retire/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Smith will retire from the New York Philharmonic at the end of this season after 36 years with the orchestra.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Philip Smith, the New York Philharmonic’s principal trumpet, announced on Tuesday that he would retire from the orchestra at the end of the 2013-14 season. He will have been a member of the orchestra for 36 years: he joined as co-principal trumpet in 1978, when Zubin Mehta, then the orchestra’s music director, hired him away from the Chicago Symphony Orchestra. He became the orchestra’s principal trumpet in 1988.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 567, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 567}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 968, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 1481, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/arts/05artsbeat-smith/05artsbeat-smith-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Philip Smith, Philharmonic’s Principal Trumpet, to Retire', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'SMITH, PHILIP', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Philharmonic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:38:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'perso