 district, is an anomaly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/alabama-small-race-reflects-g-o-p-divide/', 'snippet': 'Tuesday’s runoff election, to decide the Republican Party’s nominee for a seat in the House of Representatives from the first congressional district, is an anomaly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The city of Atmore in southwestern Alabama typically takes a turn in the national spotlight when an inmate is executed at the state prison there.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama: Small Race Reflects G.O.P. Divide', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Roy S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Young, Dean', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:42:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b7f1f8e-ad63-5846-be2e-a0c9f4b15f87', 'word_count': 421, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b7f1f8e-ad63-5846-be2e-a0c9f4b15f87'}, {'abstract': 'New Jersey voters remain pessimistic about the state’s economic situation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/new-jersey-exit-poll-economy-weighs-heavily-on-voters/', 'snippet': 'New Jersey voters remain pessimistic about the state’s economic situation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'According to early results from exit polls conducted by Edison Research, the issue that mattered most to voters in the New Jersey race for governor was the economy, with half of all voters selecting it as the key issue for them. The economy was followed by taxes, which was selected by one out of every four voters.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.J. Exit Poll: Economy Weighs Heavily on Voters', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David R. Jones', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Jones', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/857c203e-eb83-5ee6-8b48-715c9f7bcb56', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/857c203e-eb83-5ee6-8b48-715c9f7bcb56'}, {'abstract': 'In “A Case of You,” a struggling writer remakes himself into the perfect match for the woman he has his eye on.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/movies/a-case-of-you-with-the-smitten-justin-long.html', 'snippet': 'In “A Case of You,” a struggling writer remakes himself into the perfect match for the woman he has his eye on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Kat Coiro’s new film, “A Case of You,” the mildly neurotic Sam (Justin Long) is a struggling writer in Brooklyn making a living from movie novelizations, but he has a Serious Book inside him. Shamed for his bachelor status by his happily married and pregnant former classmate (Sienna Miller), Sam woos the mildly daffy coffeehouse clerk Birdie (Evan Rachel Wood, in a departure from her darker portraits), who is also a caricature artist in Prospect Park. To impress her, he studies her Facebook page and awkwardly pretends to share her interests, including cooking, Joan Baez, the guitar, Carlos Castaneda and ballroom dancing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/filmroundup/filmroundup-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Romantic Comedy: Imbibe in Moderation', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Case of You', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coiro, Kat', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Long, Justin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Sienna', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wood, Evan Rachel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Case of You (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:48:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/bad35717-a435-5886-ae67-a32cb8396981', 'word_count': 256, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bad35717-a435-5886-ae67-a32cb8396981'}, {'abstract': 'In the tight Virginia governor’s race, exit polls found voters giving the candidates equal marks on ethics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/election-2013/2013/11/05/virginia-exit-poll-mixed-on-candidates-sour-on-economy/', 'snippet': 'In the tight Virginia governor’s race, exit polls found voters giving the candidates equal marks on ethics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the tight Virginia governor’s race, exit polls found voters giving the candidates equal marks on ethics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Va. Exit Poll: Mixed on Candidates, Sour on Economy', 'kicker': 'Election Day Coverage and Results', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T22:55:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Monika L. McDermott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Monika', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'McDermott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/72adbe48-873a-5d1a-aa65-94dbdad4414f', 'word_count': 302, 'uri': 'nyt://article/72adbe48-873a-5d1a-aa65-94dbdad4414f'}, {'abstract': 'The London-based label brings its whimsical designs — including shiny red platforms, frilly dresses and mohair sweaters — to the retail chain.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/perfect-pairing-meadham-kirchhoffs-rule-breaking-topshop-collection/', 'snippet': 'The London-based label brings its whimsical designs — including shiny red platforms, frilly dresses and mohair sweaters — to the retail chain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fresh off a triumphant ready-to-wear presentation this spring — a typically demented, dazzling mash-up of Charles Addams and Leigh Bowery — the London-based fashion label Meadham Kirchhoff has put together a witty new collection for Topshop, which includes everything from a pair of glittery ruby platforms with marshmallow heels to frilly baby-doll dresses and mohair jumpers. It’s another spirited line from a design team that is determined to break the rules. “The industry has become dictatorial,” Edward Meadham says. “All we ask is that we can show our clothes exactly how we want to, exactly how it comes out of us. What people make of it after that is up to them.” Available Nov. 21. ', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Meadham Kirchhoff’s Rule-Breaking Topshop Collection', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Meadham Kirchhoff Does Topshop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Topshop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-05T23:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron Gell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15b71b73-22c5-5152-97a3-7f641604ba58', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15b71b73-22c5-5152-97a3-7f641604ba58'}, {'abstract': 'Eminem’s technique remains finely tuned, but on his latest release, “The Marshall Mathers LP 2,” his worldview remains focused on the same territory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/arts/music/eminem-grows-older-but-not-up.html', 'snippet': 'Eminem’s technique remains finely tuned, but on his latest release, “The Marshall Mathers LP 2,” his worldview remains focused on the same territory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We have watched Eminem age, all of us, difficult as it has been. We’ve seen him lash out at his mother, his then-wife, and his fans. We’ve seen him soften ever so slightly under the weight of fatherhood. We’ve seen him court protest, then express befuddlement over the hubbub. We’ve seen him retreat into drugs, and then climb out of the morass.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06EMINEM/06EMINEM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06EMINEM/06EMINEM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/arts/06EMINEM/06EMINEM-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '