 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stern, Robert A M', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T01:11:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivian Marino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interview', '_id': 'nyt://article/5cf23c73-590c-5d0c-9286-87fc6e4289f3', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5cf23c73-590c-5d0c-9286-87fc6e4289f3'}, {'abstract': 'Usually depicted as a champion of the rich, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg also started a bold antipoverty program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/opinion/bloomberg-champion-of-the-poor.html', 'snippet': 'Usually depicted as a champion of the rich, Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg also started a bold antipoverty program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DURING New York City’s mayoral race, criticism of Mayor Michael R. Bloomberg for neglecting the poor ignored his bold and unprecedented antipoverty measures. He may not have eliminated inequality or reversed the impact of the Great Recession — over the last two years, the poverty rate has crept up to 21.2 percent from 20.1 percent — but failure to acknowledge what he did in fact accomplish is not only unfair but also shortsighted. Usually depicted as a champion of the rich, Mr. Bloomberg mounted an antipoverty program at a moment when poverty as an issue was off the national radar and even politically toxic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 449, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 449}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1533, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/opinion/1106OPEDbarrett/1106OPEDbarrett-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bloomberg, Champion of the Poor', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bloomberg, Champion of the Poor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Katz, Michael B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bloomberg, Michael R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T01:11:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael B. Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d5646bb-ef03-59be-b363-f4d159b4a840', 'word_count': 747, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d5646bb-ef03-59be-b363-f4d159b4a840'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to its crack-smoking mayor, a city becomes a spectacle.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/opinion/torontos-hot-mess.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to its crack-smoking mayor, a city becomes a spectacle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — JUST the other day, a definitive Toronto image was making the rounds on Twitter. One of the turnstiles in the subway system had broken and no guards were around, so passengers had left their tickets and change in a small pile on the side. I live in an absurdly law-abiding, rule-following city. There’s one major exception: the mayor. He smokes crack. He said so on Tuesday. Twice.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Toronto’s Hot Mess', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Toronto’s Hot Mess', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Robert B', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marche, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocaine and Crack Cocaine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T01:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd