': ' In a meeting at the White House, President Obama urged a group of business leaders to press the House of Representatives to pass broad immigration legislation. The leaders included Joe Echevarria, chief executive of Deloitte LLP; Marillyn A. Hewson, chief executive of Lockheed Martin; Stephen A. Schwarzman, chairman of Blackstone, and several others who had not previously played such prominent roles in supporting an immigration overhaul. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama Presses Case for Immigration Changes', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Washington', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama Presses Case For Immigration Changes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preston, Julia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T01:33:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/68ef4171-434a-5683-b687-c876998a77cc', 'word_count': 66, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68ef4171-434a-5683-b687-c876998a77cc'}, {'abstract': 'Shareholders rejected the Oracle chief’s $78 million pay package in a nonbinding vote. But there are better ways to shrink C.E.O. pay.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/05/a-vote-goes-against-outsize-executive-pay-but-its-hardly-a-blow/', 'snippet': 'Shareholders rejected the Oracle chief’s $78 million pay package in a nonbinding vote. But there are better ways to shrink C.E.O. pay.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you’re against high executive pay, don’t cheer because Oracle’s shareholders overwhelmingly rejected Lawrence J. Ellison’s $78.4 million pay package.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1109, 'width': 1109, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/business/dbpix-dealprof/dbpix-dealprof-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Vote Goes 