ed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The only thing clear about the momentous budget conference now under way on Capitol Hill is what will not come out of it: an agreement to set the economy on a promising course with new investments that will create jobs and improve education. Republicans, locked into the iron suit of austerity, refuse to consider any spending that might stimulate economic growth.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Chance for a Budget Compromise', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Chance for a Budget Compromise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, Paul D Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House Committee on the Budget', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T02:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/97ddd7ce-1600-552c-8000-f3b9b84b2c8a', 'word_count': 516, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97ddd7ce-1600-552c-8000-f3b9b84b2c8a'}, {'abstract': 'Bill de Blasio won the mayoral election knowing where to turn for advice: counselors and supporters long embedded in New York City government and politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/nyregion/expert-hands-are-ready-to-help-inexperienced-de-blasio.html', 'snippet': 'Bill de Blasio won the mayoral election knowing where to turn for advice: counselors and supporters long embedded in