ate': '2013-11-06T05:59:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gerry Doyle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Doyle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bbf5355-fec4-57a6-b84e-15d6d3696019', 'word_count': 268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bbf5355-fec4-57a6-b84e-15d6d3696019'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (ABC) THE 47TH ANNUAL CMA AWARDS Carrie Underwood and Brad Paisley (below) return as hosts of this ceremony, billed as “country music’s biggest night” and broadcast live from the Bridgestone Arena in Nashville. Kenny Rogers, a five-time Country Music Association Award winner and recent Country Music Hall of Fame inductee, will be honored with the Willie Nelson Lifetime Achievement Award and a tribute by Jennifer Nettles, Rascal Flatts and Darius Rucker. Taylor Swift will receive the Pinnacle Award, which recognizes an artist who has made a positive impact on the appreciation of country music. Ms. Swift will take the stage with Vince Gill and Alison Krauss, the Zac Brown Band will perform with Dave Grohl of the Foo Fighters, and Hunter Hayes will team up with Jason Mraz. And Jason Aldean, Luke Bryan, Blake Shelton, Ms. Swift and George Strait will compete for the evening’s top honor, entertainer of the year. “CMA Awards Red Carpet Live,” at 7 on Great American Country, features interviews with artists and nominees as they arrive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': Non