By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9ce3a0a3-dfae-5ffa-a1e9-ebe985a39f89', 'word_count': 188, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9ce3a0a3-dfae-5ffa-a1e9-ebe985a39f89'}, {'abstract': 'Istanbul’s grand new metro system is a ticket into the unknown.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/a-train-too-far/', 'snippet': 'Istanbul’s grand new metro system is a ticket into the unknown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — Last Tuesday the city celebrated the 90th anniversary of Turkey’s founding with unusual pomp. Senior politicians cut the ribbon on a spectacular new metro system that runs some 200 feet below the Sea of Marmara and can carry 1.5 million people every day between the European and Asian sides of the city.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Train Too Far', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bridges and Tunnels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transit Systems', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bosporus (Turkey)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sea of Marmara', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T12:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba32b1c3-ac68-55a5-8294-91ca7afbc107', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba32b1c3-ac68-55a5-8294-91ca7afbc107'}, {'abstract': 'The computer networking giant announced its long-awaited plan to combat upstarts, with an “application-centric infrastructure” that it says can be up to 93 percent cheaper than competitors.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/cisco-counters-its-young-competitors-in-data-networking/', 'snippet': 'The computer networking giant announced its long-awaited plan to combat upstarts, with an “application-centric infrastructure” that it says can be up to 93 percent cheaper than competitors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cisco Systems has announced its big play for the future of data networking, a multibillion-dollar business that holds the Internet together. It’s comprehensive, probably compelling for people who already own lots of Cisco equipment (which is most large companies that operate networks), and for Cisco at least, expensive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/technology/06bits-cisco/06bits-cisco-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 412, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/06/technology/06bits-cisco/06bits-cisco-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 412}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/technology/06bits-cisco/06bits-cisco-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/technology/06bits-cisco/06bits-cisco-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1031, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/technology/06bi