lion since 2007, has frustrated unions, customers and lawmakers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In early 2009, John E. Potter, then the postmaster general, delivered a dire warning to Congress: The United States Postal Service would run out of money unless lawmakers stepped in and passed legislation to help the agency stabilize its finances.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 767, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 767}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1265, 'width': 990, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/politics/POSTAL/POSTAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amid Capitol Turmoil, Postal Crisis Drags On', 'kicker': None, 'c