}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5b2cb64-8efc-5048-90ae-b6674551039b', 'word_count': 1547, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5b2cb64-8efc-5048-90ae-b6674551039b'}, {'abstract': 'The author of new research on the effect of harsh verbal discipline on adolescents says that even the occasional lapse is “bad.”', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/06/dont-yell-at-your-children-but-if-you-do-dont-yell-at-yourself/', 'snippet': 'The author of new research on the effect of harsh verbal discipline on adolescents says that even the occasional lapse is “bad.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Personally, I wouldn’t yell at my children if they would just do what I’ve asked the first time, or maybe do the thing I’ve asked them to do 463 times in the past. Or if they didn’t chase one another through the kitchen at dinnertime, brandishing light sabers. Or if they got up when the alarm clock went off in the morning, or put their shoes on so we could leave the house, or moved that glass of milk, the one that’s right by your elbow and … too late.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Yell at Your Children. But If You Do, Don’t Yell at Yourself.', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANGER (EMOTION)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T18:43:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Kj Dell'Antonia", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kj', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "Dell'Antonia", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id