u want a European radiator.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/garden/going-beyond-the-baseboard.html', 'snippet': 'What to keep in mind if you want a European radiator.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you find yourself warming to a European-produced designer radiator, you’ll be happy to know that some models are distributed in the United States. Contact the company for the names of retailers. Or you can buy directly from overseas.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Going Beyond the Baseboard', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Beyond The Baseboard', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Radiators', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T23:09:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf6f1427-9d92-572e-ad37-bfde3a837e2c', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf6f1427-9d92-572e-ad37-bfde3a837e2c'}, {'abstract': 'Cristina Grajales Gallery presents its second solo show of Hechizoo, an innovative weaving studio in Bogotá, Colombia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/garden/textiles-with-roots-in-the-rain-forest.html', 'snippet': 'Cristina Grajales Gallery presents its second solo show of Hechizoo, an innovative weaving studio in Bogotá, Colombia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2010, Cristina Grajales Gallery in New York presented a solo exhibition of the work of Hechizoo, a textile studio founded in 2000 in Bogotá by Jorge Lizarazo, an architect-turned-weaver. Hechizoo combines native plant fibers like fique and cumare palm with nylon filament and metals to create iridescent carpets and screens.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 725, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07SHOWS1_SPAN/07CURR6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Textiles with Roots in the Rain Forest', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Textiles With Roots in the Rain Forest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Textiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T23:09:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Lasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f33c5b56-f144-515f-8816-36eb854af367', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f33c5b56-f144-515f-8816-36eb854af367'}, {'abstract': 'Brightly colored wood-patterned carpets from the appropriately named Richard Woods.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/garden/a-double-take-under-your-feet.html', 'snippet': 'Brightly colored wood-patterned carpets from the appropriately named Richard Woods.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British artist Richard Woods creates stylized renderings of construction materials (such as brick and wood) and applies them to household décor. His colorful, comic book-like graphics have appeared on chairs, tables and wallpaper, as well as on the sides of buildings. The floor has certainly not escaped his attention. His latest project, a collection of 11 parquet- and floorboard-patterned wool rugs for Memphis-Milano, are produced in Nepal, where they are woven on traditional looms. “I like the idea of making a rug out of something that’s usually underneath the rug,” Mr. Woods said, adding that he isn’t conscious of any influence his surname may have had on his work. The rugs are produced in a signed limited edition of 36 and range in size from about 3 by 5 feet ($2,466) to about 8 by 11 feet ($14,466). Shown is RW Rug #5 ($6,692). Information: 011-39-02-655-4731 or store.memphis-milano.com. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07CURR8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 825, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07CURR8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 825}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07CURR8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 746, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07CURR8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07RUGS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07RUGS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07RUGS/07RUGS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Double Take Under Your Feet', 'kicker': 'Currents | Rugs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Double Take Under Your Feet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Arlene', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpets and Rugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woods, Richard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-06T23:10:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f7325f4-c862-51ec-85f6-eb1059b76d6a', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f7325f4-c862-51ec-85f6-eb1059b76d6a'}, {'abstract': 'A 9-year-old invents a table decoration to mark both Thanksgiving and Hanukkah.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/garden/dressing-the-turkey-dress-the-menorah-too.html', 'snippet': 'A 9-year-old invents a table decoration to mark both Thanksgiving and Hanukkah.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When precocious children come up with ideas for salable inventions on long car rides, preoccupied parents typically just keep driving. But about 10 months ago, when Asher Weintraub, 9, suggested combining Thanksgiving table decorations and Hanukkah menorahs this year, since the holidays are making a rare simultaneous appearance, his parents, Anthony Weintraub and Caroline Baron, actually listened. The Manhattan family commissioned a prototype for Asher’s computer sketch of a menurkey, a menorah shaped like a turkey holding candles in its plumes. A Kickstarter campaign, also Asher’s idea, brought in $48,345 and Internet fame, and now plaster menurkeys are being sold for $50 at the Jewish Museum in New York. “When I saw it made,” Asher said, “it looked way better than I expected.” As for his next invention, he added, “Maybe an app.” Information: 212-423-3333 or shop.thejewishmuseum.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/garden/07GOODS/07CURR4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 917, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'