rebel-group.html', 'snippet': 'After routing the Congolese M23 rebels, United Nations peacekeepers are expected to turn their attention to subduing a Hutu militia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — Having helped rout one powerful rebel group in the eastern part of the Democratic Republic of Congo, United Nations peacekeepers are expected to turn their attention to subduing another, diplomats said Wednesday, as the Security Council prepared to draft a statement on the next steps in that vast, mineral-rich country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peacekeepers in Congo to Focus on Another Rebel Group', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peacekeepers in Congo to Focus on Another Rebel Group', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Department of Peacekeeping Operations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Congo, Democratic Republic of (Congo-Kinshasa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rwanda', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'March 23 Movement', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Forces for the Liberation of Rwanda', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T00:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/526c65e6-36c0-5cd8-af85-b147bd10c97d', 'word_count': 474, 'uri': 'nyt://article/526c65e6-36c0-5cd8-af85-b147bd10c97d'}, {'abstract': 'The History Channel may remake the ABC mini-series that made history when it was broadcast in 1977.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/business/media/history-channel-is-eying-remake-of-roots.html', 'snippet': 'The History Channel may remake the ABC mini-series that made history when it was broadcast in 1977.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The History Channel may remake “Roots,” the ABC mini-series that made history when it was broadcast in 1977. The cable channel confirmed that it had bought the rights to the mini-series (and the Alex Haley book that it was based upon) and had started developing an eight-hour version of it. The original “Roots,” about a multigenerational African-American family’s experiences from the time of slavery onward, was 12 hours and a national phenomenon, as evidenced by the fact that more than half of all American households tuned in for the finale. The development was first reported by Deadline.com on Tuesday, which quoted a senior vice president at the channel, Dirk Hoogstra, as saying “We would like to revive that cultural icon for a new audience.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'History Channel Is Eying Remake of ‘Roots’', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'History Channel Is Eying Remake of ‘Roots’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'History Channel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T00:43:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter',