od Watches', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Second Thoughts on Neighborhood Watches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sanford (Fla)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Trayvon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zimmerman, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T02:26:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9dd20f2-ff76-5872-a77e-6e8a2881de66', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9dd20f2-ff76-5872-a77e-6e8a2881de66'}, {'abstract': 'The National Football League must be unflinching in its investigation into accusations of bullying and abuse in the Miami Dolphins’ locker room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/opinion/subject-to-further-review.html', 'snippet': 'The National Football League must be unflinching in its investigation into accusations of bullying and abuse in the Miami Dolphins’ locker room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The National Football League once again finds itself searching beyond the X’s and O’s of the playing field to protect the game’s image as a rough-and-tumble entertainment rooted in innocent sport. The league has opened an investigation into accusations of locker room hazing on the Miami Dolphins that reportedly descended to racist and homophobic slurs and macho threats against a player and his mother. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Subject to Further Review', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Subject to Further