Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Protest Over Kelly Is Focus of Inquiry, Brown University Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protest Over Kelly Is Focus of Inquiry, Brown U. Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fitzsimmons, Emma G', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brown University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Raymond W', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Providence (RI)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T02:36:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma G. Fitzsimmons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'Fitzsimmons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bb69a07-a089-5688-b4de-00682fabf280', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bb69a07-a089-5688-b4de-00682fabf280'}, {'abstract': 'The Mexico Supreme Court on Wednesday overturned a lower court ruling that allowed a drug kingpin accused of murdering an American drug enforcement agent in the 1980s to walk free.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/world/americas/mexico-court-orders-full-sentence-in-drug-agents-death-but-killer-is-free.html', 'snippet': 'The Mexico Supreme Court on Wednesday overturned a lower court ruling that allowed a drug kingpin accused of murdering an American drug enforcement agent in the 1980s to walk free.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Mexico Supreme Court on Wednesday overturned a lower court ruling that allowed a drug kingpin accused of murdering an American drug enforcement agent in the 1980s to walk free. The effect of the high court ruling is unclear; the drug lord, Rafael Caro Quintero, left prison Aug. 9 and may not be easy to find. The American government, which filed an extradition request for him after his release, this week offered a $5 million reward for information leading to his capture. According to the high court ruling, lower court judges made a mistake when they decided there had been a jurisdiction problem in trying Mr. Caro Quintero in federal court and ordered his release. The new ruling allows the Mexican authorities to order him back to prison to complete the remaining 12 years of his 40-year sentence for the killing of the agent, Enrique Camarena, although Mexico could choose to extradite Mr. Caro Quintero if he is found. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico: Court Orders Full Sentence in Drug Agent’s Death, but Killer Is Free', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico: Court Orders Full Sentence In Drug Agent’s Death, but Killer Is Free', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Archibold, Randal C', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Caro Quintero, Rafael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Camarena, Enrique', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T02:36:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randal C. Archibold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randal', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Archibold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f31f527e-e488-59c1-b6ed-9b9666248663', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f31f527e-e488-59c1-b6ed-9b9666248663'}, {'abstract': 'Russia, which has charged Greenpeace crew members with hooliganism, refused to recognize the jurisdiction of an international tribunal in what it considers an internal legal matter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/world/europe/the-netherlands-appeals-detentions-of-greenpeace-activists-in-russia.html', 'snippet': 'Russia, which has charged Greenpeace crew members with hooliganism, refused to recognize the jurisdiction of an international tribunal in what it considers an internal legal matter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Netherlands appealed to an international tribunal to order Russia to release a ship and 30 crew members of Greenpeace International who were detained in September while protesting offshore oil exploration in the Arctic. Russia, which has since charged the crew members with hooliganism, refused to recognize the court’s jurisdiction in what it considers an internal legal matter. The tribunal of the Law of the Sea Treaty, based in Hamburg, scheduled a ruling for Nov. 22, which could increase diplomatic pressure on Russia’s government to resolve the case. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Netherlands Appeals Detentions of Greenpeace Activists in Russia', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Netherlands Appeals Detentions Of Greenpeace Activists in Russia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Netherlands', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law of the Sea (UN Convention)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T02:41:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/87ed62a5-a91d-5eee-acb6-a59562315dd3', 'word_count': 88, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87ed62a5-a91d-5eee-acb6-a59562315dd3'}, {'abstract': "What factors should determine eligibility for financial aid from the government and from colleges? Should parents' income be considered?", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/roomfordebate/2013/11/06/who-should-get-financial-aid/', 'snippet': "What factors should determine eligibility for financial aid from the government and from colleges? Should parents' income be considered?", 'lead_paragraph': '', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Should Get Financial Aid?', 'kicker': 'Room for Debate', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T02:43:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4883ae23-7b39-53f0-a7c0-45ea6f045e74', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4883ae23-7b39-53f0-a7c0-45ea6f045e74'}, {'abstract': 'Republicans who viewed Terry McAuliffe as a beatable candidate engaged in recriminations about how the party had gone wrong by nominating an outspoken social conservative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/us/politics/virginia-gop-asks-why-it-lost-to-rival-deemed-weak.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans who viewed Terry McAuliffe as a beatable candidate engaged in recriminations about how the party had gone wrong by nominating an outspoken social conservative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Republicans in Virginia awoke Wednesday with the knowledge that a bad streak had been extended: With the election of a Democratic governor, Terry McAuliffe, Republicans have lost seven of the past eight statewide, top-of-the-ballot races, including those for governor, senator and president — a run of misery dating to 2005. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/ALT-VIRGINIA-2/ALT-VIRGINIA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/us/ALT-VIRGINIA-2/ALT-VIRGINIA-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/ALT-VIRGINIA-2/ALT-VIRGINIA-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 692, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/us/ALT-VIRGINIA-2/ALT-VIRGINIA-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1