cers, and Commonfund. After years of increasing, alternative investments fell from 54 percent of assets to 47 percent. Endowment returns were sharply negative during the recession, then very strong for two years, and near zero in 2011-12. \xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Growing Endowments Change Colleges’ Investment Strategy', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Growing Endowments Change Investment Strategy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endowments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of College and University Business Officers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venture Capital', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T03:08:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1adb2eb3-d290-5511-ac9f-34a0a420fd99', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1adb2eb3-d290-5511-ac9f-34a0a420fd99'}, {'abstract': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/nyregion/winning-lottery-numbers-for-nov-6-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Lottery numbers for New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nov. 6, 2013', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winning Powerball and Lottery Numbers for Nov. 