a3f4-5129e463089f'}, {'abstract': 'Mannequins with bulging bosoms have become standard in Venezuela, reflecting the country’s embrace of plastic surgery even among those who can least afford it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/world/americas/mannequins-give-shape-to-venezuelan-fantasy.html', 'snippet': 'Mannequins with bulging bosoms have become standard in Venezuela, reflecting the country’s embrace of plastic surgery even among those who can least afford it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'VALENCIA, Venezuela — Frustrated with the modest sales at his small mannequin factory, Eliezer Álvarez made a simple observation: Venezuelan women were increasingly using plastic surgery to transform their bodies, yet the mannequins in clothing stores did not reflect these new, often extreme proportions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1258, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/world/americas/Venezuela/Venezuela-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mannequins Give Shape to a Venezuelan Fantasy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mannequins Give Shape to Venezuelan Fantasy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mannequins (Dummies)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beauty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastic Surgery', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T03:14:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eec49c01-a643-5ab2-b1fc-5c3be8157b63', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eec49c01-a643-5ab2-b1fc-5c3be8157b63'}, {'abstract': 'The judge, Col. James Pohl, has ordered the government to show him confidential correspondence about prison conditions at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, a defense lawyer said Wednesday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/us/judge-in-terrorism-case-orders-look-at-secret-records.html', 'snippet': 'The judge, Col. James Pohl, has ordered the government to show him confidential correspondence about prison conditions at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, a defense lawyer said Wednesday.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A judge presiding over the military commission’s prosecution of five people accused in the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks has ordered the government to show him confidential correspondence with the International Committee of the Red Cross about prison conditions at Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, a defense lawyer said Wednesday. The judge, Col. James Pohl, also issued an order taking control of the team that reviews correspondence between defense lawyers and the defendants, including Khalid Shaikh Mohammed. The order also relaxes some limits on what defense lawyers can discuss with their clients, said James G. Connell III, a defense lawyer for Ali Abd al Aziz Ali. The case has been bogged down in pretrial hearings, with no actual trial in sight. The judge decided that he would review the Red Cross records before deciding whether to allow the lawyers to see them. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge in Terrorism Case Orders Look at Secret Records', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Military', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge In Terrorism Case Orders Look at Secret Records', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pohl, James L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guantanamo Bay Naval Base (Cuba)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'September 11 (2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Committee of the Red Cross', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ali, Ali Abdul Aziz', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Military Tribunals', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connell, James G III', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Red Cross', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T03:18:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfafaaac-4310-58fa-a9de-74db38965e4d', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfafaaac-4310-58fa-a9de-74db38965e4d'}, {'abstract': 'Navy Cmdr. Jose Luis Sanchez, 41, was arrested in Tampa and was also charged with accepting $100,000 from an Asian ship-servicing company that overbilled the Navy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/us/a-third-navy-official-is-arrested-in-bribery-case.html', 'snippet': 'Navy Cmdr. Jose Luis Sanchez, 41, was arrested in Tampa and was also charged with accepting $100,000 from an Asian ship-servicing company that overbilled the Navy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Federal prosecutors said Wednesday that a third Navy official had been arrested on charges of accepting prostitutes and luxury travel from an Asian ship-servicing company that overbilled the Navy by millions of dollars. Navy Cmdr. Jose Luis Sanchez, 41, was arrested in Tampa and was also charged with accepting $100,000 from Glenn Defense Marine Asia, whose chief executive, Leonard Glenn Francis, was arrested in September. Federal authorities in San Diego have also charged a Navy commander, Michael V.K. Misiewicz, 46, and John B. Beliveau II, a naval investigator, in the case. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Third Navy Official Is Arrested in Bribery Case', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Military', 'cont