orted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4eb16933-dbce-5768-b267-1c8bb7ba6259', 'word_count': 827, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4eb16933-dbce-5768-b267-1c8bb7ba6259'}, {'abstract': 'A 37-year-old man was charged with eight counts, including terrorism, in attacks sabotaging a power grid in Central Arkansas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/us/arkansas-man-charged-in-power-grid-attacks.html', 'snippet': 'A 37-year-old man was charged with eight counts, including terrorism, in attacks sabotaging a power grid in Central Arkansas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A 37-year-old man was indicted Wednesday in connection with a series of attacks on the power grid in Central Arkansas earlier this year. A federal grand jury charged Jason Woodring with eight counts, including a terrorist attack against a railroad carrier. Mr. Woodring was arrested last month after the authorities said he repeatedly sabotaged electrical equipment and caused at least $2.1 million in damage. In one instance, Mr. Woodring is alleged to have sought to use a moving train to down a support tower. No one was injured in the attacks, which began in August and led to brief power failures.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Arkansas: Man Charged in Power Grid Attacks', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Failures and Blackouts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodring, Jason', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARKANSAS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T03:41:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f39d26cd-a230-5b3a-a7e8-a6ec9a72894f', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f39d26cd-a230-5b3a-a7e8-a6ec9a72894f'}, {'abstract': 'With roughly 990,000 votes counted, Washington residents appeared to reject mandatory labeling of genetically engineered products.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/us/politics/food-companies-claim-victory-against-labeling-initiative-in-washington-state.html', 'snippet': 'With roughly 990,000 votes counted, Washington residents appeared to reject mandatory labeling of genetically engineered products.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some of the nation’s major food companies declared victory on Wednesday over an initiative in Washington State that would have required labeling of some foods that contain biotech ingredients, although supporters of labeling held out hope that hundreds of thousands of uncounted votes might yet turn the tide.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Food Companies Claim Victory Against Labeling Initiative in Washington State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Food Companies Claim Victory Against Labeling Initiative in Washington State', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strom, Stephanie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grocery Manufacturers Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T03:45:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephanie Strom', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephanie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strom', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/aee6a48d-9e43-59b4-860d-9e1c2273cc16', 'word_count': 818, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aee6a48d-9e43-59b4-860d-9e1c2273cc16'}, {'abstract': 'Parker, a star running back in the N.F.L. who also passed, caught passes, punted and place-kicked, was the oldest living member of the Pro Football Hall of Fame.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/sports/football/ace-parker-pro-football-hall-of-famer-from-leather-helmet-days-dies-at-101.html', 'snippet': 'Parker, a star running back in the N.F.L. who also passed, caught passes, punted and place-kicked, was the oldest living member of the Pro Football Hall of Fame.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ace Parker, a star running back in the National Football League who could do just about everything on a football field in the days of leather helmets and 60-minute men, died on Wednesday in Portsmouth, Va. He was 101 and the oldest living member of the Pro Football Hall of Fame.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/sports/PARKER2-obit/PARKER2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/sports/PARKER2-obit/PARKER2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 753}}, {'rank': 0,