 'lead_paragraph': 'Jesse M. Furman of Federal District Court in Manhattan, found that the city, through “benign neglect,” was in violation of the of the Americans of Disabilities Act.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruling From the United States District Court for the Southern District of New York', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Decisions and Verdicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T18:10:34+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/2c00b446-f00f-58c3-8d9f-948644dfa356', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/2c00b446-f00f-58c3-8d9f-948644dfa356'}, {'abstract': 'A critical component to true health care reform is in changing our core expectations about the use of heroic measures at the end of life.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/what-our-patients-can-teach-us/', 'snippet': 'A critical component to true health care reform is in changing our core expectations about the use of heroic measures at the end of life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the man who was about to become my patient couldn’t tolerate the fatigue any longer, he asked his son, one of 10 children, to take him in their buggy from his woodworking shop to the local doctor who tended to this Amish community, located 90 miles south of Cleveland. Labs showed a white blood cell count that was 12 times normal and profound anemia, and he was driven by ambulance to our hospital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/06/science/06wellsekeres/06wellsekeres-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge'