e landed high-profile positions or new backers. But has it all been a bed of roses?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/09/08/fashion/11fashionmagazine-copy.html', 'snippet': 'Many have landed high-profile positions or new backers. But has it all been a bed of roses?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many have landed high-profile positions or new backers. But has it all been a bed of roses?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The CFDA/Vogue Fashion Fund: Where No Designer Is Left Behind', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Council of Fashion Designers of America', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T19:03:36+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Fashion & Style', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1c539eb2-21d2-5b0d-ace8-4f65a3070cd2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1c539eb2-21d2-5b0d-ace8-4f65a3070cd2'}, {'abstract': 'Economists found that the Card Act, passed in 2009, saved consumers billions of dollars by cutting through a tangle of credit card fees.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/business/economy/a-credit-card-rule-that-worked-for-consumers.html', 'snippet': 'Economists found that the Card Act, passed in 2009, saved consumers billions of dollars by cutting through a tangle of credit card fees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four years ago, Congress decided to force down the hidden fees that credit card companies collect from their customers. It passed a law called the 2009 Credit Card Accountability Responsibility and Disclosure Act — a name chosen so the law would be known as the Card Act.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The N