', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Capretta, James C', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T21:14:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/233bfc5d-5257-5958-8ce8-b55734970165', 'word_count': 1176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/233bfc5d-5257-5958-8ce8-b55734970165'}, {'abstract': 'Arlene and Ed Petty first tried a trial separation, but looking back they would have chosen a different path.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/booming/when-nest-emptied-discontent-entered.html', 'snippet': 'Arlene and Ed Petty first tried a trial separation, but looking back they would have chosen a different path.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When their last child left for college, Arlene Petty, now 64, felt resentment about her decades-long marriage to Ed Petty, also now 64. Facing an empty nest, she asked for a trial separation. In hindsight, both would have done things very differently.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/booming/10unhitched-booming-empty/10unhitched-booming-empty-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/booming/10unhitched-booming-empty/10unhitched-booming-empty-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 