 don’t let the prospect of a little extra work deter you from making the cocktail.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 440}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1501, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/07/magazine/7-cinnamon/7-cinnamon-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Simple Way to Perk Up an Old-Fashioned', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cinnamon (Spice)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T21:48:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b57d31b-1ee1-56d9-b5d9-d22bfaf02623', 'word_count': 158, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b57d31b-1ee1-56d9-b5d9-d22bfaf02623'}, {'abstract': 'Streamlined or with fruit? It has been more than a century, and people still can’t decide.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/magazine/the-great-old-fashioned-debate.html', 'snippet': 'Streamlined or with fruit? It has been more than a century, and people still can’t decide.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a terrific mini-monologue in the 1942 film “You Were Never Lovelier” in which Fred Astaire’s fast-talking would-be roué tells Rita Hayworth’s ingénue: “As they’d say in Brooklyn, I can’t bat in your league. I’m a plain, ordinary guy from Omaha, Nebraska. Just an old-fashioned, everyday Middle Westerner.. . . But you’re streamlined. You’re today. Sister, I was raised amongst the grasshoppers, I am strictly from corn.” And then the duo breaks into song and dance, which is where Jerome Kern and Johnny Mercer’s sublime ballad, “I’m Old Fashioned,” debuted.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/magazine/10drink/10drink-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Old-Fashioned Debate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I’m Old-Fashioned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schaap, Rosie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T21:49:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9031d7f-3b50-557a-b8e2-50a1e82f24e1', 'word_count': 508, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9031d7f-3b50-557a-b8e2-50a1e82f24e1'}, {'abstract': 'In this follow-up to “Game Change,” the political reporters Mark Halperin and John Heilemann offer a detailed account of the 2012 presidential campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/books/review/double-down-by-mark-halperin-and-john-heilemann.html', 'snippet': 'In this follow-up to “Game Change,” the political reporters Mark Halperin and John Heilemann offer a detailed account of the 2012 presidential campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Chasmal.” Is that a word? Here, I’ll use it in a sentence for you: “Santorum had been turfed out of office in 2006, losing his re-election bid by a chasmal 18-point margin.” According to Merriam Webster, it is indeed a word, meaning \xad“resembling a chasm.” In other words, Santorum got beaten badly. But why use other words, when “chasmal” is available?', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover/1110-bks-Kinsley-vover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':