ts/design/monet-seaside-gardens-blooming-side-by-side.html', 'snippet': '“Garden at Sainte-Adresse,” Monet’s 1867 painting of a sun-dappled seaside, has belonged to the Metropolitan Museum of Art since 1967. For the next six months, anyway, it has a new companion.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Garden at Sainte-Adresse,” Monet’s 1867 painting of a sun-dappled seaside that features the artist’s father, Adolphe, wearing a panama hat and watching boats, has belonged to the Metropolitan Museum of Art since 1967. For the next six months, anyway, it has a new companion. Lawrence J. Ellison, the chief executive and co-founder of the Oracle Corporation, has lent the museum Monet’s “Adolphe Monet Reading in a Garden,” painted the same year, in which the artist’s father — wearing the same clothes — is relaxing with a newspaper in the shade.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/arts/08VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/08/arts/08VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/arts/08VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/arts/08VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1229, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/arts/08VOGEL_SPAN/VOGEL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard',