, 'snippet': 'A writer goes from being lesbian and not wanting children, to dating men and trying to conceive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When my father died six months shy of his 83rd birthday and my 42nd, I was shocked to find that in the midst of grief, one clear desire emerged, uncontestable: I wanted a child. This was not a decision, or even really a thought; it was more like a reflex.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 371}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1265, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN/10MODERNLOVE_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'After a Parent’s Death, a Rush of Change', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grief Gives Way to an Urge, Albeit a Long Shot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'In Vitro Fertilization', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pregnancy and Childbirth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T22:47:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By E. J. Levy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'E.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Levy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/648cf5ba-772c-56e5-b6ad-c2f9d939af21', 'word_count': 1519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/648cf5ba-772c-56e5-b6ad-c2f9d939af21'}, {'abstract': 'The 25 million euro restoration of a classic Art Deco movie theater has shined a new light on the rough but storied neighborhood of Barbès.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/07/letter-from-france-in-paris-a-ragtag-resplendent-district-prepares-for-its-close-up/', 'snippet': 'The 25 million euro restoration of a classic Art Deco movie theater has shined a new light on the rough but storied neighborhood of Barbès.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Paris, a Ragtag, Resplendent District Prepares for Its Close-Up', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-07T22:48:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Sciolino', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sciolino', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/64b5fa48-eb67-5d87-9c48-a2f7cfe4de20', 'word_count': 1065, 'uri': 'nyt://article/64b5fa48-eb67-5d87-9c48-a2f7cfe4de20'}, {'abstract': 'Frederick Wiseman’s documentary “At Berkeley” takes viewers into the classrooms and the broad campus life of a well-functioning university.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/movies/at-berkeley-a-documentary-by-frederick-wiseman.html', 'snippet': 'Frederick Wiseman’s documentary “At Berkeley” takes viewers into the classrooms and the broad campus life of a well-functioning university.', 'lead_paragraph': '“At Berkeley,” the documentarian Frederick Wiseman’s magisterial examination of the University of California, Berkeley, is conspicuous for not identifying the scores of people shown teaching, studying and exchanging ideas in and out of the classroom. Some may recognize the university’s chipper, ever-smiling former chancellor Robert J. Birgeneau, who retired this year. An even more prominent figure is Robert Reich, the former secretary of labor, now a professor at Berkeley’s Goldman School of Public Policy, who delivers an insightful lecture on leadership and the need for self-evaluation. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/arts/08ATBERKELEY_SPAN/ATBERKELEY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width