o fight today’s bondage rather than as reparations for slavery of the past.', 'lead_paragraph': ' ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '21st-Century Slavery', 'kicker': 'Letter', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '21st-Century Slavery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reparations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Trafficking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Slavery', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T00:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/3fb0425b-b1bf-55c0-bb89-8fa07d2fb3d3', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3fb0425b-b1bf-55c0-bb89-8fa07d2fb3d3'}, {'abstract': 'A listing of walking tours, speaking engagements, cultural activities and Veterans Day events in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/arts/spare-times-for-nov-8-14.html', 'snippet': 'A listing of walking tours, speaking engagements, cultural activities and Veterans Day events in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Veterans Day Weekend (Friday through Monday) In keeping with a tradition largely in place since 1919, Veterans Day honors peace and those in the armed forces on the 11th day of the 11th month at the 11th hour. On Monday there will be a procession along Fifth Avenue, from 26th to 52nd Streets, starting at 11:10 a.m., with Ann E. Dunwoody, the first woman to become a four-star general and who is now retired, as the grand marshal. Sponsored by the United War Veterans Council, the parade also commemorates the 60th anniversary of the end of the Korean War. A ceremony at 10 a.m. in Madison Square Park, at Broadway and 23rd Street, will start things off. More details: vetsday.org.', 'print_secti