'value': 'Batteries', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T02:11:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jaclyn Trop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaclyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1dd7d4b1-33e4-5e18-b358-51ef74a6c3e1', 'word_count': 969, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1dd7d4b1-33e4-5e18-b358-51ef74a6c3e1'}, {'abstract': 'A group wants to bring a business improvement district to Corona and Jackson Heights in Queens. Some residents fear it would be costly and rob the area of its character.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/nyregion/in-queens-balking-at-change-even-if-its-called-improvement.html', 'snippet': 'A group wants to bring a business improvement district to Corona and Jackson Heights in Queens. Some residents fear it would be costly and rob the area of its character.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like a king surveying his empire, Hector Burgos, 74, stood on Roosevelt Avenue at 102nd Street in Queens and spread his arms wide. “This is my corner,” he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/nyregion/roosevelt-2/roosevelt-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Queens, Balking at Change, Even if It’s Called Improvement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Queens, Balking at Change, Even if It’s Called Improvement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jackson Heights (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Corona (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T02:15:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Turkewitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Turkewitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/146d61d4-84fb-57d9-bb4f-6b68abc084ba', 'word_count': 936, 'uri': 'nyt://article/146d61d4-84fb-57d9-bb4f-6b68abc084ba'}, {'abstract': 'The beleaguered judge in New York City’s stop-and-frisk litigation rightly challenged an appellate court’s decision to remove her from overseeing the case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/opinion/judge-scheindlins-case.html', 'snippet': 'The beleaguered judge in New York City’s stop-and-frisk litigation rightly challenged an appellate court’s decision to remove her from overseeing the case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The United States Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit erred badly last week when it stayed the remedies ordered by Judge Shira Scheindlin of Federal District Court to correct the civil rights violations associated with New York City’s stop-and-frisk policy, including an independent monitor to review police practices. It also unjustly damaged Judge Scheindlin’s reputation when it removed her from the case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Scheindlin’s Case', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Judge Scheindlin’s Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racial Profiling', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T02:19:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/db64dd05-2ad7-5ea1-b6b8-17a78c18d490', 'word_count': 506, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db64dd05-2ad7-5ea1-b6b8-17a78c18d490'}, {'abstract': 'Food companies would be better off voluntarily labeling genetically modified foods than fighting the passage of state laws.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/opinion/labels-for-controversial-ingredients.html', 'snippet': 'Food companies would be better off voluntarily labeling genetically modified foods than fighting the passage of state laws.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A ballot initiative in Washington State would require many foods to carry conspicuous warning labels if they use genetically engineered ingredients. The votes will not be completely tallied for several days, but a partial count shows the initiative losing by 54 percent to 46 percent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '34', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Labels for Controversial Ingredients', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Labels for Controversial Ingredients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labeling and Labels', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cargill Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T02:19:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6d0b1f61-54b7-5bc9-b578-57ac783182dd', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6d0b1f61-54b7-5bc9-b578-57ac783182dd'}, {'abstract': 'Rui Moreira, 57, achieved a rare political victory in Western Europe by being elected the mayor of Porto, Portugal, without having been affiliated with an established political party.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/world/europe/outsiders-election-gives-portuguese-a-ray-of-optimism.html', 'snippet': 'Rui Moreira, 57, achieved a rare political victory in Western Europe by being elected the mayor of Porto, Portugal, without having been affiliated with an established political party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTO, Portugal — Rui Moreira seems an unlikely answer to the populist discontent stalking Europe’s mainstream political parties. Scion of one of this city’s richest families, he studied abroad, ran the family shipping business for a while, and then invested in everything from a popular nightclub here to wine distribution in Brazil and real estate in Chile. Until recently, politics was of little interest, he said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/world/portugalweb1/portugalweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/09/world/portugalweb1/portugalweb3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/world/portugalweb1/portugalweb3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/world/portugalweb1/portugalweb3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima