r husband, Greg, owners of Dori’s Tea Cottage and Cafe, depend on travelers filing into their sun-drenched rooms full of lace, floral teacups and the scent of apple-cinnamon scones.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hit Twice by Hard Times, a Town Works to Rebound', 'kicker': 'Groveland Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hit Twice by Hard Times, a Town Works to Rebound', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yosemite National Park (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pogash, Carol', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T02:37:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Pogash', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogash', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9697fc9f-44e6-5aef-9b01-7a1e4b5d79a6', 'word_count': 1057, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9697fc9f-44e6-5aef-9b01-7a1e4b5d79a6'}, {'abstract': 'After fracturing the same leg in back-to-back seasons, the Giants’ Andre Brown is coming off injured reserve to bolster the team’s backfield.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/sports/football/twice-broken-left-leg-hasnt-deterred-giants-running-back-andre-brown.html', 'snippet': 'After fracturing the s