caafootball/stanfords-stout-defense-stymies-potent-oregon.html', 'snippet': 'The Ducks were held scoreless through three quarters by a Cardinal defense that harassed quarterback Marcus Mariota, sacking him twice and forcing two turnovers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STANFORD, Calif. — Oregon has a knack for bursting into November, a blur of pewter, green or yellow helmets, iridescent uniforms and dizzying speed. Entering Thursday night’s showdown against No. 6 Stanford, the second-ranked Ducks and their high-octane offense had not scored fewer than 42 points this season, breezing to an 8-0 record.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1331, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/08/sports/stanford/stanford-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Stanford’s Stout Defense Stymies Potent Oregon', 'kicker': 'No. 6 Stanford 26, No. 2 Oregon 20', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Stanford’s Stout Defense Stymies Potent Oregon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strauss, Ben', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oregon', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gaffney, Tyler', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T05:42:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f345a705-9ec6-59a5-a9af-bc68a8affe67', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f345a705-9ec6-59a5-a9af-bc68a8affe67'}, {'abstract': 'Measures to curb unwanted text messages would have widespread public support in a country with 1.2 billion mobile subscribers and where each mobile number receives an average of one junk text a day.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/facing-a-flood-of-junk-text-messages-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Measures to curb unwanted text messages would have widespread public support in a country with 1.2 billion mobile subscribers and where each mobile number receives an average of one junk text a day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fake receipts. Dubious massages. Short-term loans. English lessons from actual foreigners. On an average day the average Chinese person will receive a text message advertising such services and many others. Some are merely unwanted promotions. Others, like the messages from one’s “landlord” that list a new bank account you should send your money to, are outright frauds. The texts plague cellphones and have in turn helped drive the growth of mobile messaging apps such as Tencent’s WeChat.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Facing a Flood of Junk Text Messages in China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Text Messaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Mobile Ltd', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Telecom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'China Unicom (Hong Kong) Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T05:44:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Austin Ramzy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Austin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ramzy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bd034bda-0f25-5e4d-a9b3-c3d074edca41', 'word_count': 338, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bd034bda-0f25-5e4d-a9b3-c3d074edca41'}, {'abstract': 'China faces a crisis unless big economic changes are accompanied by a political overhaul, a respected Chinese economist says as Communist Party leaders prepare to meet on the nation’s economic future.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/as-plenum-starts-an-economist-sees-crisis-ahead/', 'snippet': 'China faces a crisis unless big economic changes are accompanied by a political overhaul, a respected Chinese economist says as Communist Party leaders prepare to meet on the nation’s economic future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Chinese state news media has hailed a Communist Party conference on reinvigorating the economy as a triumph even before it opens Saturday. But beforehand, one of the country’s most prominent economists has delivered a warning: China faces a crisis unless big economic changes are accompanied by a political overhaul.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Plenum Starts, an Economist Sees Crisis Ahead', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Li Keqiang', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wen Jiabao', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wu Jinglian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T05:54:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/230e8c37-a3dc-57cb-8ca9-398c07824f32', 'word_count': 659, 'uri': 'nyt://article/230e8c37-a3dc-57cb-8ca9-398c07824f32'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (WE) THE LYLAS Bruno Mars’s four sisters — Jaime, Tiara, Tahiti and Presley Hernandez, otherwise known as the Lylas (for “love you like a sister”), left — trade the sand and surf of Hawaii for Los Angeles as they pursue their dreams of musical superstardom. The series begins as the siblings arrive in California, where Tahiti struggles with leaving her two children behind, and the women discover that seeing eye to eye with a management team isn’t as easy as it looks. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/34c4d783-407e-5c4e-9e83-db17f97965ce', 'word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34c4d783-407e-5c4e-9e83-db17f97965ce'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/news-quiz-november-8-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 8, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': 