teful Old Lady’', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T10:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheila Solomon Klass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheila', 'middlename': 'Solomon', 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4028769-c4b5-52bc-a9fd-ea786b710ee8', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4028769-c4b5-52bc-a9fd-ea786b710ee8'}, {'abstract': 'Have you ever been the victim of a prank that felt more hurtful than funny?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/when-do-pranks-cross-the-line-to-become-bullying/', 'snippet': 'Have you ever been the victim of a prank that felt more hurtful than funny?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many National Football League teams have a tradition of picking on rookie players — for example, making them lug teammates’ equipment or leaving them taped to goal posts. Such indignities may not be all that different from what goes on in some high school hallways or fraternity houses. But sometimes what might seem like good-natured fun to one person is very clearly bullying and harassment to another.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/sports/BULLY-LN/BULLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/sports/BULLY-LN/BULLY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/sports/BULLY-LN/BULLY-jumbo.