: 'Obama, Under Health Law Cloud, Hits Road to Push New Public Works', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama, Under Health Law Cloud, Hits Road to Push New Public Works', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Orleans (La)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T14:48:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Campbell Robertson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Campbell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robertson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/855949a4-6c46-5546-88a7-9be7aa6d68a7', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/855949a4-6c46-5546-88a7-9be7aa6d68a7'}, {'abstract': 'The White House has issued a report on the costs of the October shutdown, the second longest since 1980.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/what-the-shutdown-cost/', 'snippet': 'The White House has issued a report on the costs of the October shutdown, the second longest since 1980.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The White House has issued a report on the costs of the October shutdown, the second longest since 1980. Readers will recall that Republicans refused to fund the government because…well actually it was a little unclear. Something to do with stopping the Affordable Care Act, or maybe just putting “points on the board.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Shutdown Cost', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shutdowns (Institutional)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T14:50:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1abc99a-c2bf-56e6-b843-19dee7ce4a2d', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1abc99a-c2bf-56e6-b843-19dee7ce4a2d'}, {'abstract': 'Anne-Marie Duff talks about taking on the burning Lady Macbeth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/theater/playing-the-crazy-women.html', 'snippet': 'Anne-Marie Duff talks about taking on the burning Lady Macbeth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Anne-Marie Duff often bares her soul onstage. Occasionally her underwear, too. At a wardrobe fitting for Lincoln Center Theater’s “Macbeth,” in which she plays Shakespeare’s “fiendlike queen,” she pointed to a transparent slip that is part of her costume and talked about the knickers she wanted to wear underneath. “The Scotland flag,” she said brightly. “Or plaid. Tartan.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10DUFF1_SPAN/10DUFF1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10DUFF1_SPAN/10DUFF1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10DUFF1_SPAN/10DUFF1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 