 1043, 'uri': 'nyt://article/21fb6bca-93c3-5746-a132-0b2e8da507ce'}, {'abstract': 'Hilton Als’s essays explore the cultural and racial implications of white womanhood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/books/review/white-girls-by-hilton-als.html', 'snippet': 'Hilton Als’s essays explore the cultural and racial implications of white womanhood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just listen to the exquisite black and brown queer kids cavorting about Christopher Street tell you how to read: “Anybody in this world can be read,” 22-year-old Maliek Wynn of Brooklyn said to me. “You read somebody to throw shade — in a bad and good way. You’re tellin’ someone about themselves. Tellin’ everything — left, right, up, down, inside, out. And it’s an education behind the telling. That’s why it’s a read.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/books/review/10BENJAMIN/10BENJAMIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 552, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/books/review/10BENJAMIN/10BENJAMIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 552}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/books/review/10BENJAMIN/10BENJAMIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 943, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/books/review/10BENJAMIN/10BENJAMIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1104, 'width': 1199, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/books/review/10BENJAMIN/10BENJAMIN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 