ization over the admission of Palestinians as full members. The move undermined America’s ability to exercise its influence in countries around the globe through the United Nations agency’s educational and aid programs, according to Western diplomats and international relations experts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Loses Voting Rights at Unesco', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Loses Voting Rights At Unesco', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubin, Alissa Johannsen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bokova, Irina', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Palestinians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T15:18:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alissa J. Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alissa', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/587a09fb-c0ec-521b-a44f-099f12e916ef', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/587a09fb-c0ec-521b-a44f-099f12e916ef'}, {'abstract': 'Parents share stories of bullying and their responses — sometimes successful, sometimes a subject of frustration and regret.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/if-a-child-is-bullied-parents-offer-advice-on-when-and-how-to-intervene/', 'snippet': 'Parents share stories of bullying and their responses — sometimes successful, sometimes a subject of frustration and regret.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last week we asked parents, “If Your Child Was Bullied, When Did You Intervene and When Did You Stay Out?” If there’s one thing the many answers demonstrated, it’s that no two cases of bullying are quite the same, and so the appropriate responses differ widely. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'If a Child Is Bullied, Parents Offer Advice on When and How to Intervene', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T15:18:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Winerip', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winerip', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f55d42b-d393-5d31-949f-4dacc6194d9c', 'word_count': 2092, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f55d42b-d393-5d31-949f-4dacc6194d9c'}, {'abstract': 'If a wedding is canceled, should the couple return the gifts? Is it O.K. to send printed envelopes instead of handwritten? What does “black tie preferred” mean?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/fashion/weddings/wedding-q-and-a.html', 'snippet': 'If a wedding is canceled, should the couple return the gifts? Is it O.K. to send printed envelopes instead of handwritten? What does “black tie preferred” mean?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cold Feet? Fork Over the Lo