91462227b4', 'word_count': 462, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bf3b1d3-8cbe-555f-807a-c691462227b4'}, {'abstract': 'The October jobs report, by itself, is not going to decide the debate among Federal Reserve officials over whether to pull back on their stimulus program.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/watching-and-waiting-for-the-fed/', 'snippet': 'The October jobs report, by itself, is not going to decide the debate among Federal Reserve officials over whether to pull back on their stimulus program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The October jobs report, strong by recent standards, is likely to increase uncertainty about the Federal Reserve’s plans for the coming months, raising doubts about the current consensus that the Fed won’t pull back until next year.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Watching and Waiting, for the Fed', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T15:27:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c1ef061-cf1f-5c6d-a18e-6b3072f42241', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c1ef061-cf1f-5c6d-a18e-6b3072f42241'}, {'abstract': 'The real meaning of that French downgrade.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/ideological-ratings/', 'snippet': 'The real meaning of that French downgrade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So S&P has downgraded France. What does this tell us?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ideological Ratings', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T15:29:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/87f52e94-e27c-5229-8738-10e4c2355665', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/87f52e94-e27c-5229-8738-10e4c2355665'}, {'abstract': 'Alissa Quart shows how underrepresented groups are organizing and challenging the status quo.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/books/review/republic-of-outsiders-by-alissa-quart.html', 'snippet': 'Alissa Quart shows how underrepresented groups are organizing and challenging the status quo.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With our civic sphere dominated by social media, advertising and political pseudo-news, it’s easy to despair that cultural subversion is a thing of the past. But in Alissa Quart’s new book, “Republic of Outsiders,” we meet the often unlikely agitators who are participating in new social and cultural revolutions using the tools of what we would once have called the Man — technology, entrepreneurialism and even finance. What emerges is a hopeful, if sometimes uneven, portrait of a mainstream culture that’s constantly being rewritten by the people at its margins.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '48', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 638, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 638}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 963, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10NEWITZ/10NEWITZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gate Crashers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gate Crashers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quart, Alissa', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T15:29:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annalee Newitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annalee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Newitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/67fef584-9106-54f5-b911-2f8f5f20bbb0', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67fef584-9106-54f5-b911-2f8f5f20bbb0'}, {'abstract': 'Simon Winchester examines the influential figures who fostered American unity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/books/review/simon-winchesters-men-who-united-the-states.html', 'snippet': 'Simon Winchester examines the influential figures who fostered American unity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On July 4, 2011, the British-born historian Simon Winchester took an oath to become an American citizen. It was a startling decision for someone Queen Elizabeth herself had made an officer of the Order of the British Empire not so long ago. Why the move? Winchester, it seems, was in love. But it wasn’t a woman who captured his heart. No, Winchester had fallen for an entire nation.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 128, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 128}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 219, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/1110-bks-MIHM-sub/1110-bks-MIHM-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nation Builders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nation Builders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winchester, Simon (1944- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T15:29:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Mihm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mihm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/efb385de-78e3-5ea3-bdf1-00a1de5e1c69', 'word_count': 1237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efb385de-78e3-5ea3-bdf1-00a1de5e1c69'}, {'abstract': 'Memories of Marie Colvin, a journalist killed in Syria, and a selection of her work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/books/review/on-the-front-line-and-under-the-wire.html', 'snippet': 'Memories of Marie Colvin, a journalist killed in Syria, and a selection of her work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If blinded in one eye by shrapnel, many journalists would consider early retirement. At the very least they would contemplate avoiding areas known for ambushes and land mines. But Marie Colvin, one of the bravest and certainly best-dressed foreign correspondents of our time, simply turned that injury, which she sustained while reporting in Sri Lanka for The Sunday Times of London, into a style statement. After an excruciating recovery involving flashbacks of the attack, this extraordinary American reporter donned a black eye patch and returned to the field to risk her life over and over again. When she was killed by a rocket attack in Syria in February 2012 on yet another assignment, colleagues were stunned, although not exactly surprised. Colvin, after all, often arrived at the front lines first and stayed longer than others. She had been stranded on a 12,000-foot mountain in Chechnya. She was nearly lynched in Egypt. She spent half her 56 years in the world’s most brutal conflict zones. Her luck couldn’t last forever.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '44', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10SUBMATLOFF/10SUBMATLOFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 511, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10SUBMATLOFF/10SUBMATLOFF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 511}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10SUBMATLOFF/10SUBMATLOFF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 986, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/books/review/10SUBMATLOFF/10SUBMATLOFF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 840, 'width': 986, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': No