ung) and rhythms (drummed) that pushes everything upward and outward, straining toward catharsis. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09HEART/09HEART-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seattle’s Addition to the Folk-Rock Boom', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sex, Regret And Other Standbys', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Head and the Heart, The (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Webster Hall', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T18:23:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/65e3288e-b225-55c3-9659-40faf29858a4', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/65e3288e-b225-55c3-9659-40faf29858a4'}, {'abstract': 'A floor-through unit with four bedrooms, five and a half baths and Gramercy Park frontage was the most expensive residential sale of the week.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/big-ticket-a-gramercy-park-key-for-15-47-million/', 'snippet': 'A floor-through unit with four bedrooms, five and a half baths and Gramercy Park frontage was the most expensive residential sale of the week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The same cachet that worked for the elite team behind 15 Central Park West continues to bring buyers with big wallets to 18 Gramercy Park South, where yet another of the 4,207-square-foot floor-through units with 40 feet of park frontage was the most expensive residential sale of the week, according to city records.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 867}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1418, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/realestate/10ticket/10ticket-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Ticket | A Gramercy Park Key for $15.47 Million', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Key Is Awarded', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T18:25:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5177881-e331-5c8a-99fa-993dfd485d7d', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5177881-e331-5c8a-99fa-993dfd485d7d'}, {'abstract': 'A new show by the 26-year-old Angeleno includes “paintings” made from Internet scavenger hunts and webcam performance videos.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/on-view-for-petra-cortright-the-web-is-the-ultimate-canvas/', 'snippet': 'A new show by the 26-year-old Angeleno includes “paintings” made from Internet scavenger hunts and webcam performance videos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Digital art has become an accepted part of every biennial and international art fair. Last month, Philips de Pury even devoted an auction to it, October’s successful Paddles On!, presented in partnership with Tumblr. But the form is still the punk rock of the art world. For the 26-year-old L.A.-based artist Petra Cortright, it’s the ideal form, because it’s both more convenient and less precious than more traditional forms like painting. “There’s so many resources,” she says, “and it doesn’t feel like there’s so much riding on it.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Petra Cortright, the Web Is the Ultimate Canvas', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T18:30:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maxwell Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maxwell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b8061b4-2375-5728-b788-f7c1d98967e8', 'word_count': 321, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b8061b4-2375-5728-b788-f7c1d98967e8'}, {'abstract': 'A historic townhouse with a once-controversial facade is on the market for $9.95 million.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/11/10/realestate/20131110-EXCLUSIVE.html', 'snippet': 'A historic townhouse with a once-controversial facade is on the market for $9.95 m