rell', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T18:34:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0c84106-72e9-5a58-9b88-99992f1a805f', 'word_count': 791, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0c84106-72e9-5a58-9b88-99992f1a805f'}, {'abstract': 'Laurie M. Tisch, whose father, Preston Robert Tisch, bought a half-interest in the New York Giants in 1991, spends Sundays in the owners’ box at the team’s stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/nyregion/love-is-giants-blue.html', 'snippet': 'Laurie M. Tisch, whose father, Preston Robert Tisch, bought a half-interest in the New York Giants in 1991, spends Sundays in the owners’ box at the team’s stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since her father, Preston Robert Tisch, bought half of the New York Giants in 1991, Laurie M. Tisch, 62, has spent fall Sundays in the owners’ box at the team’s stadium. There she can be seen jumping out of her front-row seat to cheer a touchdown in her Giants-blue blazer, custom Giants-blue cowboy boots and chunky 2011 Super Bowl ring. Indeed, Ms. Tisch — who lives on the Upper East Side with her Tibetan terrier, Lucy — has raised a true-blue Giants family. She is often joined at the game by her two grown daughters, Carolyn Tisch Blodgett and Emily Tisch Sussman, and her son-in-law, William Wilson Blodgett, as well as by her mother, Joan H. Tisch. The rest of Ms. Tisch’s week is devoted to supporting the causes she cares about through her Illumination Fund, founded in 2007, which aims to increase access and opportunity for New Yorkers in areas like the arts and nutrition.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10ROUTINE1_SPAN/1110ROUTINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love Is Giants Blue', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Love Is Giants Blue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tisch, Laurie M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T18:38:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ebff173a-92ed-5785-8068-cb4301a1f346', 'word_count': 762, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ebff173a-92ed-5785-8068-cb4301a1f346'}, {'abstract': 'With its victory on Thursday, Stanford dealt a severe blow to Oregon’s national title hopes for the second year in a row.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/sports/ncaafootball/late-loss-after-hot-start-is-too-familiar-to-oregon.html', 'snippet': 'With its victory on Thursday, Stanford dealt a severe blow to Oregon’s national title hopes for the second year in a row.', 'lead_paragraph': 'STANFORD, Calif. — Oregon players trudged through the tunnel at Stanford Stadium, toward the visitors’ locker room, after Thursday night’s 26-20 loss to the Cardinal. Their once pristine white uniforms were muddied, their once shiny green numbers muted by shadow. They were silent, mostly, and wore tight-lipped expressions, never looking back at the sea of giddy humanity that had rushed the field, awash in Cardinal Red. The clip-clop of the Ducks’ cleats on concrete was barely audible above the din.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/sports/09oregon1/09oregon1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Late Loss After Hot Start Is Too Familiar to Oregon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stanford University', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Oregon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Helfrich, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T18:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a683c72e-4870-5993-b5d0-be10997c7268', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a683c72e-4870-5993-b5d0-be10997c7268'}, {'abstract': 'A group of friends and artists convened at the Cecil in Harlem to enjoy fusion cuisine and the company of their mentor, Charles Gaines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/nyregion/at-the-cecil-nourished-and-inspired.html', 'snippet': 'A group of friends and artists convened at the Cecil in Harlem to enjoy fusion cuisine and the company of their mentor, Charles Gaines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The neon green “Cecil” sign glows at the intersection of old and new Harlem — 118th Street and St. Nicholas Avenue. The historic hotel hosts more than fusion cuisine. Alexander Smalls, the executive chef and owner with Richard Parsons, the former chief executive of Time Warner, also reopened the landmark jazz club Minton’s next door. The Cecil’s menu is playfully didactic: “An edible conversation about the food of the African diaspora,” Mr. Smalls said on Wednesday. Since the Cecil opened two months ago, patrons have been buzzing about the Afro-Asian-American food and scene. There was the actress Tamara Tunie, who plays a medical examiner on “Law & Order: SVU.” In Mr. Smalls’s home kitchen she was the guinea pig for the cinnamon-scented fried guinea hen. There were parents enjoying a rare night without their wailing baby, downtown designers, Korean-American friends, and artists starving no more.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10TABLE/10TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 352, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/10TABLE/10TABLE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 352}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/nyregion/1