eir personal gift suggestions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/04/t-magazine/t-magazine-gift-guide-women.html', 'snippet': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T19:52:50+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1923c5da-b537-5ab1-b5fc-9a7074fd35ae', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1923c5da-b537-5ab1-b5fc-9a7074fd35ae'}, {'abstract': 'I thought my 5-year-old was ready for the “Harry Potter” books. I was wrong, and I find myself verbally editing every page.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/child-proofing-harry-potter/', 'snippet': 'I thought my 5-year-old was ready for the “Harry Potter” books. I was wrong, and I find myself verbally editing every page.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The second Professor McGonagall pulls Oliver Wood from his charms class, I realize I’m in “Pinkalicious” territory again. In a flash, the entire sequence from “Harry Potter and the Sorcerer’s Stone” comes back to me: Madam Hooch orders the class not to fly; Harry hops on his broomstick; McGonagall catches him and introduces him to Wood, the captain of the Gryffindor quidditch team, as its new seeker.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Child-Proofing ‘Harry Potter’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T19:53:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynn Messina', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Messina', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13c98098-4a49-51b7-854f-3a32ae669f12', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13c98098-4a49-51b7-854f-3a32ae669f12'}, {'abstract': 'Some of Cathy Horyn’s thoughts on Mr. Ghesquière’s appointment at Louis Vuitton.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/fashion/Cathy-Horyn-on-Nicolas-Ghesquire-Choice-by-Louis-Vuitton.html', 'snippet': 'Some of Cathy Horyn’s thoughts on Mr. Ghesquière’s appointment at Louis Vuitton.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY OBSESSION THESE DAYS is to find a decent pair of sweatpants. And by decent, I mean particular: not too skinny, perhaps something in a fine knit (ribbing is O.K.), and definitely not anything pooling at my ankles. I’m willing to pay a lot of money for my dream sweats, not a fortune but certainly I can do better than Modell’s.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10RUNWAY/10RUNWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/fashion/10RUNWAY/10RUNWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 683}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': N