 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e628cad2-fa9b-53f7-8565-b607e6c0303b', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e628cad2-fa9b-53f7-8565-b607e6c0303b'}, {'abstract': 'Biscotti, the dry Italian cookies that are twice baked (which is what the name means), lend themselves to interpretation and adaptation to healthful whole grain variations.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/wholesome-biscotti-some-even-gluten-free/', 'snippet': 'Biscotti, the dry Italian cookies that are twice baked (which is what the name means), lend themselves to interpretation and adaptation to healthful whole grain variations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some pastries lend themselves to interpretation and adaptation to whole grain variations; others are best left alone in their white flour and sugar splendor. Biscotti, the dry Italian cookies that are twice baked (which is what the name means), are a kind of pastry that does. They are supposed to be hard, and don’t have to be too sweet, though most of the biscotti you find in coffee shops are – too sweet, that is.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/05/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/05/science/recipehealthpromo/recipehealthpromo-superJum