ed 90 last month, and that gave the New York Festival of Song something to sing about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ned Rorem, the composer of poetic art songs and author of sharp-witted essays and diaries, turned 90 last month. He didn’t look a day over 70 on Tuesday as he acknowledged, with a wry smile, a standing ovation from the audience at Merkin Concert Hall after an evening-long birthday tribute by the New York Festival of Song. It contained all the key ingredients of his work: a deep poetic sensibility laced with sardonic wit and a romantic’s receptivity to the sublime in nature parceled into forms that have all the economy of New York apartment living.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poetic Tribute to a Composer', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poetic Tribute To a Composer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rorem, Ned', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Festival of Song', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Merkin Concert Hall', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T23:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ad66b74-1133-5989-88db-150349117192', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ad66b74-1133-5989-88db-150349117192'}, {'abstract': 'Three young jazz musicians forging an identity as the Colin Stranahan Trio, also known as Stranahan, Zaleski, Rosato, played at Smalls on Wednesday and Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/arts/music/the-colin-stranahan-trio-performs-at-smalls.html', 'snippet': 'Three young jazz musicians forging an identity as the Colin Stranahan Trio, also known as Stranahan, Zaleski, Rosato, played at Smalls on Wednesday and Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The acoustic piano trio continues to be a stable currency in jazz, holding firm against so many other fluctuations. There’s always some attention-grabbing innovation in the field, but it’s also worth noting when a new trio simply seems to arrive at its own style, having sifted through a preponderance of options. The Colin Stranahan Trio is quietly becoming one of these, as it indicated on Thursday, in the second of two nights at Smalls.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/music/09smalls-sub/09smalls-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Drummer, a Pianist and a Bassist, by Any Name, Find Their Niche', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Drummer, a Pianist and a Bassist, by Any Name, Find Their Niche', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stranahan, Colin, Trio', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Smalls (Manhattan, NY, Music Venue)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jazz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T23:08:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Chinen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chinen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/17634296-d665-5030-978d-985c66cebcbf', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17634296-d665-5030-978d-985c66cebcbf'}, {'abstract': 'Video and photos show the extent of the damage after powerful Typhoon Haiyan tore through the center of the Philippines.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/eyewitness-reports-after-typhoon-in-philippines/', 'snippet': 'Video and photos show the extent of the damage after powerful Typhoon Haiyan tore through the center of the Philippines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 3:30 p.m., Nov. 9 Dramatic images and video from local journalists and eyewitnesses show the extent of the damage in the aftermath of Typhoon Haiyan, which  tore through the center of the Philippines on Friday. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Eyewitness Reports After Typhoon in Philippines', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T23:09:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/386ad077-68f9-5907-84e8-428d4b7e69aa', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/386ad077-68f9-5907-84e8-428d4b7e69aa'}, {'abstract': 'For the 2013 Guggenheim International Gala honoring the James Turrell and Christopher Wool, the techno DJ Richie Hawtin built an installation that illuminated the rotunda, recalling Turrell’s show last summer.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/08/art-matters-a-different-kind-of-light-show-at-the-guggenheim/', 'snippet': 'For the 2013 Guggenheim International Gala honoring the James Turrell and Christopher Wool, the techno DJ Richie Hawtin built an installation that illuminated the rotunda, recalling Turrell’s show last summer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'James Turrell isn’t the only artist who can make the Guggenheim glow. Last Wednesday, for the first night of the 2013 Guggenheim International Gala made possible by Dior, the techno wizard Richie Hawtin brought back his Plastikman persona for one night with a light show that emanated from a cubic tower that rose from the floor of the museum’s famous rotunda. The event, which this year honored Turrell (whose “Aten Reign” illuminated the museum all summer) and Christopher Wool (whose career-spanning exhibition is on view now), centered around Hawtin’s pulsing installation, which gave a nod both to the history of rave culture and to the kinds of cross-genre artworks the museum supports (including the Performa piece by Florian Hecker coming to the museum this very weekend).As Hawtin slid up and down the scales, with pops, zips and plastic sounds, the tower produced synchronized light projections. Luminaries such as Zachary Quinto, Elizabeth Olsen and Zosia Mamet, all dressed in Dior for the event, looked on, transfixed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Matters | A Different Kind of Light Show at the Guggenheim', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turrell, James', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-08T23:11:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55fd2ba9-a065-5dbf-9af7-e202e3e20d07', 'word_count': 166, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55fd2ba9-a065-5dbf-9af7-e202e3e20d07'}, {'abstract': 'Among the popular bridge books reprinted this year are two updated classics: “The Secrets of Winning Bridge,” by Jeff Rubens, and “Treasury of Bidding