n-returns-to-the-met.html', 'snippet': 'The Metropolitan Opera presents Herbert Wernicke’s production of Strauss’s fairy tale opera “Die Frau Ohne Schatten,” about a woman making the journey from spirit to humanity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are some seemingly batty elements in Strauss’s fairy tale opera “Die Frau Ohne Schatten” (“The Woman Without a Shadow”), first performed in Vienna in 1919. Even Strauss was somewhat baffled by Hugo von Hofmannsthal’s libretto. The work has confused many opera lovers as well. There was a noticeable number of empty seats at the Metropolitan Opera on Thursday night when Herbert Wernicke’s 2001 production returned for the first time in 10 years. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09SCHATTEN/09SCHATTEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 380, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09SCHATTEN/09SCHATTEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 380}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09SCHATTEN/09SCHATTEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 649, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09SCHATTEN/09SCHATTEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1298, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09SCHATTEN/09SCHATTEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/09/arts/09SCHATTEN/09SCHATTEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight