r veteran of the Police Department pleaded guilty to arranging to hack into dozens of email accounts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A New York City police detective pleaded guilty on Friday to arranging to hack into dozens of email accounts and gaining access to a federal law enforcement database to gather information on his colleagues, said Preet Bharara, the United States attorney in Manhattan. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Detective Admits Spying on Colleagues', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Detective Admits Spying on Colleagues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vargas, Edwin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T02:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d72d297-9c6d-54e5-a055-120e96bb3e62', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d72d297-9c6d-54e5-a055-120e96bb3e62'}, {'abstract': 'A former prosecutor in Texas will spend 10 days in jail for withholding evidence in a murder trial — insultingly short, but a milestone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/opinion/a-prosecutor-is-punished.html', 'snippet': 'A former prosecutor in Texas will spend 10 days in jail for withholding evidence in a murder trial — insultingly short, but a milestone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For what may be the first time on record, a former prosecutor in Texas is going to jail for failing to turn over exculpatory evidence in a murder trial. The 10-day jail sentence for the prosecutor, Ken Anderson, is insultingly short — the victim of his misconduct, Michael Morton, spent nearly 25 years in prison. But because prosecutors are so rarely held accountable for their misconduct, the sentence is remarkable nonetheless. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Prosecutor Is Punished', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Prosecutor Is Punished', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morton, Michael', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Anderson, Ken', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Legal Profession', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sentences (Criminal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'District Attorneys', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T02:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0df3685f-682f-5c1b-b797-202a28a838bb', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0df3685f-682f-5c1b-b797-202a28a838bb'}, {'abstract': 'The warning by Prime Minister Antonis Samaras against additional austerity measures goes unheeded.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/opinion/what-greece-cannot-afford.html', 'snippet': 'The warning by Prime Minister Antonis Samaras against additional austerity measures goes unheeded.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Greek society and the economy cannot afford any more measures,” Prime Minister Antonis Samaras said on Monday. There is no room or need for any more across-the-board wage and pension cuts, he declared. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Greece Cannot Afford', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What Greece Cannot Afford', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Samaras, Antonis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greece', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Commission', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Central Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'European Sovereign Debt Crisis (2010- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T02:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/834ec5e9-7b3b-5715-ba0c-8b500080b1ce', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/834ec5e9-7b3b-5715-ba0c-8b500080b1ce'}, {'abstract': 'The “salvage” logging bill is based on an antiquated notion of the role of wildfires in nature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/opinion/the-wrong-way-to-save-a-forest.html', 'snippet': 'The “salvage” logging bill is based on an antiquated notion of the role of wildfires in nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In July 1995, President Bill Clinton, in a moment of weakness he later regretted, signed a budget bill containing a rider allowing timber companies to conduct so-called salvage logging in areas burned by forest fires. The measure, advertised as necessary to forest health, would in fact have allowed indiscriminate logging and caused widespread environmental damage. It took a year of protests, court battles and legislative wrangling to undo it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wrong Way to Save a Forest', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Wrong Way to Save a Forest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Logging Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Bill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T02:39:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/ac34c9b2-4cd6-54bc-a0cf-f0f1fa1d25b5', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac34c9b2-4cd6-54bc-a0cf-f0f1fa1d25b5'}, {'abstract': 'Important new rules, plus health care reform, will provide parity in mental health treatment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/opinion/equal-coverage-for-the-mentally-ill.html', 'snippet': 'Important new rules, plus health care reform, will provide parity in mental health treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A struggle over decades to force insurers to cover mental health and addiction services on the same basis as medical and surgical costs is headed for success under new rules issued on Friday by the Obama administration. The rules will cover most Americans with health insurance, including those in many employer-sponsored plans, in other group plans, in some but not all Medicaid plans, and in policies bought on the individual markets. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Equal Coverage for the Mentally Ill', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Equal Coverage for the Mentally Ill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T02:39:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/86e10ad0-2d15-5b62-ad12-109f4655d91f', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86e10ad0-2d15-5b62-ad12-109f4655d91f'}, {'abstract': 'Whatever trouble Richie Incognito encountered — and there were numerous scrapes with the law, with coaches and with teammates — there was always a football team that wanted him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/sports/football/prized-for-his-aggression-richie-incognito-struggled-to-stay-in-bounds.html', 'snippet': 'Whatever