 York Times. “Reaching into the past for its precisely drawn memories, it casts a rich, delicate spell.” Afterward, Jerry Carlson, the host of City Cinematheque, interviews La Frances Hui, the film curator for Asia Society New York.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/e68ba7e3-37d9-5529-aaa1-8d5ba7477a92', 'word_count': 759, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e68ba7e3-37d9-5529-aaa1-8d5ba7477a92'}, {'abstract': 'The conventional account of how the 1978 Third Plenum transformed Chinais a compound of selective memories, and a deceptive guide to how the country’s steps to economic transformation really happened.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/09/portrait-of-deng-as-reformer-in-1978-plenum-ignores-history/', 'snippet': 'The conventional account of how the 1978 Third Plenum transformed Chinais a compound of selective memories, and a deceptive guide to how the country’s steps to economic transformation really happened.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China’s Communist Party leader, Xi Jinping, wants the late Deng Xiaoping’s magic. Mr. Xi will lay out proposals for economic rejuvenation at a leadership conference that started Saturday, and state-run media have likened the event to a historic meeting in 1978 when, they say, Mr. Deng began an era of market “reform and opening up.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Portrait of Deng as Reformer in 1978 Plenum Ignores History', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hua Guofeng', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhao Ziyang', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monash University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Sydney', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T08:44:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8b8ee99-f531-533e-a857-7b3036663e6a', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8b8ee99-f531-533e-a857-7b3036663e6a'}, {'abstract': 'For the sake of your executors, throw them out. Now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/booming/the-sex-toys-in-the-attic.html', 'snippet': 'For the sake of your executors, throw them out. Now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been thinking about an extremely beautiful sex toy an old boyfriend got me — I think it is on my mind because he is having heart surgery this week. This is how it is at a certain age; when you hear about an old