tate Legislatures', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-09T23:20:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erik Eckholm', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erik', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eckholm', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce81c854-15fe-5ff0-b8a8-a58ec4819389', 'word_count': 437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce81c854-15fe-5ff0-b8a8-a58ec4819389'}, {'abstract': 'Jeffrey Xiong of the Dallas Destiny demonstrated a maturity in his decision-making that allowed him to dominate each phase in many of his games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/crosswords/chess/texas-youth-is-named-mvp-of-american-league.html', 'snippet': 'Jeffrey Xiong of the Dallas Destiny demonstrated a maturity in his decision-making that allowed him to dominate each phase in many of his games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the United States Chess League began playing in 2005, there were eight teams — and some basic questions. Would the league be able to keep itself afloat financially? And would enough elite players participate to make it a success? ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Texas Youth Is Named M.V.P. of American League', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Texas Youth Is Named M.V.P. of American League', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McClain, Dylan Loeb', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Chess League', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chess', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xiong, Jeffrey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eckert, Doug', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Destiny (Chess Team)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St Louis Arch Bishops (Chess Team)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T00:47:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Chess', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dylan Loeb McClain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dylan', 'middlename': 'Loeb', 'lastname': 'McClain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc49a342-bee4-5ad0-9797-658d6d707778', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc49a342-bee4-5ad0-9797-658d6d707778'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Witkin worked for The Times for three decades and was part of the team that won a Pulitzer for coverage of the Challenger disaster.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/business/richard-witkin-95-witness-to-the-history-of-aviation.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Witkin worked for The Times for three decades and was part of the team that won a Pulitzer for coverage of the Challenger disaster.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Richard Witkin, a longtime aviation reporter for The New York Times who shared a Pulitzer Prize in 1987 for coverage of the Challenger space shuttle disaster, died on Thursday in Marlborough, Mass. He was 95.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/09/business/dog-Witkin-obit/dog-Witkin-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/09/business/dog-Witkin-obit/dog-Witkin-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'u