': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/world/africa/storied-party-of-mandela-faces-south-africa-unrest.html', 'snippet': 'Twenty years after the African National Congress swept to power in apartheid’s wake, discontent with its leaders is creating an opening for a new political party.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MARIKANA, South Africa — When Alton Dalasile got his first job as a miner in the late 1980s, he immediately joined the National Union of Mineworkers, a powerful organization that not only fought for workers’ rights but also battled the brutal system of racial segregation known as apartheid. When his union’s political ally, the African National Congress, was on the ballot in 1994 in South Africa’s first fully democratic election, Mr. Dalasile enthusiastically cast his ballot for Nelson Mandela, the country’s first black president.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/world/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA/SUB-SOUTHAFRICA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'h