'original': 'By Brooks Barnes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brooks', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b81fba57-ad95-58f2-ae7e-3f4986434e29', 'word_count': 175, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b81fba57-ad95-58f2-ae7e-3f4986434e29'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/arts/television/whats-on-sunday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '10 P.M. (Sundance) AMADEUS (1984) The 18th-century court composer Antonio Salieri (F. Murray Abraham, in an Oscar-winning performance) confesses to a deadly rivalry with Mozart (Tom Hulce, above) — and even snatches “a bit of divinity” from Mozart on his deathbed before trying to pass off the music as his own — in this adaptation of Peter Shaffer’s play by the director Milos Forman. “The glimpses of the operas are so good that one wants to see more,” Vincent Canby wrote in The New York Times. “They include ‘The Marriage of Figaro,’ about which the Emperor complains that ‘there are too many notes,’ ‘The Abduction From the Seraglio’ and ‘The Magic Flute,’ and, in one of the film’s most imaginative, most hallucinatory sequences, a parody version of ‘Don Giovanni,’ whose obscenities, of course, delight the now ailing Mozart.” Mr. Forman, who earned an Oscar for best director, he said, “has preserved the fascinating heart of Mr. Shaffer’s play, and made it available to millions who might never enter a legitimate theater. Well done.” ', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Sunday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Sunday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T17:26:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/2d3c19b9-e289-5003-a08e-9d7054744157', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2d3c19b9-e289-5003-a08e-9d7054744157'}, {'abstract': 'The suspended Miami lineman Richie Incognito said he went too far in his comments to teammate Jonathan Martin, but the exchanges were in the context of their friendship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/sports/football/dolphins-incognito-says-his-words-were-misinterpreted.html', 'snippet': 'The suspended Miami lineman Richie Incognito said he went too far in his comments to teammate Jonathan Martin, but the exchanges were in the context of their friendship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first extended comments since he was accused of bullying a teammate, Richie Incognito said that he never intended to hurt Jonathan Martin, a fellow offensive lineman with the Miami Dolphins, and that his way of motivating Martin had been misinterpreted.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Incognito Tries to Add Context to His Statements', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Incognito Tries to Add Context to His Statements', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Incognito, Richie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Miami Dolphins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bullies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan (1989- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T17:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff7e9388-8daa-57ae-8567-415547bc7b24', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff7e9388-8daa-57ae-8567-415547bc7b24'}, {'abstract': 'Approval Ratings in Recent Polls', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/10/us/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors.html', 'snippet': 'Approval Ratings in Recent Polls', 'lead_paragraph': 'Approval Ratings in Recent Polls', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/us/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848-jumbo.png', 'height': 801, 'width': 593, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/us/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848-superJumbo.png', 'height': 801, 'width': 593, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/us/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/us/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/us/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848/1110-obama-approval-versus-selected-governors-1384105938848-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Approval Ratings in Recent Polls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Governors (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brown, Edmund G Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T17:57:04+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'U.S.', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/830f047e-dd2b-5d3c-a19b-5b23c52ea67a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/830f047e-dd2b-5d3c-a19b-5b23c52ea67a'}, {'abstract': 'Senator Lindsey Graham said he would hold up administration nominations until survivors of the Benghazi attack were made available to Congress, despite the retraction of a news report that provoked Republicans’ renewed demands.', 'web_url': 'https://thecaucus.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/graham-sticks-with-threat-to-block-nominees/', 'snippet': 'Senator Lindsey Graham said he would hold up administration nominations until survivors of the Benghazi attack were made available to Congress, despite the retraction of a news report that provoked Republicans’ renewed demands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Lindsey Graham on Sunday stood by his threat to block all nominations by the Obama administration until Congress was granted access to all the survivors of the attack on the United States Mission in Benghazi, Libya, even as the news report on which Republicans based their latest demands was being retracted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Graham Sticks With Threat to Block Nominees', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T18:07:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emmarie Huetteman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emmarie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huetteman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce030cae-57e6-526b-8f32-465296afa8a7', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce030cae-57e6-526b-8f32-465296afa8a7'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a case against tightening, not for it.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/a-note-on-hysteresis-and-monetary-policy/', 'snippet': 'It’s a case against tightening, not for it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After I published Friday’s column, featuring the Wilcox et al estimates of the long-term damage done by the Great Recession (“hysteresis”, in the econ jargon), several people at the IMF research conference — Christy Romer in particular — told me that they were worried that this stuff might give ammunition to Fed hawks, who will say “See, there isn’t that much slack in the economy, so it’s time to tighten.” Actually, something like this has happened in the UK fiscal debate, so it’s a real issue.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Note On Hysteresis And Monetary Policy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T18:22:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bdd9e5f-b458-51af-9d41-161f6f2b28e5', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bdd9e5f-b458-51af-9d41-161f6f2b28e5'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time since Typhoon Haiyan struck the Philippines, aerial views are showing the extent of the damage in some parts of the country, cut off because of downed communication lines.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/10/aerial-views-of-devastation-in-the-philippines/', 'snippet': 'For the first time since Typhoon Haiyan struck the Philippines, aerial views are showing the extent of the damage in some parts of the country, cut off because of downed communication lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aerial views of areas hard hit by Typhoon Haiyan show the extent of the destruction across the central Philippines, where emergency management officials say they fear as many as 10,000 people died just in the city of Tacloban in one of the most powerful storms recorded. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Aerial Views of Devastation in the Philippines', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Aquino, Benigno S III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T18:27:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/300dd284-b2e0-529a-a5bf-5c29123ed369', 'word_count': 579, 'uri': 'nyt://article/300dd284-b2e0-529a-a5bf-5c29123ed369'}, {'abstract': 'A 16-year-old was in custody after someone approached a 20-year-old man, demanded his winter jacket and when he was refused, returned and opened fire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/nyregion/robbery-attempt-unfolded-before-shooting-at-bryant-park-rink-police-say.html', 'snippet': 'A 16-year-old was in custody after someone approached a 20-year-old man, demanded his winter jacket and when he was refused, returned and opened fire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was a crisp Saturday night, the skaters jumping onto the freshly groomed ice in the oasis of Bryant Park in Midtown, Frank Sinatra and Billie Holiday in the background. Nearby, a wedding party was in full tilt at the Bryant Park Grill; vendors were cleaning up their stalls.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/SKATING1/SKATING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Robbery Attempt Preceded Ice Rink Shooting, Police Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Robbery Attempt Preceded Ice Rink Shooting, Police Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bryant Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ice Skating', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mera, Adonis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Contreras, Javier', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dunton, Cory', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T18:44:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro'