rparts from the United States are expected to start a second round of talks aimed at reaching a landmark trans-Atlantic accord to lower tariffs and harmonize regulation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/business/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-nov-11.html', 'snippet': 'European Union trade negotiators and their counterparts from the United States are expected to start a second round of talks aimed at reaching a landmark trans-Atlantic accord to lower tariffs and harmonize regulation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TRADE TALKS European Union trade negotiators and their counterparts from the United States are expected to start a second round of talks in Brussels on Monday aimed at reaching a landmark trans-Atlantic accord to lower tariffs and harmonize regulations. The talks, scheduled to last until Friday, follow reports of the United States spying on German Chancellor Angela Merkel, which prompted some lawmakers to demand that the talks cover privacy protection. Ms. Merkel has said that privacy should be dealt with separately from the trade talks to help ensure a deal can be reached to spur growth and create jobs. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Nov. 11', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Nov. 11', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-10T22:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_