ber, V. Prem Watsa, the Canadian immigrant success story and chairman of Fairfax Financial Holdings, was huddled in the offices of his Toronto law firm, Torys, trying to salvage the biggest bet of his career.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/blackberry1/blackberry1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'BlackBerry’s Woes Draw Canada’s Contrarian Mogul Into Spotlight', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'BlackBerryu2019s Woes Draw Canadau2019s Contrarian Mogul Into Spotlight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Watsa, V Prem', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackBerry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fairfax Financial Holdings Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:03:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gelles and Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gelles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c63297ff-b6dd-55ad-9600-8eab6b7b8e0d', 'word_count': 1377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c63297ff-b6dd-55ad-9600-8eab6b7b8e0d'}, {'abstract': 'Has Obamacare made it un-P.C. to be concerned by a serious burden on a middle-class family’s well-being?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/opinion/daring-to-complain-about-obamacare.html', 'snippet': 'Has Obamacare made it un-P.C. to be concerned by a serious burden on a middle-class family’s well-being?', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — THE Anthem Blue Cross representative who answered my call told me that there was a silver lining in the cancellation of my individual P.P.O. policy and the $5,400 annual increase that I would have to pay for the Affordable Care Act-compliant option: now if I have Stage 4 cancer or need a sex-change operation, I’d be covered regardless of pre-existing conditions. Never mind that the new provider network would eliminate coverage for my and my son’s long-term doctors and hospitals.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daring to Complain About Obamacare', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Daring to Complain About Obamacare', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gottlieb, Lori', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Anthem Blue Cross', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Facebook Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:10:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lori Gottlieb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lori', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gottlieb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/47519635-0651-5816-bf41-9f8bbbc19d0a', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47519635-0651-5816-bf41-9f8bbbc19d0a'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks’ J. R. Smith missed eight of nine shots, committed four turnovers and spent the fourth quarter on the bench in his regular-season debut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/sports/basketball/smith-returns-but-his-game-does-not.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks’ J. R. Smith missed eight of nine shots, committed four turnovers and spent the fourth quarter on the bench in his regular-season debut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The loudest roar at Madison Square Garden on Sunday was not produced by a Carmelo Anthony jumper or a strong defensive effort by the Knicks. There were few such moments in their embarrassing 120-89 loss to the San Antonio Spurs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Smith Returns, but His Game Does Not', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Smith Returns, but His Game Does Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Nate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, J R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:13:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da0b1d67-dfcd-5f77-960e-047b5173ca2d', 'word_count': 515, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da0b1d67-dfcd-5f77-960e-047b5173ca2d'}, {'abstract': 'Five journalists have died so far this year in Pakistan, and by some accounts, the dangers of reporting in the nation have been intensifying.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/world/asia/danger-persists-for-reporters-in-pakistan-despite-vow-to-protect-them.html', 'snippet': 'Five journalists have died so far this year in Pakistan, and by some accounts, the dangers of reporting in the nation have been intensifying.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — The killers were waiting for Ayub Khattak, a small-town reporter in northwestern Pakistan, as he returned to his house one evening in October. They gunned him down just outside his door.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Danger Persists for Reporters in Pakistan, Despite Vow to Protect Them', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Danger Persists for Reporters in Pakistan, Despite Vow to Protect Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Committee to Protect Journalists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:21:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10180f68-afb4-59e1-8ba8-aea14084100e', 'word_count': 1081, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10180f68-afb4-59e1-8ba8-aea14084100e'}, {'abstract': 'The latest ruling in O’Bannon vs. N.C.A.A., in which athletes’ compensation is at stake, leaves both sides claiming victory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/sports/ncaabasketball/ncaa-dodges-a-bullet-but-change-is-on-the-way.html', 'snippet': 'The latest ruling in O’Bannon vs. N.C.A.A., in which athletes’ compensation is at stake, leaves both sides claiming victory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday, after United States District Judge Claudia Wilken made her latest ruling in O’Bannon v. the N.C.A.A., two men involved in the matter spoke with each other by telephone. One was Ed O’Bannon, a former U.C.L.A. basketball star; the other, Sonny Vaccaro, the sneaker marketing executive turned perpetual N.C.A.A. antagonist.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.C.A.A. Dodges a Bullet, but Change Is on the Way', 'kicker': 'On College Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.C.A.A. Dodges a Bullet, But Change Is on the Way', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vaccaro, Sonny', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Bannon, Ed", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football (College)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:29:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'College Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Greg Bishop', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Greg', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bishop', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e755104-b492-5296-8487-968cf93ac4be', 'word_count': 923, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e755104-b492-5296-8487-968cf93ac4be'}, {'abstract': 'We turn our backs on hundreds of thousands of veterans who have “bad paper” and thus do not qualify as veterans under federal law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/opinion/the-vets-we-reject-and-ignore.html', 'snippet': 'We turn our backs on hundreds of thousands of veterans who have “bad paper” and thus do not qualify as veterans under federal law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TODAY, we honor the nation’s 22 million veterans, including more than 2.5 million who served in Iraq, Afghanistan and other fronts in the war against Al Qaeda. But we are turning our backs on hundreds of thousands of veterans who were discharged “under conditions other than honorable” and so do not qualify as veterans under federal law. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Vets We Reject and Ignore', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Vets We Reject And Ignore', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:33:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/12ed2bf7-d52b-5e7c-9831-67c847caab35', 'word_count': 745, 'uri': 'nyt://article/12ed2bf7-d52b-5e7c-9831-67c847caab35'}, {'abstract': 'Homelessness is on the decline among veterans, but it’s urgent to accelerate our efforts at a time when federal support for housing investments is in jeopardy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/opinion/new-hope-for-homeless-vets.html', 'snippet': 'Homelessness is on the decline among veterans, but it’s urgent to accelerate our efforts at a time when federal support for housing investments is in jeopardy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Each Veterans Day we lament the number of men and women who have ably served in uniform but find themselves lost, broken and homeless once out of it. Their stories are tragic and seemingly endless. For all the well-intentioned talk about meeting the needs of homeless veterans, it remains a slow and difficult process that sometimes fails. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Hope for Homeless Vets', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Hope for Homeless Vets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Veterans Affairs Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:35:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Larry Oaks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Larry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Oaks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7817841c-ac7e-542f-84dc-01d07e2577ab', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7817841c-ac7e-542f-84dc-01d07e2577ab'}, {'abstract': 'The socialist government dispatched soldiers to a major chain of electronic goods stores, ordering prices slashed there and in other shops it has accused of gouging.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/world/americas/venezuelan-soldiers-deployed-to-stores.html', 'snippet': 'The socialist government dispatched soldiers to a major chain of electronic goods stores, ordering prices slashed there and in other shops it has accused of gouging.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CARACAS, Venezuela — The Christmas shopping season has started with a jolt here, with the socialist Venezuelan government dispatching soldiers to “occupy” a major chain of electronic goods stores,