w.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/opinion/krugman-the-plot-against-france.html', 'snippet': 'It’s another case of ideology posing as economic analysis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Friday Standard & Poor’s, the bond-rating agency, downgraded France. The move made headlines, with many reports suggesting that France is in crisis. But markets yawned: French borrowing costs, which are near historic lows, barely budged.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Plot Against France', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Plot Against France', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krugman, Paul', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Standard & Poor's Corp", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rehn, Olli', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit Ratings and Credit Rating Agencies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:55:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/54482974-f340-5450-a0c0-d73ae7844c35', 'word_count': 793, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54482974-f340-5450-a0c0-d73ae7844c35'}, {'abstract': 'Grass-roots activists, especially members of the Tea Party, distrust Gov. Chris Christie’s adherence to the party’s principles and resent his favor within the mainstream media.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/nyregion/conservative-republicans-recoil-at-the-notion-that-christie-is-the-partys-savior.html', 'snippet': 'Grass-roots activists, especially members of the Tea Party, distrust Gov. Chris Christie’s adherence to the party’s principles and resent his favor within the mainstream media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Time magazine splashed Chris Christie’s profile on its latest cover. High-profile Republicans, including the only female Hispanic governor in the nation, are urging him to run for president. MSNBC’s “Morning Joe” program seems to be anointing him the savior of the Republican Party. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/us/jp-CHRISTIE/jp-CHRISTIE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Conservative Republicans Recoil at the Notion That Christie Is the Party’s Savior', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Conservative Republicans Recoil at the Notion That Christie Is the Party’s Savior', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Christie, Christopher J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tea Party Movement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:56:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2c16dcb-877b-5de2-89d4-2a3d020a3963', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2c16dcb-877b-5de2-89d4-2a3d020a3963'}, {'abstract': 'Millions will be eligible for no-premium policies, and others will pay more for new and better coverage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/opinion/high-and-low-premiums-in-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'Millions will be eligible for no-premium policies, and others will pay more for new and better coverage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The debate over the effect the Affordable Care Act will have on individuals and families who buy their own policies has mostly been waged in anecdotes. Supporters of the law point to grateful individuals who were previously unable to get insurance or paid exorbitant premiums but found affordable coverage on the new health insurance exchanges. Critics counter with frustrated people who liked their old policies but will now be forced to buy a more comprehensive policy and pay a higher premium for it. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High and Low Premiums in Health Care', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'High and Low Premiums in Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T01:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/92869404-b808-564f-8014-d5db761df9a3', 'word_count': 517, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92869404-b808-564f-8014-d5db761df9a3'}, {'abstract': 'In their efforts to attract children, television networks are starting to show programs online before they appear on old-fashioned TV.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/business/media/same-time-same-channel-tv-woos-kids-who-cant-wait.html', 'snippet': 'In their efforts to attract children, television networks are starting to show programs online before they appear on old-fashioned TV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Eric Nelson’s 6-year-old daughter, Charlotte, and 10-year-old son, Asa, discover that they cannot rewind or fast-forward a TV show, they are perplexed — and their father is, too. It is hard to explain the limitations of live television to children who have grown up in an on-demand world. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Same Time, Same Channel? TV Woos Kids Who Can’t Wait', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Same Time, Same Channel? TV Woos Kids Who Can’t Wait', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web-Original Programming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nickelodeon', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Disney Channel', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Netflix Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T02:07:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/faa831c3-5cee-5d4c-800f-6f339aaf9fb4', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/faa831c3-5cee-5d4c-800f-6f339aaf9fb4'}, {'abstract': 'The confirmation of two new members to the Federal Election Commission, one of the most dysfunctional agencies in Washington, offers a ray of hope.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/opinion/new-faces-for-a-hobbled-commission.html', 'snippet': 'The confirmation of two new members to the Federal Election Commission, one of the most dysfunctional agencies in Washington, offers a ray of hope.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Senate’s confirmation of two new members to the Federal Election Commission, one of the most dysfunctional and politically riven agencies in Washington, offers a ray of hope. The work of the commission has been stymied for months thanks to a standoff engineered by obstinate Republicans. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Faces for a Hobbled Commission', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Faces for a Hobbled Commission', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Election Commission', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodman, Lee E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ravel, Ann M', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citizens United v Federal Election Commission (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T02:10:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f5efe84-594e-5ad6-86ae-a397170959a7', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f5efe84-594e-5ad6-86ae-a397170959a7'}, {'abstract': 'The CBS newsmagazine issued a rare retraction and apology for its report on an attack on Americans in Libya, saying it was misled by a source.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/business/media/60-minutes-airs-apology-on-benghazi.html', 'snippet': 'The CBS newsmagazine issued a rare retraction and apology for its report on an attack on Americans in Libya, saying it was misled by a source.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lara Logan was scheduled to deliver a report on Sunday’s “60 Minutes” about disabled veterans who climb mountains. Instead, she appeared in front of the newsmagazine’s trademark black backdrop and issued an apology.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘60 Minutes’ Airs Apology on Benghazi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘60 Minutes’ Airs Apology On Benghazi Reporting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Apologies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stelter, Brian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Benghazi Attack (2012)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Benghazi (Libya)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davies, Dylan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Logan, Lara', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS News', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T02:11:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Stelter and Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stelter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37f6e1f1-3e6e-538f-bd7a-bd30c4b9fbfe', 'word_count': 1284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37f6e1f1-3e6e-538f-bd7a-bd30c4b9fbfe'}, {'abstract