 the South China Sea.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/china-offers-relatively-modest-aid-for-typhoon-victims/', 'snippet': 'China extended far more generous assistance to the Philippines after a storm in 2011, before relations between the countries deteriorated over territorial disputes in the South China Sea.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As international aid pours into the Philippines for victims of Typhoon Haiyan, China has offered $100,000 in cash, a figure that seems modest compared with its other recent contributions for humanitarian relief abroad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Offers Relatively Modest Aid for Typhoon Victims', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ACEH PROVINCE (INDONESIA)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T11:15:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane Perlez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Perlez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb0a80c2-6741-5495-a223-0a311ecb8dbe', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb0a80c2-6741-5495-a223-0a311ecb8dbe'}, {'abstract': 'A glimpse inside the life of the former Rutgers basketball coach who was fired for mistreating his players.', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/behind-the-cover-story-jonathan-mahler-on-mike-rice-rehabilitation-and-aggression-in-college-sports/', 'snippet': 'A glimpse inside the life of the former Rutgers basketball coach who was fired for mistreating his players.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jonathan Mahler, a contributing writer for the magazine, wrote this week’s cover story about Mike Rice, the Rutgers basketball coach who was fired for mistreating his players. Mahler last wrote for the magazine about Oakland’s Occupy movement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/magazine/02floor-mahler195/02floor-mahler195-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 259, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/magazine/02floor-mahler195/02floor-mahler195-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 259, 'width': 190, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/magazine/02floor-mahler195/02floor-mahler195-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2012/01/02/magazine/02floor-mahler195/02floor-mahler195-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2012/01/02/magazine/02floor-mahler195/02floor-mahler195-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Cover Story: Jonathan Mahler on Mike Rice, Rehabilitation and Aggression in College Sports', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Mike Jr (1969- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T11:19:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Nolan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nolan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29b44a9a-b33c-5061-9160-2f57204dab56', 'word_count': 866, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29b44a9a-b33c-5061-9160-2f57204dab56'}, {'abstract': 'As this Retro Report recalls, 50 million people in the United States and Canada lost power on Aug. 14, 2003. But steps are being taken to reduce the risk of a future large-scale collapse.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/booming/the-blackout-that-exposed-the-flaws-in-the-grid.html', 'snippet': 'As this Retro Report recalls, 50 million people in the United States and Canada lost power on Aug. 14, 2003. But steps are being taken to reduce the risk of a future large-scale collapse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a late Thursday afternoon in the summer of 2003, everything turned off. As this week’s Retro Report video illustrates, in the span of a few minutes, the biggest power outage in United States history brought swaths of the Northeast, the Midwest and Canada to a standstill. Around 50 million people were left without power. In the days and weeks that followed, reporters and investigators raced to pinpoint the source of the outage, while larger questions swirled about the stability of the power grid in the 21st century. Here, a Times reporter who covers energy technology reflects on that day and the changes that resulted. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Blackout That Exposed the Flaws in the Grid', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Failures and Blackouts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FirstEnergy Corporation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North American Electric Reliability Corp', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Northeastern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ohio', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T11:23:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5638dad3-e5a7-5363-b85d-dec64f81a0a1', 'word_count': 1345, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5638dad3-e5a7-5363-b85d-dec64f81a0a1'}, {'abstract': 'Start-ups are gathering “hyperlocal” data from all over and analyzing it in order to project economic trends from seemingly unconnected bits of information.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/daily-report-hoping-to-see-big-pictures-in-a-blizzard-of-tiny-data-points/', 'snippet': 'Start-ups are gathering “hyperlocal” data from all over and analyzing it in order to project economic trends from seemingly unconnected bits of information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Soloff is recruiting an army of “hyperdata” collectors, Quentin Hardy reports.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'r