re are not new frauds, just new avenues for deception. As the financial world has evolved into a high-speed race to trade assets while investment strategies are kept secret, both regulators and investors face the challenge of finding the fine line between permissible trading and manipulation aimed at generating unfair profits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 467, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 467}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 797, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1368, 'width': 1758, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12-WHITECOLLAR/12-WHITECOLLAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Markets Evolve, as Does Financial Fraud', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Commodities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'High-Frequency and Flash Trading', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Securities and Commodities Violations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Commodity Futures Trading Commission', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Securities and Exchange Commission', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T12:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter J. Henning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Henning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c37dd4f-ba6f-57c8-8052-cbb6464b6189', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c37dd4f-ba6f-57c8-8052-cbb6464b6189'}, {'abstract': 'Destroyed buildings lined every road of Tacloban, the city hit hardest by the typhoon, and many streets were still so clogged with debris that they were barely discernible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/world/asia/philippines-storm-surge-leaves-scenes-of-devastation.html', 'snippet': 'Destroyed buildings lined every road of Tacloban, the city hit hardest by the typhoon, and many streets were still so clogged with debris that they were barely discernible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TACLOBAN, the Philippines — Decomposing bodies still lie along the roads, like a corpse in a pink, short-sleeve shirt and blue shorts facedown in a black, muddy puddle 100 yards from the airport. Just down the road is a church that was supposed to be an evacuation center but is littered with the bodies of those who drowned inside.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Struggle for Survival in Philippine City Shattered by Typhoon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Struggle for Survival in Land Shattered by Typhoon', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tacloban (Philippines)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T12:04:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c394ce4-6041-5f80-96ae-76161152d662', 'word_count': 1378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c394ce4-6041-5f80-96ae-76161152d662'}, {'abstract': 'A show at the Victoria & Albert Museum focuses on Chinese Painting while the Tate Britain showcases the work of Vija Celmins.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/snapshots-from-the-fall-art-season-in-london/', 'snippet': 'A show at the Victoria & Albert Museum focuses on Chinese Painting while the Tate Britain showcases the work of Vija Celmins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The tiny figures are painted in brushstrokes thinner than a hair — a bride dressed in festive red, merchants with their wares, would-be bureaucrats studying for a state exam in a state pavilion — set against a bay, a stand of trees. They are part of “Prosperous Suzhou,” a vast panorama of urban life painted in 1759 by Xu Yang, one of the many works on view in “Masterpieces of Chinese Painting 700-1900” at the Victoria & Albert Museum here through Jan. 19.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Snapshots From the Fall Art Season in London', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Celmins, Vija', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tate Britain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T12:18:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9d7b81c-0e21-59ae-9286-058396a5e7d4', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9d7b81c-0e21-59ae-9286-058396a5e7d4'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street has recognized the value of Twitter as an investing tool, but a question remains about how best to sift half a billion daily messages to gain an edge on the market.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/separating-the-market-moving-tweets-from-the-chaff/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street has recognized the value of Twitter as an investing tool, but a question remains about how best to sift half a billion daily messages to gain an edge on the market.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carl C. Icahn wields it as a megaphone. Traders and analysts use it to chat publicly about stocks. Eyewitnesses employ it to post messages about news events before they make headlines.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 377, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 377}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1286, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/nyregion/DBPIX-SOCIAL/DBPIX-SOCIAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Separating the Market-Moving Tweets From the Chaff', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Separating the Market-Moving Tweets From the Chaff', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Stock Exchange', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T12:29:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df753d1e-bef3-53fd-ab49-4ed5612d4459', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df753d1e-bef3-53fd-ab49-4ed5612d4459'}, {'abstract': 'India’s politicians ignore women’s issues in electoral campaigns because they do not see women as a voting block.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/indias-politicians-ignore-women-voters-in-election-campaigns/', 'snippet': 'India’s politicians ignore women’s issues in electoral campaigns because they do not see women as a voting block.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the eve of Diwali, I was walking around the inner circle of Connaught Place, a well-known shopping center in Delhi, with a journalist friend. The business arcade teemed with people. Suddenly loud, belligerent voices tore through the festive air. We stopped.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013