ed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c79f9bc7-7e78-59f0-aacb-8226d949cc53', 'word_count': 231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c79f9bc7-7e78-59f0-aacb-8226d949cc53'}, {'abstract': 'The author, a consultant at a behavioral economics firm, discusses studies that show how minor changes to work practices can have effects on honesty.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/honesty-that-benefits-all/', 'snippet': 'The author, a consultant at a behavioral economics firm, discusses studies that show how minor changes to work practices can have effects on honesty.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It seems that headlines too often highlight the bad deeds of players in financial markets. There are insider trading scandals. Traders collude on interest rate manipulation. Executives backdate options. We often hear the excuse, “Everyone else was doing it, so I didn’t think it was wrong.”', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honesty That Benefits All', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honesty That Benefits All', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bonuses', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T15:55:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Doug Steiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Doug', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/896e5911-37e5-5cd8-990f-7951f956b24c', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/896e5911-37e5-5cd8-990f-7951f956b24c'}, {'abstract': 'How to dominate a trade show. Twenty apps for small businesses. Do you check up on workers who take sick days to see if they really are sick?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/today-in-small-business-now-accepting-bitcoin/', 'snippet': 'How to dominate a trade show. Twenty apps for small businesses. Do you check up on workers who take sick days to see if they really are sick?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: Now Accepting Bitcoin', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T16:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gene Marks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Marks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff11e6aa-cb21-5fa7-a182-0ef59dbab0b2', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff11e6aa-cb21-5fa7-a182-0ef59dbab0b2'}, {'abstract': 'Can Francis-era Catholicism move beyond its post-Vatican II internal conflicts?', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/the-francis-era-synthesis-or-civil-war/', 'snippet': 'Can Francis-era Catholicism move beyond its post-Vatican II internal conflicts?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My colleague Laurie Goodstein had a good piece yesterday about conservative Catholics who feel unsettled by\xa0Pope Francis’s approach to the papal office, which seems like a good hook for returning, a month later, to my own take on the Francis experiment. In that piece, I talked a bit about the idea of a “religious center” —\xa0meaning a way of being religious that’s simultaneously modern and devout, engaged with contemporary realities but still rooted in a recognizably Biblical worldview – and argued that since the 1960s it’s become harder for believers of any traditional faith to claim that kind of ground. The tendency, instead, has been toward either toward a kind of separatism and retrenchment on the one hand, or accommodation and then often dissolution on the other – and this has been true for Jews and Protestants as it has been for Catholics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Francis Era: Synthesis or Civil War?', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'John Paul II', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T16:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82529546-c102-5bd5-a734-a811432e3d74', 'word_count': 1875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82529546-c102-5bd5-a734-a811432e3d74'}, {'abstract': 'Pushkar Fair is a five-day camel and livestock fair held in the town of Pushkar, Rajasthan, every year.', 'we