//boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/introducing-capitalizing-on-china/', 'snippet': 'When the owner first traveled to China, she was told the following by an American official whose sole job was to help American companies do business in China: “You don’t want to be here or do business here. You won’t survive.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I started Auction Systems Auctioneers and Appraisers almost 18 years ago, my vision wasn’t to own a multinational company. And I certainly did not imagine that I would one day be dividing my time between China and the United States, routinely spending three weeks abroad and then five weeks back home.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Introducing: Capitalizing on China', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Auction Systems Auctioneers and Appraisers Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T18:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Weidenhamer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weidenhamer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/619564ce-8657-50dc-9a55-ca65d2db1f21', 'word_count': 741, 'uri': 'nyt://article/619564ce-8657-50dc-9a55-ca65d2db1f21'}, {'abstract': 'A pie that is sweet with spices but not too sugary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/health/pumpkin-pie.html', 'snippet': 'A pie that is sweet with spices but not too sugary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of my all-time favorite pies, this one is sweet with spices but not very sugary. Because of the small amount of molasses, this is darker than classic pumpkin pie. Make it with fresh roasted pumpkin, or use canned pumpkin. I am finding small “pie pumpkins” in supermarkets, and they’re perfect for the job.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1361, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12recipehealth/12recipehealth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pumpkin Pie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name