Michael Kassan, will present daily radio reports in New York on advertising and media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'American Advertising Federation, Washington, renamed its annual Addy Awards competition as the American Advertising Awards. James Edmund Datri, president and chief executive of the organization, said he hoped that local chapters would still call the awards that are presented to winners Addy awards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Accounts and People of Note in the Advertising Industry', 'kicker': 'Webdenda', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Relations and Publicity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T18:32:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e6a3736-21f7-5c5e-b945-2c8c2e369205', 'word_count': 1126, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e6a3736-21f7-5c5e-b945-2c8c2e369205'}, {'abstract': 'Reactions made it onto social media sites as fans, friends and musicians woke to news of the shooting deaths of members of the band Yellow Dogs.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/fans-and-friends-react-to-murder-suicide-involving-an-iranian-band/', 'snippet': 'Reactions made it onto social media sites as fans, friends and musicians woke to news of the shooting deaths of members of the band Yellow Dogs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Early Monday, a rock musician in East Williamsburg, Brooklyn, killed three other musicians before taking his own life, the police and neighbors said. Two of the victims were members of a rock band of Iranian expatriates called the Yellow Dogs. The gunman was another Iranian-American musician, the police said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fans and Friends React to the Shooting Deaths of Iranian Band Members', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T18:34:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f2d97b6-a2de-53e8-b05c-50d39dacb9ac', 'word_count': 117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f2d97b6-a2de-53e8-b05c-50d39dacb9ac'}, {'abstract': 'Countless prosecutors, regulators and congressional aides swap their government résumés for seven-figure salaries at law firms and lobbying shops.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/slowing-the-revolving-door-between-public-and-private-jobs/', 'snippet': 'Countless prosecutors, regulators and congressional aides swap their government résumés for seven-figure salaries at law firms and lobbying shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has been called “corrupt,” “corrosive” and “hazardous to our health.” Yet, Washington’s revolving door spins on.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/dealbook/12REVOLVING2_SPAN/12-REVOLVING2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/