ion and Unicef announced last week.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '20 Million in Mideast to Get Polio Vaccine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prevention: 20 Million in Mideast To Get Polio Vaccine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNeil, Donald G Jr', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poliomyelitis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Epidemics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vaccination and Immunization', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T19:19:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Donald G. McNeil Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donald', 'middlename': 'G.', 'lastname': 'McNeil', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f48e7b2-7501-5a1b-91e4-e0d655942bb5', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f48e7b2-7501-5a1b-91e4-e0d655942bb5'}, {'abstract': 'The story of the soldiers from Maine who beat Robert E. Lee in Virginia.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/fighting-across-the-rappahannock/', 'snippet': 'The story of the soldiers from Maine who beat Robert E. Lee in Virginia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Charlie Clark basked in the warmth of a budding romance on a cold autumn day in 1863. His friend and fellow lieutenant in the Union Army, Solomon Russell, had fallen for a Southern belle in war-torn Virginia. On the morning of Nov. 7, 1863, the officers left their camp in Warrenton to call upon her. They made their way to the home of the widow Rosina Dixon and found the focus of Russell’s desire: the 15-year-old Anna. Whatever words passed between the Yankee officer and rebel maiden went unrecorded, though Clark referenced the encounter years later in his reminiscences, noting that Russell “was deeply in love” with Anna.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fighting Across the Rappahannock', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T19:20:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d72e70f3-41d7-5b7d-a7f1-374c665e1b85', 'word_count': 1696, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d72e70f3-41d7-5b7d-a7f1-374c665e1b85'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday was a bad day for Fantex, the fledgling company promoting initial public offerings of National Football League stars, as its first two prospects were sidelined.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/injuries-for-2-n-f-l-players-in-public-offering-deal/', 'snippet': 'Sunday was a bad day for Fantex, the fledgling company promoting initial public offerings of National Football League stars, as its first two prospects were sidelined.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sunday was a bad day for Fantex, the fledgling company promoting initial public offerings of National Football League stars.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/subJockstock/subJockstock-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'im