s of the typhoon in the Philippines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Tuesday, 5:44 p.m. | As the full scale of the devastation wrought across the islands of the Philippines over the weekend by Typhoon Haiyan came into fuller view on Monday, governments around the world have pledged aid to the victims. The Pentagon has dispatched an advance team of 90 marines and sailors, and U.S.A.I.D. has pledged emergency shelter and hygiene materials and 55 tons of food. The American Embassy in Manila has donated $100,000 for water and sanitation assistance.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Help Philippines Typhoon Victims', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T20:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liam Stack and Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b388799-21f7-562b-9c51-bed7083abb2e', 'word_count': 907, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b388799-21f7-562b-9c51-bed7083abb2e'}, {'abstract': 'The big questions are about John Chen holding the top two jobs at the troubled smartphone maker and his commuting from California.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/blackberrys-turnaround-starts-all-thumbs/', 'snippet': 'The big questions are about John Chen holding the top two jobs at the troubled smartphone maker and his commuting from California.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BlackBerry’s turnaround is starting out all thumbs. The $85 million worth of stock handed to the company’s new boss, John Chen, over five years at least provides the right incentives. But the struggling Canadian company surely needs more attention than one man doing both top jobs, especially if he’s commuting from California.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'BlackBerry’s Turnaround Starts All Thumbs', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executive Compensation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smartphones', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chen, John S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BlackBerry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T20:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Beales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d2f9564-7aec-5aa8-9511-aeb47c7f20b6', 'word_count': 398, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d2f9564-7aec-5aa8-9511-aeb47c7f20b6'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists have identified an ancient species of platypus, its diet and habitat, all from the discovery of a single fossil tooth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/science/single-tooth-tells-of-long-extinct-platypus.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists have identified an ancient species of platypus, its diet and habitat, all from the discovery of a single fossil tooth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Based on the discovery of a single tooth, researchers say they have identified an ancient species of giant platypus. The finding provides new clues about the lineage of the modern platypus. “The fossil record is very, very patchy for the platypus, and these are a unique group of mammals,” said the lead researcher, Rebecca Pian, a vertebrate paleontologist at Columbia University and the American Museum of Natural History. Unlike most mammals, they lay eggs instead of giving birth to live offspring; their snouts are covered with electroreceptors that can detect underwater prey; and the male has a venomous spur on its hind feet.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12platypus/12platypus-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Single Tooth Tells of Long-Extinct Platypus', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evolution: Single Tooth Tells of Long-Extinct Platypus', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paleontology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mammals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Endangered and Extinct Species', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T20:28:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sindya N. Bhanoo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sindya', 'middlename': 'N.', 'lastname': 'Bhanoo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15a4cd73-a591-5707-a679-f86f4b0da20b', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15a4cd73-a591-5707-a679-f86f4b0da20b'}, {'abstract': 'For big-name chefs tending to culinary empires large and small, the urge (and often pressure) to expand from a single, signature restaurant can be irresistible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/dining/when-one-kitchen-isnt-enough.html', 'snippet': 'For big-name chefs tending to culinary empires large and small, the urge (and often pressure) to expand from a single, signature restaurant can be irresistible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAMBRIDGE, Mass. — When Tony Maws designed the open kitchen at Craigie on Main, the celebrated restaurant he opened here five years ago, he positioned his workstation to serve as a kind of welcome mat. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'capti