'nyt://slideshow/db0057cf-d947-5dc7-8ac5-ada485264238', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/db0057cf-d947-5dc7-8ac5-ada485264238'}, {'abstract': 'The song “I’m Old Fashioned” wasn’t about the cocktail, but it’s a standard worth revisiting (and a good excuse to marvel at Fred Astaire’s singing voice).', 'web_url': 'https://6thfloor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/the-old-fashioned-in-song-and-dance/', 'snippet': 'The song “I’m Old Fashioned” wasn’t about the cocktail, but it’s a standard worth revisiting (and a good excuse to marvel at Fred Astaire’s singing voice).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 12:15 p.m. | My Drink column this month was partially inspired by the song “I’m Old Fashioned,” by Jerome Kern and Johnny Mercer. It debuted in the 1942 romantic comedy “You Were Never Lovelier,” in a total charmer of a song-and-dance routine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Old-Fashioned, in Song and Dance', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T20:53:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d78d597-522d-51ea-8e37-b5fc3086cabf', 'word_count': 260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d78d597-522d-51ea-8e37-b5fc3086cabf'}, {'abstract': 'As the prospect of a nuclear deal with Iran becomes more real, Secretary of State John Kerry is having to fend off those who want to pre-empt it — like Israel and Iran hawks in Congress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/world/middleeast/so-close-on-iran-kerry-defends-continued-talks.html', 'snippet': 'As the prospect of a nuclear deal with Iran becomes more real, Secretary of State John Kerry is having to fend off those who want to pre-empt it — like Israel and Iran hawks in Congress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABU DHABI, United Arab Emirates — Secretary of State John Kerry came up a few disputed words short of closing a landmark nuclear deal with Iran on Sunday in Geneva. Now he is defending the diplomacy that led to that near miss against a rising chorus of critics at home and abroad.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuclear_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuclear_cnd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuclear_cnd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuclear_cnd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1457, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuclear_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuclear_cnd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/world/middleeast/11nuclear_cnd/11nuc