mplex, and it often seems as if things are far beyond our control. It leads to a feeling of anxiety. Plus, we’re so busy making money, trying to make ends meet, that it seems all but impossible to manage it in any meaningful way. Who has the time to track a monthly budget?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/business/111113bucks-carl-sketch/111113bucks-carl-sketch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tidying Up Your Financial Life', 'kicker': 'The Sketch Guy', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T21:03:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carl Richards', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carl', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richards', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/990f0a9b-c151-5234-b226-5216438a3d72', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/990f0a9b-c151-5234-b226-5216438a3d72'}, {'abstract': 'In “Bully Pulpit,” Doris Kearns Goodwin examines Theodore Roosevelt’s friendship-turned-rivalry with William Howard Taft and his way of harnessing the press to challenge monopolies and advance his vision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/books/bully-pulpit-doris-kearns-goodwins-book-on-roosevelt.html', 'snippet': 'In “Bully Pulpit,” Doris Kearns Goodwin examines Theodore Roosevelt’s friendship-turned-rivalry with William Howard Taft and his way of harnessing the press to challenge monopolies and advance his vision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The interplay between personality and politics, temperament and leadership is one of the key themes animating Doris Kearns Goodwin’s telling books about Abraham Lincoln (“Team of Rivals”), Franklin D. Roosevelt (“No Ordinary Time”) and Lyndon B. Johnson (“Lyndon Johnson and the American Dream”). The same is true of her sprawling new book, “The Bully Pulpit,” which gives us revealing portraits of Theodore Roosevelt and his close friend, handpicked successor and eventual bitter rival, William Howard Taft.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge'