bstract': 'A survey by the writers’ organization PEN American Center has found that a large majority of its members are deeply concerned about the extent of government surveillance of email and phone records.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/books/pen-american-center-survey-finds-caution-among-members.html', 'snippet': 'A survey by the writers’ organization PEN American Center has found that a large majority of its members are deeply concerned about the extent of government surveillance of email and phone records.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A survey by the writers’ organization PEN American Center has found that a large majority of its members are deeply concerned about recent revelations regarding the extent of government surveillance of email and phone records, with more than a quarter saying that they have avoided, or are seriously considering avoiding, controversial topics in their work.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Surveillance Leaves Writers Wary', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Surveillance Leaves Writers Wary', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Noam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'PEN American Center', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:14:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bea49fb-9602-5b6d-b530-d80b0a9d326d', 'word_count': 418, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bea49fb-9602-5b6d-b530-d80b0a9d326d'}, {'abstract': 'An ambitious program at Symphony Space on Friday looked at the day before John F. Kennedy’s assassination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/arts/music/november-21-1963-the-day-before-at-symphony-space.html', 'snippet': 'An ambitious program at Symphony Space on Friday looked at the day before John F. Kennedy’s assassination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next to birthdays of prominent public figures, nothing engenders mass reflection and artistic endeavor as readily as big, round anniversaries of historical milestones. We’re just 10 days away from one such date: Nov. 22, the 50th anniversary of President John F. Kennedy’s assassination in Dallas, which after half a century continues to take a dramatic toll on the collective American psyche.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 896}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1372, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12DAY/12DAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Quiet Before the Shots', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Quiet Before The Shots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Symphony Space', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:17:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/19f9a7bf-f2da-503d-aeca-c837651c86da', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19f9a7bf-f2da-503d-aeca-c837651c86da'}, {'abstract': 'The filmmaker Ken Burns is starting a web project to encourage Americans to recite the Gettysburg Address.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/the-gettysburg-address-as-recited-by-colbert-and-you/', 'snippet': 'The filmmaker Ken Burns is starting a web project to encourage Americans to recite the Gettysburg Address.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The filmmaker Ken Burns has found one way to bring together Republicans and Democrats in this politically divided time: Ask them to recite the Gettysburg Address, which Abraham Lincoln delivered on Nov. 19, 1863, at the dedication of the cemetery at the Civil War battlefield. The website Learn the Address features videos of notable names reciting the speech, including all the living American presidents and dozens of celebrities like Taylor Swift, Usher, Steven Spielberg, Uma Thurman, Shane Victorino and Bill O’Reilly. Other well-known reciters include Stephen Colbert and Gabrielle Giffords.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gettysburg Address, as Recited by Colbert and You', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Ken', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:20:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Jensen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jensen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94cb3cc7-b563-5447-973d-d7ed68d9c8f0', 'word_count': 275, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94cb3cc7-b563-5447-973d-d7ed68d9c8f0'}, {'abstract': 'Arvo Pärt’s mystical luminosity was paired with Sibelius and Mozart at the White Light Festival on Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/arts/music/arvo-part-works-in-lincoln-center-white-light-festival.html', 'snippet': 'Arvo Pärt’s mystical luminosity was paired with Sibelius and Mozart at the White Light Festival on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If any artist is emblematic of the spirit manifest in Lincoln Center’s White Light Festival, it might be Arvo Pärt. An Estonian composer based in Berlin for much of his career, Mr. Pärt achieved wide renown in the mid-1980s through a series of recordings on the German label ECM. His rise to prominence was also abetted by the conductor Neeme Järvi, a countryman whose continued advocacy was evident in a festival concert by the Estonian National Symphony Orchestra and the Estonian Philharmonic Chamber Choir at Avery Fisher Hall on Sunday evening.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Estonian Master, Through Lens of Compatriots', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Estonian Master, Through Lens of Compatriots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Part, Arvo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White Light Festival (Lincoln Center, NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Estonian Philharmonic Chamber Choir', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/96017550-572c-50ee-a008-c9e440807471', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96017550-572c-50ee-a008-c9e440807471'}, {'abstract': 'Recent\xa0developments\xa0in health and\xa0science\xa0news. This week: India hopes to join the exclusive Mars club, and a newly discovered dinosaur from the T. rex family.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/science/watch-out-for-falling-space-junk-and-asteroids.html', 'snippet': 'Recent\xa0developments\xa0in health and\xa0science\xa0news. This week: India hopes to join the exclusive Mars club, and a newly discovered dinosaur from the T. rex family.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fiery chunks of a European satellite fell from the sky, the latest in a parade of what scientists worryingly call “uncontrolled entries.” And new research showed that asteroids like the one that exploded over Russia in February will probably hit Earth more often than previously expected. All in all, not a bad week to begin a long journey to Mars.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/science/12WEEK_SPAN/12WEEK-SUB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Watch Out for Falling Space Junk and Asteroids', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quenqua, Douglas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Asteroids', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dinosaurs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelyabinsk (Russia)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fossils', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:21:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Douglas Quenqua', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Douglas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Quenqua', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Summary', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d9c204b-8d50-580a-8d0d-8db7fe890f69', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d9c204b-8d50-580a-8d0d-8db7fe890f69'}, {'abstract': 'Letter to the editor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/science/the-universes-end.html', 'snippet': 'Letter to the editor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO THE EDITOR:', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Universe’s End', 'kicker': 'Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Universe’s End', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Higgs Boson', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:25:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2c6386c-931b-52ee-b9aa-d26b9fc273a8', 'word_count': 90, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2c6386c-931b-52ee-b9aa-d26b9fc273a8'}, {'abstract': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/weekend-gun-report-november-8-10-2013/', 'snippet': 'A weekend in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Texas company has made the world’s first metal gun using a 3D printer. The fully functioning, semi-automatic .45-caliber pistol made by Austin-based Solid Concepts is modeled on on the Browning 1911 firearm. It’s been safely fired 50 times, and as for accuracy, the gun was able to strike a target bull’s-eye at more than 30 yards.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Weekend Gun Report: November 8-10, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:26:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/07619a57-3e5a-517c-9aba-b5e29e77ca1a', 'word_count': 2541, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07619a57-3e5a-517c-9aba-b5e29e77ca1a'}, {'abstract': 'American Ballet Theater closed its fall season on Sunday; now it remains to be seen which dancers will make advances in the spring season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/arts/dance/a-fall-season-of-grand-revival-for-american-ballet-theater.html', 'snippet': 'American Ballet Theater closed its fall season on Sunday; now it remains to be seen which dancers will make advances in the spring season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No ballet ensemble has a soul more divided than that of American Ballet Theater. Some people think it’s one of the world’s greatest companies; others think it’s not really a company at all. Both arguments make sense, and they largely correspond to which side of Lincoln Center Plaza the troupe is playing. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/BALLET1/BALLET1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Weeks That Kindle Hope', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Two Weeks That Kindle Hope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:33:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alastair Macaulay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alastair', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macaulay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ea132e8-4a49-57e2-bff7-ec6a2c3c9f6a', 'word_count': 1021, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ea132e8-4a49-57e2-bff7-ec6a2c3c9f6a'}, {'abstract': 'Jimmie Johnson bolsters his Nascar Sprint Cup series points lead, and Marc Márquez becomes the youngest rider to win a MotoGP title.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/automobiles/monday-motorsports-jimmie-johnson-eyes-sixth-title.html', 'snippet': 'Jimmie Johnson bolsters his Nascar Sprint Cup series points lead, and Marc Márquez becomes the youngest rider to win a MotoGP title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kevin Harvick won the battle, but Jimmie Johnson may have won the war on Sunday in Nascar’s Sprint Cup Series race at Phoenix International Raceway. On the white flag lap, Harvick passed the leader, Carl Edwards, who was running out of fuel, and then held on for the final lap to take the checkered flag. Kasey Kahne came in second. Johnson was third, earning a decisive number of points in the quest for his sixth Sprint Cup season title.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/automobiles/12MOTORSPORTS-image/12MOTORSPORTS-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'