r': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kahne, Kasey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dillon, Austin', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hornish, Sam Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Raikkonen, Kimi', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Jimmie', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenseth, Matt', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Force, John', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harvick, Kevin', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:35:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jerry Garrett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jerry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garrett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e7c19cf5-0f39-5ca9-96cb-ef9bd284d9c2', 'word_count': 810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e7c19cf5-0f39-5ca9-96cb-ef9bd284d9c2'}, {'abstract': 'From the Philippines to Haiti, recovering from disasters becomes the norm, not the exception.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/from-the-philippines-to-haiti-disaster-recovery-is-a-way-of-life/', 'snippet': 'From the Philippines to Haiti, recovering from disasters becomes the norm, not the exception.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For many millions of people living in the planet’s poorest, most populous places, a state of recovery from what used to be called “natural” disasters has become the norm, not some exceptional circumstance. The central Philippines, now reeling from the impact of Typhoon Haiyan, a super storm if ever there was one, are just the latest place in which huge human losses follow a disaster that, in a rich country, would almost assuredly mainly exact a financial toll. See Keith Bradsher’s wrenching reports here and here for details on the damage. And the immediate search and rescue efforts are just a warmup for years of relocation, recovery and rebuilding.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/asia/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH/20131111PHILIPPINES-slide-VUFH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Philippines to Haiti, Disaster Recovery is a Way of Life', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Earthquakes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'MANILA (PHILIPPINES)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Population', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tidal Waves and Tsunamis', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Bopha (2012)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoons', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sumatra (Indonesia)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:36:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1737be1-674d-5a58-b64c-d8456113c68e', 'word_count': 546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1737be1-674d-5a58-b64c-d8456113c68e'}, {'abstract': '“Queen of the Night” will relaunch the Diamond Horseshoe in the basement of the Paramount Hotel.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/supper-club-to-reopen-with-carnal-take-on-magic-flute/', 'snippet': '“Queen of the Night” will relaunch the Diamond Horseshoe in the basement of the Paramount Hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A famed theater-district supper club will reopen on New Year’s Eve with a high-tech “carnal” reimagining of “The Magic Flute” that aims to blur the lines between the audience and the performers. “Queen of the Night” is created by Randy Weiner, a founder of The Box burlesque space on the Lower East Side and a producer of the smash success “Sleep No More” downtown. Like “The Donkey Show,” the disco adaptation of “A Midsummer Night’s Dream” that Mr. Weiner created with his wife, Diane Paulus, in 1999, “Queen of the Night” puts the audience into the middle of a reconfigured classic theater piece – in this case Mozart’s opera. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Supper Club to Reopen With ‘Carnal’ Take on ‘Magic Flute’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paulus, Diane', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosen, Aby J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weiner, Randy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Box (Manhattan, NY, Nightclub)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Diamond Horseshoe (Manhattan, NY, Nightclub)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:38:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08b0c383-559b-57e5-9f3f-0c40badf0ddf', 'word_count': 378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08b0c383-559b-57e5-9f3f-0c40badf0ddf'}, {'abstract': 'The Renaissance wunderkammer, or cabinet of curiosities — a personal collection of fabulous, rare, sometimes grotesque relics — inspires tableaus of the season’s most opulent baubles and fanciful curios.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/17/t-magazine/objects-world-of-wonder.html', 'snippet': 'The Renaissance wunderkammer, or cabinet of curiosities — a personal collection of fabulous, rare, sometimes grotesque relics — inspires tableaus of the season’s most opulent baubles and fanciful curios.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Renaissance wunderkammer, or cabinet of curiosities — a personal collection of fabulous, rare, sometimes grotesque relics — inspires tableaus of the season’s most opulent baubles and fanciful curios.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'T WINTER TRAVEL', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:40:51+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/4b1cf7f7-f194-56d9-8ac4-d329c929e5ee', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/4b1cf7f7-f194-56d9-8ac4-d329c929e5ee'}, {'abstract': 'German authorities are reacting to calls to release information quickly about paintings, many looted, that were discovered in Munich.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/arts/design/germany-to-form-task-force-on-looted-art.html', 'snippet': 'German authorities are reacting to calls to release information quickly about paintings, many looted, that were discovered in Munich.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After an avalanche of criticism at home and abroad, the German government announced late Monday it will establish a task force to investigate, “as quickly and as transparently as possible,” the provenance of a cache of more than 1,400 artworks that are suspected of being traded or looted during the Nazis’ reign and that are now in the hands of authorities in Bavaria. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 370, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 370}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 631, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1263, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/arts/12GERMANART/12GERMANART-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Germany to Form Task Force on Looted Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Germany to Form Task Force on Looted Art', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'va