 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/lennons-school-detention-sheets-head-to-auction/', 'snippet': 'Detention papers from John Lennon’s school days are set to be auctioned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Lennon always described himself as a cut-up during his school years, an authority-baiting revolutionary in the making. But even keeping in mind the wisecracking assertiveness he cultivated during the Beatles years, and beyond, you always suspected that he was exaggerating.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lennon’s School Detention Sheets Head to Auction', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lennon, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:54:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cc5959f-008a-5f50-9589-940380b09133', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cc5959f-008a-5f50-9589-940380b09133'}, {'abstract': 'Curators from the Crystal Bridges Museum in Arkansas are scouring the country for a comprehensive survey of contemporary American art.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/crystal-bridges-museum-conducts-ambitious-survey-of-contemporary-american-art/', 'snippet': 'Curators from the Crystal Bridges Museum in Arkansas are scouring the country for a comprehensive survey of contemporary American art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art, the institution founded in Bentonville, Ark., by Alice L. Walton, the Walmart heiress, is only two years old. But it has embarked on a mission that even more established museums might fear to take on: a comprehensive survey of contemporary American art, formed by visits to hundreds of artists’ studios, large and small, successful and almost unheard-of, across the country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/11/arts/11artsbeat-crystal/11artsbeat-crystal-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crystal Bridges Museum Conducts Ambitious Survey of Contemporary American Art', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd91ee8-2feb-5580-89f5-1e76fc7c0cc6', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd91ee8-2feb-5580-89f5-1e76fc7c0cc6'}, {'abstract': 'Rachel Shelasky is the president and founder of Hollywood Fourth, a promotional apparel company.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/business/for-an-upgrade-skip-the-vegetarian-meal.html', 'snippet': 'Rachel Shelasky is the president and founder of Hollywood Fourth, a promotional apparel company.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’M an entrepreneur in the promotional clothing and products business. That entrepreneurial spirit is in my blood.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/business/12flier/12flier-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For an Upgrade, Skip the Vegetarian Meal', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For an Upgrade, Skip the Vegetarian Meal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:55:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Shelasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shelasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc709a45-c8f0-512e-afc1-780425095a80', 'word_count': 618, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc709a45-c8f0-512e-afc1-780425095a80'}, {'abstract': 'The Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art is planning a comprehensive survey of contemporary American art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/arts/design/art-survey-planned.html', 'snippet': 'The Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art is planning a comprehensive survey of contemporary American art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art, the institution founded in Bentonville, Ark., by Alice L. Walton, the Wal-Mart heiress, is only two years old. But it has decided to set out on a mission even more established museums might fear: a comprehensive survey of contemporary American art, formed by visits to hundreds of artists’ studios across the country. The resulting show, “State of the Art,” will bring together the work of 100 artists for a show that will open on \xa0Sept. 13\xa0and continue through \xa0Jan. 5, 2015. For the last several months, the museum’s president, Don Bacigalupi, and an assistant curator for special projects, Chad Alligood, have been traveling by plane and car to almost every part of the country, relying on an initial list of 10,000 artists, to find works they will include in the show. They have visited more than 400 studios and artists so far, in dozens of cities, but also in rural places so small that the roads to them have not shown up on the curators’ GPS devices. “We’ve come to recognize that many extraordinary artists may be known in their own locales, but have yet to emerge on the national stage,” Mr. Alligood said. “Their work, however, deserves consideration from a national audience.” “State of the Art” could be seen as a traditionalist alternative to a show like the Whitney Biennial, but there are currently no plans to make it a recurring event.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Survey Planned', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Survey Planned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Crystal Bridges Museum of American Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T22:56:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf537290-d56f-5b44-a207-f09098eaea87', 'word_count': 240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf537290-d56f-5b44-a207-f09098eaea87'}, {'abstract': 'Monday’s highlights from around the Web include an argument for why the tech industry is to blame for overpriced toast. Plus, examining the popularity of messaging apps like WhatsApp, which are attracting Facebook’s users.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/todays-scuttlebot-messaging-apps-threaten-facebook-and-4-toast/', 'snippet': 'Monday’s highlights from around the Web include an argument for why the tech industry is to blame for overpriced toast. Plus, examining the popularity of messaging apps like WhatsApp, which are attracting Facebook’s users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'ran