ormers in space. Technological advances of recent decades have made it possible to move sound about a room — and even enhance, distort or multiply it as it travels about — while keeping the musician rooted in place.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sounds That Fly on Digital Wings', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sounds That Fly on Digital Wings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Steiger, Rand', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-11T23:19:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/77dca352-5dbf-5f69-b8e5-64182e529261', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/77dca352-5dbf-5f69-b8e5-64182e529261'}, {'abstract': 'Readers responding to a Sunday Review article cite the virtues and vices of email.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/opinion/is-the-letter-dead-not-on-this-page.html', 'snippet': 'Readers responding to a Sunday Review article cite the virtues and vices of email.', 'lead_paragraph': ' ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/opinion/1112LETTERS/1112LETTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/opinion/1112LETTERS/1112LETTERS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 762}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre