ublican of Oklahoma, was killed in a plane crash on Sunday, Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel confirmed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Perry Inhofe, the son of Senator James M. Inhofe, Republican of Oklahoma and ranking member of the Armed Services Committee, was killed in a plane crash on Sunday, Defense Secretary Chuck Hagel confirmed Monday. Aaron Sauer, an investigator for the National Transportation Safety Board, said at a briefing on Monday that only one person was on board the twin-engine plane when it crashed in Owasso,. The plane had taken off from Salina, Kan., and was approaching the Tulsa airport for landing at the time, he said. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Oklahoma: Senator’s Son Dies in Crash Near Tulsa', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Plains', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Oklahoma: Senator’s Son Dies In Crash Near Tulsa', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenny, Steve', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inhofe, Perry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Inhofe, James M', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T02:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/028cb114-a285-57de-868f-40b8a1ecaf3c', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/028cb114-a285-57de-868f-40b8a1ecaf3c'}, {'abstract': 'The Yellow Dogs were far from undiscovered; they had appeared in an award-winning film and been prof