al Profession', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Debevoise & Plimpton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T02:52:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Martin-Kessler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin-Kessler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/61ff12d0-733c-5734-afaf-df48532f08ed', 'word_count': 402, 'uri': 'nyt://article/61ff12d0-733c-5734-afaf-df48532f08ed'}, {'abstract': 'Drugs made John Cox feel numb to the struggles he endured growing up gay. Now he has embraced the doctrine of Narcotics Anonymous.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/nyregion/misery-did-not-work-but-vanity-saved-him.html', 'snippet': 'Drugs made John Cox feel numb to the struggles he endured growing up gay. Now he has embraced the doctrine of Narcotics Anonymous.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As a child, John Cox, 44, did not like getting dirty; he did not like to roughhouse; he did not like a lot of the activities that other boys seemed to love. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/NEEDIEST/NEEDIEST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'i