World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Nossiter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nossiter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9eb0a2ad-8275-5afc-9802-560e47706ba4', 'word_count': 1190, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9eb0a2ad-8275-5afc-9802-560e47706ba4'}, {'abstract': 'In his final address as president of American Roman Catholic bishops, Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan urged them to help Christians who are persecuted overseas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/us/bishops-are-urged-to-expand-priorities.html', 'snippet': 'In his final address as president of American Roman Catholic bishops, Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan urged them to help Christians who are persecuted overseas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BALTIMORE — Cardinal Timothy M. Dolan, in his final address as president of the nation’s Roman Catholic bishops, called on them Monday to take up the cause of Christians in places like Iraq, Syria, Nigeria and India who are persecuted and killed for their faith. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/us/subjpCATHOLIC/subjpCATHOLIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/us/subjpCATHOLIC/subjpCATHOLIC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/us/subjpCATHOLIC/subjpCATHOLIC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/us/subjpCATHOLIC/subjpCATHOLIC