eb5a2-f618-5616-8e70-55381f01d821', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/006eb5a2-f618-5616-8e70-55381f01d821'}, {'abstract': 'Journalists covering the devastation of Typhoon Haiyan deliver messages from survivors to loved ones as people all over the world struggle to find out what happened to their friends and relatives.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/11/messages-to-and-from-survivors-of-typhoon-haiyan/', 'snippet': 'Journalists covering the devastation of Typhoon Haiyan deliver messages from survivors to loved ones as people all over the world struggle to find out what happened to their friends and relatives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated 7:35 a.m., Nov. 12 The messages to loved ones from survivors of Typhoon Haiyan were scrawled on paper plates and scraps of paper. Jiggy Manicad collected them as he reported on the devastation from Tacloban for a Philippines television station and took them back to Manila on Sunday. When GMA News broadcast and posted them online, he delivered what some families, unable to reach friends and relatives since Friday, were desperate to hear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Messages to and From Survivors of Typhoon Haiyan', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tacloban (Philippines)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T03:20:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9