ing Andy Warhol’s “Nine Gold Marilyns (Reversal Series),” that a New York dealer purchased for $8 million.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week’s high-stakes contemporary art auctions got off to a solid, though unexciting, start at Phillips on Monday night. Although there were some disappointments, there were also some record prices for artists, including the Japanese avant-garde painter Kazuo Shiraga; the American installation artist, performance artist and sculptor David Hammons; as well as some of today’s trendier names, like Jacob Kassay, Nate Lowman and Lucien Smith.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 781}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregion/AUCTION/AUCTION-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/nyregi