:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9400ab73-5bbc-5bb8-bc8f-b749c0689e43', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9400ab73-5bbc-5bb8-bc8f-b749c0689e43'}, {'abstract': 'Israeli officials hope to win China to their side in dealings with Iran, Syria and the Palestinians.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/israel-increasingly-courting-china-as-an-ally/', 'snippet': 'Israeli officials hope to win China to their side in dealings with Iran, Syria and the Palestinians.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As an Israeli diplomat, Dore Gold has sat down with his country’s prime ministers, United States presidents and Palestinian negotiators, all in search of that elusive solution to the Middle East conflict.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Israel Increasingly Courting China as an Ally', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T07:11:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c524c4e-69f2-5e29-a3d5-0933144cdccb', 'word_count': 915, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c524c4e-69f2-5e29-a3d5-0933144cdccb'}, {'abstract': 'Answer this question about Veterans Day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/test-yourself-history-nov-12-2013/', 'snippet': 'Answer this question about Veterans Day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take the Quiz', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Test Yourself | History, Nov. 12, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T09:15:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f872408-c27f-5d1a-807e-5d338f4c3413', 'word_count': 25, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f872408-c27f-5d1a-807e-5d338f4c3413'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of couples converged on Mao Zedong’s hometown to exchange wedding vows, weeks before the country will celebrate the 120th anniversary of his birth.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/seeking-maos-matrimonial-blessing/', 'snippet': 'Dozens of couples converged on Mao Zedong’s hometown to exchange wedding vows, weeks before the country will celebrate the 120th anniversary of his birth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shaoshan, the birthplace of Mao Zedong, is no stranger to visitors: Last year, 8.5 million tourists journeyed to this small, county-level city in the mountains of Hunan Province. But on the morning of Nov. 10, with just over a month until the highly anticipated 120th anniversary of the chairman’s birth, Shaoshan hosted a new kind of pilgrim: 50 couples from across China who came to the city to participate in a “Collective Red Wedding.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeking Mao’s Matrimonial Blessing', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T09:26:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Century', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Century', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d06b5ab-c18b-517c-bef8-8606f1c62b11', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d06b5ab-c18b-517c-bef8-8606f1c62b11'}, {'abstract': 'What do aides set up for President Obama when he travels abroad?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/6-qs-about-the-news-obamas-portable-zone-of-secrecy/', 'snippet': 'What do aides set up for President Obama when he travels abroad?', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “Obama’s Portable Zone of Secrecy (Some Assembly Required),” Michael S. Schmidt and Eric Schmitt write about security precautions that the president and other senior officials must take when traveling abroad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/world/security-LN/security-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/world/security-LN/security-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/1