firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88d86e13-9ca0-50d6-92fe-738c9d41b253', 'word_count': 1853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88d86e13-9ca0-50d6-92fe-738c9d41b253'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/the-gun-report-november-12-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Saturday, four members of the Texas chapter of Moms Demand Action for Gun Sense in America held a lunch meeting in Arlington, and nearly 40 armed members of Open Carry Texas, a gun rights advocacy group, waited outside. Police monitored the incident at the Blue Mesa Grill,\xa0but took no action because state law allows people to openly carry guns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 12, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T14:00:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/89a31e35-dbcb-5944-b05f-b2984ea6fe9e', 'word_count': 1364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/89a31e35-dbcb-5944-b05f-b2984ea6fe9e'}, {'abstract': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions. Today’s pick: leather cover-ups for your most beloved personal devices.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/holiday-the-daily-gift-shinola-macbook-sleeve/', 'snippet': 'Every day from now until Chris