zation': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c2e6c626-86d1-58ec-bbbf-6c4fd074872c', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2e6c626-86d1-58ec-bbbf-6c4fd074872c'}, {'abstract': 'For the 13th edition of the performance-focused biennial in New York, the artist Ryan McNamara has created a melange of dance choreography and musical references featuring a disorienting surprise for attendees.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/after-hours-at-performa-ryan-mcnamaras-pop-rock-haunted-house/', 'snippet': 'For the 13th edition of the performance-focused biennial in New York, the artist Ryan McNamara has created a melange of dance choreography and musical references featuring a disorienting surprise for attendees.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Ryan McNamara has become known in recent years for twisting uber-familiar pop references into his party-ready performance pieces. At Robert Wilson’s annual Watermill Benefit in 2011, he and a partner sang “Islands in the Stream,” the Dolly Parton-Kenny Rogers duet, while buried up to their necks in the ground. At the 2010 Whitney Biennial he transformed a corner of the museum into a karaoke jam called the Whitney Houston Biennial. McNamara billed “MEƎM: A Story Ballet About the Internet, the elaborate, multidancer piece he created for this year’s Performa festival as “a choreographic exploration of the online world as a space of engagement.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | At Performa, Ryan McNamara’s Pop-Rock Haunted House', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McNamara, Ryan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T16:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1e193d3-1cc4-5c06-865f-580cacbec167', 'word_count': 391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1e193d3-1cc4-5c06-865f-580cacbec167'}, {'abstract': 'US Airways and American Airlines reached a settlement with the Justice Department that will allow the two companies to go forward with their merger.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/u-s-said-to-be-near-settling-american-us-airways-merger-lawsuit/', 'snippet': 'US Airways and American Airlines reached a settlement with the Justice Department that will allow the two companies to go forward with their merger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After months of setbacks and delays, the merger of American Airlines and US Airways to create the world’s largest airline became all but certain on Tuesday after the airlines reached a settlement with the Justice Department just two weeks before a scheduled trial.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/business/JP-AIR/JP-AIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/13/business/JP-AIR/JP-AIR-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/business/JP-AIR/JP-AIR-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/business/JP-AIR/JP-AIR-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 20