n even faster clip than Central Harlem as a whole.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING.html', 'snippet': 'The area’s population, historically dominated by blacks, has diversified at an even faster clip than Central Harlem as a whole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The area’s population, historically dominated by blacks, has diversified at an even faster clip than Central Harlem as a whole.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8/20131117-LIVING-slide-M3Z8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Living Along Central Park North', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T20:52:33+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/a98a5ff2-8fbf-562d-a3b4-2ca96d91f8cd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/a98a5ff2-8fbf-562d-a3b4-2ca96d91f8cd'}, {'abstract': 'The area’s population, historically dominated by blacks, has diversified at an even faster clip than Central Harlem as a whole.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/realestate/living-along-central-park-north.html', 'snippet': 'The area’s population, historically dominated by blacks, has diversified at an even faster clip than Central Harlem as a whole.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The moment Gary Davis popped his head out of the subway station on Central Park North and Lenox Avenue in 2004, he understood he was looking at an extraordinary spot. An architect and real estate developer, he had been invited to the block by a lawyer for the owner of a two-story corner building there, and though Mr. Davis recalls not being “very excited about Harlem,” he was quick to see the site’s potential. He then sent a photographer 120 feet above the street in a bucket attached to a crane arm; the resulting pictures showed breathtaking panoramic views of Central Park and miles beyond.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How the Word ‘North’ Affects Prices', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How the Word ‘North’ Affects Prices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gill, John Freeman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harlem (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T20:52:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Freeman Gill', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': 'Freeman', 'lastname': 'Gill', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a5fc2bd-01ed-544c-a1c6-17cf6e90d94d', 'word_count': 545, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a5fc2bd-01ed-544c-a1c6-17cf6e90d94d'}, {'abstract': 'The Philadelphia school district is putting 27 buildings, some over 100 years old, on the market. One company is willing to pay $100 million for them all.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/realestate/commercial/philadelphia-schools-see-cash-in-old-classrooms.html', 'snippet': 'The Philadelphia school district is putting 27 buildings, some over 100 years old, on the market. One company is willing to pay $100 million for them all.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — The financially troubled school district here is seeking buyers for more than two dozen school buildings that it shuttered last summer in one of the country’s biggest school closing programs.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mult