bject', 'value': 'Appraisals and Valuation (Property)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Area Planning and Renewal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T20:54:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Hurdle', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hurdle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e3ae18a-b4c3-5628-a08d-89bc6f87c023', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e3ae18a-b4c3-5628-a08d-89bc6f87c023'}, {'abstract': 'Sushi Dojo is a fresh newcomer in the East Village; Kurumazushi is a veteran of the Midtown sushi scene.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/dining/reviews/restaurant-review-sushi-dojo-in-the-east-village-and-kurumazushi-in-midtown.html', 'snippet': 'Sushi Dojo is a fresh newcomer in the East Village; Kurumazushi is a veteran of the Midtown sushi scene.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Disco music with raw fish in the East Village may not strike you as a winning formula unless you remember when Avenue A had what was probably the only sushi bar in the city with a mirror ball and a D.J. booth. Everybody called it Disco Sushi, and I loved it for reasons that had nothing to do with the food. I had eaten enough good sushi to know I couldn’t afford it. But cold rice, fake wasabi and sinewy fish mattered much less when vinyl records and the mirror ball were spinning, the tables were filling up with musicians waiting for a 1 a.m. gig at Brownies, and we were all on our third round of sake bombs.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{