 the “total installation,” an art form that can bear some resemblance to a meticulously dressed movie set. It’s an idea that the art critic and filmmaker Amei Wallach confronts head-on in “Ilya and Emilia Kabakov: Enter Here,” a dynamically shot documentary that keeps journeying into the Soviet past as it is remembered and reworked by Mr. Kabakov and his wife and partner, Emilia.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 320, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 320}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 546, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 995, 'width': 1866, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/arts/ILYA/ILYA-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Reworking Their Soviet Past', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reworking Their Soviet Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kabakov, Emilia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kabakov, Ilya', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wallach, Amei', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-12T22:40:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicolas Rapold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicolas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rapold', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea75fccb-9fe2-5853-83f3-aa9c18db140b', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ea75fccb-9fe2-5853-83f3-aa9c18db140b'}, {'abstract': 'Richard Allan, the director for public policy for Facebook in Europe, the Middle East and Africa, said the company received 8,500 requests from the European Union affecting 10,000 user accounts during the first six months of this year.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/12/in-europe-thousands-of-requests-for-facebook-data/', 'snippet': 'Richard Allan, the director for public policy for Facebook in Europe, the Middle East and Africa, said the company received 8,500 requests from the European Union affecting 10,000 user accounts during the first six months of this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRUSSELS — Online surveillance by the United States was the main subject of a hearing on Monday evening organized by the European Parliament’s civil liberties committee. But one of the more noteworthy parts of the session was a presentation by a senior Facebook employee who described demands by European Union governments.', 'source': 'Th