'snippet': 'After one of the worst typhoons on record hit the country, many are offering aid, but relief efforts are hampered by the scale of the damage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Five days after one of the worst typhoons on record hit the Philippines, the magnitude of the catastrophe is barely captured in the preliminary statistics: nearly 2,000 people listed as dead and many thousands more missing; more than 600,000 people displaced; countless homes and roads crushed by surging water. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agony in the Philippines', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agony in the Philippines', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Evacuations and Evacuees', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T01:48:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2529971a-673d-5f14-8855-8f3610d4620c', 'word_count': 395, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2529971a-673d-5f14-8855-8f3610d4620c'}, {'abstract': 'The government should raise the minimum pay for garment workers and index it to inflation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/opinion/a-living-wage-in-bangladesh.html', 'snippet': 'The government should raise the minimum pay for garment workers and index it to inflation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The government of Bangladesh is expected to soon announce an increase in the minimum wage for workers in the country’s clothing factories, which are big suppliers to Western retailers like Walmart and H&M. Its decision could improve the lives of millions of families that struggle to eke out an existence on as little as the equivalent of about $38 a month, the current minimum wage.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Living Wage in Bangladesh', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Living Wage in Bangladesh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minimum Wage', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wage', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rana Plaza Building Collapse, Bangladesh (2013)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Factories and Manufacturing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'H & M Hennes & Mauritz AB', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T01:51:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1293d30b-94b6-5409-8c1c-33cefb365654', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1293d30b-94b6-5409-8c1c-33cefb365654'}, {'abstract': 'The amateur model in college sports is in serious trouble, with a federal district judge certifying a class-action suit against the N.C.A.A.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/opinion/fairness-for-college-athletes.html', 'snippet': 'The amateur model in college sports is in serious trouble, with a federal district judge certifying a class-action suit against the N.C.A.A.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The amateur model in college sports is in serious trouble, with a federal district judge on Friday certifying a class-action suit against the National Collegiate Athletic Association. Under N.C.A.A. rules, student athletes may not receive compensation — a policy that effectively blocks players from entering into group licensing agreements. The N.C.A.A., however, sells the names and images of players for use in game footage, photographs and video games.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fairness for College Athletes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fairness for College Athletes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Collegiate Athletic Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Title IX (Gender Discrimination Legislation)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Bannon, Ed", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T01:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/02db9783-9388-5a08-9f9d-441c02d1033f', 'word_count': 272, 'uri': 'nyt://article/02db9783-9388-5a08-9f9d-441c02d1033f'}, {'abstract': 'State and local governments have maintained that the tribe, the Wampanoag Tribe of Gay Head (Aquinnah), forfeited its right to build a casino on the Vineyard in the 1980s when it agreed to a land settlement.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/us/tribe-claims-approval-for-marthas-vineyard-casino-reviving-fight.html', 'snippet': 'State and local governments have maintained that the tribe, the Wampanoag Tribe of Gay Head (Aquinnah), forfeited its right to build a casino on the Vineyard in the 1980s when it agreed to a land settlement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — An Indian tribe on Martha’s Vineyard said Tuesday that it had obtained approval from a federal agency to open a casino on tribal land on the resort island, but others challenged that conclusion and said the tribe had no such authority.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/VINEYARD/VINEYARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/13/us/VINEYARD/VINEYARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/VINEYARD/VINEYARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/VINEYARD/VINEYARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/VINEYARD/VINEYARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75