me in six years, was named American League manager of the year on Tuesday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his eight eventful seasons with the Boston Red Sox, Terry Francona never received a first-place vote for the Manager of the Year award. This was mostly a function of the way voters judge managers, rewarding those perceived to do more with less. The Red Sox always had high payrolls and thus high expectations.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/sports/Y-KEPNER/Y-KEPNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Goodbye, Boston; Hello, Manager of the Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Goodbye, Boston; Hello, Manager of the Year', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francona, Terry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Red Sox', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T02:02:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a98a4cf7-d63d-54e0-b74c-52a820946cf7', 'word_count': 814, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a98a4cf7-d63d-54e0-b74c-52a820946cf7'}, {'abstract': 'The governor, Jay Nixon, urged an end to incentives that lure jobs from one state to the other, rather than luring new jobs to the region.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/us/missouris-governor-calls-for-end-to-contest-of-incentives.html', 'snippet': 'The governor, Jay Nixon, urged an end to incentives that lure jobs from one state to the other, rather than luring new jobs to the region.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KANSAS CITY, Mo. — The long-running competition for jobs between Kansas and Missouri that has elicited all manner of battlefield imagery about arming and disarming, border wars and turf battles now has Gov. Jay Nixon of Missouri signaling for a new one: truce.', 'print_sec