y not be viable, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Casey B. Mulligan is an economics professor at the University of Chicago. He is the author of “The Redistribution Recession: How Labor Market Distortions Contracted the Economy.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Slow Death of the Employer Mandate', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Massachusetts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T05:01:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey B. Mulligan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d4c24d8-9ca3-55af-9b55-6c5d48930cb9', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d4c24d8-9ca3-55af-9b55-6c5d48930cb9'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Lumbard drew new attention to organized crime after pursuing mob figures who were found to be meeting together in a rural New York town in 1957.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/nyregion/eliot-h-lumbard-who-investigated-the-apalachin-mob-meeting-is-dead-at-88.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Lumbard drew new attention to organized crime after pursuing mob figures who were found to be meeting together in a rural New York town in 1957.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eliot H. Lumbard, a New York prosecutor and law-enforcement leader who helped expose organized crime through his investigation of the infamous Apalachin meeting of mob leaders in 1957, died on Nov. 6 in Nashua, N.H. He was 88.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 812, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 812}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 757, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1513, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/us/LUMBARD-2-obit/LUMBARD-2-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Eliot H. Lumbard, 88, Dies; Pursued Mob Leaders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eliot H. Lumbard, 88; Pursued Mob Leaders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yardley, William', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lumbard, Eliot H (1925-2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T05:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Yardley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yardley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f54d948-7607-59c0-835e-cf746394f1b1', 'word_count': 925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f54d948-7607-59c0-835e-cf746394f1b1'}, {'abstract': 'In the devastated Philippine town of Tacloban, aid is piling up with no way to deliver it, fuel is plentiful but merchants are too fearful to sell it, and disposal of the dead is halted by gunfire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/world/asia/aid-groups-in-philippines-fear-more-devastation-has-yet-to-be-revealed.html', 'snippet': 'In the devastated Philippine town of Tacloban, aid is piling up with no way to deliver it, fuel is plentiful but merchants are too fearful to sell it, and disposal of the dead is halted by gunfire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TACLOBAN, the Philippines — Typhoon gridlock threatened rescue operations in the most devastated part of the Philippines on Wednesday, with aid piling up but few ways to distribute it, plentiful gasoline but no merchants willing to sell it, and an influx of emergency volunteers but no place to house them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Logistical Hurdles Paralyze Relief Effort at the Center of a Typhoon’s Fury', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Logistical Hurdles Paralyze Relief Effort at the Center of a Typhoon’s Fury', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradsher, Keith', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disasters and Emergencies', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Humanitarian Aid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tacloban (Philippines)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Save the Children', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T05:51:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Keith Bradsher and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Keith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bradsher', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f8c4036d-6968-5695-939e-d4765025ac9f', 'word_count': 1192, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f8c4036d-6968-5695-939e-d4765025ac9f'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/arts/television/whats-on-wednesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOON (HBO2) LOVE, MARILYN (2012) Actors and various contemporaries recite from recently discovered diaries and letters written by Marilyn Monroe, above, in what David DeWitt, writing in The New York Times, called “a respectful love letter to Monroe,” who is presented by the director, Liz Garbus, “as a sexpot, feminist and Tennessee Williams heroine come to life, noble in her respect and need for a sensitive, considerate humanity.” Some, like Glenn Close, Viola Davis and Uma Thurman, nail their readings. Others, like Ben Foster, “get a bit cringe-worthy,” Mr. DeWitt said. “But the intelligence and dynamism of Ms. Garbus’s approach could hardly fail to make you appreciate Monroe’s growth as an actor.” The documentary includes footage of Monroe performing or giving interviews. “More so,” Mr. DeWitt added, “you’ll have sympathy for the hard-working woman whose self-improvement lists included exhortations of things she ‘must’ do and ‘never’ should do.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Wednesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Wednesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a83f748-a6ea-506e-9b8f-53d0fdba2fa5', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a83f748-a6ea-506e-9b8f-53d0fdba2fa5'}, {'abstract': 'Poppy cultivation and production hit record levels this year, and programs to counteract them have floundered, a new United Nations study said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/world/asia/afghan-opium-cultivation-and-production-seen-rising.html', 'snippet': 'Poppy cultivation and production hit record levels this year, and programs to counteract them have floundered, a new United Nations study said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — Despite years of international effort to reel back Afghanistan’s opium culture, cultivation and production hit record levels this year, and programs to counteract them have floundered, according to a new United Nations study.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/13/world/OPIUM/OPIUM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan Opium Cultivation and Production Seen Rising', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Afghan Opium Cultivation And Production Seen Rising', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGH