count': 1403, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a58f9cf9-3074-5138-b461-6abf78ed89ad'}, {'abstract': 'China’s new national security committee, which is expected to be led by President Xi Jinping, will deal with cybersecurity, relations with Tibet and unrest in the Xinjiang region, Chinese experts say.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/world/asia/national-security-committee-china.html', 'snippet': 'China’s new national security committee, which is expected to be led by President Xi Jinping, will deal with cybersecurity, relations with Tibet and unrest in the Xinjiang region, Chinese experts say.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China’s new national security committee is mainly based on the Washington model. It will put at the disposal of the Chinese president, Xi Jinping, a highly empowered group of security experts who can work the levers of the country’s vast security apparatus — and presumably respond more nimbly than the country’s multilayered party, police and military bureaucracies have been known to do.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/china/china-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/world/china/china-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/china/china-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 696, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/china/china-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1392, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None