ders-would-critique-her-ideas-instead-they-judged-her-choices/', 'snippet': 'Like many women, I found being a full-time mother with a full-time job impossibly stressful. But many readers thought that by setting better boundaries with my boss, or having a more can-do attitude, I could have made the plague of overwork affect...', 'lead_paragraph': 'When KJ Dell’Antonia’s article about my book, “Maxed Out: American Moms on the Brink,” was published on Motherlode last week (“Being a Working Mother Means Always Having to Say You’re Sorry“), I was thrilled to see it generating passionate discussion in the comments section. This is, after all, the main reason I wrote “Maxed Out” — to get people talking about the structural issues holding women back in their careers and their lives.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Maxed Out’ Author Thought Readers Would Critique Her Ideas. Instead, They Judged Her Choices.', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Leaves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paid Time Off', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Work-Life Balance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T16:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katrina Alcorn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katrina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alcorn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/09c34e4d-4d2d-595a-a176-10532841a537', 'word_count': 1694, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09c34e4d-4d2d-595a-a176-10532841a537'}, {'abstract': 'The military-backed government’s efforts to extinguish the memory of Rabaa al-Adawiya, the worst mass killing in Egypt’s history, are extensive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/world/middleeast/memory-egypt-mass-killing.html', 'snippet': 'The military-backed government’s efforts to extinguish the memory of Rabaa al-Adawiya, the worst mass killing in Egypt’s history, are extensive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — The police arrested the girls, interrogated them for hours, and then strip-searched and detained them for 10 days. They were charged with serious crimes, including endangering national security, for what the authorities regarded as an act of subversion: passing out yellow balloons.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/cairo/cairo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/world/cairo/cairo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/cairo/cairo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/cairo/cairo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/cairo/cairo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/world/cairo/cairo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None