’s a roundup of items from all over that may be interesting to Times readers and to the readers of this blog:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Roundup: Staff Departures, an ‘Incorrect Promise’ and More', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T17:12:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/599aa644-0f48-58a4-83d9-98ae902fda2d', 'word_count': 711, 'uri': 'nyt://article/599aa644-0f48-58a4-83d9-98ae902fda2d'}, {'abstract': 'As lawmakers tried to find out how much the White House knew about defects in the federal health insurance website, the chief digital architect for the marketplace said he had provided status updates to the Obama administration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/us/officials-say-they-dont-know-cost-of-health-website-fixes.html', 'snippet': 'As lawmakers tried to find out how much the White House knew about defects in the federal health insurance website, the chief digital architect for the marketplace said he had provided status updates to the Obama administration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The chief digital architect for the federal health insurance marketplace said Wednesday that he met periodically with White House aides to discuss the status of the website over the last three years, but he said the meetings focused narrowly on specific technical issues and therefore gave the president no clear warning of the disaster that ensued on Oct. 1.', 'print_secti