rian country without suffering repercussions.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/navigating-the-constraints-on-reporting-from-china/', 'snippet': 'A comparison of China to Nazi Germany raises the question of how journalists based in China can continue to write compelling stories about an important but authoritarian country without suffering repercussions.', 'lead_paragraph': '‘‘I ask myself why I stay on here,’’ William L. Shirer wrote in Berlin on Sept. 20, 1940, as World War II deepened and Nazi censorship of his CBS radio broadcasts became intolerable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Navigating the Constraints on Reporting from China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shirer, William L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winkler, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg Business News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T22:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26fb8543-1a75-5bcb-83cd-ad3ddd1ae43a', 'word_count': 650, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26fb8543-1a75-5bcb-83cd-ad3ddd1ae43a'}, {'abstract': 'Other celebrities have started websites to offer their version of the good life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/fashion/