e, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14FURNITURE_SPAN/14CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14FURNITURE_SPAN/14CURR1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14FURNITURE_SPAN/14CURR1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For D.I.Y.’ers, Designer Hardware', 'kicker': 'Currents | Furniture', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For D.I.Y.’ers, Designer Hardware', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hirst, Arlene', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Furniture', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Do It Yourself', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wilson, Henry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-13T23:22:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arlene Hirst', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arlene', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirst', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d14da376-b4b3-50c3-aa2b-0e184f4fc97c', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d14da376-b4b3-50c3-aa2b-0e184f4fc97c'}, {'abstract': 'Classic flatware by the mid-century Danish designer Kay Bojesen is back in production.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/garden/bringing-beauty-to-hand.html', 'snippet': 'Classic flatware by the mid-century Danish designer Kay Bojesen is back in production.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Danish designer Kay Bojesen, who was born in 1886 and died in 1958, believed that objects must be nice to hold and a pleasure to look at. Trained as a silversmith at Georg Jensen, he created a flatware pattern in 1938 that won the grand prize at the 1951 Milan Triennale, a biennial design showcase. It has been called Grand Prix ever since. Mr. Bojesen’s granddaughter, Susanne Bojesen Rosenqvist, lately reintroduced the pattern, which has been in and out of production since its inventor’s death. Ms. Rosenqvist, who said she has eaten with her grandfather’s utensils ever since she could hold a spoon, praised details like the small hump between the knife’s shaft and blade, which supports your forefinger when you cut, and the spoon’s milled edges, designed to capture drips. A five-piece place setting in stainless steel is $150 from Anise, 212-933-1406 or kaybojesen.dk.\xa0', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 827, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 827}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 948, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/garden/14GOODS/14CURR2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnai