ntral banks in the United States and Europe, finding the policy to have been a double-edged sword.', 'lead_paragraph': ' As Wall Street tries to gauge when the Federal Reserve might start tapering its stimulus program, a new study from the McKinsey Global Institute illustrates just how deep the impact of such efforts has been since 2007. But it also makes clear that the benefits haven’t been distributed equally.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Winners and Losers From Stimulus', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Debt (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Quantitative Easing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'McKinsey Global Institute', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T00:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96b6e377-4d94-5043-86b0-2b5e7cc5c71c', 'word_count': 580, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96b6e377-4d94-5043-86b0-2b5e7cc5c71c'}, {'abstract': 'Wednesday’s highlights from around the Web include a report that Snapchat, a photo-messaging service, rejected a $3 billion offer from Facebook. Plus, Yahoo auctions off old domains, including sandwich.com.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/13/todays-scuttlebot-a-snapchat-spurn-and-yahoo-to-shed-sandwich-com/', 'snippet': 'Wednesday’s highlights from around the Web include a report that Snapchat, a photo-messaging service, rejected a $3 billion offer from Facebook. Plus, Yahoo auctions off old domains, including sandwich.com.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day, The New York Times’s staff scours the Web for interesting and peculiar items.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 500, 'width': 500, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/11/11/blogs/scuttlebot/scuttlebot-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Today’s Scuttlebot: A Snapchat Spurn, and Yahoo to Shed Sandwich.com', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T00:08:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93e4fadf-f0e4-5a95-a9