t://article/ac355cdd-d42b-5abb-b086-56990a9d2e7a', 'word_count': 873, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ac355cdd-d42b-5abb-b086-56990a9d2e7a'}, {'abstract': 'About 2,000 people are enrolling in private health care plans daily through the state’s website, officials said, a rate that has picked up considerably over the past few weeks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/us/california-health-exchange-beats-all-others-in-enrollment-officials-say.html', 'snippet': 'About 2,000 people are enrolling in private health care plans daily through the state’s website, officials said, a rate that has picked up considerably over the past few weeks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its first month of business, California’s insurance exchange enrolled more people than any other state-run exchange and more than the federal exchange serving 36 states, which has been paralyzed by technological failures. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California Health Exchange Beats All Others in Enrollment, Officials Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California Exchange Beats All Others in Enrollment', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Peter V', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicaid', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T01:52:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Abby Goodnough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Abby', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodnough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6fd6131-dd3e-5a0d-84c3-77d48df926b1', 'word_count': 408, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6fd6131-dd3e-5a0d-84c3-77d48df926b1'}, {'abstract': 'The United States says Iran was unwilling to agree to a unified proposal, while Iran says France thwarted progress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/world/middleeast/iran-and-western-powers-clash-over-why-nuclear-talks-failed.html', 'snippet': 'The United States says Iran was unwilling to agree to a unified proposal, while Iran says France thwarted progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEHRAN — Less than a week before the next round of nuclear talks in Geneva, it is still not clear why the last round failed, and who exactly walked away from the deal. Iran’s foreign minister, Mohammad Javad Zarif, has laid the blame on the Western powers, saying they were divided. He says he has little to do now but wait for the world powers to get their act together. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iran and Western Powers Clash Over Why Nuclear Talks Failed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iran and Western Powers Clash Over Why Nuclear Talks Failed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zarif, Mohammad Javad', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shariatmadari, Hossein', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T01:52:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Erdbrink', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Erdbrink', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b2b5a3c-c818-5521-b38f-3914ebc27593', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b2b5a3c-c818-5521-b38f-3914ebc27593'}, {'abstract': 'The Tigers’ Max Scherzer, who went 21-3 with 2.90 earned run average and 240 strikeouts, won the A.L. Cy Young Award despite not ever having pitched a complete game in his career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/sports/baseball/no-complete-games-but-a-cy-young-award-for-detroits-max-scherzer.html', 'snippet': 'The Tigers’ Max Scherzer, who went 21-3 with 2.90 earned run average and 240 strikeouts, won the A.L. Cy Young Award despite not ever having pitched a complete game in his career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Detroit Tigers’ Max Scherzer did something on Wednesday that no starting pitcher had ever done before. He won a Cy Young Award before registering his first career complete game.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 368, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 368}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 627, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1255, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/sports/Y-JP-KEPNER/Y-JP-KEPNER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Complete Games but a Cy Young Award', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Complete Games But a Cy Young Award', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scherzer, Max', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cy Young Award', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Detroit Tigers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kershaw, Clayton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T01:53:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tyler Kepner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/52cf53db-82fd-5d7d-8efc-9973bb382ac5', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/52cf53db-82fd-5d7d-8efc-9973bb382ac5'}, {'abstract': 'A team began exhuming the remains of João Goulart, the Brazilian president ousted in a 1964 coup supported by the United States, to examine whether he was poisoned by spies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/world/americas/brazil-forensic-team-exhumes-leaders-remains.html', 'snippet': 'A team began exhuming the remains of João Goulart, the Brazilian president ousted in a 1964 coup supported by the United States, to examine whether he was poisoned by spies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A team of forensic experts on Wednesday began exhuming the remains of João Goulart, the Brazilian president ousted in a 1964 coup supported by the United States, to examine whether he was poisoned by spies while living in exile in Argentina. The authorities carried out the exhumation in São Borja, a city in southern Brazil, at the urging of Mr. Goulart’s family. They are seeking to examine a claim by a former Uruguayan intelligence operative that Mr. Goulart was assassinated by agents of Operation Condor, a joint campaign by South American military dictatorships in the 1970s and ’80s to eliminate political dissidents. Mr. Goulart had long been thought to have died from natural causes. Officials said that his remains would be flown to the capital, Brasília, to undergo testing. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: Forensic Team Exhumes Leader’s Remains', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: Forensic Team Exhumes Leader’s Remains', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goulart, Joao', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forensic Science', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T01:58:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/d7ccbcd1-dd9d-5e74-a000-d577a13ac83b', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d7ccbcd1-dd9d-5e74-a000-d577a13ac83b'}, {'abstract': 'The drug has been approved by the Food and Drug Administration to treat relapses of a rare blood cancer called mantle cell lymphoma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/business/drug-to-treat-blood-cancer-gains-fda-approval.html', 'snippet': 'The drug has been approved by the Food and Drug Administration to treat relapses of a rare blood cancer called mantle cell lymphoma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new cancer drug that has attracted considerable attention from doctors and investors won approval from the Food and Drug Administration on Wednesday. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Imbruvica, Drug to Treat Blood Cancer, Gains F.D.A. Approval', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drug to Treat Blood Cancer Gains F.D.A. Approval', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pollack, Andrew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cancer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {