source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, November 14, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T03:17:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/9070c777-3d1e-56fe-81d5-f2e9cc16b55c', 'word_count': 40, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9070c777-3d1e-56fe-81d5-f2e9cc16b55c'}, {'abstract': 'Corrections appearing in print on November 14, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/pageoneplus/corrections-november-14-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Corrections appearing in print on November 14, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FRONT PAGE', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: November 14, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T03:18:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4b4ef7c-6119-5311-9a8a-0a81e8bcd5f7', 'word_count': 571, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4b4ef7c-6119-5311-9a8a-0a81e8bcd5f7'}, {'abstract': 'During a public debate on gambling, one of India’s top law enforcement officials remarked that arguing to legalize betting is “like saying if you can’t prevent rape, enjoy it.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/world/asia/india-official-criticized-for-a-reference-to-rape.html', 'snippet': 'During a public debate on gambling, one of India’s top law enforcement officials remarked that arguing to legalize betting is “like saying if you can’t prevent rape, enjoy it.”', 'lead_paragraph': ' One of India’s top law enforcement officials drew criticism on Wednesday for making an offhand reference to rape during a public debate on gambling, remarking that arguing to legalize betting is “like saying if you can’t prevent rape, enjoy it.” In a country newly sensitized to sexual violence, the remarks by Ranjit Sinha, director of the Central Bureau of Investigation, immediately echoed on Twitter and were covered by television news channels. Some activists called on Mr. Sinha, who heads a bureau supervising corruption and other grave crimes, including rape and murder, to step down. Mr. Sinha swiftly released a statement of apology: “I regret any hurt caused, as the same was inadvertent and unintended,” it read, explaining that he was condemning such reasoning, and adding, “I reiterate my deep sense of respect for women and commitment to gender issues.” ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'India: Official Criticized for a Reference to Rape', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Asia', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'India: Official Criticized for a Reference to Rape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sinha, Ranjit', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T03:19:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ellen Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ellen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ef94557-7ff8-573f-adc9-f39