'', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T05:06:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71db68b5-d169-5cd8-ad21-d40666f9b51e', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71db68b5-d169-5cd8-ad21-d40666f9b51e'}, {'abstract': 'The Nets dropped their third straight game, as Marcus Thornton, with 24 points, led the host Kings to their first victory in six games.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/sports/basketball/nets-continue-skid-in-sacramento.html', 'snippet': 'The Nets dropped their third straight game, as Marcus Thornton, with 24 points, led the host Kings to their first victory in six games.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SACRAMENTO — For weeks, the Nets seemed willing to tie their poor play to their newness as a group. The process of adjusting to a new system, to new teammates, justified their string of surprising losses, and few could challenge them on that point.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1432, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/14nets-1/14nets-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nets, Continuing Skid in Sacramento, Offer No Excuses', 'kicker': 'Kings 107, Nets 86', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nets, Continuing Skid in Sacramento, Offer No Excuses', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sacramento Kings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Nets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Deron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McLemore, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Paul (1977- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T05:51:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Keh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a87b4073-f612-5ce2-ae83-9a8cfa4729c9', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a87b4073-f612-5ce2-ae83-9a8cfa4729c9'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (FX Movie Channel) WALL STREET: MONEY NEVER SLEEPS (2010) Michael Douglas, below, returns as the reptilian Gordon Gekko who, after eight years in prison, has landed in the spotlight once again for writing a critical and prescient book about the state of the markets. Shia LaBeouf portrays the investment banker Jake Moore, one of Gekko’s fans and the live-in love of Gekko’s daughter (Carey Mulligan). Frank Langella is the old-school broker who has been like a father to Jake. And Josh Brolin is the newest snake in town. Let the games resume. “To the question ‘What went wrong?’ the film offers an answer that is both irrefutable and unsatisfying: human nature,” A. O. Scott wrote in The New York Times. And yet, he added, something vital here works. The director, Oliver Stone, “is not the man to explain Wall Street, or to stoke public indignation at its crimes,” he said. “But no one else could turn it into a show like ‘Wall Street.’\xa0” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/4dc9d2ee-a140-516a-adf0-b189a5b01dc7', 'word_count': 727, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4dc9d2ee-a140-516a-adf0-b189a5b01dc7'}, {'abstract': 'The move raises the chance that Boeing will move assembly of the new 777X jet from the Seattle area, the company’s traditional manufacturing base.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/business/boeing-workers-reject-labor-deal-in-washington-state.html', 'snippet': 'The move raises the chance that Boeing will move assembly of the new 777X jet from the Seattle area, the company’s traditional manufacturing base.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Members of a union representing thousands of Boeing employees voted late Wednesday to reject a controversial labor deal that would have cut compensation but have kept assembly of the company’s new 777X jets in Washington State, raising the chance that Boeing will move more production away from its traditional manufacturing base in the Seattle area.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Boeing Workers Reject Labor Deal in Washington State', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boeing Company', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Washington (State)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T06:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Gough', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gough', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b5c0094-ca2b-5391-80d6-ed33c54b6db4', 'word_count': 428, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b5c0094-ca2b-5391-80d6-ed33c54b6db4'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/news-quiz-november-14-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 14, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T06:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6924374d-6a14-5f9e-8ede-54ac838c9d85', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6924374d-6a14-5f9e-8ede-54ac838c9d85'}, {'abstract': 'Chinese animal rights advocates are buoyed by news the government is moving toward ending the mandatory testing of cosmetics on animals, in line with growing international norms.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/china-moving-to-end-some-cosmetics-testing-on-animals/', 'snippet': 'Chinese animal rights advocates are buoyed by news the government is moving toward ending the mandatory testing of cosmetics on animals, in line with growing international norms.', 'lead_paragraph': '“YES!” wrote Hou Xiaomu, an animal lover, on Weibo, about the news that China’s food and drug authorities are moving toward ending the testing of cosmetics on animals. About 300,000 animals — rabbits, mice and others —\xa0 may be used each year in testing cosmetics here, Humane Society International estimates.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Moving to End Some Cosmetics Testing on Animals', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cosmetics and Toiletries', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rabbits', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T06:34:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didi Kirsten Tatlow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didi', 'middlename': 'Kirsten', 'lastname': 'Tatlow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9edfdd5d-f70d-53f9-892e-817bd00f6af9', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9edfdd5d-f70d-53f9-892e-817bd00f6af9'}, {'abstract': 'On Friday, coal-fired heating systems will be turned on in much of northern China, a major factor in worsening air pollution.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/northern-chinese-brace-for-smog-spike-as-winter-heating-kicks-in/', 'snippet': 'On Friday, coal-fired heating systems will be turned on in much of northern China, a major factor in worsening air pollution.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Harbin —\xa0a metropolis in China’s northeastern reaches —\xa0made international headlines last month when it experienced air pollution so abysmal that the government closed all schools and officials urged the city’s 11 million residents to stay indoors as visibility dropped to just 10 meters, roughly the width of a typical traffic intersection.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Northern Chinese Brace for Smog Spike as Winter Heating Kicks In', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Heating', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Harbin (China)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T07:02:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Century', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Century', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3240b939-1fc5-5448-94c7-8ebe1ccfb274', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3240b939-1fc5-5448-94c7-8ebe1ccfb274'}, {'abstract': 'Yan Jun’s rescue of a Japanese boy from drowning, at risk to his own life, came at a difficult time in relations between China and Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/japan-honors-chinese-student-for-heroism/', 'snippet': 'Yan Jun’s rescue of a Japanese boy from drowning, at risk to his own life, came at a difficult time in relations between China and Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prime Minister Shinzo Abe of Japan has honored a Chinese student for his “courageous act” in rescuing a Japanese boy from drowning, a bright spot in an otherwise tense period in diplomatic relations.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Japan Honors Chinese Student for Heroism', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Awards, Decorations and Honors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T07:10:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bree Feng', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bree', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feng', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aa8a083-fff3-5250-868a-e7ceb3ed33c3', 'word_count': 427, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aa8a083-fff3-5250-868a-e7ceb3ed33c3'}, {'abstract': 'Yang Maodong was detained by the police in early August on allegations of “assembling a crowd to disrupt order in a public place.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/world/asia/chinese-rights-campaigner-held-hunger-strike-lawyer-says.html', 'snippet': 'Yang Maodong was detained by the police in early August on allegations of “assembling a crowd to disrupt order in a public place.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — A prominent human rights campaigner in southern China won his first meeting with a lawyer on Thursday after more than three months in detention and said he had been on a hunger strike, one of his lawyers said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Chinese Rights Campaigner Held Hunger Strike, Lawyer Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'C