n Brooklyn street is pretty pushy.', 'web_url': 'https://cityroom.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/hungry-and-panhandling/', 'snippet': 'Metropolitan Diary: A man on a Downtown Brooklyn street is pretty pushy.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Dear Diary:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hungry and Panhandling', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beggars', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Downtown Brooklyn (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T14:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mel Glenn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glenn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/290c9fda-7d72-526f-a73d-bc94e97ea142', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/290c9fda-7d72-526f-a73d-bc94e97ea142'}, {'abstract': 'There are many ways to teach children to be generous without denying them the usual pile of gifts.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/the-holidays-a-bit-more-giving-a-bit-less-getting/', 'snippet': 'There are many ways to teach children to be generous without denying them the usual pile of gifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some people react to my obsession with parenting, money and values by assuming that it has little to do with them. Take my friends in a low-key Midwestern state, who are both public-sector employees. Wasn’t this topic, they wondered, something that only affluent suburban parents or private-school people needed to worry about?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 765, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1530, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-ron-charity/motherlode-ron-charity-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Holidays: A Bit More Giving, a Bit Less Getting', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hanukkah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nonprofit Organizations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T14:34:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ron Lieber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ron', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lieber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce156211-8521-5a40-8029-05a1f695ab4e', 'word_count': 767, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce156211-8521-5a40-8029-05a1f695ab4e'}, {'abstract': 'The company was founded in 1807 by Ignaz Pleyel, who studied with Josef Haydn.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/storied-french-piano-manufacturer-to-close/', 'snippet': 'The company was founded in 1807 by Ignaz Pleyel, who studied with Josef Haydn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Ending an era on a mournful chord, Pleyel, the storied French piano manufacturer whose pianos were once favored by Frédéric Chopin and Maurice Ravel, has announced that it will close its workshop after two centuries of production.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Storied French Piano Manufacturer to Close', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pianos', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T14:40:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Donadio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Donadio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/202d7f7f-42a4-5ee1-ab34-8d8c0acb9759', 'word_count': 224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/202d7f7f-42a4-5ee1-ab34-8d8c0acb9759'}, {'abstract': 'The French-Dutch airline says it will not take part in a plan to inject 300 million euros into the faltering Italian flag carrier.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/business/international/air-france-klm-signals-wavering-faith-in-alitalia.html', 'snippet': 'The French-Dutch airline says it will not take part in a plan to inject 300 million euros into the faltering Italian flag carrier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Air France-KLM, the French-Dutch airline, said Thursday that it would not take part in a plan to inject 300 million euros into Alitalia, arguing that the faltering Italian flag carrier was not prepared to take sufficient steps to reduce its mounting debt.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Air France-KLM Signals Wavering Faith in Alitalia', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE-KLM', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ALITALIA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T14:43:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicola Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicola', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f05a3808-4c93-5d7d-882f-1779e2399cbe', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f05a3808-4c93-5d7d-882f-1779e2399cbe'}, {'abstract': 'The census of homeless school children has grown dramatically in recent years.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/homeless-kids-in-rough-schools/', 'snippet': 'The census of homeless school children has grown dramatically in recent years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Working-aged adults who lost their jobs, homes and savings to the recession will have a difficult enough time establishing normal lives when the economy rights itself. The trauma will be especially deep and long lasting for the burgeoning population of children who were driven into homelessness — or even given up by their parents — when the world turned upside down in the Great Recession of 2008.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Homeless Kids in Rough Schools', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Week', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T14:48:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent Staples', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Staples', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1884a173-bfaa-5642-b692-49797447254b', 'word_count': 251, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1884a173-bfaa-5642-b692-49797447254b'}, {'abstract': 'Janet L. Yellen, the nominee to succeed Ben S. Bernanke as chief of the Federal Reserve, faces questioning from the Senate Banking Committee.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/live-blog-yellens-confirmation-hearing/', 'snippet': 'Janet L. Yellen, the nominee to succeed Ben S. Bernanke as chief of the Federal Reserve, faces questioning from the Senate Banking Committee.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Janet L. Yellen, the vice chairwoman of the Federal Reserve, testified Thursday before the Senate Banking Committee at a hearing on her nomination to succeed Ben S. Bernanke as Fed chief. In her opening statement, released by the Fed on Wednesday, Ms. Yellen made the case for the Fed’s current stimulus program, declaring, “I believe that supporting the recovery today is the surest path to returning to a more normal approach to monetary policy.” A running account of the hearing follows.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yellen’s Confirmation Hearing', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T14:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af03b7bc-9ddd-5041-b8a7-02d42c908a46', 'word_count': 3085, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af03b7bc-9ddd-5041-b8a7-02d42c908a46'}, {'abstract': 'For people with severe arthritis, knee or hip replacement may have an added benefit: a reduction in the risk for cardiovascular disease.', 'web_url': 'h