}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26383ea4-aeb4-5fea-8b62-df40e429d238', 'word_count': 281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26383ea4-aeb4-5fea-8b62-df40e429d238'}, {'abstract': 'Deborah Anna Luepnitz, a couples therapist, says an unhappy spouse can benefit by realizing that “sometimes what is lacking in your partner is what you lack yourself.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/booming/backing-off-wanting-it-all-from-a-spouse.html', 'snippet': 'Deborah Anna Luepnitz, a couples therapist, says an unhappy spouse can benefit by realizing that “sometimes what is lacking in your partner is what you lack yourself.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In last week’s Unhitched, Ed and Arlene Petty discussed some of the issues that led to their divorce after 28 years of marriage, including her feelings of discontent after their last child left for college (“When Nest Emptied, Discontent Entered”). As a follow-up, we asked a couples therapist about the role of expectations in a marriage. Did you face a similar issue in your divorce? Or were you faced with other challenges? If so, we’d like to hear from you for this series.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/booming/10unhitched-booming-empty/10unhitched-booming-empty-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/booming/10unhitched-booming-empty/10unhitched-booming-empty-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/booming/10unhitched-booming-empty/10unhitched-booming-empty-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 752, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/boo