rd_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3426dc87-537c-551a-820d-57c5394d8f55'}, {'abstract': 'Was Jefferson Davis really a better protector of habeas corpus than Abraham Lincoln?', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/the-great-writ-north-and-south/', 'snippet': 'Was Jefferson Davis really a better protector of habeas corpus than Abraham Lincoln?', 'lead_paragraph': 'During the Civil War both the federal and Confederate governments had to deal with a pressing question far from the battlefield: how to balance the rights enshrined in their respective constitutions against effectively fighting the war. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Great Writ, North and South', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Habeas Corpus', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Jefferson F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T18:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank J. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e5efba14-f741-5409-b0ac-cef773ab7cba', 'word_count': 1573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e5efba14-f741-5409-b0ac-cef773ab7cba'}, {'abstract': 'Many domestic workers from the Philippines are still waiting for news of families left behind in areas struck by Typhoon Haiyan.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/for-filipino-workers-abroad-there-is-nothing-worse-than-the-waiting/', 'snippet': 'Many domestic workers from the Philippines are still waiting for news of families left behind in areas struck by Typhoon Haiyan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing I read about the typhoon was actually on Facebook. Posted on one of my friend’s status updates was something about the wind getting stronger in our part of the Philippines. After that, all of my friends began to panic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 626, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 626}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 835, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/style/motherlode-typhoon/motherlode-typhoon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Filipino Workers Abroad, ‘There Is Nothing Worse Than the Waiting’', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Typhoon Haiyan (2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Singapore', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T18:04:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': "By Marifel Mosquera as told to Rob O'Brien", 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/080a7da8-474d-5dac-bd2f-8c3216c49c9e', 'word_count': 698, 'uri': 'nyt://article/080a7da8-474d-5dac-bd2f-8c3216c49c9e'}, {'abstract': 'In this lesson, students will apply inferencing skills to create comics, videos, or “missing chapters” showing what happens after their favorite literary works end.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/speculation-spoilers-and-sequels-making-inferences-to-predict-what-happens-next/', 'snippet': 'In this lesson, students will apply inferencing skills to create comics, videos, or “missing chapters” showing what happens after their favorite literary works end.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Overview | How do great authors build suspense and keep us engaged? What skills do readers need to make predictions? In this lesson, students will discuss how they “read” their favorite television shows in order to make predictions about what will happen, then apply these skills to speculate about what happens to literary characters after their favorite novels or plays end. Finally, they will use the inferences they gain through close reading to create imagined futures for these characters in comic strips, next chapters, letters, journals or videos.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 828, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 828}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 743, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1485, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/10/arts/10CURTAIN1-LN/10CURTAIN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Speculation, Spoilers and Sequels: Making Inferences to Predict What Happens Next', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print