zation': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/315f6de0-3c26-5e37-9cad-14ca74c07224', 'word_count': 367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/315f6de0-3c26-5e37-9cad-14ca74c07224'}, {'abstract': 'The Web services part of Amazon announced two businesses aimed at increasing the number of people it touches — one to make iPads and similar devices work like desktops, and the other to bring high-definition gaming to any mobile device.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/amazon-web-services-gets-personal-and-pretty/', 'snippet': 'The Web services part of Amazon announced two businesses aimed at increasing the number of people it touches — one to make iPads and similar devices work like desktops, and the other to bring high-definition gaming to any mobile device.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAS VEGAS — Amazon Web Services, the cloud-computing part of Amazon’s sprawling online empire, is known for its globe-spanning system of millions of computer servers, data storage systems and complex software, estimated to be five times larger than 14 other cloud computing providers combined.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/technology/14bits-aws/14bits-aws-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/technology/14bits-aws/14bits-aws-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 801}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/technology/14bits-aws/14bits-aws-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/technology/14bits-aws/14bits-aws-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's