 'headline': {'main': 'Acrostic', 'kicker': 'November 17, 2013', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acrostic Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T18:22:58+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Crosswords & Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'subsection_name': 'Premium', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/935db204-4ce7-5566-9649-6025a1d1f550', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/935db204-4ce7-5566-9649-6025a1d1f550'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Kane’s new book won the 2012 Donald Hall Prize in Poetry.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/poems-against-loss-joan-naviyuk-kane-talks-about-hyperboreal/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Kane’s new book won the 2012 Donald Hall Prize in Poetry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The poems of Joan Naviyuk Kane are lyrical blasts from a far northern landscape of history and myth. From the first lines of her second book, “Hyperboreal,” just published by the University of Pittsburgh Press, Ms. Kane transports us: “Arnica nods heavy-headed on the bruised slope./Peaks recede in all directions, in heat-haze,/Evening in my recollection.” The poet Arthur Sze, who picked the book for the 2012 Donald Hall Prize in Poetry, calls her poems “vivid, disturbing and mysterious.” Ms. Kane, 36, is Inuit/Inupiaq and lives a few miles from where she grew up in Anchorage. Her family originally came from King Island and Mary’s Igloo, Alaska. Recruited by Harvard, she attended the university as an undergraduate, and then earned an M.F.A. from Columbia. Below are excerpts from an email interview.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 744, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 744}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 826, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1197, 'width': 965, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/books/14kane/14kane-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poems Against Loss: Joan Naviyuk Kane Talks About ‘Hyperboreal’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T18:25:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dana Jennings', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dana', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jennings', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b049b1d6-053c-5567-937f-09706400311c', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b049b1d6-053c-5567-937f-09706400311c'}, {'abstract': 'Senators raised few questions about the qualifications of Janet L. Yellen, the nominee for Federal Reserve chairwoman, but criticized the central bank’s policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/business/economy/fed-itself-is-focus-of-janet-yellens-confirmation-hearing.html', 'snippet': 'Senators raised few questions about the qualifications of Janet L. Yellen, the nominee for Federal Reserve chairwoman, but criticized the central bank’s policies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The questions that Janet L. Yellen faced on Thursday from senators considering her nomination to lead the Federal Reserve made two things fairly clear: The job is hers, and it’s not going to be easy.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Yellen Hearing, Senators Push for Fed Changes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Focus Is on Economy At Yellen Hearing: Senators Express\r\nFrustration\r\nAt Slow Growth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appelbaum, Binyamin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Banking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T18:31:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Binyamin Appelbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Binyamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Appelbaum', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef88ee7c-31a6-52ed-9491-47fb38f7f684', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef88ee7c-31a6-52ed-9491-47fb38f7f684'}, {'abstract': 'Genevieve Sabourin, an aspiring actress who said she had a brief affair with the actor three years ago, was sentenced to 210 days in jail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/nyregion/woman-is-found-guilty-of-stalking-alec-baldwin.html', 'snippet': 'Genevieve Sabourin, an aspiring actress who said she had a brief affair with the actor three years ago, was sentenced to 210 days in jail.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After a week of courtroom drama, featuring a star turn from Alec Baldwin and tearful histrionics from a woman accused of stalking him, it was a judge who had the last and defining word on Thursday: guilty on all charges.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/nyregion/baldwin-1/baldwin-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 448, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/nyregion/baldwin-1/baldwin-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 448}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/nyregion/baldwin-1/baldwin-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/nyregion/baldwin-1/baldwin-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 1776, 'subType': 'su