P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T19:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Cain Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': 'Cain', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f0dcf34-4cd9-59d0-a703-6152bb3e4259', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f0dcf34-4cd9-59d0-a703-6152bb3e4259'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition at the American Museum of Natural History explores poison from many points of view, from the world of literature and history to the world of science and medicine.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/arts/design/the-power-of-poison-at-american-museum-of-natural-history.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition at the American Museum of Natural History explores poison from many points of view, from the world of literature and history to the world of science and medicine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Vampire bat saliva and a zebra longwing butterfly, devil’s gardens and fossilized fish teeth, golden-frog secretions and the sap of a manchineel tree: Pity the poor witches of Shakespeare’s “Macbeth” who had to settle for “tooth of wolf” and “tongue of dog.” Their boiling caldron makes an appearance in an exhibition opening Saturday at the American Museum of Natural History — “The Power of Poison“ — and so do they, black robed and stirring the pot as green smoke rises. But they don’t possess even a fraction of the esoteric ingredients the museum has assembled for this elaborate show, nor do they have the museum’s powers to brew something so alluring out of such potentially grim material. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15POISONS_SPAN/15POISONS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Touch of the Toxic, for Good or Ill', 'kicker': 'Museum Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Touch Of the Toxic, For Good or Ill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rothstein, Edward', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'valu