eve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reddicliffe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c6b8cfa-f777-5abb-98ae-a763ee40a9a3', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c6b8cfa-f777-5abb-98ae-a763ee40a9a3'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/the-gun-report-november-14-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no official set of criteria or definition for a mass shooting, but the F.B.I. considers mass murder to be a spasm of violence perpetrated by one person that takes at least four lives in the same location. By that metric, we’ve already had several just this month. And if the wounded are counted, the tally grows even higher.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 14, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T19:37:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd6b6ad-86e9-5f65-b94f-9bb3a7ec9002', 'word_count': 1391, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd6b6ad-86e9-5f65-b94f-9bb3a7ec9002'}, {'abstract': 'Did the president lie when he said that Americans who like their policies would be able to keep them?', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/obamas-health-care-promise/', 'snippet': 'Did the president lie when he said that Americans who like their policies would be able to keep them?', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are important questions about whether the fix President Obama offered today for Americans whose insurance policies were cancelled will help them, whether it will hinder the broad goals of the health insurance reform law, and whether it will satisfy the opponents of reform.\xa0 We will start to address them later on the editorial page.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Health Care Promise', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T19:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d1e50b4d-5e0e-50ff-ade4-a0be092924a2', 'word_count': 499, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d1e50b4d-5e0e-50ff-ade4-a0be092924a2'}, {'abstract': 'For its latest set-top box, Apple recommends an Internet connection of at least 2.5 megabits per second. Plus, how to shed the “Recommended for You” notification on Android.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/technology/personaltech/getting-up-to-speed-with-an-apple-tv-and-ditching-android-widgets.html', 'snippet': 'For its latest set-top box, Apple recommends an Internet connection of at least 2.5 megabits per second. Plus, how to shed the “Recommended for You” notification on Android.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. How fast does my Internet connection have to be to stream movies on an Apple TV?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting Up to Speed With an Apple TV, and Ditching Android Widgets', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Android (Operating System)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T19:48:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9b920cd-388e-5705-810a-7a85199542a8', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9b920cd-388e-5705-810a-7a85199542a8'}, {'abstract': 'The positive effect on economic growth would most likely overstate the benefits, because of the way gross domestic product is measured.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/outsourcing-chores-the-economic-impact/', 'snippet': 'The positive effect on economic growth would most likely overstate the benefits, because of the way gross domestic product is measured.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My It’s the Economy column last Sunday explained how you too can live like an economist: by outsourcing lower-value services in order to give yourself more time to work, do rewarding things with your children or otherwise play. Outsourcing household production usually smacks of something only a hedge-fund billionaire or perhaps the Monopoly Man would do, but it is probably a good investment for plenty of middle-class people, too, since doing so can improve their future expected earnings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Outsourcing Chores: The Economic Impact', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economics (Theory and Philosophy)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gross Domestic Product', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Outsourcing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T19:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Rampell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rampell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5c5052c2-e92f-5062-b8b5-9d2e27201fc7', 'word_count': 313, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c5052c2-e92f-5062-b8b5-9d2e27201fc7'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama announced a fix to his signature health care law that will allow existing customers to keep their insurance plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/us/100000002552507/selections-from-obama-on-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama announced a fix to his signature health care law that will allow existing customers to keep their insurance plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Obama announced a fix to his signature health care law that will allow existing customers to keep their insurance plans.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/us/politics/Obama/Obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/us/politics/Obama/Obama-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'j