re at the Brooklyn Public Library will present readings by emerging African-born writers on Saturday at its central location.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/nyregion/young-african-writers-hold-forth-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'The Dweck Center for Contemporary Culture at the Brooklyn Public Library will present readings by emerging African-born writers on Saturday at its central location.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Miser has always felt that New York’s public libraries constitute the kind of cultural and civic asset that’s so obviously valuable yet often taken for granted. In a city of world-class art institutions, museums, performance halls, film festivals and athletic stadiums, some of the most vital programming unfolds among the stacks, as it were, in branches across the five boroughs, and is typically free and open to the public.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '35', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Young African Writers Hold Forth in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Public Library', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'St George Library Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T20:26:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By A. C. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/10f0bc21-21b9-5c3b-9fad-b7d50f013e7f', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10f0bc21-21b9-5c3b-9fad-b7d50f013e7f'}, {'abstract':