tween Paris St.-Germain and Anderlecht, United States midfielder Sacha Kljestan, who is a mainstay for the Belgian team, found himself chirping back and forth with the P.S.G. star Zlatan Ibrahimovic.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 775, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 775}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1587, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15USMT/15USMT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kljestan Seeks to Impress U.S. With His Play, Not His Mustache', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "United States Men's National Soccer Team", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kljestan, Sacha', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dempsey, Clint', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klinsmann, Jurgen', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahimovic, Zlatan', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T20:37:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fca1af1-6486-5d87-a466-63b9f13744ae', 'word_count': 636, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fca1af1-6486-5d87-a466-63b9f13744ae'}, {'abstract': 'CBS said it would broadcast a two-hour special on Feb. 9, the date the Beatles made their live American television debut in 1964.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/50-years-later-cbs-and-grammys-to-commemorate-beatles-appearance-on-ed-sullivan/', 'snippet': 'CBS said it would broadcast a two-hour special on Feb. 9, the date the Beatles made their live American television debut in 1964.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The 50th anniversary of the Beatles’ first visit to the United States is shaping up to be nearly as noisy as the original event, but without crowds of screaming fans congregating at Kennedy Airport and the Plaza Hotel and, of course, without the Beatles themselves. CBS announced on Thursday that it would show a two-hour special, “The Night That Changed America: A Grammy Salute to the Beatles,” on Feb. 9 at 8 p.m. – the same date and time slot (and on the same network) as “The Ed Sullivan Show,” on which the Beatles made their live American television debut. The show will include covers of Beatles songs by current stars (none of which have been announced) in performances to be taped Jan. 27.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '50 Years Later, CBS and Grammys to Commemorate Beatles’ Appearance on ‘Ed Sullivan’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Ed', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatles, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T20:39:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70b5648f-c824-5743-a3bf-5b84db817dbb', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70b5648f-c824-5743-a3bf-5b84db817dbb'}, {'abstract': 'Doris Kearns Goodwin’s “Bully Pulpit” is built around two relationships: one between the reformist politicians Theodore Roosevelt and William Howard Taft, and the other between power and the press.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/books/review/doris-kearns-goodwins-bully-pulpit.html', 'snippet': 'Doris Kearns Goodwin’s “Bully Pulpit” is built around two relationships: one between the reformist politicians Theodore Roosevelt and William Howard Taft, and the other between power and the press.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you find the grubby spectacle of today’s Washington cause for shame and despair — and, really, how could you not? — then I suggest you turn off the TV and board Doris Kearns Goodwin’s latest time machine. Let her transport you back to the turn of the 20th century, to a time when this country had politicians of stature and conscience, when the public believed that government could right great wrongs, when, before truncated attention spans, a 50,000-word exposé of corruption could sell out magazines and galvanize a reluctant Congress. The villains seemed bigger, too, or at least more brazen — industrial barons and political bosses who monopolized entire industries, strangled entire cities. And “change” was not just a slogan. “There are but a handful of times in the history of our country,” Goodwin writes in her introduction, “when there occurs a transformation so remarkable that a molt seems to take place, and an altered country begins to emerge.” The years covered in this book are such a time. It makes a pretty grand story.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2/1117-bks-KELLER-sub2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Heroes and Crusaders', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Heroes and Crusaders', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keller, Bill', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Bully Pulpit: Theodore Roosevelt, William Howard Taft, and the Golden Age of Journalism (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodwin, Doris Kearns', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T20:40:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Keller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Keller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d04f899a-3307-5ce4-9ac9-b066c112ea5b', 'word_count': 2544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d04f899a-3307-5ce4-9ac9-b066c112ea5b'}, {'abstract': 'There were no speeches at a memorial for Lou Reed held at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/at-memorial-for-lou-reed-just-music/', 'snippet': 'There were no speeches at a memorial for Lou Reed held at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lou Reed lived what was often a loud rock ‘n’ roll life filled with loud rock ‘n’ roll songs. So it was only fitting that an outdoor memorial service held in Manhattan on Thursday began with an unannounced burst of guitar feedback, startling pigeons and passers-by alike, before it coalesced into the opening chords of his song “The Blue Mask,” on which Mr. Reed defiantly sang, “I loathe and despise repentance.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At Memorial for Lou Reed, Just Music', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Paying Tribute to Reed, With Nothing but Reed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Lou (1942-2013)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Velvet Underground (Music Group)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T20:45:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dave Itzkoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dave', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Itzkoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4c9fd99e-f5a5-5b4f-b5e3-1863ed4db811', 'word_count': 304, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4c9fd99e-f5a5-5b4f-b5e3-1863ed4db811'}, {'abstract': 'An unprecedented continental-scale war game was intended to determine how prepared the nation is for a cyberattack against electric systems.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/us/coast-to-coast-simulating-onslaught-against-power-grid.html', 'snippet': 'An unprecedented continental-scale war game was intended to determine how prepared the nation is for a cyberattack against electric systems.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In windowless rooms from here to California, nearly 10,000 electrical engineers, cybersecurity specialists, utility executives and F.B.I. agents furiously grappled over 48 hours with an unseen “enemy” who tried to turn out the lights across America. The enemy injected computer viruses into grid control systems, bombed transformers and substations and knocked out power lines by the dozen.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Attack Ravages Power Grid. (Just a Test.)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Attack Ravages Power Grid. (Just a Test.)', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberattacks and Hackers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Security and Warning Systems', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'North American Electric Reliability Corp', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T20:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32699713-89e1-568c-8481-ed3dd17d7867', 'word_count': 1019, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32699713-89e1-568c-8481-ed3dd17d7867'}, {'abstract': 'Novart, Bordeaux’s biennial art and performance festival, will showcase the work of Michael E. Smith–and there will be dance parties open to the public as well.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/in-bor