nippet': 'The police had confronted the man to arrest him on a weapons charge at the suburban Milwaukee hospital.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Police in a Milwaukee suburb shot and wounded a man brandishing a handgun inside a children’s hospital on Thursday after officers had tried to arrest him on a warrant inside the hospital’s neonatal care unit, the authorities said. No one else was injured during the shooting.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Police Shoot Man Fleeing With Gun in Wisconsin Children’s Hospital', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wisconsin: Police Shoot Man in Hospital', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Milwaukee (Wis)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Timothy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wisconsin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T21:22:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57df02af-cdd6-51e8-8b76-909c3b7ec827', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57df02af-cdd6-51e8-8b76-909c3b7ec827'}, {'abstract': 'After being called out by a publishers’ group, Rap Genius revealed that it already had a deal with Sony/ATV Music Publishing and would pursue other deals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/business/media/rap-genius-says-it-will-seek-licenses-for-lyrics.html', 'snippet': 'After being called out by a publishers’ group, Rap Genius revealed that it already had a deal with Sony/ATV Music Publishing and would pursue other deals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rap Genius, a website that was accused by music publishers on Monday of reprinting thousands of song lyrics without permission, revealed that it had a major licensing deal all along — and also indicated that the site was likely to pursue more such deals in the future rather than fight with publishers over copyright.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Rap Genius Says It Will Seek Licenses for Lyrics', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'RapGenius.com', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'SONY/ATV Music Publishing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "National Music Publishers' Assn", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copyrights and Copyright Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T21:23:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Sisario', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sisario', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaeb1054-fc4b-5e19-b5dc-9d0fa3818d55', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaeb1054-fc4b-5e19-b5dc-9d0fa3818d55'}, {'abstract': 'Robbie Rogers, a midfielder with the Los Angeles Galaxy, talked about his decision to come out publicly and his excitement about the future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/robbie-rogers-reflects-on-season-in-spotlight-as-gay-athlete.html', 'snippet': 'Robbie Rogers, a midfielder with the Los Angeles Galaxy, talked about his decision to come out publicly and his excitement about the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robbie Rogers generally prefers to avoid reminiscing. Even this week, as he considered all that had happened over the past 12 months — his decision to announce his sexual orientation, his brief retirement and his return to soccer as the first openly gay male athlete in a prominent North American professional league — he interspersed his memories with sizable dollops of excitement about what lies ahead.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 635, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1270, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/sports/soccer/15rogers/15rogers-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rogers Reflects on Season in the Spotlight as a Gay Athlete', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rogers Reflects on a Season in the Spotlight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borden, Sam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogers, Robbie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Galaxy (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T21:24:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Borden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Borden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/effb75cb-fdb3-50f2-a372-8d627c108a30', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/effb75cb-fdb3-50f2-a372-8d627c108a30'}, {'abstract': 'Sean Glass, founder of Win Music and a frequent D.J. at tech events, sees Internet services as the future of an industry it devastated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/nyregion/record-label-owner-playing-along-with-tech.html', 'snippet': 'Sean Glass, founder of Win Music and a frequent D.J. at tech events, sees Internet services as the future of an industry it devastated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Alan Chan, the chief executive of Bre.ad, a link-shortening service, gave himself a 30th-birthday party in October, the event took place on a Sunday night — hangovers be damned — in a stylish loft in SoHo. Mr. Chan, who had just sold Bre.ad to Yahoo, had arranged, in the extravagant manner of the New York City tech world, for the Sugarhill Gang, an ’80s-era hip-hop group, to perform. Equally in keeping with local start-up fashion, he had also arranged for his gathering to be managed musically by the D.J. and independent-record-label owner Sean Glass.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17DJ_SPAN/17DJ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Record Label Owner Playing Along With Tech', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Playing Along With Tech', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Disc Jockeys', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Audio Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glass, Sean', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T21:33:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42e8fb60-106f-548f-bb90-c07146946bfd', 'word_count': 1341, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42e8fb60-106f-548f-bb90-c07146946bfd'}, {'abstract': 'The business that would be separated focuses on selling surgical and anti-infection products and medical devices for pain management, respiratory and digestive health.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/kimberly-clark-to-spin-off-health-care-unit/', 'snippet': 'The business that would be separated focuses on selling surgical and anti-infection products and medical devices for pain management, respiratory and digestive health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kimberly-Clark said on Thursday that it would pursue a potential spinoff its health care business, becoming the latest company to slim down its operations to help bolster its stock price.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/business/dbpix-kimberly/dbpix-kimberly-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy'