, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cook County (Ill)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Janssen Pharmaceutica', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Purdue Pharma', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Endo Pharmaceuticals Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:17:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a0988c5-dd81-557c-8e66-e9a4b52f4ae0', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a0988c5-dd81-557c-8e66-e9a4b52f4ae0'}, {'abstract': 'German authorities, trying to speed the identification of some of 1,400 works apparently lost during the Nazi era, said that they would soon begin posting information online.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/arts/design/information-on-art-trove-to-start-going-online.html', 'snippet': 'German authorities, trying to speed the identification of some of 1,400 works apparently lost during the Nazi era, said that they would soon begin posting information online.', 'lead_paragraph': 'German authorities, trying to speed the identification of some of 1,400 works apparently lost during the Nazi era, said that they would soon begin posting information on 590 of those with questionable provenances on the website lostart.de, a database of art looted or missing since World War II. “Publication will start next week,” according to a statement issued by the Culture Ministry that quoted Ingeborg Berggreen-Merkel, who spent decades in government service helping to run cultural institutions in Germany and who was appointed to lead a group of art experts tasked with researching the history of the works. So far 25 works have been posted. “Possible rightful claimants can now more quickly identify missing art works and in relevant cases make their claims heard,” the statement said. Such news is welcome to claimants like David Toren, an 88-year-old New Yorker who recognized one of the works, a painting by Max Liebermann, as having once hung in the home of a great-uncle. State prosecutors took possession of the art in February from the apartment of Cornelius Gurlitt as part of a tax case.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Information on Art Trove to Start Going Online', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Information on Art Trove To Start Going Online', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Arts and Antiquities Looting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:22:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alison Smale and Patricia Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Patricia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/dfc47faa-a615-530d-9cd1-fb7bf5557a10', 'word_count': 182, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dfc47faa-a615-530d-9cd1-fb7bf5557a10'}, {'abstract': 'After Thomas Hooven graduated from medical school, his girlfriend of 12 years ended their relationship. It was only three weeks befo