 New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ada4c4e-2786-5887-b554-1467a71cb231', 'word_count': 13, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ada4c4e-2786-5887-b554-1467a71cb231'}, {'abstract': 'Left by his fiancée, a doctor rebuilds himself in the company of his patients.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/fashion/Modern-Love-Nursing-a-Wound-in-an-Appropriate-Place-.html', 'snippet': 'Left by his fiancée, a doctor rebuilds himself in the company of his patients.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I started my pediatrics residency on the cardiology unit, which was appropriate: my heart had a giant hole in it. Just after I graduated from medical school, as I was moving into my fiancée’s New York apartment, she ended our relationship. We went out to dinner that night, and after we came home, she told me we were through.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 766, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 766}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 802, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1604, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2017/10/06/fashion/17MODERNLOVE/17MODERNLOVE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Nursing a Wound in an Appropriate Setting', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nursing a Wound in an Appropriate Setting', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hooven, Thomas', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Courtship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Modern Love (Times Column)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:31:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thomas Hooven', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thomas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hooven', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0136929f-311b-5268-83fd-c18a478097a3', 'word_count': 1518, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0136929f-311b-5268-83fd-c18a478097a3'}, {'abstract': '“The Salon: Art & Design” at the Park Avenue Armory has art and antiques from what seems to be every period and place, from Bactrian sculptures to new, exploding furniture.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/arts/design/the-salon-art-design-a-wide-range-at-park-avenue-armory.html', 'snippet': '“The Salon: Art & Design” at the Park Avenue Armory has art and antiques from what seems to be every period and place, from Bactrian sculptures to new, exploding furniture.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The Salon: Art & Design,” the smart young fair at the Park Avenue Armory this weekend, is doing an excellent job of splitting the difference between the auction-house randomness and white-cube-gallery control. As its title suggests, it is wide open in terms of material — art, craft, design, antiques from any period or place can be found here. It is up to the dealers to provide the focus, which they do. This means controlled diversity. You can bounce from concentrated views of French Art Deco to early Modern art to pre-Columbian ceramics in one aisle. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 735}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 837, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1673, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15JPSALON2/JPSALON2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Little Bit of Everything in One Place', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Little Bit of Everything in One Place', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANTIQUES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:33:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e9dd950a-828c-5a6d-a100-04c4c147de7c', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e9dd950a-828c-5a6d-a100-04c4c147de7c'}, {'abstract': 'Gougères, little savory French cream puffs seasoned with cheese, can be offered to guests alongside a glass as they arrive for Thanksgiving dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/dining/a-nibble-to-keep-the-wine-company.html', 'snippet': 'Gougères, little savory French cream puffs seasoned with cheese, can be offered to guests alongside a glass as they arrive for Thanksgiving dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the Thanksgiving wine tasting, we started on the drinks before the food was served. There’s a good chance we’ll do that at home, too. But with the idea of offering guests a little something alongside a glass as they arrive for Thanksgiving, enough to take the edge off without spoiling appetites, I’ll serve gougères, little savory French cream puffs seasoned with cheese. Mine, enriched with cranberries and Cheddar, will pay homage to New England instead of Paris. I’ve made them already. They’re in the freezer, and they’ll be warmed in the oven before I enlist a granddaughter to pass them from a napkin-lined basket.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1452, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/dining/20PAIR_SPAN/20PAIR_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Nibble to Keep the Wine Company', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pairings', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name'