le occupies the foreground. By surrealistic contrast, the immediate background is filled with the smoking wreckage of bombed buildings, where a few pedestrians pass by. While the title obliquely explains, “Beirut Residents Continue to Flock to Southern Neighborhoods,” the impression you get is of obnoxious rich kids out for a sensation-seeking drive.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Poignant Images, With Posterity the Ultimate Winner', 'kicker': 'Art Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poignant Images, With Posterity the Ultimate Winner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Museum', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Johnson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Johnson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/178b1a09-693a-5656-aa71-688c0c6ed9c3', 'word_count': 972, 'uri': 'nyt://article/178b1a09-693a-5656-aa71-688c0c6ed9c3'}, {'abstract': 'The cultural movement called Afrofuturism is the subject of a new show at the Studio Museum in Harlem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/11/15/arts/design/20131115_AFROFUTURISM.html', 'snippet': 'The cultural movement called Afrofuturism is the subject of a new show at the Studio Museum in Harlem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cultural movement called Afrofuturism is the subject of a new show at the Studio Museum in Harlem