7-885c89454bca'}, {'abstract': 'Bulgari opened the doors of its Rome headquarters and nearby laboratory to T for a rare look at how its one-of-a-kind and limited collections of jewelry come together.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/visiting-the-source-where-bulgaris-rare-baubles-come-to-life/', 'snippet': 'Bulgari opened the doors of its Rome headquarters and nearby laboratory to T for a rare look at how its one-of-a-kind and limited collections of jewelry come together.', 'lead_paragraph': 'var data;function jsonSlideshowCallback(response){data = response;}NYTD.options = {source: data,cropType: \'blog480\',appendTo: \'fullScreenSlideShow\',showHeadLine: \'false\', renderstyle: "embeddedSlideShowTmag"}', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where Bulgari’s Rare Baubles Come to Life', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Visiting The Source: Bulgari', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jewels and Jewelry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bulgari SpA', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jaipur (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:54:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rocky Casale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rocky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Casale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c9ca7be-3d58-542d-b373-c8df21fbfb10', 'word_count': 568, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c9ca7be-3d58-542d-b373-c8df21fbfb10'}, {'abstract': 'Will Rawls dives deep into the folklore of the Balkans, with “The Planet-Eaters,” at the Chocolate Factory.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/arts/dance/will-rawls-performs-the-planet-eaters-at-chocolate-factory.html', 'snippet': 'Will Rawls dives deep into the folklore of the Balkans, with “The Planet-Eaters,” at the Chocolate Factory.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Does folk dance have a place in contemporary culture? The intriguing question came to the choreographer Will Rawls after a 2008 life-changing trip to the Balkans. While there, he began thinking about using folklore as a way to discover, in him, a new kind of dancer that could embody both the present and tradition. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/RAWLS/RAWLS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hoofbeats by the Sea', 'kicker': 'Dance Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hoofbeats by the Sea Mix With the Warding Off of Evil Spirits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chocolate Factory, The', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rawls, Will', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:54:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gia Kourlas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kourlas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8eca9ce-f284-57bf-867b-fd619c4090bd', 'word_count': 438, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8eca9ce-f284-57bf-867b-fd619c4090bd'}, {'abstract': 'A somewhat-changed Paramore still followed Hayley Williams’ energetic lead with its new songs at Madison Square Garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/arts/music/paramore-plays-madison-square-garden.html', 'snippet': 'A somewhat-changed Paramore still followed Hayley Williams’ energetic lead with its new songs at Madison Square Garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fist pumping, head banging, Finger pointing, high kicking, jumping, racing around the stage and leading arena singalongs, Hayley Williams was in her element when Paramore performed on Wednesday night at Madison Square Garden. She was the petite, orange-haired, perpetually animated embodiment of the narrator of her songs, who faces down and joyfully overpowers one frustration after another, moving from complaints and sarcasm to self-empowerment.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/arts/paramore/paramore-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Orange-Haired Dynamo and Friends Grow Up', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Orange-Haired Dynamo and Friends Grow Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paramore (Music Group)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:55:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cce9d620-f39f-5c6c-8c1c-b8344c351cf0', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cce9d620-f39f-5c6c-8c1c-b8344c351cf0'}, {'abstract': '“Faust,” the concluding installment of the “Men of Power” tetralogy, is Alexander Sokurov’s freehanded adaptation of Goethe’s great allegorical drama.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/movies/faust-is-last-film-in-alexander-sokurovs-men-of-power.html', 'snippet': '“Faust,” the concluding installment of the “Men of Power” tetralogy, is Alexander Sokurov’s freehanded adaptation of Goethe’s great allegorical drama.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the end credits, a note identifies “Faust,” Alexander Sokurov’s brooding, hallucinatory, freehanded adaptation of Goethe’s great allegorical drama, as the concluding installment of a four-film sequence, the “Men of Power” tetralogy that also includes “Moloch” (1999), “Taurus” (2001) and “The Sun” (2005). Those movies are intimate and unsettling visits with some of the chief monsters of the 20th century: Hitler, Lenin and Hirohito. What links them is a lust for power at once madly destructive and profoundly lonely. While Mr. Sokurov does not exactly express sympathy for these devils, he refuses to view them as anything other than human.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Muse of Goethe, Intensified', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Muse Of Goethe, Intensified', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sokurov, Aleksandr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Faust (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T22:55:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/67ebff9e-0fa6-5a67-a465-f79b90aa1bee', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67ebff9e-0fa6-5a67-a465-f79b90aa1bee'}, {'abstract': 'Decisions about limiting the exposure to nuts on airlines are often left to the discretion of an individual flight crew, and they are not always willing to comply.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/what-should-airlines-do-about-children-with-peanut-allergies/', 'snippet': 'Decisions about limiting the exposure to nuts on airlines are often left to the discretion of an individual flight crew, and they are not always willing to comply.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lianne and Joshua Mandelbaum never step on an airplane without six vials of injectable epinephrine and a bottle of liquid Benadryl. That’s because Joshua, who is 8 years old, is deathly allergic to peanuts. If exposed to them, he can go into anaphylactic shock. But even with the injectable epinephrine, he needs to be rushed to the hospital for emergency care. This makes flying scary; there aren’t many long-term medical options at 35,000 feet in the sky.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Should Airlines Do About Children With Peanut Allergies?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALLERGIES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Peanuts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T23:00:07+0000', 'document_