organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bcd8d697-35f7-5a59-a45b-5f834dc8b814', 'word_count': 95, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bcd8d697-35f7-5a59-a45b-5f834dc8b814'}, {'abstract': 'In “The Great Beauty,” a sybaritic writer, now 65, considers the essence of Rome and his place in it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/movies/the-great-beauty-starring-toni-servillo.html', 'snippet': 'In “The Great Beauty,” a sybaritic writer, now 65, considers the essence of Rome and his place in it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time you see Jep Gambardella, the Roman sensualist magnificently, poetically adrift in “The Great Beauty,” he has a cigarette clenched in the center of his big, bared, ocher-stained teeth. People are surging all around him, their bodies pulsating to music that has transformed a multitude into an organism that beats like a heart. As he sways amid this delirium, Jep smiles with welcoming arms and lidded eyes, an attitude that brings to mind one of those marble saints scattered around Rome forever locked in rapture. And then Jep joins the dance, surrendering to a throng that, in absorbing him, turns an orgiastic reverie into something like a religious communion.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Glory of Rome, the Sweetness of Life', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Glory of Rome, The Sweetness of Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorrentino, Paolo', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Servillo, Toni', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Beauty (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-14T23:41:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Man