.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Central Intelligence Agency is secretly collecting bulk records of international money transfers handled by companies like Western Union — including transactions into and out of the United States — under the same law that the National Security Agency uses for its huge database of Americans’ phone records, according to current and former government officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1284, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/us/15bulk/15bulk-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'C.I.A. Collects Global Data on Transfers of Money', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'C.I.A. Collects Global Data On Transfers Of Money', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Savage, Charlie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mazzetti, Mark', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'USA PATRIOT Act', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T00:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charlie Savage and Mark Mazzetti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charlie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Savage', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mazzetti', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/424f9f3f-ea04-518e-aaca-5a1376b6f69c', 'word_count': 1209, 'uri': 'nyt://article/424f9f3f-ea04-518e-aaca-5a1376b6f69c'}, {'abstract': 'Is it possible to regularly beat the stock market averages? Robert Shiller, one of this year’s Nobel Prize-winning economists, has it right.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/opinion/rattner-whos-right-on-the-stock-market.html', 'snippet': 'Is it possible to regularly beat the stock market averages? Robert Shiller, one of this year’s Nobel Prize-winning economists, has it right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IF you’ve been wondering whether it’s possible to regularly beat the stock market averages — a natural question with the market at an all-time high — you didn’t get any guidance from the Nobel Prize committee this year: Two of the winning economists disagree on that perennial issue. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 1000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-thumbStandard-v5.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/rattner-contributor/rattner-contributor-thumbLarge-v5.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 