paragraph': 'You’ll forget many of the songs the moment you leave “Bubble Boy,” a musical being given its world premiere by the American Theater Group in Rahway. Still, when you look back on this likable and lightweight show, you’ll probably remember the good time you had when you first heard them.', 'print_section': 'NJ', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/1117ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 331, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/1117ARTSNJ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 331}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/1117ARTSNJ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/1117ARTSNJ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1131, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN/17ARTSNJ1_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘A Bubble Around My Heart’', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | New Jersey', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘A Bubble Around My Heart’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jaworowski, Ken', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hamilton Stage for the Performing Arts (Rahway, NJ)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Cinco', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daurio, Ken', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Perez, Gerianne', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCarrell, Chris', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maguire, Erin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Howes, Benjamin', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sloyer, Gabriel', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paul, Alex Grace', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Theater Group', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T01:18:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/36a002ce-252c-53bb-b726-944981b4e473', 'word_count': 658, 'uri': 'nyt://article/36a002ce-252c-53bb-b726-944981b4e473'}, {'abstract': 'Will inflation phobia tear Europe apart after the establishment of a common currency was supposed to unite the Continent?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/opinion/krugman-the-money-trap.html', 'snippet': 'Will inflation phobia tear Europe apart after the establishment of a common currency was supposed to unite the Continent?', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Greece hit the skids almost four years ago, some analysts (myself included) thought that we might be seeing the beginning of the end for the euro, Europe’s common currency. Others were more optimistic, believing that tough love — temporary aid tied to reform — would soon produce recovery. Both camps were wrong. What we actually got was a rolling crisis that never seems to reach any kind of resolution. Every time Europe seems ready to go over the edge, policy makers find a way to avoid complete disaster. But every time there are hints of true recovery, something else goes wrong.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/paul-krugman/paul-krugman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'capt