ted States Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit embarrassed itself again on Wednesday by reaffirming a hasty and ill-considered decision last month to remove the presiding judge from the court battle over New York City’s stop-and-frisk program and to stay her remedies for the policy’s civil rights violations.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Stop-and-Frisk Case Takes Another Turn', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Stop-and-Frisk Case Takes Another Turn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search and Seizure', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil Rights and Liberties', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scheindlin, Shira A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T02:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ab6f6c6-d945-5d77-a7ad-431bc8db3482', 'word_count': 485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ab6f6c6-d945-5d77-a7ad-431bc8db3482'}, {'abstract': 'Investigators say groups of traders from several major banks may have influenced currency benchmarks to benefit their employers — actions that may not have been illegal but do highlight lax regulation.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/14/u-s-investigates-currency-trades-by-major-banks/', 'snippet': 'Investigators say groups of traders from several major banks may hav