, 'snippet': 'A writer visits Yangon, the country’s former capital city, and finds echoes of the colonial past that inspired “Burmese Days.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Myanmar, a long-isolated nation now opening up to the world after decades of brutal military rule, one still finds romantic echoes of the former British colony that inspired the young author to pen his first novel, ‘Burmese Days.’', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Myanmar, Retracing George Orwell’s Steps', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TDesign', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Osborne', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Osborne', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6892500-fa6b-56f0-a413-d62e0768a307', 'word_count': 2989, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6892500-fa6b-56f0-a413-d62e0768a307'}, {'abstract': 'With her unexpected arrangements of objects, the furniture and interior designer brings the English countryside to her London house.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/t-magazine/the-well-composed-life-of-faye-toogood.html', 'snippet': 'With her unexpected arrangements of objects, the furniture and interior designer brings the English countryside to her London house.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer Faye Toogood finds exceptional beauty in unexpected arrangements of objects, and uses them to create installations for fashion houses — and her own house.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Well-Composed Life of Faye Toogood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '20