 Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/755dfa3b-79f5-5ae4-a8f2-e268820ce0dd', 'word_count': 908, 'uri': 'nyt://article/755dfa3b-79f5-5ae4-a8f2-e268820ce0dd'}, {'abstract': 'One year after taking leadership of the party, Xi Jinping is looking like an assertive president who sits well above his six colleagues on the Politburo Standing Committee, a sharp contrast to his predecessor, Hu Jintao.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/xi-in-godfather-mold-looks-assertive-and-even-imperial/', 'snippet': 'One year after taking leadership of the party, Xi Jinping is looking like an assertive president who sits well above his six colleagues on the Politburo Standing Committee, a sharp contrast to his predecessor, Hu Jintao.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The president of China, Xi Jinping, has admitted to watching “The Godfather,” and this week he proved he could be a shrewd student of one of that film’s themes: the art of amassing and applying power in a small, secretive circle of men.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Xi, in ‘Godfather’ Mold, Looks Assertive and Even Imperial', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorbachev, Mikhail S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hu Jintao', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mao Zedong', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston University', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Politburo Standing Committee of the Communist Party of China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T05:40:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/381933b7-08bc-5853-ba3c-f871eb790663', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/381933b7-08bc-5853-ba3c-f871eb790663'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '5:45 P.M. (Sho2) OUT OF SIGHT (1998) In this slick noir caper directed by Steven Soderbergh and based on the novel by Elmore Leonard, Jack Foley (George Clooney, above), the most charming bank robber you will ever meet, escapes from prison to join his partner (Ving Rhames) for one last heist: to rob the home of their former prison mate (Albert Brooks). Along the way they cross paths with Karen Sisco (Jennifer Lopez), a federal marshal who becomes caught between attraction and professional responsibility when she and Jack begin to wonder what could happen if only they had different occupations. “The hard-boiled beauty of the cinematography (by Elliot Davis, who has shot three previous Soderbergh films) brings out the story’s own innate color and creates a warmly inviting backdrop for the central star-crossed romance,” Janet Maslin wrote in The New York Times. “The film’s sleek moodiness and visual sophistication are so effective that there’s even a scene here that makes Detroit look like the most romantic city in the world.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s on Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/29806984-0e5a-5f24-80c9-b7aaf6253a6c', 'word_count': 768, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29806984-0e5a-5f24-80c9-b7aaf6253a6c'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/news-quiz-november-15-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 15, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T06:30:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ea99000-0ac7-576a-8b13-0a274825e666', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ea99000-0ac7-576a-8b13-0a274825e666'}, {'abstract': 'The final five-day test match for Sachin Tendulkar prompted a full meltdown of ecstatic prose, as scribes all over the country tried to capture the final bittersweet moments of the cricket giant’s career.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/hearts-throbbed-minds-wavered-as-tendulkar-began-final-match/', 'snippet': 'The final five-day test match for Sachin Tendulkar prompted a full meltdown of ecstatic prose, as scribes all over the country tried to capture the final bittersweet moments of the cricket giant’s career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Even under ordinary circumstances, India’s newspaper writers are not known for bottling up their emotions. But the last cricket outing of Sachin Tendulkar this week prompted a full meltdown of ecstatic prose, as scribes all over the country tried to capture the final bittersweet moments of a career that has provided one of India’s most satisfying plotlines of the last two decades.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/world/asia/15-sachin-IndiaInk/15-sachin-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/world/asia/15-sachin-IndiaInk/15-sachin-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/world/asia/15-sachin-IndiaInk/15-sachin-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 738, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/world/asia/15-sachin-IndiaInk/15-sachin-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1475, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'super