your community or around the world?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/what-would-you-invent-to-make-the-world-a-better-place-2/', 'snippet': 'What problem would you try to address, either in your community or around the world?', 'lead_paragraph': 'An auto mechanic invented a tool to make births safer. He literally dreamed it up one night after watching a YouTube video about how to extract a lost cork from a wine bottle. If all goes well, doctors hope the inexpensive device might save lives — potentially millions of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/14/world/jp-birth1-LN/jp-birth1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Would You Invent to Make the World a Better Place?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T10:00:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef764dc3-5910-597c-a69c-38b33fcfcac1', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef764dc3-5910-597c-a69c-38b33fcfcac1'}, {'abstract': 'The photographs of Saul Leiter, who is the subject of a new film, depict gorgeous, poignant and fleeting moments in New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/beauty-in-the-everyday/', 'snippet': 'The photographs of Saul Leiter, who is the subject of a new film, depict gorgeous, poignant and fleeting moments in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is something so poignant about Saul Leiter’s work that looking at it can feel like taking a dart to the heart. Drenched in luxuriant, saturated colors, the images instantly transport the viewer into the photographer’s shoes: peeping from beneath an awning to a snow-swept street, or through a befogged cafe window, weeping with condensation, to a man taking pause on a wintry sidewalk. Intimate and empathetic, Mr. Leiter’s photographs relay what all New Yorkers know about their roaring, daunting home: that life in the city is filled with stolen glimpses and fleeting, quietly personal and often gorgeous moments.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Beauty in the Everyday', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'pr