slature here, paint faded and fell from the last mural José Clemente Orozco completed before he died. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mexico’s Not-So-Favorite Son', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mexico’s Not-So-Favorite Son', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cave, Damien', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Orozco, Jose Clemente', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico City (Mexico)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guadalajara (Mexico)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T15:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Damien Cave', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Damien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cave', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9651e91e-ffe4-58ba-a334-7c50474aef0d', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9651e91e-ffe4-58ba-a334-7c50474aef0d'}, {'abstract': 'Times critics on “Nebraska,” “The Great Beauty” and “Faust.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/video-reviews-of-nebraska-the-great-beauty-and-faust/', 'snippet': 'Times critics on “Nebraska,” “The Great Beauty” and “Faust.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In this week’s video, Times critics share their thoughts on Alexander Payne’s bittersweet comedy “Nebraska,” Paolo Sorrentino’s “The Great Beauty” and Alexander Sokurov’s version of “Faust.” See all of this week’s reviews.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Video Reviews of ‘Nebraska,’ ‘The Great Beauty’ and ‘Faust’', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Payne, Alexander', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sokurov, Aleksandr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sorrentino, Paolo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T15:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49595bfd-b3bd-5a9b-b786-82f2dd3c6cd4', 'word_count': 32, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49595bfd-b3bd-5a9b-b786-82f2dd3c6cd4'}, {'abstract': 'Honesty is the best policy when telling a prospective employer about an ambiguous ending to a previous job. But that doesn’t mean “I was fired!” is the best icebreaker.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/jobs/how-to-explain-that-lost-job.html', 'snippet': 'Honesty is the best policy when telling a prospective employer about an ambiguous ending to a previous job. But that doesn’t mean “I was fired!” is the best icebreaker.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My 27-year-old daughter was fired from a job under confusing circumstances. She had been hired as a project coordinator for a construction management firm. Although she had no background in the field, the company was aware of this and willing to train her. She had a rocky start with a project manager but then was reassigned and had an excellent working relationship with her new manager. At a review she was told, “This job will be yours in a year unless you choose to leave.” Six weeks later, she was terminated, and told she lacked the necessary “skill set.” The project manager she had worked with took a new job elsewhere shortly thereafter. In all, my daughter was there 10 months.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York 