t', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pear', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/20a6bd9f-8336-53b5-9b24-4bf35bd824ef', 'word_count': 1128, 'uri': 'nyt://article/20a6bd9f-8336-53b5-9b24-4bf35bd824ef'}, {'abstract': '“Whoopi Goldberg Presents Moms Mabley” is a documentary recalling the influential and groundbreaking comic whose career was largely unfilmed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/arts/television/whoopi-goldbergs-documentary-on-moms-mabley.html', 'snippet': '“Whoopi Goldberg Presents Moms Mabley” is a documentary recalling the influential and groundbreaking comic whose career was largely unfilmed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With her toothless grin, floppy hat and tell-it-like-it-is persona, Moms Mabley may be one of the most influential comedians you don’t know. She rose to fame in the early decades of the 20th century on the chitlins circuit — the collection of stages around the country that employed black entertainers during segregation — and she would go on to a career that spanned more than 50 years. In that time, she pushed beyond racial and gender barriers, but she drew mainstream attention only starting in the 196os (she died in 1975) and little of her work has survived on film or video. That hasn’t deterred Whoopi Goldberg.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Comedy Pioneer in the Floppy Hat', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Comedy Pioneer in the Floppy Hat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mekado', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 