024af15', 'word_count': 947, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b85ef0f-ec49-5d36-a2ba-25b1e024af15'}, {'abstract': 'Why deregulation might be a better response to cancellations and rate shock than “grandfathering” existing plans.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/what-obamacare-needs-now/', 'snippet': 'Why deregulation might be a better response to cancellations and rate shock than “grandfathering” existing plans.', 'lead_paragraph': '… is not at all the same as what freaking-out Congressional Democrats think they need politically, and what the president tried to provide to them yesterday. That’s because all of the “if you like your plan, you keep your plan” ideas in the wind right now, including the White House’s pledge yesterday to allow/pressure insurers to temporarily extend plans that don’t meet the new law’s specifications, are likely to either do nothing meaningful at all to halt the flood of cancellations, or else exacerbate the threat to Obamacare’s viability that the busted website has created, by siphoning off precisely the healthy, lower-risk enrollees the new system needs to be sustainable.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What Obamacare Needs Now …', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Landrieu, Mary L', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T15:38:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e2e93c1e-042b-59f8-9ac5-786d73a62438', 'word_count': 1001, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e2e93c1e-042b-59f8-9ac5-786d73a62438'}, {'abstract': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/17/realestate/17ressales_graphic.html', 'snippet': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Information on sales in New York, New Jersey and Connecticut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 643, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 643}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 956, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1911, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17re-matrix-image/17re-matrix-image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Residential Sales Around the Region', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island (NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Westchester County (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T15:39:22+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/de485708-7798-56b8-865c-d5f9988442cd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/de485708-7798-56b8-865c-d5f9988442cd'}, {'abstract': 'Flannery O’Connor’s journal addressed to God was written when she was a 20-year-old student at the Iowa Writers’ Workshop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/books/review/flannery-oconnors-prayer-journal.html', 'snippet': 'Flannery O’Connor’s journal addressed to God was written when she was a 20-year-old student at the Iowa Writers’ Workshop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This slender, charming book must be approached with a special tact. To read it feels a little like an intrusion on inwardness itself. The volume contains, alongside a lightly corrected transcription, a facsimile of the Sterling notebook in which Flannery O’Connor, just 20 years old, began a journal addressed to God. Written in her neat hand, it is reproduced complete with the empty final pages (her concluding words are “there is nothing left to say of me”) and not omitting a bit of musical notation floating on the inside of the back cover. The prayers, attempts at prayer and meditations on faith and art contained in it were written in 1946 and 1947, while O’Connor was a student in Iowa. The brilliance that would make her fictions literary classics is fully apparent in them. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/17robinson-3/17robinson-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/17robinson-3/17robinson-3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 724}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/17robinson-3/17robinson-3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/17robinson-3/17robinson-3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/17robinson-3/17robinson-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/books/review/17robinson-3/17robinson-3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna