tter how loving, leaning down to read over one’s shoulder.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/let-go-of-the-college-essay-and-let-your-teenager-speak-for-herself/', 'snippet': 'Nothing is so deadly to the necessary college memoirist’s perspective as Mom or Dad, no matter how loving, leaning down to read over one’s shoulder.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recently I told the story in the Wall Street Journal of a father who offered me, an independent college applications counselor, a $10,000 check to write his son’s college essays. Never mind that his son was standing right there. I didn’t take the check. Instead I took the boy: We fled his father’s Midtown Manhattan office and went for a walk, along sidewalks crowded with people who had gone to Ivy League colleges, non-Ivy League colleges and no colleges at all, to the park, where we could really talk.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/style/motherlode-essays/motherlode-essays-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/style/motherlode-essays/motherlode-essays-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 492}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/style/motherlode-essays/motherlode-essays-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/style/motherlode-essays/motherlode-essays-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1346, 'width': 1642, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/style/motherlode-essays/motherlode-essays-thumb