on': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14e2ad15-7603-57b4-a8ff-415ddb63b00f', 'word_count': 2810, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e2ad15-7603-57b4-a8ff-415ddb63b00f'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Milarsky will be presented with the prize at a concert by the Juilliard Orchestra that he is conducting Friday night.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/conductors-prize-goes-to-jeffrey-milarsky/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Milarsky will be presented with the prize at a concert by the Juilliard Orchestra that he is conducting Friday night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ditson Conductor’s Award, a prize for distinguished contributions to American music, given annually by Columbia University, will be presented to the conductor and percussionist Jeffrey Milarsky at Alice Tully Hall on Friday night, during a concert by the Juilliard Orchestra that Mr. Milarsky is conducting. The $5,000 award, which was established in 1945, will be presented by the pianist Gilbert Kalish, the head of the Ditson advisory committee.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-cond/15artsbeat-cond-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-cond/15artsbeat-cond-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-cond/15artsbeat-cond-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-cond/15artsbeat-cond-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thu