ding “Redskins” a racist slur for all its rah-rah fondness among hometown fans at kick-off time. No less offended, the editorial board of the student newspaper at Neshaminy High School in Bucks County, Penn., has voted to banish the word from their pages, arguing that it’s time for their own Neshaminy Redskins (10-and-1 and a state powerhouses) to be called something less insensitive toward genocidal history. “The word ‘Redskin’ is racist and very much so,” the board explained in its decision to drop the name from editions of The Playwickian. “It is not a term of honor, but a term of hate.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'High Schoolers Against the Redskin Name', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Organizational', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Snyder, Daniel M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Redskins', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bucks County (Pa)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T16:37:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Francis X. Clines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Francis', 'middlename': 'X.', 'lastname': 'Clines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b6ff45e-2b7f-507d-ab63-4348efc85061', 'word_count': 416, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b6ff45e-2b7f-507d-ab63-4348efc85061'}, {'abstract': 'Send your questions, share your stories and tell us what topics interest you most.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/realestate/submit-your-real-estate-questions.html', 'snippet': 'Send your questions, share your stories and tell us what topics interest you most.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Got an upstairs neighbor who thinks there’s nothing wrong with coming home at 3 a.m. and hurling her three-inch heels across the uncarpeted hardwood floor? Or maybe you’re wondering if your co-op can really just decide to ban pets and tell you to find a new home for your 55-pound bulldog. Or you want to know what to do about the next-door neighbor who installed an eight-foot fence that you’re certain has veered into your backyard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-image2-articleLarge-v8.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-image2-articleLarge-v8.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-image2-jumbo-v8.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-image2-superJumbo-v8.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-image2-thumbStandard-v9.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-image2-thumbStandard-v9.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17ask-image2/17ask-ima