ing advice from parents whose children made healthy eating choices in the school cafeteria and beyond to college.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/booming/how-do-you-teach-kids-to-eat-well-when-youre-not-with-them.html', 'snippet': 'Seeking advice from parents whose children made healthy eating choices in the school cafeteria and beyond to college.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You are what you eat, from your head down to your feet!” Growing up in the 1970s, I had the benefit of having “Time for Timer’s” advice on healthy eating drummed into me weekly during Saturday morning cartoon binges. I may endlessly “hanker for a hunka, a slab, a slice, a chunka” cheese, but I also knew that no kid could survive on sugar alone, because “all those motors in your body need a lot of fuel to go on,” like a healthy breakfast and a balanced snack.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/booming/15parent-booming-healthy/15parent-booming-healthy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/booming/15parent-booming-healthy/15parent-booming-healthy-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/booming/15parent-booming-healthy/15parent-booming-healthy-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/booming/15parent-booming-healthy/15parent-booming-healthy-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1318, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15