ady Gaga promoted “Artpop,” her latest album, at the opening of H&M’s Times Square store.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/fashion/Lady-Gaga-Opens-the-HM-Times-Square-Store-.html', 'snippet': 'Lady Gaga promoted “Artpop,” her latest album, at the opening of H&M’s Times Square store.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LADY GAGA’S ARRIVAL on Wednesday night atop a pink Skyline sightseeing bus was cheeky, all right. Fanning out her waist-length hair and wearing a paint-streaked H&M cat suit, she worked the public like a flaxen Cleopatra waving from her barge. ', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lady Gaga Drops In at H&M and the Crowd Goes ... Well, You Know', 'kicker': 'On The Runway', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'And the Crowd Goes ... Well, You Know', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'H & M Hennes & Mauritz AB', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lady Gaga', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marant, Isabel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Times Square and 42nd Street (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T17:42:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ruth La Ferla', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ruth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'La Ferla', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ac3104-eee9-5fe4-b90a-0d4cf391a659', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ac3104-eee9-5fe4-b90a-0d4cf391a659'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/the-gun-report-november-15-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': '* The first 3D-printed gun, the “Liberator .380,” the design of which is widely available online, could emerge as a national security threat when a law banning undetectable firearms expires next month. The Undetectable Firearms Act, first passed in 1988, requires guns to have enough steel to set off a metal detector, but the Liberator uses only the smallest bits of metal for ammunition and a firing pin the size of a roofing nail. Some senators have proposed an updated version of the bill that would ban the design, manufacture, sale, import, export and possession of the plastic guns. The blueprint for the Liberator .380 has been downloaded 100,000 times since it was designed last year. “The fact that anyone with the right equipment can make a fully-functioning weapon from their own home with the click of a mouse is a truly frightening concept,” Sen. Bill Nelson said in a statement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 15, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T17:43:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d890f667-5035-5f9a-b8ce-68e353cffa3b', 'word_count': 1504, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d890f667-5035-5f9a-b8ce-68e353cffa3b'}, {'abstract': 'This establishment aims to recreate the period of government canteens, with diners issued ration coupons, and servers authentically brusque.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/travel/restaurant-report-state-run-food-shop-no-37-in-hanoi.html', 'snippet': 'This establishment aims to recreate the period of government canteens, with diners issued ration coupons, and servers authentically brusque.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dining scene in Hanoi has flourished in recent years. Travelers can feast on international fare like sushi and tapas, as well as on innovative takes on Vietnamese cuisine. But this tiny restaurant, which opened in the fall of 2012, evokes a simpler time: the decade starting in 1976, when the state controlled the economy so tightly that restaurants were barred from having names, and privately owned businesses were illegal.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/17BITES/17BITES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Restaurant Report: State-Run Food Shop No. 37 in Hanoi', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Past, on a Plate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hanoi (Vietnam)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T17:45:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabeth Rosen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c53100df-bc43-5469-b407-08069ce45eb8', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c53100df-bc43-5469-b407-08069ce45eb8'}, {'abstract': '‘The Most Happy Fella,’ a story about a farmer captivated by a young waitress, closes the 50th anniversary season of Goodspeed Musicals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/nyregion/a-review-of-the-most-happy-fella-at-the-goodspeed-opera-house.html', 'snippet': '‘The Most Happy Fella,’ a story about a farmer captivated by a young waitress, closes the 50th anniversary season of Goodspeed Musicals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been noted that in the age of cellphones, the romance between Romeo and Juliet would not end in tragedy. But add the Internet to the plot of “The Most Happy Fella,” and the romance never happens. An immigrant farmer might still be captivated by a young, pretty hash-house waitress on his visit to San Francisco. He might still leave a piece of jewelry — although it wouldn’t be a tie pin — as a tip, along with a charmingly effusive love note. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 605, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1210, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyregion/17ARTSCT1_SPAN/1117ARTSCT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love in the Time Before the Internet', 'kicker': 'Theater Review | Connecticut', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline'