al': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1c9c1b62-c150-5756-9f97-f9f9d44e5a92', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1c9c1b62-c150-5756-9f97-f9f9d44e5a92'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/magazine/the-11-313-issue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BROCCOLI’S EXTREME MAKEOVER', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 11.3.13 Issue', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reply All The 11.3.13 Issue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T17:57:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/67b9fefc-f252-5efd-8ad2-18e6842493cf', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/67b9fefc-f252-5efd-8ad2-18e6842493cf'}, {'abstract': 'She appears to know my lineage better than I do.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/magazine/what-cynthia-ozick-taught-me-about-my-grandfather.html', 'snippet': 'She appears to know my lineage better than I do.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cynthia Ozick and I have long differed on the name of my grandfather. Every decade or so, we run into each other at some New York gathering, and after exchanging pleasantries, I say, again, that the first name of my paternal grandfather, an immigrant from Ukraine, was Kusel (pronounced k’SEEL.) She informs me, once more, that it was Yekutiel, a name I’d never heard before I met her. Our discussions have always been cordial. Considering the fact that she is someone who is celebrated for her erudite essays as well as for her novels, she has been admirably free of condescension. I would compare the tone of our disagreement to a respectful difference in interpretation by two scholars — or maybe between one scholar and another person.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '58', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/magazine/17lives/mag-17Lives-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 501, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/magazine/17lives/mag-17Lives-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 240, 'width': 501, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/magazine/17lives/17lives-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/magazine/17lives/17lives-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/magazine/17lives/17lives-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Cynthia Ozick Taught Me About My Grandfather', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Kusel by Any Other Name', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grandparents', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trillin, Calvin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ozick, Cynthia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T17:57:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Calvin Trillin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Calvin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Trillin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/795d9aa5-23ee-5a1f-9dc1-f9fae4487b85', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/795d9aa5-23ee-5a1f-9dc1-f9fae4487b85'}, {'abstract': 'Rain man of his own mind.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/magazine/put-me-in-coach-im-ready-to-pay.html', 'snippet': 'Rain man of his own mind.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My granddaughter is being asked to pay more than $2,000 to be on a traveling sports team. The coach of her high-school team, who also coaches the unaffiliated traveling team, is asking for the payment as a condition of my granddaughter’s participation on the regular high-school squad. Is this unethical behavior by the coach? Is it proper for the person paying the fee (me) to bring this issue to the attention of the school system? How do I avoid retribution by the coach against my granddaughter?\xa0CHET M., ORINDA, CALIF.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None,