ia/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of events around the globe curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Exposed! Harley-Davidson’s\xa0Lost Photographs, 1915-1916,\xa0Milwaukee\xa0More than 50 black-and-white photographs documenting the early years of the Harley-Davidson Motor Company are on display\xa0through Jan. 1, in Milwaukee at the\xa0Harley-Davidson Museum. The photos, printed from a collection of more than 400 fragile glass-plate negatives, provide a glimpse back nearly 100 years ago and include employee portraits, depictions of the company’s 1916 racing team and images used for marketing.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/1117CALENDAR01/1117CALENDAR01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/1117CALENDAR01/1117CALENDAR01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/1117CALENDAR01/1117CALENDAR01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/1117CALENDAR01/1117CALENDAR01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/1117CALENDAR01/1117CALENDAR01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/17/travel/1117CALENDAR01/1117CALENDAR01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption'