e of the previous edition.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For classical music fans and scholars – and increasingly, for those devoted to other musical genres, including non-Western forms as well as jazz and popular music – the various editions of the Grove Dictionary of Music and Musicians have been the principal resource for generations. Originally published in 1878 as a four-volume set, edited by Sir George Grove (but without his name in the title), the Grove took a huge leap with its sixth edition, which was so thoroughly revamped that when it appeared in 1980, “New” was added to the title. The current New Grove Dictionary of Music and Musicians, published in 2001, fills 29 volumes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-grove/15artsbeat-grove-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 571, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-grove/15artsbeat-grove-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 571}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-grove/15artsbeat-grove-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-grove/15artsbeat-grove-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 694, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-grove/15artsbeat-grove-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/arts/15artsbeat-grove/15artsbeat-grove-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth