ow.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 799, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/dbpix-packard/dbpix-packard-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Finding Strength in Humility', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Executives and Management (Theory)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:05:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tony Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9ab9e1f-7d80-568d-a592-a50c1439d813', 'word_count': 752, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9ab9e1f-7d80-568d-a592-a50c1439d813'}, {'abstract': 'The spinoff of GE Capital’s North America retail finance business will help the company focus on its core businesses.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/general-electric-finally-gets-past-the-jack-welch-era/', 'snippet': 'The spinoff of GE Capital’s North America retail finance business will help the company focus on its core businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'General Electric is finally putting the ghost of its former chief executive Jack Welch out to pasture. On Friday, the conglomerate said it intended to spin off its North America retail finance business. That will help return GE Capital to its roots of lending to midmarket companies and its parent’s industrial concerns.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'General Electric Finally Gets Past the Jack Welch Era', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Initial Public Offerings', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Welch, John F Jr', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GE Capital Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:07:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da413d75-f3a8-51b6-950c-34f2c601b863', 'word_count': 392, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da413d75-f3a8-51b6-950c-34f2c601b863'}, {'abstract': 'Peter Newman, the producer, and Antonia Dauphin, a casting agent, live at 1 Fifth Avenue, no stranger to Hollywood types.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/realestate/houseful-of-handfuls.html', 'snippet': 'Peter Newman, the producer, and Antonia Dauphin, a casting agent, live at 1 Fifth Avenue, no stranger to Hollywood types.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One Fifth Avenue, the 27-story Art Deco apartment tower built in the late 1920s at the corner of Eighth Street, has a reputation as a Hollywood building. The directors who’ve called it home include Brian De Palma, Paul Mazursky, Ira Sachs and Tim Burton. It’s no wonder that Peter Newman, a film producer and a professor at New York University, and Antonia Dauphin, a casting agent who is about to direct her first feature, are so comfortable there.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17super/17super-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17super/17super-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17super/17super-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/realestate/17super/17super-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 