to the beat of a drum in the backyard, flames jumping from a caldron set in a circle drawn in the dirt. One by one they placed pieces of paper into the fire — with words of a burden they wanted to shed — and watched sparks rise into the Brooklyn night sky.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Brooklyn, Friday Night Rites', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Brooklyn, Friday Night Rites', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Liz', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Witchcraft', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pagans and Paganism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catland (Brooklyn, NY, Retail Store)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bushwick (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Occult Sciences', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/be98576e-17b3-53d5-b315-8ffb73f04804', 'word_count': 587, 'uri': 'nyt://article/be98576e-17b3-53d5-b315-8ffb73f04804'}, {'abstract': 'The experiment by the veteran sonic experimentalists was a commission for the Dia Art Foundation.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/art-matters-from-matmos-a-musical-libretto-performed-by-random-strangers/', 'snippet': 'The experiment by the veteran sonic experimentalists was a commission for the Dia Art Foundation.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There’s something suspicious about the work we do,” said Drew Daniel of the Baltimore experimental duo Matmos, “because it has an eerie ability to seem alien.” Daniel and Martin Schmidt, his partner in creativity and in life, are known for pulling sounds from unorthodox sources: squishing organs on operating tables, rats pattering across cages, rose petals being crushed. To create the sounds for their last album, “The Marriage of True Minds,” the duo conducted a Ganzfeld experiment — a parapsychological technique used to test for ESP — on subjects in Baltimore and Oxford, England. Participants were asked to lie on the floor, cover their eyes with Ping-Pong balls and listen to blasting white noise, then describe what they saw in their mind’s eye. “We’ve had some ideas that other people may object to or find a little odd,” Daniel admitted.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Matters | From Matmos, a Musical Libretto Performed by Random Strangers', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dia Art Foundation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Matmos (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:17:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Baumgardner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baumgardner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/68d78883-11aa-59ee-8586-01de79d3f1ab', 'word_count': 278, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68d78883-11aa-59ee-8586-01de79d3f1ab'}, {'abstract': 'The merger between American Airlines and US Airways comes after airlines have struggled for decades, cutting costs and slimming down service to turn around a trend of diminishing profits.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/video/business/100000002554411/david-gillen-fewer-choices-in-the-air.html', 'snippet': 'The merger between American Airlines and US Airways comes after airlines have struggled for decades, cutting costs and slimming down service to turn around a trend of diminishing profits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The merger between American Airlines and US Airways comes after airlines have struggled for decades, cutting costs and slimming down service to turn around a trend of diminishing profits.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 507, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/business/video-gillen-airlines/video-gillen-airlines-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fewer Choices in the Air', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'US Airways Group Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:18:03+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'Channon Hodge and David Gillen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Channon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gillen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/d3eea40f-fb21-593c-96b2-d546ae510bcd', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/d3eea40f-fb21-593c-96b2-d546ae510bcd'}, {'abstract': 'Three people who struggled to use HealthCare.gov have founded HealthSherpa, a minimalist website that tells consumers what plans are available in their area.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/affordable-care-act/2013/11/15/programmers-create-new-way-to-navigate-health-law/', 'snippet': 'Three people who struggled to use HealthCare.gov have founded HealthSherpa, a minimalist website that tells consumers what plans are available in their area.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The stumbling rollout of the federally run online health exchange has frustrated tens of thousands of Americans and sent some looking for alternative sources of information on where they can buy health insurance, and what it will cost them, under the Affordable Care Act. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Programmers Find New Way to Navigate Health Plans', 'kicker': 'In Practice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'King, Angus Jr', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kaiser Family Foundation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Maine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:28:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jess Bidgood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jess', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bidgood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8fc1951-adeb-56d9-b800-661ad808b8c9', 'word_count': 901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8fc1951-adeb-56d9-b800-661ad808b8c9'}, {'abstract': 'The prime ministers of Canada, India and Mauritius stayed away from the summit meeting to protest the treatment of Tamils during the civil war.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/world/asia/abuse-accusations-overshadow-commonwealth-summit-in-sri-lanka.html', 'snippet': 'The prime ministers of Canada, India and Mauritius stayed away from the summit meeting to protest the treatment of Tamils during the civil war.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — Sri Lanka’s president, Mahinda Ra