ll-stay-on-tv/', 'snippet': 'After announcing that “Moyers & Company” would end in January, the host and his producers received an outpouring of support and lined up new funding.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The fans of Bill Moyers spoke, and he listened. Mr. Moyers announced late last month that his public television show “Moyers & Company” would end with the Jan. 3, 2014, program. But on Friday, the program’s executive producer, Judy Doctoroff, told a meeting of public television officials that the program would stay on the air after all, after receiving “thousands of heartfelt and well-written messages saying ‘don’t go.’ ” New funding was also lined up, she said. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Moyers Will Stay on TV', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T19:58:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By ELIZABETH JENSEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'JENSEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa78e226-6a01-5859-8737-44acaefd26a7', 'word_count': 152, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa78e226-6a01-5859-8737-44acaefd26a7'}, {'abstract': 'A question about the history of Manhattan’s rigid right-angled street grid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/nyregion/the-story-of-manhattans-rectangular-street-grid.html', 'snippet': 'A question about the history of Manhattan’s rigid right-angled street grid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. When did Manhattan’s rectangular street grid first begin appearing?', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/17/nyreg