inction in the Northeast, turkeys are now relatively abundant, and some dwell in Manhattan, on Staten Island and in the Bronx.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If Benjamin Franklin had gotten his way, a gold-plated turkey would have presided atop every flagpole where the American bald eagle now stands. Franklin considered the bald eagle a “bird of bad moral character,” while the turkey was “a much more respectable bird,” and “though a little vain and silly, a Bird of Courage.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Bird of Courage and Success', 'kicker': 'City Room', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Franklin’s ‘Bird of Courage’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T21:05:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Taft', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taft', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/868bec4c-f41f-5c6e-a3bc-2c8ebf771407', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/868bec4c-f41f-5c6e-a3bc-2c8ebf771407'}, {'abstract': 'Automakers typically wait a few years to update a vehicle’s underpinnings, but Kia made major – albeit hard to see – changes to the Sorento for 2014. Here’s a video review.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/automobiles/the-well-concealed-newness-of-the-kia-sorento.html', 'snippet': 'Automakers typically wait a few years to update a vehicle’s underpinnings, but Kia made major – albeit hard to see – changes to the Sorento for 2014. Here’s a video review.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the hypercompetitive automotive industry, a car is often produced for four to six years, getting an update halfway through its life. Visually, this is the “new grille and taillights” phase. While full sheet metal overhauls are expensive, a new schnoz and back end can be done efficiently. These cosmetic revisions are a good way to ignite new sales.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 343, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 343, 'width': 679, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/automobiles/video-driven-kia-sorento/video-driven-kia-sorento-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Well-Concealed Newness of the Kia Sorento', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kia Motors Corp', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T21:10:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tom Voelk', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Voelk', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05e53bbc-ee43-5d1b-8828-42168a64c2f4', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05e53bbc-ee43-5d1b-8828-42168a64c2f4'}, {'abstract': 'After canceling a date there last March, the San Francisco Symphony gave a delayed performance of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony at Carnegie Hall on Thursday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/arts/music/san-francisco-symphony-performs-at-carnegie-hall.html', 'snippet': 'After canceling a date there last March, the San Francisco Symphony gave a delayed performance of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony at Carnegie Hall on Thursday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the San Francisco Symphony canceled an East Coast tour in March because of a players’ strike, one event that went by the board was a Carnegie Hall performance of Mahler’s Ninth Symphony, to have been led by the ensemble’s music director, Michael Tilson Thomas. The loss disappointed many, since this combination of orchestra and conductor is typically potent in Mahler.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bated Breath, as a Baton Is Raised for a Specialty', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bated Breath, as a Baton Is Raised for a Specialty', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Francisco Symphony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T21:12:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba4a02e-a92d-5066-bd38-949f00f8c03a', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba4a02e-a92d-5066-bd38-949f00f8c03a'}, {'abstract': 'The Choir of Men and Boys at St. Thomas Church and the Fretwork ensemble presented a program of mostly Renaissance works on Tuesday, along with the premiere of Nico Muhly’s “My Days.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/arts/music/my-days-homage-to-elizabethan-music-at-st-thomas-church.html', 'snippet': 'The Choir of Men and Boys at St. Thomas Church and the Fretwork ensemble presented a program of mostly Renaissance works on Tuesday, along with the premiere of Nico Muhly’s “My Days.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“My Days” is the title of a program of mostly Renaissance works for voices and viols that was presented Tuesday at St. Thomas  by that church’s Choir of Men and Boys and the wonderful English viol consort Fretwork. It’s also the title of an arresting new work by Nico Muhly, a touching declaration of fraternity with the great Elizabethan composers that had its United States premiere that evening.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '