es', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strange Paradise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T21:15:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carolina Irving, Miguel Flores-Vianna and Charlotte Di Carcaci', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carolina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Irving', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Miguel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flores-Vianna', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Charlotte', 'middlename': 'Di', 'lastname': 'Carcaci', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f6a4b87-36ae-59b3-9962-9c3e792745e4', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f6a4b87-36ae-59b3-9962-9c3e792745e4'}, {'abstract': 'American officials appear to be seeking a solution in which Iran would be allowed to enrich uranium at the low level of 3.5 percent during an interim agreement and also under a comprehensive accord.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/world/middleeast/solution-may-be-near-for-iran-nuclear-deal-us-official-says.html', 'snippet': 'American officials appear to be seeking a solution in which Iran would be allowed to enrich uranium at the low level of 3.5 percent during an interim agreement and also under a comprehensive accord.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — A senior Obama administration official said on Friday that a solution could be found for one of the major stumbling blocks to an agreement that would freeze Iran’s nuclear program, and that the accord might be achieved next week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Compromise May Be Near for Iran Nuclear Deal, U.S. Official Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Compromise May Be Near for Iran Nuclear Deal, U.S. Official Says', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael R', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Economic Sanctions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-15T21:17:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael R. Gordon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Gordon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a79abf37-b003-548c-a8c1-e0b73af5ccc8', 'word_count': 964, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a79abf37-b003-548c-a8c1-e0b73af5ccc8'}, {'abstract': 'Hofesh Shechter Company performed a premiere of “Sun” at the Howard Gilman Opera House at BAM.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/arts/dance/hofesh-shechter-company-at-howard-gilman-opera-house.html', 'snippet': 'Hofesh Shechter Company performed a premiere of “Sun” at the Howard Gilman Opera House at BAM.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hofesh Shechter’s “Sun” is cheeky. First the voice of the Israeli-born choreographer, a popular success in Britain, announces that before starting, his company will show a bit of the ending, “so that you know everything is going to be just fine.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multi