f0a8bc8'}, {'abstract': 'No matter where the journey takes us, T tries to broaden how we see things and to make sense of the cultural moment we live in.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/15/editors-letter-think-big/', 'snippet': 'No matter where the journey takes us, T tries to broaden how we see things and to make sense of the cultural moment we live in.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had the odd coincidence of reading Lawrence Osborne’s piece on Burma — in which he examines the country today alongside the one George Orwell wrote about in his first novel, “Burmese Days” — at the same time my husband happened to be reading Orwell’s “1984” aloud to our children.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Think Big', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Think Big', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T00:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deborah Needleman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deborah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Needleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08ca5c28-3559-545b-b83d-2455ee3b9089', 'word_count': 397, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08ca5c28-3559-545b-b83d-2455ee3b9089'}, {'abstract': 'Gone is the closeted, often intolerant Washington; the capital is now perhaps the gayest place in the nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/fashion/Washington-DC-has-thriving-gay-lesbian-and-transgender-population.html', 'snippet': 'Gone is the closeted, often intolerant Washington; the capital is now perhaps the gayest place in the nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — My earliest sense of what it meant to be gay in the nation’s capital came more than a decade ago when I was a 