ame': 'organizations', 'value': 'Monsanto Company', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'DuPont Co', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetic Engineering', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:07:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2bb268c-a3c3-51fb-9f34-803aec609860', 'word_count': 1318, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2bb268c-a3c3-51fb-9f34-803aec609860'}, {'abstract': 'The International Criminal Court’s charges of crimes against humanity has led to tension with the African Union.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/world/africa/african-call-to-delay-kenyans-trials-fails-at-un.html', 'snippet': 'The International Criminal Court’s charges of crimes against humanity has led to tension with the African Union.', 'lead_paragraph': 'UNITED NATIONS — An African-led attempt to postpone the trials of Kenya’s top two leaders at the International Criminal Court collapsed on Friday when it failed to gain enough support on the United Nations Security Council, an outcome bitterly criticized by Kenya and other African nations that accused the Council’s majority of a patronizing mistrust.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'African Call to Delay Kenyans’ Trials Fails at U.N.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'African Call to Delay Kenyans’ Trials Fails at U.N.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruto, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AFRICAN UNION', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Security Council (UN)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:10:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44a4c7f4-331c-56be-86ce-3163a2eb0333', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44a4c7f4-331c-56be-86ce-3163a2eb0333'}, {'abstract': 'He was a sweetheart, genuinely funny, and a drunk.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/opinion/cavett-tough-way-to-lose-a-friend.html', 'snippet': 'He was a sweetheart, genuinely funny, and a drunk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every writer knows that unless you were born gifted with either supreme confidence or outsize ego, handing in your work holds, in some cases, admitted terror. If that’s too strong, at least fairly high anxiety. Even if what you wrote seems unusually good to you, part of you is vulnerable to the suggestion that you may have laid an egg. A bad one. As W.C. Fields might have put it as your editor, “Sadly, my little lad, you have contrived in this instance to produce a specimen of odoriferous hen fruit.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/04/opinion/cavett-contributor/contibutors-images-slide-CVN5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tough Way to Lose a Friend', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McCourt, Malachy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Addiction (Psychology)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:12:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dick Cavett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cavett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/33a6c248-c7b3-5f9e-bdb5-da124699b45c', 'word_count': 1367, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33a6c248-c7b3-5f9e-bdb5-da124699b45c'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama has been on quite an apology tour over the rollout of health care reform.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/opinion/collins-whos-sorry-now.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama has been on quite an apology tour over the rollout of health care reform.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barack Obama’s loyal supporters are heavy of heart. Perhaps their chief source of comfort is that the Obamacare mess hit the headlines at about the same time as the crack-smoking mayor of Toronto. At least the president didn’t claim he was drunk when he wrote the health care bill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/gail-collins/gail-collins-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 