gift-guide-home.html', 'snippet': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every day from now until Christmas, the editors of T are sharing their personal gift suggestions.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gifts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:14:39+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/1f1d7bbb-9e6f-5a80-9758-87fd354fa67b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/1f1d7bbb-9e6f-5a80-9758-87fd354fa67b'}, {'abstract': 'The federal police began arresting a dozen powerful political figures, bankers and businessmen convicted in a vast vote-buying scandal that surfaced more than eight years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/world/americas/brazil-arrests-begin-in-vote-fraud-case.html', 'snippet': 'The federal police began arresting a dozen powerful political figures, bankers and businessmen convicted in a vast vote-buying scandal that surfaced more than eight years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The federal police on Friday began arresting a dozen powerful political figures, bankers and businessmen convicted in a vast vote-buying scandal that surfaced more than\xa0eight years ago. More than a year ago, Brazil’s highest court set the prison sentences for officials from the governing Workers Party, but the court’s consideration of appeals in the landmark corruption trial and what appeared to have been bureaucratic problems had delayed sending those found guilty in the scheme to prison. It is rare for high-profile Brazilian politicians convicted of crimes to serve time in prison. But this week the Supreme Federal Tribunal ruled that the convicted officials must soon start their prison terms. On Friday, José Genoino Guimarães Neto, a legislator who is a former president of the Workers Party, turned himself in at a police building in São Paulo and thrust his fist in the air in an act of defiance. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil: Arrests Begin in Vote-Fraud Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil: Arrests Begin in Vote-Fraud Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Workers' Party (Brazil)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Federal Tribunal (Brazil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Genoino Guimaraes Neto, Jose', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:17:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/b3066b0b-a4d9-5a20-9519-fe1e4f349dbb', 'word_count': 148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b3066b0b-a4d9-5a20-9519-fe1e4f349dbb'}, {'abstract': 'Insurance executives expressed mixed feelings about whether President Obama’s proposal to prevent cancellation of insurance policies for millions of Americans could work in every state.', 'web_url': 'https