le/891c9eed-58fc-550c-8ee3-33b12d30684d', 'word_count': 1550, 'uri': 'nyt://article/891c9eed-58fc-550c-8ee3-33b12d30684d'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of fliers are accompanied by pets legally certified as emotional support animals, sometimes raising eyebrows, and doubts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/business/emotional-support-with-fur-draws-complaints-on-planes.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of fliers are accompanied by pets legally certified as emotional support animals, sometimes raising eyebrows, and doubts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Gigi Griffis, a writer who travels around the world as she works, and Luna, her sprightly 4-year-old Schnauzer-Yorkie mix, are nearly inseparable. They have dined in Mexican cafes near Puerto Vallarta, navigated the Paris Metro and hiked the alpine foothills of the Matterhorn.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/business/SUPPORT/SUPPORT-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Emotional Support, With Fur, Draws Complaints on Planes', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emotional Support, With Fur, Draws Complaints on Planes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Service Dogs and Other Animals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Witz, Billy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:27:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Billy Witz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Billy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Witz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/707c34df-4230-5932-96f3-42da39e53e97', 'word_count': 1077, 'uri': 'nyt://article/707c34df-4230-5932-96f3-42da39e53e97'}, {'abstract': 'A special session of the Toronto City Council removed Mayor Rob Ford’s power to appoint some city officials, after he admitted using crack cocaine and binge drinking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/world/americas/canada-toronto-council-curbs-mayor.html', 'snippet': 'A special session of the Toronto City Council removed Mayor Rob Ford’s power to appoint some city officials, after he admitted using crack cocaine and binge drinking.', 'lead_paragraph': ' After Mayor Rob Ford of Toronto, a self-confessed crack cocaine user, binge drinker and impaired driver, refused to step down, the Toronto City Council began stripping away his powers on Friday. A special session of the Council removed the mayor’s power to appoint the members of the city’s executive committee as well as the deputy mayor. It also transferred any powers Mr. Ford would have as mayor during a declared emergency to the deputy mayor. On Monday the Council will consider measures to eliminate the budget and staff for Mr. Ford’s office. Mr. Ford said he would challenge the sanctions in court. The Council has no legal means to remove the mayor from office. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Toronto Council Curbs Mayor', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Toronto Council Curbs Mayor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ford, Robert B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T02:33:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a44d5952-0a28-5bca-b2bd-ad3de7b83123', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a44d5952-0a28-5bca-b2bd-ad3de7b83123'}, {'abstract': 'Some can see racism where it is absent, and others can willfully ignore any possibility that it could ever be present.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/opinion/blow-disrespect-race-and-obama.html', 'snippet': 'Some can see racism where it is absent, and others can willfully ignore any possibility that it could ever be present.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In an interview with the BBC this week, Oprah Winfrey said of President Obama: “There is a level of disrespect for the office that occurs. And that occurs, in some cases, and maybe even many cases, because he’s African-American.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles-m-blow-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/02/opinion/charles-m-blow/charles