elf-Defense', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Worthy, Kym L', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Detroit (Mich)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T03:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bcd5816-13d8-5ddf-a830-71123d101137', 'word_count': 283, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bcd5816-13d8-5ddf-a830-71123d101137'}, {'abstract': 'Hawaii’s new law caps a remarkable year for progress on same-sex marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/opinion/a-leap-for-equality.html', 'snippet': 'Hawaii’s new law caps a remarkable year for progress on same-sex marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Wednesday, Gov. Neil Abercrombie of Hawaii signed a bill that will allow same-sex couples to marry in the state, starting Dec. 2. The measure, ending a two-decade legal and political battle, caps a remarkable year of progress toward ensuring the basic civil rights of gay Americans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Leap for Equality', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Leap for Equality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hawaii', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABERCROMBIE, NEIL', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T03:10:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e02a40cf-1fc5-5c6a-bac0-b5171f0199da', 'word_count': 323, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e02a40cf-1fc5-5c6a-bac0-b5171f0199da'}, {'abstract': 'A family from Queens gets some help from the Neediest Cases as it starts the gradual process of rebuilding a life. Readers can help, too.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/opinion/starting-over-after-hurricane-sandy.html', 'snippet': 'A family from Queens gets some help from the Neediest Cases as it starts the gradual process of rebuilding a life. Readers can help, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Hurricane Sandy approached, Joseph Duodu, his wife and two daughters evacuated from their home on the Rockaway Peninsula and drove to a motel on Queens Boulevard. The family had packed only an overnight bag with a change of clothes because they thought they would be back home the next day. They ended up living in the motel for five months. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Starting Over After Hurricane Sandy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Starting Over After Hurricane Sandy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times Neediest Cases Fund', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Catholic Charities Brooklyn and Queens', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T03:10:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c6235d-b148-5fbf-a6c4-a32661291ab4', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c6235d-b148-5fbf-a6c4-a32661291ab4'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McCormack helped take the Browns to N.F.L. championships in 1954 and 1955 and became a league coach and executive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/16/sports/football/mike-mccormack-hall-of-fame-browns-lineman-dies-at-83.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. McCormack helped take the Browns to N.F.L. championships in 1954 and 1955 and became a league coach and executive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mike McCormack, a Hall of Fame tackle for the Cleveland Browns in the 1950s and early ’60s who protected quarterback Otto Graham and opened holes for fullback Jim Brown and then became an N.F.L. coach and executive, died on Friday in Palm Desert, Calif. He was 83.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/sports/McCormack-obit-1/McCormack-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 846, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/sports/McCormack-obit-1/McCormack-obit-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 846}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/sports/McCormack-obit-1/McCormack-obit-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 726, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/sports/McCormack-obit-1/McCormack-obit-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1452, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '