the local mall. Writing in the The New York Times, Janet Maslin said this comedy, written and directed by Kevin Smith, “mixes clever bits and an appealing quirkiness (which goes a long way) with gross-out practical jokes, needless repetition and obvious padding, since it has no real plot.” She added: “Mr. Lee’s Brodie has the grunge and surliness to give him credibility here, but he also has a sweet, funny indignation over life’s little outrages, which are actually this film’s most heartfelt concerns.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Today', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T06:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/cbe39e01-7b56-50dc-93e4-f761b58dd795', 'word_count': 735, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cbe39e01-7b56-50dc-93e4-f761b58dd795'}, {'abstract': 'Barangay 88, which sits on a peninsula and is one of Tacloban’s most populous neighborhoods, endured massive destruction by last week’s typhoon in the Philippines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/world/asia/tacloban-philippines-typhoon-haiyan.html', 'snippet': 'Barangay 88, which sits on a peninsula and is one of Tacloban’s most populous neighborhoods, endured massive destruction by last week’s typhoon in the Philippines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TACLOBAN, the Philippines — In the corner of what used to be her living room, Mary Grace Golondrina, 20, dug through the mud and recovered a trophy — first-place runner-up in a fund-raiser for