 readiness for some personal freedoms and further economic reforms, all under firm one-party rule.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/opinion/sunday/chinas-new-agenda.html', 'snippet': 'Beijing’s leaders signal a readiness for some personal freedoms and further economic reforms, all under firm one-party rule.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In one of several surprising and potentially welcome shifts in policy, China’s leaders announced Friday that they would relax China’s draconian one-child policy and end its brutal “re-education through labor” camps. They also outlined several ambitious economic initiatives that could make the country more hospitable to private enterprise in the coming years.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s New Agenda', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s New Agenda', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forced Labor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-16T19:30:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a681acf8-f229-5a4a-88fc-c1482ee0d19b', 'word_count': 651, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a681acf8-f229-5a4a-88fc-c1482ee0d19b'}, {'abstract': 'The health care law has yet another brush with death.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/opinion/sunday/douthat-the-three-burials-of-obamacare.html', 'snippet': 'The health care law has yet another brush with death.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE first time Obamacare seemed finished, doomed, doornail-dead, the voters of Massachusetts played the would-be executioner. In January 2010, they sent a pickup-driving Republican to the Senate to fill Ted Kennedy’s seat, apparently depriving the health care bill of its crucial 60th vote and sending Democrats scrambling for a Plan B. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-jumbo.png', 'height': 512, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1000, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/03/opinion/ross-douthat/ross-douthat-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'c