 Times reporter covering the aftermath of Typhoon Haiyan, answered readers’ questions about doing his job under difficult conditions and the relief efforts underway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Keith Bradsher, the Hong Kong bureau chief for The New York Times, has been reporting on the aftermath of the powerful typhoon that hit the Philippines on Nov. 8, mostly from Tacloban, the city that was flattened when the storm made landfall. Mr. Bradsher answered a selection of readers’ questions, submitted via Facebook and Twitter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/world/asia/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/16/world/asia/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/world/asia/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/world/asia/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/16/world/asia/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/16/world/asia/20131117_PHILIPPINES-slide-XBOI/20131117_P