0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Jacobs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jacobs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bdba4fc-1bdf-55c2-b65b-49b523f91b76', 'word_count': 892, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bdba4fc-1bdf-55c2-b65b-49b523f91b76'}, {'abstract': 'A look inside the new Sims Municipal Recycling Facility in Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/11/18/arts/design/20131118RECYCLE.html', 'snippet': 'A look inside the new Sims Municipal Recycling Facility in Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A look inside the new Sims Municipal Recycling Facility in Brooklyn.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B/20131118RECYCLE-slide-FT5B-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Home for Recycling', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sunset Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T21:14:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/83e6cfa6-967c-54c4-944c-65deb52571de', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/83e6cfa6-967c-54c4-944c-65deb52571de'}, {'abstract': 'The new Sims Municipal Recycling Facility opening soon in Sunset Park, Brooklyn, promises to reduce recycling costs and create jobs, all in a pleasing waterfront structure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/arts/design/sims-municipal-recycling-facility-designed-by-selldorf.html', 'snippet': 'The new Sims Municipal Recycling Facility opening soon in Sunset Park, Brooklyn, promises to reduce recycling costs and create jobs, all in a pleasing waterfront structure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recycling in New York is a scrappy business. Billions have gone toward building water tunnels, power plants, subways and sewage treatment facilities, but little toward an infrastructure of recycling. In turn, New Yorkers have been slow to separate bottles and cans the way they flip a light switch or swipe a MetroCard: Recycling remains less an everyday fact of life than a do-good option, like tipping the mail carrier at the holidays.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Grace Note for a Gritty Business', 'kicker': 'Architecture Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Grace Note for a Gritty Business', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kimmelman, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sanitation Department (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Infrastructure (Public Works)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sunset Park (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sims Municipal Recycling Facility', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Selldorf Architects', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T21:15:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Kimmelman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kimmelman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd835831-6150-55f9-87d7-7830141c5028', 'word_count': 1069, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd835831-6150-55f9-87d7-7830141c5028'}, {'abstract': 'Benjamin Britten’s “Noye’s Fludde,” an opera that includes child performers, was presented by Lighthouse International and Park Avenue Christian Church.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/arts/music/brittens-noyes-fludde-with-young-performers.html', 'snippet': 'Benjamin Britten’s “Noye’s Fludde,” an opera that includes child performers, was presented by Lighthouse International and Park Avenue Christian Church.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Benjamin Britten loved composing pieces for children, not just for children to enjoy but also to perform. There is no better example that “Noye’s Fludde” (“Noah’s Flood”), a 60-minute opera based on a 15th-century mystery play, written for amateurs, especially children, with professionals mixed in. This telling of the biblical story was first performed in 1958 at Orford Church in Suffolk, England. It was presented as part of Britten’s Aldeburgh Festival with artists from the English Opera Group along with a large local cast, including a children’s choir. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/PARK/PARK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/PARK/PARK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/PARK/PARK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/PARK/PARK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1341, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 