 {'main': 'Treasury Auctions for the Week of Nov. 18', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Treasury Auctions Set for this Week', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Credits, Deductions and Exemptions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T22:48:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e3d6d3c-58aa-5df4-b3ce-26f6c37551b3', 'word_count': 449, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e3d6d3c-58aa-5df4-b3ce-26f6c37551b3'}, {'abstract': 'The Czech writer Ivan Klima’s new book, a memoir, begins in a Nazi camp and ends with the Velvet Revolution of 1989.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/books/ivan-klimas-my-crazy-century-spans-decades-of-czech-life.html', 'snippet': 'The Czech writer Ivan Klima’s new book, a memoir, begins in a Nazi camp and ends with the Velvet Revolution of 1989.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Czech writer Ivan Klima’s new book, a memoir, is called “My Crazy Century.” It begins in 1941, when together with his family Mr. Klima, who until then hadn’t even been aware that he was Jewish, was imprisoned in the Nazi camp at Terezin, and it concludes with the Velvet Revolution of 1989, ending years of dictatorship and repression. “Sometimes, it was funny crazy,” Mr. Klima said last week, while visiting New York. “But mostly, it was crazy crazy.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 774}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 794, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1587, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/klima/klima-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Optimism Outlasted a Lifetime of Horrors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Optimism Outlasted A Lifetime Of Horrors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGrath, Charles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klima, Ivan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Czechoslovakia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T22:50:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles McGrath', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McGrath', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8328338-cd65-561f-a724-85e83fb5c54c', 'word_count': 1062, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8328338-cd65-561f-a724-85e83fb5c54c'}, {'abstract': 'Retailers including Target, J.C. Penney and Home Depot, will report earnings, with a look to the holiday shopping season.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/business/economic-reports-for-the-week-of-nov-18.html', 'snippet': 'Retailers including Target, J.C. Penney and Home Depot, will report earnings, with a look to the holiday shopping season.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAC TRIAL Jury selection is scheduled to begin Tuesday in the trial of Michael S. Steinberg, the most senior employee at the hedge fund SAC Capital Advisors indicted in insider trading. Federal prosecutors have accused Mr. Steinberg of trading on secret information about technology companies. Though SAC has been at the center of the government’s insider trading investigation for years, Mr. Steinberg is the first former SAC employee to stand trial. Six others, including the fund itself, have pleaded guilty. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Nov. 18', 'kicker': 'Looking Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Economic Reports for the Week of Nov. 18', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Company Reports', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T22:52:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/679f8d03-cef2-5872-8a39-37af59266d07', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/679f8d03-cef2-5872-8a39-37af59266d07'}, {'abstract': 'Sturgill Simpson and his band toyed around with bluegrass, Southern rock and the hard country of the 1970s, at Hill Country in Manhattan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/arts/music/sturgill-simpsons-rowdy-and-tame-numbers-at-hill-country.html', 'snippet': 'Sturgill Simpson and his band toyed around with bluegrass, Southern rock and the hard country of the 1970s, at Hill Country in Manhattan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no end to the variety of night life in New York, but it remains an open question whether this city could ever be home to a genuine honky-tonk. Native to the South, that would be loosely defined as part bar, part performance venue, part staging ground for a battle royal. The music matters, but it’s only one element of the tapestry.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/STURGILL/STURGILL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Kentucky Singer Faces Down a Manhattan Crowd', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Kentucky Singer Faces Down a Manhattan Crowd', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T22:53:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/4854ae77-89f8-5fb4-923b-8df24b811be6', 'word_count': 585, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4854ae77-89f8-5fb4-923b-8df24b811be6'}, {'abstract': 'The Orlando Consort brought a program of early music, both sacred and earthly, to the Church of St. Mary the Virgin.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/arts/music/orlando-consort-presents-program-of-machaut.html', 'snippet': 'The Orlando Consort brought a program of early music, both sacred and earthly, to the Church of St. Mary the Virgin.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a concert of late medieval and early Renaissance vocal music presented in a church, you might expect to hear churchy music. And there was much of that in the second half of the Orlando Consort’s program at the Church of St. Mary the Virgin near Times Square on Saturday evening, presented by the Miller Theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Love Affair That Burned for Centuries, at Least in Song', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Love Affair That Burned for Centuries, at Least in Song', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orlando Consort', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T22:55:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By James R. Oestreich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Oestreich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dd86a61-b2f0-57a2-8f0b-cb9a68af7452', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dd86a61-b2f0-57a2-8f0b-cb9a68af7452'}, {'abstract': 'Historical projects on Twitter aim to recreate events like Kristallnacht and the assassination of President John F. Kennedy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/business/media/history-comes-to-life-with-tweets-from-the-past.html', 'snippet': 'Historical projects on Twitter aim to recreate events like Kristallnacht and the assassination of President John F. Kennedy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIKE watching a building collapse in slow motion, a Twitter account run by a group of German historians provides hour-by-hour updates of the horrors of Kristallnacht, which culminated in a night of anti-Jewish terror 75 years ago in Nazi Germany that plunged the country on a path to the Holocaust.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1457, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/business/link2/link2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'History Comes to Life With Tweets From Past', 'kicker': 'Link By Link', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'History Comes to Life With Tweets From Past', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cohen, Noam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'History (Academic Subject)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T22:56:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noam Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98ab4d08-f8d8-503a-a392-592e651419e3', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98ab4d08-f8d8-503a-a392-592e651419e3'}, {'abstract': 'The choreographer Arturo Vidich, collaborating with Maximilian Balduzzi, employed novel contraptions and effects in his piece at the Abrons Arts Center on Friday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/arts/dance/arturo-vidich-at-the-abrons-arts-center.html', 'snippet': 'The choreographer Arturo Vidich, collaborating with Maximilian Balduzzi, employed novel contraptions and effects in his piece at the Abrons Arts Center on Friday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Underground Theater at the Abrons Arts Center often goes by affectionate characterizations like “dungeon” and “cave.” Its subterranean aura, murky lighting and pockmarked concrete walls ensure that whatever happens will seem a little bit creepy. So it was a fitting location for Arturo Vidich’s “142241,” a duet (or quartet, if you count the audience participants) that attempted, as a news release put it, “to tune in to the invisible worlds that influence this world, if you believe in that sort of thing.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/VIDICH/VIDICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 515, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/VIDICH/VIDIC