t://article/5c6e73a6-ef5b-5c34-b6a0-165c32c7ce7e', 'word_count': 495, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5c6e73a6-ef5b-5c34-b6a0-165c32c7ce7e'}, {'abstract': 'Ronald K. Brown’s Evidence company was the first dance troupe at BRIC’s new performance space, in Fort Greene, Brooklyn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/arts/dance/ronald-k-brown-dancers-at-bric-house-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'Ronald K. Brown’s Evidence company was the first dance troupe at BRIC’s new performance space, in Fort Greene, Brooklyn.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRIC House, the snazzily redesigned headquarters of BRIC, the venerable Brooklyn arts organization, opened last month, but it wasn’t until Wednesday night that the building’s flexible performance space had its first dance show. There couldn’t have been a better first choice than the Brooklyn company of Ronald K. Brown. This is dancing that consecrates. The warmth and artistry and infectious joy made this house into a home.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/ROANLD/ROANLD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 294, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/ROANLD/ROANLD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 294}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/ROANLD/ROANLD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/ROANLD/ROANLD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1005, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/arts/ROANLD/RO