cys-parade-but-not-the-thanksgiving-dinner.html', 'snippet': 'Amy Kule, the executive producer of the Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade, said being the maestro has kept her out of the kitchen on the holiday for 17 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amy Kule spent a couple of afternoons with Maureen O’Hara in the late 1990s.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/BREAD/BREAD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Charge of the Macy’s Parade, but Not the Thanksgiving Dinner', 'kicker': 'Breaking Bread', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Charge of the Macy’s Parade, but Not the Thanksgiving Dinner', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haberman, Clyde', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kule, Amy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-17T23:58:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Haberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee9a741d-ba16-59ce-98de-3037d62e8e79', 'word_count': 1164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee9a741d-ba16-59ce-98de-3037d62e8e79'}, {'abstract': 'Post-revolutionary Cuba responded to racial inequality more effectively than any country in the Americas. But racism proved more persistent.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/17/a-lesson-from-cuba-on-race/', 'snippet': 'Post-revolutionary Cuba responded to racial inequality more effectively than any country in the Americas. But racism proved more persistent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a recent article for The Stone, Gary Gutting posed a challenge. He urged readers to \xa0look “past the outrage on race” provoked by the Trayvon Martin case and to focus on what he aptly described as the “deeper issue” that sustains the edifice of racial inequality —\xa0our unjust economic system. Under this system, people compete for basic goods and services in what seems to be a fair and non-discriminating market. But since they enter this market from vastly different social circumstances, competition is anything but fair. Those who already possess goods have a much better chance of renewing their access to them, whereas those who don’t have little chance of ever getting them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Lesson From Cuba on Race', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T00:15:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alejandro de la Fuente', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alejandro', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de la Fuente', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc697f6-18c1-5a83-8a33-3576eef2aec4', 'word_count': 1490, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc697f6-18c1-5a83-8a33-3576eef2aec4'}, {'abstract': 'Voters elected Bill de Blasio, but New York has always been a city of unofficial mayors.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/nyregion/real-mayors-of-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Voters elected Bill de Blasio, but New York has always been a city of unofficial mayors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Voters elected Bill de Blasio, but New York has always been a city of unofficial mayors.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/15/nyregion/MAYOR_MARTA2BW/MAYOR_MARTA2BW-arti