ies of mysterious deaths, he searches for the real killer and ends up face to face with the grim reaper. “With material for a half-dozen different movies here, Mr. Jackson has no trouble keeping ‘The Frighteners’ spinning,” Janet Maslin wrote in The New York Times. “Phantoms skitter across the screen in record numbers, and Mr. Fox presides over the story with dependable skill.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Monday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T05:17:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/471c6598-b23a-5f76-8467-00c8875bfd9a', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/471c6598-b23a-5f76-8467-00c8875bfd9a'}, {'abstract': 'The opposition candidate for prime minister appealed to voters in the outsourcing hub by characterizing his Bharatiya Janata Party as the champion of information technology and the governing Congress Party as the enemy of social media.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/narendra-modi-casts-b-j-p-as-tech-friendly-party-during-bangalore-rally/', 'snippet': 'The opposition candidate for prime minister appealed to voters in the outsourcing hub by characterizing his Bharatiya Janata Party as the champion of information technology and the governing Congress Party as the enemy of social media.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BANGALORE — In his first campaign stop in southern India, Narendra Modi, the opposition candidate for prime minister, appealed to voters in this o