 face off at auction.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/high-winning-bid-for-photo-by-maos-wife/', 'snippet': 'Maoist-era art is attracting soaring prices as private collectors and public museums in China face off at auction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A black-and-white photograph of a landscape snapped by Mao Zedong’s fourth wife, Jiang Qing, has sold for 391,000 renminbi, or $64,000, about 20 times the presale estimate, at Huachen Auctions in Beijing. The unexpectedly high price provides another sign of a bullish market for Mao-era art, driven by the competition among private collectors and public museums and libraries that are seeking to enhance their holdings.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19sino-photo/19sino-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19sino-photo/19sino-photo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 731}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19sino-photo/19sino-photo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 841, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19sino-photo/19sino-photo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1955, 'width': 1605, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19sino-photo/19sino-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19sino-photo/19sino-photo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidt