 off by a short circuit in an electrical appliance, according to Xinhua, the state-run news agency. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tibetan Monastery’s Prayer Hall Lost in Fire', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lithang Monastery (Tibet)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tibet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T14:33:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Qin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Qin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4b63763-bd84-52c6-bc27-a1eee952363e', 'word_count': 494, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4b63763-bd84-52c6-bc27-a1eee952363e'}, {'abstract': 'The private equity firm Advent International has reached a deal to take private Unit4, a software provider based in the Netherlands.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/advent-international-to-take-dutch-firm-private-for-1-58-billion/', 'snippet': 'The private equity firm Advent International has reached a deal to take private Unit4, a software provider based in the Netherlands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 9:51 a.m. | LONDON — The private equity firm Advent International has reached a deal to take private Unit4, a software provider based in the Netherlands, for 1.17 billion euros in cash, or $1.58 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Advent International to Take Dutch Firm Private for $1.58 Billion', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Private', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private Equity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Software', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ADVENT INTERNATIONAL CORP', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T14:42:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ec7ca64b-8d58-58ca-8724-a385fe29026e', 'word_count': 331, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ec7ca64b-8d58-58ca-8724-a385fe29026e'}, {'abstract': 'Not hard if you actually read the stuff.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/the-new-keynesian-case-for-fiscal-policy-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Not hard if you actually read the stuff.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s been a bit funny on the academic front being a Keynesian during a Keynesian crisis. Much of the academic profession decided more than 30 years ago that the whole thing was nonsense and what we needed was an equilibrium model of the business cycle. By the time the utter failure of the equilibrium project became apparent, you had a whole generation of economists who knew that Keynesianism of any form was nonsense based on what they had heard somewhere, so they didn’t read any of the stuff, old or new — and were flabbergasted to learn that there was in fact an extensive New Keynesian literature that provided a justification for fiscal policy at the zero lower bound.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The New Keynesian Case for Fiscal Policy (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T14:49:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed87e973-99b3-51e1-8f4e-be66a29eba79', 'word_count': 523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed87e973-99b3-51e1-8f4e-be66a29eba79'}, {'abstract': 'The unusual challenge to the collection of millions of domestic telephone records had been filed directly to the Supreme Court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/us/justices-reject-challenge-to-nsa-program.html', 'snippet': 'The unusual challenge to the collection of millions of domestic telephone records had been filed directly to the Supreme Court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The Supreme Court on Monday turned away an unusual challenge to a National Security Agency surveillance program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Justices Reject Challenge to N.S.A. Program', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Security Agency', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Electronic Privacy Information Center', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T15:27:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline'