global network that looted $45 million from bank machines last spring.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/nyregion/with-5-more-indictments-new-clues-in-atm-robbery-case.html', 'snippet': 'The authorities indicted six more people in connection with a global network that looted $45 million from bank machines last spring.', 'lead_paragraph': "When eight men from Queens were indicted last spring as part of a global network that looted $45 million from A.T.M.'s, an unanswered question was what happened to the money.", 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1087, 'width': 815, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19ATM/19ATM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'With More Indictments, New Clues in A.T.M. Robbery Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Clues Emerge\r\nIn A.T.M. Thefts', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bank Robberies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Loretta E', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T17:49:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/273e8509-3567-506b-90e7-1354a3874c54', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/273e8509-3567-506b-90e7-1354a3874c54'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. McMillan, the author of “Who Asked You?,” says, “If I wanted you to know exactly what I thought about things, I’d write nonfiction.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/the-read-around-terry-mcmillan/', 'snippet': 'Ms. McMillan, the author of “Who Asked You?,” says, “If I wanted you to know exactly what I thought about things, I’d write nonfiction.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In “The Read Around,” a weekly video feature, authors discuss the when, where and how behind their latest books. Below, Terry McMillan, the author of “Waiting to Exhale” and, most recently, “Who Asked You?,” talks about why she prefers writing in the first person, how she gets to know her characters and why it’s important for writers to be diverse readers.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Read Around: Terry McMillan', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMillan, Terry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T17:55:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c38aa949-5716-5d24-8d35-f3c460a0e541', 'word_count': 61, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c38aa949-5716-5d24-8d35-f3c460a0e541'}, {'abstract': 'John Moffitt, who walked away from about $1 million in salary from the 9-1 Broncos, said continuing to play for money was likely to injure him further and deepen his gloom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/sports/football/quitting-the-nfl-for-john-moffitt-the-money-wasnt-worth-it.html', 'snippet': 'John Moffitt, who walked away from about $1 million in salary from the 9-1 Broncos, said continuing to play for money was likely to injure him further and deepen his gloom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — John Moffitt chugged mugs of black coffee and talked almost giddily about how, the week before, he called John Elway, the head of football operations for the Denver Broncos, to tell him he was quitting the National Football League, leaving behind the money and the fame, but also the constant pain and the danger.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/19moffitt/19moffitt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/19moffitt/19moffitt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'