'An outstanding group of opera singers paid tribute to Richard Tucker at Avery Fisher Hall on Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A dream team of opera singers assembled at Avery Fisher Hall for the Richard Tucker Gala on Sunday, an evening that included Stephanie Blythe, Joyce DiDonato, Renée Fleming, Susan Graham and Eric Owens. But before any of them sang a note, it was the voice of Tucker that filled the hall in a recording of “Thine Alone,” in which cantorial ardor and classical training blended into that combination of polish and popular appeal that made him one of the best-loved tenors of his time.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/19TUCKER/19TUCKER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For a Tenor’s Centennial, Celebrating His Legacy With a Cast of Opera Stars', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For a Tenor&#8217;s Centennial, Celebrating His Legacy With a Cast of Opera Stars', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tucker, Richard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T22:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/99389035-0278-5beb-8702-e7f552898be9', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99389035-0278-5beb-8702-e7f552898be9'}, {'abstract': 'A 255-year-old elephant fetus on which Carl Linnaeus based his taxonomy of Asian elephants was actually African, new research shows.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/science/a-historical-elephants-new-identity.html', 'snippet': 'A 255-year-old elephant fetus on which Carl Linnaeus based his taxonomy of Asian elephants was actually African, new research shows.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1752, King Adolf Fredrik of Sweden acquired a remarkable curiosity: an elephant fetus preserved in a jar. It did not take long for a fellow Swede, the famed naturalist Carl Linnaeus, to pay an eager visit to Drottningholm Palace to examine the withered specimen. ', 'print_secti