oking at the circumstances behind the continued incarceration of Amir Hekmati, who has not been charged.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The family of Amir Hekmati, a former American Marine who has been incarcerated in Iran for more than two years even though his espionage conviction was overturned, has been contacted by the United Nations for details on his case, Mr. Hekmati’s sister said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 716, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1433, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/19TEHRAN/19TEHRAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Agency Seeks Details on American Held in Iran', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Agency Seeks Details On American Held in Iran', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hekmati, Amir Mirzaei', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kildee, Daniel T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T22:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33400234-4e71-52dd-9cd2-7aef5e03511c', 'word_count': 668, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33400234-4e71-52dd-9cd2-7aef5e03511c'}, {'abstract': 'A Tallis Scholars concert on Saturday at Alice Tully Hall, part of the White Light Festival, included work by John Tavener, who died last week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/arts/music/tallis-scholars-feature-taverner-works-at-white-light-concert.html', 'snippet': 'A Tallis Scholars concert on Saturday at Alice Tully Hall, part of the White Light Festival, included work by John Tavener, who died last week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The British composer John Tavener, who died last week at 69, frequently collaborated with the Tallis Scholars, the superb a cappella ensemble founded and conducted by Peter Phillips. It seemed fitting that as an encore to the group’s impressive concert of Renaissance and contemporary music on Saturday at Alice Tully Hall, it offered a Tavener work as a tribute: his setting of the Lord’s Prayer. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Exploring Spirituality, and Ending on a Prayer', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Exploring Spirituality, And Ending On a Prayer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schweitzer, Vivien', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White Light Festival (Lincoln Center, NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tavener, John (1944-2013)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tallis Scholars', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T22:20:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vivien Schweitzer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vivien', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schweitzer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba92f112-0f50-524d-9e73-49932ff2986a', 'word_count': 369, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba92f112-0f50-524d-9e73-49932ff2986a'}, {'abstract': 'Alarm Will Sound played a Steve Reich premiere based on Radiohead on Saturday at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/arts/music/alarm-will-sound-plays-steve-reichs-version-of-radiohead.html', 'snippet': 'Alarm Will Sound played a Steve Reich premiere based on Radiohead on Saturday at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David Bowie, Tortoise, the Orb, Sufjan Stevens, Dan Deacon: The list of pop and rock performers and groups who have shown the composer Steve Reich’s influence is lengthy and continuing. On Saturday night at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, Mr. Reich turned the tables, as Alarm Will Sound presented the New York premiere of his “Radio Rewrite,” based on two songs by the British rock band Radiohead. The performance was part of this adventurous new-music ensemble’s season-long residency, which includes formal events like this one, as well as unusual programs, like a pop-up concert that would unfold without warning in the museum’s Charles Engelhard Court on Monday at noon.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/arts/alarm/alarm-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hearing What Radiohead Has Inspired', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hearing What Radiohead Has Inspired', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name