 'lead_paragraph': 'When Ilir Topalli gets that yearly Christmas card from the management of the small Upper East Side building where he has lived for 10 years, the one that gently nudges residents to tip the staff, it contains the names of the superintendent, the doorman and the porter who trudges out with the trash. Also listed is someone who is not on the co-op’s payroll: the superintendent’s wife, who is the de facto housekeeper for many of the apartments.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/19APPRAISAL/19APPRAISAL-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Need Condo Cleaned? Consider the Superintendent’s Family', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Need Condo Cleaned? Consider the Superintendent’s Family', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Building Service Employees', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nir, Sarah Maslin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T22:54:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24a874d8-9fcb-535b-b1b5-9b79e952b7f5', 'word_count': 959, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24a874d8-9fcb-535b-b1b5-9b79e952b7f5'}, {'abstract': 'The preface to a new book on mathematics — a subject woven into the very existence of our lives that’s embraced by very few of us.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/science/excerpt-love-and-math.html', 'snippet': 'The preface to a new book on mathematics — a subject woven into the very existence of our lives that’s embraced by very few of us.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s a secret world out there. A hidden parallel universe of beauty and elegance, intricately intertwined with ours. It’s the world of mathematics. And it’s invisible to most of us. This book is an invitation to discover this world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Excerpt: ‘Love and Math’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-18T23:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Frenkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Frenkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Text', '_id': 'nyt://article/10075a1f-327e-55ba-aceb-4fa0999c4667', 'word_count': 2956, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10075a1f-327e-55ba-aceb-4fa0999c4667'}, {'abstract': 'In the former Soviet Union, Edward Frenkel was denied admission to the best mathematics program because he was a Jew. But as he recounts in “Love & Math,” the now-renowned mathematician didn’t let that stop him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/science/in-love-math-fighting-discrimination-through-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'In the former Soviet Union, Edward Frenkel was denied admission to the best mathematics program because he was a Jew. But as he recounts in “Love & Math,” the now-renowned mathematician didn’t let that stop him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1984, when he was 16, Edward Frenkel was subjected to a malicious interrogation. Already a brilliant budding mathematician, he had applied for admission to “Mekh-Mat” at Moscow State University, the top mathematics program in the Soviet Union. But when he attended the critical oral entrance exam, his dream of becoming a professional mathematician came crashing down.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 902, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 902}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/science/19SCIB/19SCIB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1363, 'subType': 'superJumbo'