ument.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/egyptian-protesters-destroy-tahrir-square-monument-erected-by-interim-government/', 'snippet': 'Hours after the military-led government dedicated a memorial to the uprisings that toppled two authoritarian presidents in two years, protesters swarmed the monument.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, Tuesday, 9:56 a.m. | Just hours after Egypt’s military-led interim government tried to cement its claim to revolutionary legitimacy — with the dedication of a memorial to the uprisings that toppled two authoritarian presidents in two years — protesters swarmed the monument in the center of Tahrir Square on Monday night and defaced it, chanting, “The revolution’s returned to Tahrir.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Protesters Destroy Tahrir Square Monument Erected by Interim Government', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T00:32:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey and Liam Stack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Liam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/99c43b0f-f9b5-55b6-9ba1-38f7c6ab0c6d', 'word_count': 424, 'uri': 'nyt://article/99c43b0f-f9b5-55b6-9ba1-38f7c6ab0c6d'}, {'abstract': 'The Howard Hughes Corporation, which controls the South Street Seaport under a lease with the city, says it wants to enliven the area and establish a destination for both tourists and New Yorkers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/nyregion/seaport-redevelopment-plan-inc