imes', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/18/nyregion/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8/DIRTBIKE-ss-slide-6SD8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Many Wheels, but No Place to Ride Them', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL-TERRAIN VEHICLES (ATV)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T01:11:20+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'New York', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/26992748-898b-5897-bae1-0b2b592336b5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/26992748-898b-5897-bae1-0b2b592336b5'}, {'abstract': 'The attackers behind the siege of the Westgate shopping mall had been living in Nairobi and plotted the attack for several months, a Western official briefed on the investigation said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/world/africa/kenya-new-details-on-mall-attackers.html', 'snippet': 'The attackers behind the siege of the Westgate shopping mall had been living in Nairobi and plotted the attack for several months, a Western official briefed on the investigation said.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The attackers behind the siege of the Westgate shopping mall that left more than 60 people dead in September had been living in Nairobi and plotted the attack for several months, a Western official briefed on the investigation said Monday. Kenyan officials say they believe they have determined the identities of the four attackers who stormed the mall. All four of the men are Somali citizens, though one of the men, previously identified as Hassan Abdi Dhuhulow, grew up in Norway. Remains recovered from the mall that are believed to be those of the attackers are still undergoing forensic testing at an F.B.I. laboratory, the Western official said. A Somali militant group, the Shabab, claimed responsibility for the attack. The four men entered the country from Somalia in June and lived in Nairobi’s Somali neighborhood, Eastleigh. Kenyan authorities initially said that up to 15 assailants were involved in the attack, but only four are visible on mall surveillance tapes. Four other men have been charged as accomplices. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Kenya: New Details on Mall Attackers', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kenya: New Details on Mall Attackers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nairobi, Kenya, Westgate Mall Shootings (2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kulish, Nicholas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shabab', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nairobi (Kenya)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T01:12:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kulish', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kulish', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc6de7e2-bd78-572a-96d3-d324958a18f3', 'word_count': 167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc6de7e2-bd78-572a-96d3-d324958a18f3'}, {'abstract': 'Complaints about noisy dirt bikes and reckless driving by riders who disobey laws are increasing, with more than 200 cases reported this summer alone.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/nyregion/for-new-york-citys-dirt-bikers-there-is-nowhere-to-ride.html', 'snippet': 'Complaints about noisy dirt bikes and reckless driving by riders who disobey laws are increasing, with more than 200 cases reported this summer alone.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The young man tore down the asphalt, the roar of his dirt bike trailing like a comet’s tail. When it seemed he could not go any faster, he went higher, hauling the bike into a near-vertical wheelie but never slowing down. A dozen other riders crisscrossed his path, their own front wheels aloft to the perfect fall sky.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 384}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 655, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/DIRTBIKE1/DIRTBIKE1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For New York City’s Dirt Bikers, There Is No Place to Ride', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Dirt Bikers in the City, There Is No Place to Ride', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nir, Sarah Maslin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Motorcycles, Motor Bikes and Motorscooters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALL-TERRAIN VEHICLES (ATV)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T01:13:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Maslin Nir and J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Maslin', 'lastname': 'Nir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5816e5a6-fed4-597c-9dd2-0ce8bfc4b88e', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5816e5a6-fed4-597c-9dd2-0ce8bfc4b88e'}, {'abstract': 'The executive, María de los Angeles González, 55, agreed to cooperate with prosecutors, suggesting there could be further revelations about corruption at the government-controlled bank, the Economic and Social Development Bank of Venezuela.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/world/americas/venezuela-former-bank-official-pleads-guilty-in-bribery-case.html', 'snippet': 'The executive, María de los Angeles González, 55, agreed to cooperate with prosecutors, suggesting there could be further revelations about corruption at the government-controlled bank, the Economic and Social Development Bank of Venezuela.', 'lead_paragraph': ' A former executive at a Venezuelan bank pleaded guilty in a New York federal court on Monday to charges stemming from a scheme in which she took bribes in exchange for steering millions of dollars of the bank’s business to an American brokerage firm. The executive, María de los Angeles González, 55, agreed to cooperate with prosecutors, suggesting there could be further revelations about corruption at the government-controlled bank, the Economic and Social Development Bank of Venezuela, known as Bandes. A plea agreement signed by Ms. González indicated that the corruption she was involved in went much further than previously revealed and that she admitted involvement in several other payoff schemes at Bandes and another government-run bank where she worked as an officer, Industrial Bank of Venezuela. The agreement said that the charges that Ms. González pleaded guilty to carried sentences totaling up to 55 years in jail. Ms. González was arrested in Miami in May. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Former Bank Official Pleads Guilty in Bribery Case', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Former Bank Official Pleads Guilty in Bribery Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gonzalez, Maria de los Angeles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Economic and Social Development Bank of Venezuela', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T01:23:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7279c06-d75f-5497-b7d4-dbb58d68f7a0', 'word_count': 156, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7279c06-d75f-5497-b7d4-dbb58d68f7a0'}, {'abstract': 'In Lower Manhattan, the security continues to be very tight — too tight for some New Yorkers who remember living in a more freewheeling city.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/nyregion/more-than-a-decade-after-9-11-a-bull-market-for-barriers-and-checkpoints.html', 'snippet': 'In Lower Manhattan, the security continues to be very tight — too tight for some New Yorkers who remember living in a more freewheeling city.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When United Airlines Flight 175 hit the South Tower, the windows in Mark Scherzer’s apartment collapsed inward in a fine spray of glass shards. Then the tower collapsed and a metal beam flew in, true as an arrow. Dust, inches thick, covered his floors, bed and shelves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/GOTHAM1/GOTHAM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/GOTHAM1/GOTHAM1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/GOTHAM1/GOTHAM1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/GOTHAM1/GOTHAM1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/nyregion/GOTHAM1/GOTHAM1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, '