, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bears', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cutler, Jay', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trestman, Marc', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T01:45:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Strauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Strauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14f30f6e-ea5c-51fa-871c-dfaa5909bad0', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14f30f6e-ea5c-51fa-871c-dfaa5909bad0'}, {'abstract': 'The stumbles in the rollout of the Obama administration’s health reform are frustrating, but they are not a broad indictment of government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/opinion/a-new-gop-excuse-for-doing-nothing.html', 'snippet': 'The stumbles in the rollout of the Obama administration’s health reform are frustrating, but they are not a broad indictment of government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With unrestrained glee, Republicans are using the calamitous debut of the Affordable Care Act as their latest justification for undermining all of health care reform. But they’re not stopping there. The Obama administration’s fumbling is apparently a good excuse for them to do nothing on immigration reform, on a budget agreement, and on any other initiative coming out of the White House.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New G.O.P. Excuse for Doing Nothing', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New G.O.P. Excuse for Doing Nothing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T01:50:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2420e62b-7a14-5cda-8009-032f065f1ab7', 'word_count': 542, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2420e62b-7a14-5cda-8009-032f065f1ab7'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Park’s best-selling books starred a sassy grade schooler with an imperfect grasp of English grammar who always found herself in some sort of predicament.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/arts/barbara-park-author-of-junie-b-jones-series-dies-at-66.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Park’s best-selling books starred a sassy grade schooler with an imperfect grasp of English grammar who always found herself in some sort of predicament.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Barbara Park, whose children’s books starring Junie B. Jones, a 6-year-old dispenser of abundant opinions, Runyonesque wisecracks and dubious syntax, have sold tens of millions of copies and delighted all but the most grammatically puritanical parents and teachers, died on Friday at her home in Scottsdale, Ariz. She was 66.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima