b_date': '2013-11-19T01:50:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margalit Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margalit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/cd0038bb-81f2-56dd-a26e-346509e8b43f', 'word_count': 672, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cd0038bb-81f2-56dd-a26e-346509e8b43f'}, {'abstract': 'My writing brain has been waiting for something exactly like the dizzyingly overfull, warp-speed web.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/18/the-internet-a-welcome-distraction/', 'snippet': 'My writing brain has been waiting for something exactly like the dizzyingly overfull, warp-speed web.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every time somebody says to me, “It’s so impressive how you manage to get writing done despite being on Facebook/Twitter/etc. all the time,” I cringe. I’ve been hit by a backhanded compliment. I’m surfing, tweeting and emailing — leaving my digital prints everywhere and probably picking up some nasty computer viruses — while serious writers are working pristinely, heroically beyond the clutches of the Internet.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Internet: A Welcome Distraction', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T02:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marie Myung-Ok Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marie', 'middlename': 'Myung-ok', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1236782-549a-5eff-96de-bbfcb420d1ee', 'word_count': 1237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1236782-549a-5eff-96de-bbfcb420d1ee'}, {'abstract': 'In Alabama, a bizarre arrangement allows elected judges to override a jury verdict of life in prison and unilaterally impose a death sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/opinion/death-meted-out-by-politicians-in-robes.html', 'snippet': 'In Alabama, a bizarre arrangement allows elected judges to override a jury verdict of life in prison and unilaterally impose a death sentence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In nearly all of the 32 states that permit capital punishment, a jury makes the final decision on whether a defendant will live or die. Not so in Alabama, where elected judges may override a jury verdict of life in prison and unilaterally impose a death sentence. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Death Meted Out by Politicians in Robes', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Death Meted Out by Politicians in Robes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Capital Punishment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sotomayor, Sonia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T02:00:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/43ac1223-4c6f-51db-ad71-d92c5c02f480', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/43ac1223-4c6f-51db-ad71-d92c5c02f480'}, {'abstract': 'An official from a European group of retailers claimed that American retailers were trying to avoid paying for safety improvements at factories and criticized an inspection effort by Walmart.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/business/international/europeans-fault-american-safety-effort-in-bangladesh.html', 'snippet': 'An official from a European group of retailers claimed that American retailers were trying to avoid paying for safety improvements at factories and criticized an inspection effort by Walmart.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tensions broke into the open on Monday involving two large groups of retailers — one overwhelmingly American, the other dominated by Europeans — that have formed to improve factory safety in Bangladesh. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/business/Garment/Garment-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/business/Garment/Garment-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/business/Garment/Garment-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/business/Garment/Garment-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/business/Garment/Garment-thumbStand