, more than 30 animal rights organizations have petitioned the government, a partner in the event, to cancel the shows because of cruelty to the animals.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Stop Animal Circus Shows, Advocates Tell Government', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACROBATS AND ACROBATICS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ANIMALS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Circuses', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tigers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangdong Province (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hong Kong', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T03:10:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shaojie Huang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shaojie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Huang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19a33e77-5a04-501f-987a-04b102aad066', 'word_count': 649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19a33e77-5a04-501f-987a-04b102aad066'}, {'abstract': 'Hampered by a strained hamstring, point guard Raymond Felton is shooting below his career average and struggling defensively.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/sports/basketball/felton-is-missing-shots-and-those-he-guards-are-not.html', 'snippet': 'Hampered by a strained hamstring, point guard Raymond Felton is shooting below his career average and struggling defensively.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GREENBURGH, N.Y. — Raymond Felton was a spectator for most of Monday’s practice. He sat on a training table next to Tyson Chandler, whose fractured right leg was no longer encased in a protective boot. This counted as progress for the Knicks, whose training facility has doubled as a sanitarium this season.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 949, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 949}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 648, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1295, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/sports/KNICKS/KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Felton Is Missing Shots, and Those He Guards Are Not', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Felton Is Missing Shots, and Those He Guards Are Not', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Felton, Raymond', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sports Injuries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T03:19:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e71e79ad-59bc-50b3-90d7-d5b292fd31ac', 'word_count': 957, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e71e79ad-59bc-50b3-90d7-d5b292fd31ac'}, {'abstract': 'Colorado’s new rules will help fulfill the promise of natural gas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/opinion/nocera-frackings-achilles-heel.html', 'snippet': 'Colorado’s new rules will help fulfill the promise of natural gas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s not very often that someone starts his career as a geologist and then winds up as governor, but John Hickenlooper, the governor of Colorado, can make that claim. “We had fracking when I was a working geologist in 1981,” he told me on Monday. “It was very primitive. What really changed the world is when we got horizontal drilling. It was a technique that allowed you to recover a lot more natural gas.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/11/01/opinion/nocera-circular/nocera-circu