76-5371-9737-8f736a6a2fcc', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ae30d54-e976-5371-9737-8f736a6a2fcc'}, {'abstract': 'Ten years ago, Republicans closed ranks to push through Medicare coverage for prescription drugs, misleading the public while adding billions to the federal deficit, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/medicare-part-d-republican-budget-busting/', 'snippet': 'Ten years ago, Republicans closed ranks to push through Medicare coverage for prescription drugs, misleading the public while adding billions to the federal deficit, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Bartlett held senior policy roles in the Reagan and George H.W. Bush administrations and served on the staffs of Representatives Jack Kemp and Ron Paul. He is the author of “The Benefit and the Burden: Tax Reform — Why We Need It and What It Will Take.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Medicare Part D: Republican Budget-Busting', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Budget (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T05:01:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Bartlett', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bartlett', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/780b7001-b213-51ed-a5dd-1d57d273d406', 'word_count': 1140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/780b7001-b213-51ed-a5dd-1d57d273d406'}, {'abstract': 'This word has appeared in five New York Times articles in the past year.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/word-of-the-day-defrock/', 'snippet': 'This word has appeared in five New York Times articles in the past year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'defrock •\\(ˌ)de-ˈfräk\\• verb ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Word of the Day | defrock', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T05:06:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f51858cd-fb4f-5099-9bf0-fd89123168c2', 'word_count': 202, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f51858cd-fb4f-5099-9bf0-fd89123168c2'}, {'abstract': 'LaTroy Hawkins, 40, followed Marlon Byrd’s lead, becoming the latest Met to play well enough to price himself out of the team’s plans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/sports/baseball/hawkins-leaves-mets-for-rockies.html', 'snippet': 'LaTroy Hawkins, 40, followed Marlon Byrd’s lead, becoming the latest Met to play well enough to price himself out of the team’s plans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LaTroy Hawkins, 40, followed Marlon Byrd’s lead, becoming the latest Met to play well enough to price himself out of the team’s plans. Hawkins agreed to a one-year, $2.5 million contract with the Colorado Rockies, and will have a chance to be the team’s closer, according to a source with knowledge of the negotiations. In 72 relief appearances with the Mets, Hawkins compiled a 2.93 earned run average and had 13 saves. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hawkins Leaves Mets for Rockies', 'kicker': 'Sports Briefing | Baseball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hawkins Leaves Mets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Mets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hawkins, Latroy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Colorado Rockies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T05:11:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Rohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rohan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/11ce2388-d81e-535d-a222-9d8a7a92c5d1', 'word_count': 72, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11ce2388-d81e-535d-a222-9d8a7a92c5d1'}, {'abstract': 'The suspension of a prize-winning reporter has provided more inspiration for the animators at Next Media of Taiwan.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/another-animated-take-on-bloomberg-news/', 'snippet': 'The suspension of a prize-winning reporter has provided more inspiration for the animators at Next Media of Taiwan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Next Media Animation of Taiwan is staying at the vanguard of coverage of the Bloomberg News self-censorship saga. It has posted its second take on the scandal — which, of course, Bloomberg says is not a scandal. Top Bloomberg editors have denied killing a story on a Chinese tycoon and his ties to Communist Party leaders for political reasons, despite accounts from several Bloomberg employees that that was the case.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Animated Take on Bloomberg News', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Forsythe, Michael', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winkler, Matthew', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bloomberg Business News', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Next Media Animation Ltd', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T05:50:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/95be8517-037f-5001-8af9-7a14a8ba9719', 'word_count': 203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95be8517-037f-5001-8af9-7a14a8ba9719'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '4:45 P.M. (IFC) JACKIE BROWN (1997) Pam Grier, above, stars as Jackie Brown, a flight attendant who makes ends meet by smuggling money from Mexico to the United States for a gun dealer named Ordell Robbie (Samuel L. Jackson) in this adaptation of the book “Rum Punch,” by Elmore Leonard, written for the screen and directed by Quentin Tarantino. When she is caught by a government agent (Michael Keaton), Jackie seeks to escape her menial existence with the help of a kindly bail bondsman (Robert Forster). “Among the best news about the film is that Samuel L. Jackson’s role is even splashier than the one he had in ‘Pulp Fiction’ and that his performance is even more of a treat,” Janet Maslin wrote in The New York Times. “The film more than justifies its long, happy stretches of simply watching Ordell work his scams on the unsuspecting.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e7a8668-30ed-5438-a326-ae8826fd8061', 'word_count': 725, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e7a8668-30ed-5438-a326-ae8826fd8061'}, {'abstract': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/news-quiz-november-19-2013/', 'snippet': 'See what you know about the news of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'See what you know about the news below. To prepare, you might scan the articles or summaries on today’s paper. Good luck!', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'News Quiz | November 19, 2013', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T06:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anastasia Economides', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anastasia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Economides', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/17b07a89-5f2e-50c6-9a38-8064b71f6502', 'word_count': 22, 'uri': 'nyt://article/17b07a89-5f2e-50c6-9a38-8064b71f6502'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Prasad spoke about India’s expectations from the annual United Nations climate change conference in Warsaw, Poland.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/a-conversation-with-indias-chief-climate-change-negotiator-ravi-shankar-prasad/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Prasad spoke about India’s expectations from the annual United Nations climate change conference in Warsaw, Poland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WARSAW, Poland — The annual United Nations climate change conference, which runs from Nov. 11 to 22, started with an emotional appeal from the Philippine negotiator Yeb Sano, who declared that he would be fasting “until a meaningful outcome is in sight” in the wake of the \xa0“staggering” devastation from Typhoon Haiyan in his country.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-negotiator-IndiaInk/19-negotiator-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-negotiator-IndiaInk/19-negotiator-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-negotiator-IndiaInk/19-negotiator-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-negotiator-IndiaInk/19-negotiator-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's