uwahatis-cosmetic-development/', 'snippet': 'The author writes about the changes that his hometown has undergone over the years.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I come from Guwahati—a small town in the northeastern part of India,” I used to tell my friends in Minnesota, until one person asked me how large is Guwahati. When I answered, he looked at me shocked, “A small town of\xa0only\xa01.4 million people?” I smiled sheepishly because it was partly true, and partly untrue. Untrue because I had grown up believing that my Guwahati is a small town. True because, nowadays even I suspect that during my absence over the years—like a young girl in a large family — Guwahati has as if stealthily grown up without my notice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 305, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 305}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 521, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1042, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/19/world/asia/19-flood-IndiaInk/19-flood-IndiaInk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Guwahati’s Cosmetic Development', 'kicker': 'India Ink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Floods', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Rupee (Currency)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping Centers and Malls', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Assam State (India)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guwahati (India)', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T13:47:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aruni Kashyap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aruni', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kashyap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a34ef44b-288e-50f8-bb27-d6e4115877c3', 'word_count': 1794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a34ef44b-288e-50f8-bb27-d6e4115877c3'}, {'abstract': 'Getting the facts on retirement right.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/the-geezers-are-not-alright/', 'snippet': 'Getting the facts on retirement right.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Washington Post editorial board wants to cut Medicare and Social Security. That has been its consistent position as long as I can remember. And what it advocates, always, are cuts in benefits, not costs — that is, while it may give lip service to efforts to control health-care costs (which seem to be going surprisingly well, in one of the untold success stories of Obamacare), what it has pushed repeatedly are things like a rise in the Medicare age. These are the kind of moves that are considered serious inside the Beltway. And as you might imagine, the Post has gone wild over recent suggestions that Social Security should be expanded, not cut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Geezers Are Not Alright', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T13:48:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/19f4fc63-b9b3-510b-aef9-89a792eb123d', 'word_count': 420, 'uri': 'nyt://article/19f4fc63-b9b3-510b-aef9-89a792eb123d'}, {'abstract': 'Coaching hires typically takes years to evaluate, but all eight new coaches in the league are either exceeding expectations or providing hope for the future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/sports/football/changing-coaches-has-improved-fortunes-in-nfl.html', 'snippet': 'Coaching hires typically takes years to evaluate, but all eight new coaches in the league are either exceeding expectations or providing hope for the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'N.F.L. teams are rarely patient. Owners and general managers are more apt to replace a struggling coach than to support him. This past off-season, eight teams switched coaches, not including New Orleans, which welcomed the return of Sean Payton after his one-year suspension. A coaching hire typically takes years to evaluate, but through 12 weeks, all eight coaches are either exceeding expectations or providing hope for the future.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/sports/20nflscore1/20nflscore1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/sports/20nflscore1/20nflscore1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/sports/20nflscore1/20nflscore1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/sports/20nflscore1/20nflscore1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/sports/20nflscore1/20nflscore1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'