 the background, the Iranian foreign minister, Mohammad Javad Zarif, strides through a vast, elegant hallway, skips down carpeted steps and pushes through glass-paneled doors. Then, seated, he looks directly at a video camera and asks: “What is dignity? What is respect? Are they negotiable? Is there a price tag?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'On YouTube, Iranian Minister Says ‘Join Us’ in Ending Crisis', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zarif, Mohammad Javad', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T17:13:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30711f98-29ae-5422-b2ea-dc3ea40c6297', 'word_count': 631, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30711f98-29ae-5422-b2ea-dc3ea40c6297'}, {'abstract': 'Edward Everett, who spoke before Lincoln delivered his famous speech, has been unfairly forgotten.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/the-other-gettysburg-address/', 'snippet': 'Edward Everett, who spoke before Lincoln delivered his famous speech, has been unfairly forgotten.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Even before the address was given, Americans knew that a great speech was coming, and that it would come at Gettysburg. The battle had been so comprehensive, and its result so profound, that a lasting statement was needed to mark the burial of the dead. That the final resting place of the soldiers was in the North, conveniently close to media outlets, only added to the logic of a solemn utterance for the ages. Accordingly, an invitation went out to the person most likely to give it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Other Gettysburg Address', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Public Speaking', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lincoln, Abraham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gettysburg (Pa)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T17:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Widmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Widmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa7e1c8e-b5dd-5d61-8501-ce1f4a308295', 'word_count': 1976, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa7e1c8e-b5dd-5d61-8501-ce1f4a308295'}, {'abstract': 'The plan, submitted to a judge for approval, would pay an estimated 8,000 patients who have been forced to have the flawed all-metal artificial hip replaced.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/business/johnson-johnson-to-offer-2-5-billion-hip-device-settlement.html', 'snippet': 'The plan, submitted to a judge for approval, would pay an estimated 8,000 patients who have been forced to have the flawed all-metal artificial hip replaced.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Johnson & Johnson and lawyers for patients injured by a flawed hip implant announced a multibillion-dollar deal on Tuesday to settle thousands of lawsuits, but it was not clear whether the deal would satisfy enough claimants.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1084, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/business/HIP/HIP-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Johnson & Johnson in Deal to Settle Hip Implant Lawsuits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'J.&J. in Deal to Settle Hip Implant Lawsuits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Implants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Johnson & Johnson', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toledo (Ohio)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T17:18:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a96ae69-6ece-50ab-9c85-679cf12aad21', 'word_count': 952, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a96ae69-6ece-50ab-9c85-679cf12aad21'}, {'abstract': 'Some artists called it a mass desecration, but the buildings’ owner, Jerry Wolkoff, said he would erect a wall where painters could work again.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/nyregion/5pointz-a-graffiti-mecca-in-queens-is-wiped-clean-overnight.html', 'snippet': 'Some artists called it a mass desecration, but the buildings’ owner, Jerry Wolkoff, said he would erect a wall where painters could work again.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Graffiti is often denounced as vandalism, but the deliriously festooned, sprawling warehouses at the western edge of Queens rose far above that. Blanketed with giddy images, drawing street artists from around the world, 5Pointz was a decades-old legal haven considered both a “United Nations of Graffiti” and a semi-rebellious statement in a city some feel is growing too antiseptic. “Save 5Pointz,” the infamous British street artist Banksy urged in his final message to New Yorkers, after he wrapped his monthlong spree clandestinely decorating the city’s streets in October.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 339, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 339}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 578, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1157, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/nyregion/FIVEPOINTZ1/FIVEPOINTZ1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Night Falls, and 5Pointz, a Graffiti Mecca, Is Whited Out in Queens', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Night Falls, and a Graffiti Mecca Is Whited Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graffiti', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': '5Pointz Arts Center', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolkoff, Jerry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T17:24:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cara Buckley and Marc Santora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Marc', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Santora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/652d9ad7-8514-5014-8bd7-8a22eef1da7c', 'word_count': 1078, 'uri': 'nyt://article/652d9ad7-8514-5014-8bd7-8a22eef1da7c'}, {'abstract': 'Ayr.com, a new online women’s wear destination, launches today with two lines of stylish skinny jeans.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/site-to-be-seen-from-the-makers-of-bonobos-a-shopping-site-for-the-ladies/', 'snippet': 'Ayr.com, a new online women’s wear destination, launches today with two lines of stylish skinny jeans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since 2007, men have been ordering pants from Bonobos.com, trying them on at home and returning them if they don’t fit. It was a way of shopping that fit the lifestyle of 20- and 30-somethings: without ever setting foot in a store or having to pay shipping costs. Today, the team behind Bonobos introduces Ayr.com, the women’s version of their successful men’s wear clearing house. Initially, the site will offer two styles of denim: skinny jeans ($175) and a cigarette leg ($165), each available in either a light or a dark wash. “I like to say you could do yoga in these jeans,” said the design director Jac Cameron, a veteran of Calvin Klein and Madewell. “I wanted to recreate a silhouette working with the stretch of the fabric to create a jean that molds to the body as you wear it.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'From the Makers of Bonobos, a Shopping Site for the Ladies', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jeans (Apparel)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kors, Michael', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bonobos.com', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Calvin Klein Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'J Crew Group', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Madewell', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T17:27:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d5956d2-f9e3-5d8c-8818-e4763ad0889a', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d5956d2-f9e3-5d8c-8818-e4763ad0889a'}, {'abstract': 'Half a century after President John F. Kennedy was killed, the city has been coming to grips with the worst moment in its history.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/11/12/us/20131114_DALLAS.html', 'snippet': 'Half a century after President John F. Kennedy was killed, the city has been coming to grips with the worst moment in its history.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Half a century after President John F. Kennedy was killed, the city has been coming to grips with the worst moment in its history.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/12/us/20131114_DALLAS-slide-KIR0/20131114_DALLAS-sli