le Nassau County enclave rebounding from the ravages of Hurricane Sandy, thanks to a network of close-knit, multigenerational families.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/realestate/island-park-sandy-as-mother-of-reinvention.html', 'snippet': 'An affordable Nassau County enclave rebounding from the ravages of Hurricane Sandy, thanks to a network of close-knit, multigenerational families.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, two days after Hurricane Sandy walloped the islet of Island Park, Rosmarie T. Bovino, the school superintendent, along with her principals and teachers, walked the square mile of the school district to see what each of its families needed. Though the two schools, the administration building and the public library had been devastated, Dr. Bovino, who calls the schools “the heart of the village,” wanted to “make sure the children had food to eat.” ', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Island Park: Sandy as Mother of Reinvention', 'kicker': 'Living in', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sandy as Mother of Reinvention', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fischler, Marcelle Sussman', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricane Sandy (2012)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nassau County (NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Island Park (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T19:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcelle Sussman Fischler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcelle', 'middlename': 'Sussman', 'lastname': 'Fischler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None},