e, including the singer Judy Collins, attended Pratt Institute’s Legends 2013 gala benefit, which honored four eminences in design and culture and raised nearly $800,000 for student scholarships. Held at the Mandarin Oriental Hotel in New York, the event was hosted by Ted Allen, of the Food Network series “Chopped.” The honorees were the writer Pete Hamill; the artist James Turrell; David Easton, an interior designer; and Margaret Russell, the editor in chief of Architectural Digest.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pratt Institute Celebrates Four Leaders in Design and Culture', 'kicker': 'Currents | Events', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pratt Institute', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T19:41:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elaine Louie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elaine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Louie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cddf5ce7-36a0-534a-933b-d3b1e4ad1f58', 'word_count': 496, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cddf5ce7-36a0-534a-933b-d3b1e4ad1f58'}, {'abstract': 'The first group of potential jurors included a member of Occupy Wall Street member and people who had been investigated by the S.E.C.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/jury-selection-begins-in-sac-insider-trading-trial/', 'snippet': 'The first group of potential jurors included a member of Occupy Wall Street member and people who had been investigated by the S.E.C.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Updated, 5:36 p.m. | Selection of a 12-member jury from a pool of about 100 p