'abstract': 'Other trends include plans with higher deductibles and programs that offer financial incentives for employees to take steps to improve their health.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/your-money/private-exchanges-rise-as-health-care-options.html', 'snippet': 'Other trends include plans with higher deductibles and programs that offer financial incentives for employees to take steps to improve their health.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE troubled rollout of the federal health insurance marketplace this fall has given the word “health exchange” a bad name. Nonetheless, some companies are choosing to offer their employees health benefits via private exchanges — online insurance marketplaces that are separate from the federal system.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/CHANGES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 534, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/CHANGES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 534}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/CHANGES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/CHANGES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 1574, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/20CHANGES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/20CHANGES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20CHANGES/20CHANGES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Private Exchanges Rise as Health Care Options', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Private Exchanges Rise as Health Care Options', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Savings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sears Holdings Corporation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:17:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d98de59f-bd52-5c47-8e56-385a948a50b9', 'word_count': 1183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d98de59f-bd52-5c47-8e56-385a948a50b9'}, {'abstract': 'People who have terminal diseases are living longer. Experts say simple strategies can make the most of the money at hand for those with foresight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/your-money/planning-for-a-future-in-the-face-of-terminal-illness.html', 'snippet': 'People who have terminal diseases are living longer. Experts say simple strategies can make the most of the money at hand for those with foresight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PATRICK SKELDON, a commercial airline pilot, started having trouble walking in the autumn of 2003. His doctor thought he had a vitamin deficiency and prescribed supplements. When those didn’t work, the doctor referred him to a neurologist. The next year, he was told he had amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, more commonly known as Lou Gehrig’s disease. He was 59.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DEATH_SPAN/20DEATH_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Planning for a Future in the Face of Terminal Illness', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Planning for a Future in the Face of Terminal Illness', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sullivan, Paul', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:18:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Sullivan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sullivan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/15c2e830-8343-5201-a987-65eb42f4da3a', 'word_count': 1901, 'uri': 'nyt://article/15c2e830-8343-5201-a987-65eb42f4da3a'}, {'abstract': 'The share of medical costs shouldered by retirees is growing, highlighting the need to save a lot more now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/your-money/you-plan-your-retirement-then-you-get-the-health-bill.html', 'snippet': 'The share of medical costs shouldered by retirees is growing, highlighting the need to save a lot more now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JEFF STRACK, a 61-year-old sales manager in Charlotte, N.C., enjoys his work and is in good health. But the prospect of paying for health costs after he retires weighs on him.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'You Plan Your Retirement, Then You Get the Health Bill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'You Plan Your Retirement, Then You Get the Health Bill', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Long-Term Care Insurance', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nursing Homes', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fidelity Investments', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Employee Benefit Research Institute', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Association for Long-Term Care Insurance', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/126ba553-5f0d-5a0a-85b2-ba849b7717b7', 'word_count': 2198, 'uri': 'nyt://article/126ba553-5f0d-5a0a-85b2-ba849b7717b7'}, {'abstract': 'One way that doctors stand out from the general population is in advance planning for the end of life, something that is gradually finding acceptance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/your-money/how-doctors-die.html', 'snippet': 'One way that doctors stand out from the general population is in advance planning for the end of life, something that is gradually finding acceptance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRAVE. You hear that word a lot when people are sick. It’s all about the fight, the survival instinct, the courage. But when Dr. Elizabeth D. McKinley’s family and friends talk about bravery, it is not so much about the way Dr. McKinley, a 53-year-old internist from Cleveland, battled breast cancer for 17 years. It is about the courage she has shown in doing something so few of us are able to do: stop fighting.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/DOCTORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/DOCTORS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/DOCTORS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/DOCTORS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/20DOCTORS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/20DOCTORS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20DOCTORS_SPAN/20DOCTORS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Doctors Die: Showing Others the Way', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Doctors Die', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorenstein, Dan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:19:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Gorenstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gorenstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93a2f5b6-4519-5212-b115-33d64ff1922d', 'word_count': 1646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93a2f5b6-4519-5212-b115-33d64ff1922d'}, {'abstract': 'A financial planner proposes “life panels,” chosen in advance, for people whose quality of life and mental capacity have  deteriorated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/your-money/for-those-at-deaths-door-a-case-for-life-panels.html', 'snippet': 'A financial planner proposes “life panels,” chosen in advance, for people whose quality of life and mental capacity have  deteriorated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AT the beginning of 2012, my mother was 95 years old. She lived in an assisted-living center, with hospice care, in a hospital bed 24/7. She was hollow-eyed and emaciated. Though she had moments of clarity, she was confused, anxious and uncomfortable. Her quality of life was minimal, at best. And the cost to keep her in this condition had risen to close to $100,000 a year.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUB-ESSAY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUB-ESSAY_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUB-ESSAY_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUB-ESSAY_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1495, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUBESSAY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUBESSAY_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/your-money/20SUBESSAY_SPAN/20SUBESSAY_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Those at Death’s Door, a Case for ‘Life Panels’', 'kicker': 'Essay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Those at Death’s Door, a Case for ‘Life Panels’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Living Wills and Health Care Proxies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Financial Planners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:21:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bob Goldman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bob', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8ba39759-09ea-504f-928b-0daceda56620', 'word_count': 1407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8ba39759-09ea-504f-928b-0daceda56620'}, {'abstract': 'The network has struggled most in the ratings this fall, and it announced five new series as it canceled “Betrayal.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/business/media/abc-shuffles-its-prime-time-lineup.html', 'snippet': 'The network has struggled most in the ratings this fall, and it announced five new series as it canceled “Betrayal.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ABC, the network that has struggled most in the ratings this fall, announced a series of changes to its prime-time schedule Tuesday, which included the addition of five new series and the cancellation of one flop. The network also unveiled a new entrant in its long-running effort to fashion a hit comedy in the half-hour following its biggest hit, “Modern Family.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'ABC Shuffles Its Prime-Time Lineup', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ABC INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ratings (Audience Measurement)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:25:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Carter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/53a580d1-47f6-5dcd-a490-e4f45a24891a', 'word_count': 257, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53a580d1-47f6-5dcd-a490-e4f45a24891a'}, {'abstract': 'Future Brown, a D.J. supergroup of genre-mashing artist-creators, gave its debut performance at MoMA PS1 last Sunday.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/19/art-matters-art-underground-music-and-basketball-collide-in-queens/', 'snippet': 'Future Brown, a D.J. supergroup of genre-mashing artist-creators, gave its debut performance at MoMA PS1 last Sunday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last Sunday afternoon, two different rhythms resounded through the VW Dome in the courtyard of MoMA PS1 in Queens. One was provided by Future Brown — a new D.J. supergroup made up of the genre-bending artists and musicians Fatima Al Qadiri; Asma Maroof and Daniel Pineda of Nguzunguzu; and J-Cush of Lit City Trax. The second, which synced well with the first, came from the steady bounce of basketballs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Art Matters | Art, Underground Music and Basketball Collide in Queens', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoMA PS1', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Queens (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-19T23:34:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'sect