es.com/2013/11/20/us/california-los-angeles-airport-shooting-suspect-leaves-hospital.html', 'snippet': 'Paul A. Ciancia, 23, accused of killing a federal agent at the Los Angeles International Airport, was released from a hospital Monday and taken to a federal holding facility, the authorities said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The man accused of killing a federal agent at Los Angeles International Airport was released from Ronald Reagan UCLA Medical Center on Monday\xa0and taken to a federal holding facility, the authorities said\xa0Tuesday. The suspect, Paul A. Ciancia, 23, is believed to have opened fire in the crowded terminal on Nov. 1, killing Gerardo I. Hernandez, 39, a\xa0Transportation\xa0Security Administration\xa0agent, and wounding two others. A spokesman for the United States attorney’s office said that “no details about his custody status or location are being released at this time.” Mr. Ciancia led police officers through a chase in the terminal and was shot in the head and leg. He was listed in critical condition for more than 10 days, and federal investigators were not able to question him. Mr. Ciancia could face the death penalty if convicted.\xa0 ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'California: Los Angeles Airport Shooting Suspect Leaves Hospital', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | West', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'California: Airport Shooting Suspect Leaves Hospital ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ciancia, Paul A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles International Airport', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Gerardo I', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Transportation Security Administration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name'