': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/6da8487e-f016-56df-8f12-286fb458d826', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6da8487e-f016-56df-8f12-286fb458d826'}, {'abstract': 'A report looks into the effects of solitary confinement at the campus of jails and how it can be a basket into which society drops the disruptive mentally ill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/nyregion/mentally-ill-and-jailed-in-isolation-at-rikers-island.html', 'snippet': 'A report looks into the effects of solitary confinement at the campus of jails and how it can be a basket into which society drops the disruptive mentally ill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the annals of Rikers Island comes a document titled, “Three Adolescents With Mental Illness in Punitive Segregation in Rikers Island.” Punitive segregation means solitary confinement for 23 hours a day. Schoolwork, if it comes, is passed through a slot in the cell door. Toothpaste is available once a day. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mentally Ill, and Jailed in Isolation at Rikers Island', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mentally Ill, And Jailed In Isolation', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rikers Island Prison Complex', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solitary Confinement', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T01:35:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf499cca-860b-505d-b49f-16988aaa0119', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf499cca-860b-505d-b49f-16988aaa0119'}, {'abstract': 'Indonesia has taken offense at reports that its close trading partner, Australia, used its embassies in Asia to collect intelligence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/world/asia/nsa-spying-scandal-tarnishes-relations-between-indonesia-and-australia.html', 'snippet': 'Indonesia has taken offense at reports that its close trading partner, Australia, used its embassies in Asia to collect intelligence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JAKARTA, Indonesia — The relationship between Indonesia and Australia, Pacific neighbors with a long history of cooperation and trade, has in recent years been marked by disagreements on a range of issues, including human rights, terrorism and asylum seekers. But relations reached a new low over the weekend over the latest bombshell from the surveillance scandal involving a third country, the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/world/JAKARTA/JAKARTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/world/JAKARTA/JAKARTA-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/world/JAKARTA/JAKARTA-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'ca