ajor': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Americans for Prosperity', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALASKA', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Carolina', 'rank': 18, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T01:40:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70d586df-d0a2-5408-b048-408c34399b8e', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70d586df-d0a2-5408-b048-408c34399b8e'}, {'abstract': 'The pianist Olli Mustonen brought his intensity to Shostakovich, Rachmaninoff and Bach at Zankel Hall.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/arts/music/the-pianist-olli-mustonen-brings-exuberance-to-zankel-hall.html', 'snippet': 'The pianist Olli Mustonen brought his intensity to Shostakovich, Rachmaninoff and Bach at Zankel Hall.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After playing Shostakovich’s Piano Sonata No. 2 in B minor at Zankel Hall last Tuesday evening, the pianist Olli Mustonen wiped the sweat from his brow and looked at the audience with an expression that hovered between exhaustion and resignation. He had just offered an impassioned rendition of this tormented piece, composed in 1943 after Shostakovich had been evacuated during the Siege of Leningrad. The composer dedicated the work to an important mentor, his teacher Leonid Nikolayev, who had died the previous year. Mr. Mustonen played the opening movement’s frenzied surges with powerful clarity, beautifully contrasting them with the yearning melody that unfolds between demonic outbursts. He brought a searching insight to the second movement Largo, with an emotionally subdued character that offers a respite between the angst of the outer movements. Mr. Mustonen’s judicious use of pedal and vivid touch created an impressive range of colors in the turbulent concluding section, in which a ruminative melody unfurls over rumbling bass chords and later, in the left hand, under intense right-hand patterns. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/OLLI/OLLI-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 361, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/OLLI/OLLI-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 361}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/OLLI/OLLI-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 616, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/OLLI/OLLI-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1232, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/OLLI/OLLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/OLLI/OLLI-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge