 I lived, you did the Hustle and other disco horrors when you were in public but — if you were to be considered a teen of good taste — when you got home, it was Jackson Browne who lived on your turntable*.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Handy Way of Communicating', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T03:00:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d62ba8d-78ac-568d-8f3b-f161a99061e9', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d62ba8d-78ac-568d-8f3b-f161a99061e9'}, {'abstract': 'Of the 13 states that have so far said they will allow consumers to renew canceled plans, all but four are led by Republican governors and have generally been opposed to the new health care law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/us/states-vary-in-stances-on-renewal-of-health-policies-deemed-noncompliant.html', 'snippet': 'Of the 13 states that have so far said they will allow consumers to renew canceled plans, all but four are led by Republican governors and have generally been opposed to the new health care law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just a few days after President Obama said that millions of consumers should be able to keep their old insurance plans for another year — even if they did not meet the requirements of his health care law — he is finding support among states that would not exactly be described as allies.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In S