d them to perform sexual acts. Justice David McCombs of the Superior Court of Ontario said that expert witnesses effectively refuted claims by Dr. Doodnaught’s lawyers that the women were suffering from sexual hallucinations brought on by anesthesia drugs. Dr. Doodnaught will be sentenced early next year and faces another hearing about his medical license. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Canada: Doctor Convicted of Molesting Female Patients', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Canada: Doctor Convicted of Molesting Female Patients', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Austen, Ian', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anesthesia and Anesthetics', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Doodnaught, George', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toronto (Ontario)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T04:18:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Austen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Austen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/a8c5962e-0070-56ac-bbd6-2c1d25bc4d1b', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a8c5962e-0070-56ac-bbd6-2c1d25bc4d1b'}, {'abstract': 'The rulings came a day after three Russian crew members from the ship, the Arctic Sunrise, were also granted bail.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/world/europe/russia-judges-grant-bail-to-nine-greenpeace-activists.html', 'snippet': 'The rulings came a day after three Russian crew members from the ship, the Arctic Sunrise, were also granted bail.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Russian judges in St. Petersburg granted bail to nine more crew members of a Greenpeace International ship who were arrested in September after a protest against oil drilling in the Arctic, all of them foreigners. The rulings came a day after three Russian crew members from the ship, the Arctic Sunrise, were also granted bail, though the detention of yet another activist, Colin Russel of Australia, was extended until February, as the investigation into the protest against an off-shore oil rig in the Pechora Sea continues. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia: Judges Grant Bail to Nine Greenpeace Activists', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Russia: Judges Grant Bail to Nine Greenpeace Activists', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Greenpeace', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Offshore Drilling and Exploration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T04:22:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/32aa4535-89e4-5304-833d-035bff214012', 'word_count': 86, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32aa4535-89e4-5304-833d-035bff214012'}, {'abstract': 'The National Assembly voted to give President Nicolás Maduro decree powers for one year, which will allow him to create laws on his own, without going through the legislative process.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/world/americas/venezuela-assembly-hands-more-powers-to-president.html', 'snippet': 'The National Assembly voted to give President Nicolás Maduro decree powers for one year, which will allow him to create laws on his own, without going through the legislative process.', 'lead_paragraph': ' The National Assembly on Tuesday voted to give President Nicolás Maduro decree powers for one year, which will allow him to create laws on his own, without going through the legislative process. The so-called special powers permit Mr. Maduro, a socialist, to make laws aimed at fighting corruption and regulating the economy, but critics say that in practice those areas are broad enough that there may be few limits over the reach of his decrees. Many Venezuelan presidents have been given similar decree powers, including Mr. Maduro’s predecesor and mentor, Hugo Chávez, who died in March. Mr. Maduro, who is grappling with runaway inflation and severe shortages of many basic goods, has said that he will quickly move to create a law widening price controls and capping business profits. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Venezuela: Assembly Hands More Powers to President', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Venezuela: Assembly Hands More Powers to President', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T04:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/2ba8163f-5f8d-5c6e-94e1-66580a6e9a24', 'word_count': 129, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2ba8163f-5f8d-5c6e-94e1-66580a6e9a24'}, {'abstract': 'Millions of Zimbabwe residents are at risk of waterborne diseases because of a water and sanitation crisis in the capital, Harare, Human Rights Watch said in a report.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/world/africa/zimbabwe-sanitation-crisis-causes-new-cholera-risk.html', 'snippet': 'Millions of Zimbabwe residents are at risk of waterborne diseases because of a water and sanitation crisis in the capital, Harare, Human Rights Watch said in a report.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Millions of Zimbabwe residents are at risk of waterborne diseases including a resumption of cholera because of a water and sanitation crisis in the capital, Harare, Human Rights Watch said in a report on Tuesday. The report, issued five years after cholera killed more than 4,000 Zimbabweans and sickened 100,000, described a collapse in water and sanitation services. Residents must often drink from shallow, unprotected wells befouled by sewage, according to the report, which was based on research conducted over the last two years. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zimbabwe: Sanitation Crisis Causes New Cholera Risk', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Africa', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zimbabwe: Sanitation Crisis Causes New Cholera Risk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zimbabwe', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Human Rights Watch', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value':