n': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29a6fae-8db4-5645-8aad-1270fa9f39bc', 'word_count': 713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29a6fae-8db4-5645-8aad-1270fa9f39bc'}, {'abstract': 'Enemies left, enemies right, and then there’s his family. Building an Afghan legacy is even more complicated than it appears.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/magazine/how-is-hamid-karzai-still-standing.html', 'snippet': 'Enemies left, enemies right, and then there’s his family. Building an Afghan legacy is even more complicated than it appears.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Karzai family graveyard lies a few miles outside Kandahar, on the edge of the village of Karz. On the day I drove there, burned-out cars stood rusting by the sides of the road, children splashed through open drains and bullet holes riddled the mud walls opposite checkpoints. Amid all this, the graveyard stood out — gleaming, immaculate. Straggling bougainvillea and mulberry trees blossomed over the calligraphic tiles topping the cream-colored walls. Through the double gates were lines of cypresses. In the middle stood a domed enclosure containing the graves of the clan elders.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24karzais1/mag-24Karzais-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24karzais1/mag-24Karzais-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24karzais1/mag-24Karzais-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '