yt://article/6214bc10-8223-5448-b45c-9c6c1a9d7363', 'word_count': 6746, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6214bc10-8223-5448-b45c-9c6c1a9d7363'}, {'abstract': 'Seventy years after three of the bloodiest days in modern American history, the battle continues to bring the missing men back home.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/magazine/the-search-for-the-lost-marines-of-tarawa.html', 'snippet': 'Seventy years after three of the bloodiest days in modern American history, the battle continues to bring the missing men back home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We had been on the island for about an hour when we found the first skeleton. It was a pile of yellow bones tucked inside a cardboard box. Mark Noah squatted down for a look. He is a stocky man of 48, with a light buzz of blond hair and the wind-beaten eyes of a lifelong outdoorsman. Since 2008, he has been traveling to the tiny Pacific atoll of Tarawa to search for the remains of more than 500 Marines who died there in World War II. Sometimes locals dig up their bones and leave them in his storage locker.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24mia3/24mia3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 579, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24mia3/24mia3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 579, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24mia3/24mia3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24mia3/24mia3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7