obs Returns Home', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brilliant, Lawrence B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Laurene Powell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jobs, Steven P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T13:00:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Wingfield', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wingfield', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f915b891-0dd9-5a99-9e16-611333c8c26b', 'word_count': 992, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f915b891-0dd9-5a99-9e16-611333c8c26b'}, {'abstract': 'A JPMorgan Chase settlement offers a rare glimpse into Wall Street’s mortgage machine before the financial crisis. | A former Dell employee at the center of an insider trading case has not been accused of wrongdoing. | An Alabama county’s unusual plan to exit from bankruptcy may create a template. | Devon Energy is near a deal to buy GeoSouthern Energy for about $6 billion.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/morning-agenda-a-glimpse-into-jpmorgans-mortgage-machine/', 'snippet': 'A JPMorgan Chase settlement offers a rare glimpse into Wall Street’s mortgage machine before the financial crisis. | A former Dell employee at the center of an insider trading case has not been accused of wrongdoing. | An Alabama county’s unusual ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'JPMORGAN SETTLEMENT OFFERS LOOK INTO MORTGAGE MACHINE \xa0|\xa0 The record $13 billion settlement between JPMorgan Chase and the Justice Department on Tuesday wraps up a series of state and federal investigations that offer a rare glimpse into Wall Street’s mortgage machine before the financial crisis, Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Ben Protess report in DealBook. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Morning Agenda: A Glimpse Into JPMorgan’s Mortgage Machine', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T13:12:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11ccb0da-ea4c-5975-9d24-addffe783f58', 'word_count': 1951, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11ccb0da-ea4c-5975-9d24-addffe783f58'}, {'abstract': 'There is no way to know how the government’s cooperating witness in the trial of Michael S. Steinberg will come across to the jury.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/cooperating-witness-a-key-in-sac-insider-trading-case/', 'snippet': 'There is no way to know how the government’s cooperating witness in the trial of Michael S. Steinberg will come across to the jury.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Justice Department has had a perfect record in winning insider trading cases since it began its most recent campaign in 2009. Now, it will put that record to the test as the trial of Michael S. Steinberg, a former portfolio manager at SAC Capital Advisors, begins this week. The case will highlight the crucial issue in most white-collar crime prosecutions: What did the defendant know about the illegal nature of the transactions?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/business/dbpix-henn