unlikely.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/political-questions-about-the-jobs-report/', 'snippet': 'Did Census Bureau employees fake unemployment data in a way that could have altered the official jobless rate and aided President Obama’s re-election campaign? It seems unlikely.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With the economy dominating the campaign for the White House last fall, did the government cook the books to make the unemployment rate move lower and help President Obama’s re-election chances? Was manipulation responsible for lowering the unemployment rate to 7.8 percent in September 2012 from 8.1 percent in August, a big deal when the numbers came out in October 2012, just weeks before the election?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Political Questions About the Jobs Report', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2012', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Census Bureau', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Post', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T14:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nelson D. Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nelson', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef2eb813-53ef-5c28-81e5-a3636c4e4ede