 mess, and reflects very badly on Obama. But the future of the reform depends not on policy per se but on whether the IT issues can be fixed well enough soon enough, a subject on which I have zero expertise.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of Obamacare', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T16:02:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a44f4406-9a1d-5db1-bc06-46e0560f57de', 'word_count': 292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a44f4406-9a1d-5db1-bc06-46e0560f57de'}, {'abstract': 'The owner of a restaurant chain is sentenced to prison for tax evasion. How a small-business exemption could undermine an online sales tax. Are we in a tech bubble?', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/today-in-small-business-577-million-vacation-days/', 'snippet': 'The owner of a restaurant chain is sentenced to prison for tax evasion. How a small-business exemption could undermine an online sales tax. Are we in a tech bubble?', 'lead_paragraph': 'What’s affecting me, my clients and other small-business owners today.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Today in Small Business: 577 Million Vacation Days', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Start-ups', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2