serve tries to calibrate the unemployment target in its monetary policy, it can afford to aim for a far lower rate without inviting an unacceptable level of inflation, two economists write.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/the-unemployment-rate-at-full-employment-how-low-can-you-go/', 'snippet': 'As the Federal Reserve tries to calibrate the unemployment target in its monetary policy, it can afford to aim for a far lower rate without inviting an unacceptable level of inflation, two economists write.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jared Bernstein is a senior fellow at the Center on Budget and Policy Priorities. Dean Baker is a co-director of the Center for Economic and Policy Research. They are the authors of “Getting Back to Full Employment: A Better Bargain for Working People,” being published this week.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unemployment Rate at Full Employment: How Low Can You Go?', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Greenspan, Alan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meyer, Laurence H', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yellen, Janet L', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Congressional Budget Office', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T18:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsec