: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c04d2e2c-db24-5f5b-b4a5-0e238c75b227', 'word_count': 1100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c04d2e2c-db24-5f5b-b4a5-0e238c75b227'}, {'abstract': 'Human fingers work fine on touch screens for most purposes, but a stylus may bring out your inner artist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/technology/personaltech/painting-with-a-stylus-despite-what-steve-jobs-said.html', 'snippet': 'Human fingers work fine on touch screens for most purposes, but a stylus may bring out your inner artist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When he introduced the iPhone and iPad, Steven P. Jobs asserted the touch-screen devices didn’t need a stylus because humans come with 10 great touch-screen controllers sticking out of our palms: fingers. He was proved right, and most new smartphones and tablets don’t require a stylus to work their touch screen.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/21smart-inline1/21smart-inline1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Painting With a Stylus, Despite What Steve Jobs Said', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Painting With a Stylus, Despite What Steve Jobs Said', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eaton, Kit', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mobile Applications', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T18:07:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kit Eaton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kit', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eaton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e0d0287-99ab-5618-bd8c-07f8fe8e25b7', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e0d0287-99ab-5618-bd8c-07f8fe8e25b7'}, {'abstract': 'The riot grrrl legend, the subject of the documentary “The Punk Singer,” reflects on her early days with Bikini Kill, battling Lyme disease and life with husband Adam Horovitz of the Beastie Boys. Plus: see an exclusive clip from the film here.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/q-a-kathleen-hanna-on-love-illness-and-the-life-affirming-joy-of-punk-rock/', 'snippet': 'The riot grrrl legend, the subject of the documentary “The Punk Singer,” reflects on her early days with Bikini Kill, battling Lyme disease and life with husband Adam Horovitz of the Beastie Boys. Plus: see an exclusive clip from the film here.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the incendiary lead singer of the band Bikini Kill, Kathleen Hanna became the most famous face of the riot grrrl movement, the early-’90s feminist counterpart to grunge. (She coined the phrase “smells like teen spirit,” which her friend Kurt Cobain would make famous.) Later, she moved from the Pacific Northwest to New York City, where she fronted the socially conscious dance-rock outfit Le Tigre, and most recently she founded the band the Julie Ruin, which released the kinetic record “Run Fast” in September.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A. | Kathleen Hanna on Love, Illness and the Life-Affirming Joy of Punk Rock', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Person: Rock’s True Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Julie Ruin (Music Group)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Le Tigre', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T18:24:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT DIEHL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DIEHL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37a938d9-a5b5-507a-af98-a786895f14d1', 'word_count': 1347, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37a938d9-a5b5-507a-af98-a786895f14d1'}, {'abstract': 'When voters are asked to weigh in on reproductive rights issues directly, the results often go counter to the restrictive trend at the legislative level.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/albuquerque-rejects-20-week-abortion-ban/', 'snippet': 'When voters are asked to weigh in on reproductive rights issues directly, the results often go counter to the restrictive trend at the legislative level.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier in 2013, the House proposed a ban on abortion after 20 weeks, and twelve states have gone ahead and enacted such bans. But when Americans are asked if legislators should be spending their time restricting the abortion window, most respondents say no. And the more Americans hear about what a 20-week bans really entail, the more they grow wary of them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Albuquerque Rejects 20-Week Abortion Ban', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALBUQUERQUE (NM)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T18:30:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Juliet Lapidos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Juliet', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lapidos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cc9430f5-e3e3-5a0a-a11e-532047a51903', 'word_count': 161, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cc9430f5-e3e3-5a0a-a11e-532047a51903'}, {'abstract': 'Master Bank, which has a cousin of President Vladimir V. Putin on its board, could require the largest bailout in recent years. Its managers have been accused of siphoning off assets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/business/international/bank-with-putin-link-gets-license-revoked.html', 'snippet': 'Master Bank, which has a cousin of President Vladimir V. Putin on its board, could require the largest bailout in recent years. Its managers have been accused of siphoning off assets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — Russia’s central bank on Wednesday revoked the license of a midsize Russian bank, Master Bank, and accused its management of siphoning off assets in insider deals, in one of the larger bank failures here in recent years.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 381, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 381}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1299, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/BANK/BANK-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Russia Revokes License of a Bank With Ties to Putin', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bank With Ties to Putin Loses Its License', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Master Bank', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T18:33:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14cf3448-2efa-5a9e-b4d0-676866483028', 'word_count': 640, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14cf3448-2efa-5a9e-b4d0-676866483028'}, {'abstract': 'Too often, media content producers seem to fear technological shifts that ultimately help them grow, the author writes.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/broadcasters-fight-against-aereo-doesnt-serve-their-interests/', 'snippet': 'Too often, media content producers seem to fear technological shifts that ultimately help them grow, the author writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The latest TV industry technophobia is just as repetitive as a 1980s rerun. American broadcasters, including Walt Disney-owned ABC, have garnered support in their Supreme Court bid to shut down the online video start-up Aereo. The arguments echo those used 30 years ago when networks tried to block the VCR, after which business boomed. For a creative profession, media firms sure can lack imagination.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Broadcasters’ Fight Against Aereo Doesn’t Serve Their Interests', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Aereo Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T18:39:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/df2d7be4-fa82-5d6c-8417-a3ff72d85c3b', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/df2d7be4-fa82-5d6c-8417-a3ff72d85c3b'}, {'abstract': 'The university withdrew its invitation to Ramy Jan, a founder of the Egyptian Nazi Party, a group that promotes Arab racial supremacy, to address a conference next month in Washington on the future of Egypt .', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/egyptian-nazi-will-no-longer-participate-at-georgetown-conference/', 'snippet': 'The university withdrew its invitation to Ramy Jan, a founder of the Egyptian Nazi Party, a group that promotes Arab racial supremacy, to address a conference next month in Washington on the future of Egypt .', 'lead_paragraph': 'Georgetown University has come under fire for inviting a founder of the Egyptian Nazi Party to a conference planned for December on the future of Egypt, which will feature a keynote speech by Representative Keith Ellison of Minnesota, the first Muslim member of the United States Congress, and Dalia Mogahed, a former adviser to President Obama. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egyptian Nazi Will No Longer Participate at Georgetown Conference', 'kicker': 'The Lede',