“Every Day a Visitor,” the residents of a retirement home decide to play an all-encompassing game, and in certain ways, it saves their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ending up in a retirement home could be joyous — if you’ve always wanted to relive dorm life and would like it even better with everybody having gotten cranky and lost both their youthful good looks and their hearing. (“You have to say everything twice in this place.”) And with no choice about which drugs you take or when. Richard Abrons apparently gave this prospect some thought before writing “Every Day a Visitor,” which Woodie King Jr.’s New Federal Theater is presenting at the Clurman Theater with a colorful, lovable and mostly mature cast. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/21EVERYDAY/21EVERYDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 550, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/21EVERYDAY/21EVERYDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 550}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/21EVERYDAY/21EVERYDAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 939, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/21EVERYDAY/21EVERYDAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1189, 'width': 1297, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/21EVERYDAY/21EVERYDAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/arts/21EVERYDAY/21EVERYDAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwid