d by tech-savvy young people with no ideological aims before being “stolen by” the Islamists who took power in democratic elections.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Secretary of State John Kerry argued on Wednesday that Egypt’s 2011 revolution was started by tech-savvy young people with no ideological aims before being “stolen by” Islamists from the Muslim Brotherhood, who behaved autocratically after winning parliamentary and presidential elections.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt’s Revolution Was ‘Stolen’ by Muslim Brotherhood, Kerry Says', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tahrir Square (Cairo)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T23:06:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Mackey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mackey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1aa37c3-e2d9-57a0-a9f4-1a42319c4779', 'word_count': 312, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1aa37c3-e2d9-57a0-a9f4-1a42319c4779'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama awards Medals of Freedom; a study compares daily quizzes with exams; and a “real” mayor of New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/news/minute/2013/11/20/the-new-york-times-minute-9/', 'snippet': 'President Obama awards Medals of Freedom; a study compares daily quizzes with exams; and a “real” mayor of New York City.', 'le