 to family and friends in his home village has won admiration as an unusually generous act of filial piety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When 26-year-old Tang Guo left his hometown in Sichuan Province for the neighboring province of Yunnan in 1993, all he had was 2 renminbi in his pocket and, as Mr. Tang put it, a willingness to “eat bitterness,” a Chinese term for resilience and toughness. Twenty years later, Mr. Tang is the head of a real estate construction group with 20 subsidiaries and fixed assets worth more than 2 billion renminbi, or about $328 million.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/world/20SINO-Huaying03/20SINO-Huaying03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/20/world/20SINO-Huaying03/20SINO-Huaying03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/world/20SINO-Huaying03/20SINO-Huaying03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/world/20SINO-Huaying03/20SINO-Huaying03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/20/world/20SINO-Huaying03/20SINO-Huaying03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/20/world/20SINO-Huaying03/20SINO-Huaying03-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 