//www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/garden/belated-yes-forgotten-no-a-tribute-to-dan-kiley.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition in Boston celebrates the life and work of the well-known landscape architect.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Imagine not celebrating the 100th anniversary of the architect Mies van der Rohe’s birth,” said Charles Birnbaum, the founder of the Cultural Landscape Foundation. But in September 2012, that’s precisely the fate that befell Dan Kiley, the seminal postwar landscape architect behind the Jefferson National Expansion Memorial in St. Louis, featuring Eero Saarinen’s Gateway Arch, and Patterns, the garden of the du Pont home in Wilmington, Del.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 565, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 565}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 964, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1927, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21SHOWS/21SHOWS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Belated, Yes; Forgotten, No: A Tribute to Dan Kiley', 'kicker': 'Currents | Shows', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Belated, Yes. Forgotten, No.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shattuck, Kathryn', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landscaping', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kiley, Dan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-20T23:41:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Home', 'section_name': 'Home & Garden', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/49e0ed5c-55d5-5fdb-a268-15be0864fc0b', 'word_count': 160, 'uri': 'nyt://article/49e0ed5c-55d5-5fdb-a268-15be0864fc0b'}, {'abstract': 'The president of an Italian design retailer offers to furnish your New York home if you let him live there for a year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/garden/a-loft-thats-a-real-showplace.html', 'snippet': 'The president of an Italian design retailer offers to furnish your New York home if you let him live there for a year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Diego Paccagnella, the president of Design-Apart, a company that sells custom Italian furnishings, wanted to display samples in New York, he found someone in Manhattan with a 2,600-square-foot loft who was willing to move out for a year and give it to him rent-free. Mr. Paccagnella; his wife, Livia; and their 16-month-old son, Giulio (all at top right), moved in and redecorated the apartment as a live-in showroom. In a year, the Paccagnellas will move out, leaving about a half-million dollars in furnishings for the owners to keep, while they find and redo another New York home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/garden/21OPEN_SPAN/21OPEN3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Loft That’s a Real Showplace', 'kicker': 'Currents | Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A 