0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Detrick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Detrick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fe2aebb-0c37-5a96-b911-5f471cf63e1a', 'word_count': 364, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fe2aebb-0c37-5a96-b911-5f471cf63e1a'}, {'abstract': 'Designers sprinkle pearls all over; Nike is introducing an update of its FuelBand bracelet; a shearling collar adds style and a new collection of winter-white shirts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/fashion/fall-fashion-its-all-about-the-details.html', 'snippet': 'Designers sprinkle pearls all over; Nike is introducing an update of its FuelBand bracelet; a shearling collar adds style and a new collection of winter-white shirts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The holidays are upon us — time to break out the pearls. They may have shed their patrician pedigree some time ago, but this season the makeover is almost decadent, though in the nicest way: a fat pearl hiding under the sole of Nicholas Kirkwood pumps; a single strand attached to dresses at Valentino; pearls as trim running up and down and around tailored Alexander McQueen separates. In jewelry, they’re affixed in surprising new ways to necklaces, rings and cuffs by Aurélie Bidermann, Delfina Delettrez and others. Earlier this year, everyone was head over heels about the Dior pearls worn as a single earring, on the back and front of the earlobe. Now, for resort, they come in pretty pink and bright blue. Seriously, they could become a girl’s best friend.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/fashion/21BROWSEPEARLS_SPAN/21BROWSEPEARLS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg