es Foundation is seeking to decrease unintended pregnancies and sexually transmitted diseases with “a next-generation condom.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/health/condom-contest-produces-812-ideas-for-improvement.html', 'snippet': 'The Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation is seeking to decrease unintended pregnancies and sexually transmitted diseases with “a next-generation condom.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The condom of the future might be made of cow tendon or fish skin. It might have “shape memory” to instantly mold to a specific man. Or it might come with pull tabs so a man could slip it on with little fuss. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Condom Contest Produces 812 Ideas for Improvement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Condom Contest Produces 812 Ideas for Improvement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belluck, Pam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condoms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gates, Bill and Melinda, Foundation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sexually Transmitted Diseases', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastics', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Contests and Prizes', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T00:46:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pam Belluck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belluck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fbeca8a3-4566-5fa3-adaa-2195d2cfc0fa', 'word_count': 491, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fbeca8a3-4566-5fa3-adaa-2195d2cfc0fa'}, {'abstract': 'On Oct. 24, according to the Metropolitan Transportation Authority, 5,985,311 subway rides were taken in the city, the most since daily record-keeping began 28 years ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/nyregion/in-october-a-day-for-the-new-york-city-subways-ridership-record-book.html', 'snippet': 'On Oct. 24, according to the Metropolitan Transportation Authority, 5,985,311 subway rides were taken in the city, the most since daily record-keeping began 28 years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The weather was mild on the subway system’s perfect day — clear skies to coax New Yorkers outdoors, paired with a breeze that discouraged long walks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In October, a Day for the New York City Subway’s Ridership Record Book', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Normal Fall Day? Not to the Subway Record Keepers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subways', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Records and Achievements', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Metropolitan Transportation Authority', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T00:47:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Flegenheimer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flegenheimer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76a2d962-64df-58c0-8161-bb275027c6cf', 'word_count': 511, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76a2d962-64df-58c0-8161-bb275027c6cf'}, {'abstract': 'Times readers debated the ethics of a photograph of the free dive