 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeakel, Lee', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T02:10:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/98249e9b-92e4-5006-9ecf-1c1549a6c437', 'word_count': 335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98249e9b-92e4-5006-9ecf-1c1549a6c437'}, {'abstract': 'John Kerry may be poised to begin delivering a major goal President Obama has long sought: an agreement with Iran to curb its nuclear program.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/world/middleeast/active-and-improvising-kerry-is-taking-on-tough-problems.html', 'snippet': 'John Kerry may be poised to begin delivering a major goal President Obama has long sought: an agreement with Iran to curb its nuclear program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — John Kerry has made no secret of his ambitions as secretary of state. On a visit to the Church of the Nativity in Bethlehem last March, he watched as two bearded patriarchs pleaded with President Obama to bring peace to the Holy Land. Clasping their hands, Mr. Kerry said, “I’m going to work as hard as I can to get it done.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/world/kerry/kerry-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 414, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/world/kerry/kerry-articleLarge.jpg'