light.”', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/a-novel-scorned/', 'snippet': '“Gone With the Wind” was my “Twilight.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was in middle school, I read Margaret Mitchell’s epic romance, “Gone With the Wind.” Not once. Not twice. But continuously. Each time I finished the novel, I began again, flipping open the broken-spined paperback so many times the book split in half, yielding two portable sections of text. I preferred a break of at least several hours between readings, but sometimes compulsion forced me to begin again only moments after finishing it.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Novel Scorned', 'kicker': 'Private Lives', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Novel Scorned', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gone With the Wind (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Teenagers and Adolescence', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T02:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Claire Needell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Claire', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Needell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7dd5431-2a7c-5b6d-87e6-edf41ecbf3d6', 'word_count': 1178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7dd5431-2a7c-5b6d-87e6-edf41ecbf3d6'}, {'abstract': 'As a Russian heavyweight named Magomed Abdusalamov lay unconscious in a Manhattan hospital, people involved in the sport tried to explain opportunity and risk in boxing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/sports/reconciling-a-sports-violent-appeal-as-a-fighter-lies-in-a-coma.html', 'snippet': 'As a Russian heavyweight named Magomed Abdusalamov lay unconscious in a Manhattan hospital, people involved in the sport tried to explain opportunity and risk in boxing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three men sat inside a Manhattan diner. Their fighter, the Russian heavyweight Magomed Abdusalamov, remained in a medically induced coma at Roosevelt Hospital, across the street.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/sports/subBOXING/subBOXING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headli