gman for the Navy, and then returned to Yale to get his Ph.D. on the Danish philosopher Soren Kierkegaard.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 911, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/opinion/video-opdoc-1963/video-opdoc-1963-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘November 22, 1963’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dallas (Tex)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T02:42:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Errol Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Errol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0ad8c56-4a3f-5ded-848b-457555076aa9', 'word_count': 384, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0ad8c56-4a3f-5ded-848b-457555076aa9'}, {'abstract': 'President Juan Manuel Santos announced that he would run for re-election, saying that he wanted to finish the work he started in seeking a peace deal with the country’s largest rebel group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/world/americas/colombia-president-a-us-ally-seeks-another-term.html', 'snippet': 'President Juan Manuel Santos announced that he would run for re-election, saying that he wanted to finish the work he started in seeking a peace deal with the country’s largest rebel group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Juan Manuel Santos announced Wednesday that he would run for re-election, saying that he wanted to finish the work he started in seeking a peace deal with the country’s largest rebel group. “When you see the light at the end of the tunnel you don’t go backwards,” Mr. Santos, one of the closest allies of the United States in Latin America, said on television. “We will finish the job.” The negotiations with the rebel group, the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia, have advanced slowly, and there are still significant obstacles to an agreement to end the nearly 50-year-old conflict. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Colombia: President, a U.S. Ally, Seeks Another Term', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | The Americas', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Colombia: President, a U.S. Ally, Seeks Another Term', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colombia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Santos, Juan Manuel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T02:45:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Neuman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Neuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe0ca93d-5592-503e-899a-b70b3257ac00', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe0ca93d-5592-503e-899a-b70b3257ac00'}, {'abstract': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, November 21, 2013.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/pageoneplus/quotation-of-the-day-for-thursday-november-21-2013.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Thursday, November 21, 2013.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I don’t expect you to understand. I mean, how many people go to work and say, literally say, ‘I might die tonight.’ But that’s boxing.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day for Thursday, November 21, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T02:45:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 