won the National Book Award on Wednesday night for “The Good Lord Bird,” an irreverent, sharp-eyed novel narrated by an escaped slave. It was published by Riverhead Books, part of Penguin Random House. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 834}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 737, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1691, 'width': 1217, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/us/BOOKAWARD/BOOKAWARD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Good Lord Bird’ Is Surprise Winner for National Book Award in Fiction', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Good Lord Bird’ Is Surprise Winner For National Book Award in Fiction', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'National Book Awards', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Packer, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McBride, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T04:02:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Bosman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bosman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80279476-4f30-5a7e-9765-f36211cd1f4c', 'word_count': 837, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80279476-4f30-5a7e-9765-f36211cd1f4c'}, {'abstract': 'Mrs. Miller, the last surviving child of Walt Disney, co-founded a museum dedicated to the memory of her father as a human being rather than a brand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/business/diane-disney-miller-79-keeper-of-walts-flame-dies.html', 'snippet': 'Mrs. Miller, the last surviving child of Walt Disney, co-founded a museum dedicated to the memory of her father as a human being rather than a brand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Diane Disney Miller, Walt Disney’s last surviving child, who stood up for Frank Gehry’s spectacularly abstract design for the Walt Disney Concert Hall in Los Angeles and co-founded a museum dedicated to the memory of her father as a human being rather than a brand, died on Tuesday in Napa Valley, Calif., where she had a home. She was 79.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1474, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/MILLER-1-obit/MILLER-1-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Diane Disney Miller, 79, Keeper of Walt’s Flame, Dies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Diane Disney Miller, 79, Keeper of Walt’s Flame', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Diane Disney (1933-2013)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Disney, Walt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Museums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T04:04:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel E. Slotnik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Slotnik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb2f0be4-d7c6-5a43-858e-2239dd711b0b', 'word_count': 633, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb2f0be4-d7c6-5a43-858e-2239dd711b0b'}, {'abstract': 'Water levels in the Great Lakes, which reached historic lows earlier this year, have recovered because of heavy snowfall and spring rains, scientists said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/us/great-lakes-recover-substantial-water-levels.html', 'snippet': 'Water levels in the Great Lakes, which reached historic lows earlier this year, have recovered because of heavy snowfall and spring rains, scientists said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Water levels in the Great Lakes,\xa0which reached historic lows earlier this year, have recovered substantially\xa0because of heavy snowfall and spring rains, government scientists said. Lakes Michigan and Huron saw a 20-inch rise this year—nearly twice the normal amount, said Keith Kompoltowicz, who monitors the lakes for the Army Corps of Engineers. Levels remain below long-term averages in some of the lakes, and it is hard to predict whether the gains will hold, said Drew Gronewold, a hydrologist with the National Oceanographic and Atmospheric Administration. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Great Lakes Recover Substantial Water Levels', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Midwest', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Great Lakes Levels Rise', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Lakes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Huron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lake Michigan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snow and Snowstorms', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARMY CORPS OF ENGINEERS', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kompoltowicz, Keith', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T04:08:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/46bd5ef5-fdcd-5246-9c7e-6f540eb2ef78', 'word_count': 84, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46bd5ef5-fdcd-5246-9c7e-6f540eb2ef78'}, {'abstract': 'About 80 percent of people who enrolled in a massive open online course from the University of Pennsylvania had already earned a bachelor’s degree, according to a survey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/education/online-courses-attract-degree-holders-survey-finds.html', 'snippet': 'About 80 percent of people who enrolled in a massive open online course from the University of Pennsylvania had already earned a bachelor’s degree, according to a survey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 80 percent of people who enrolled in a massive open online course, or MOOC, from the University of Pennsylvania had already earned a bachelor’s degree, according to a survey of 34,000 students who had at least started one of the 24 courses the university offered on the Coursera platform. Although Coursera’s founders have presented their MOOCs as a way to democratize higher education by making it available online, free, to anyone in the world, the Penn survey found that in the United States and developing countries alike, most Coursera students were well educated, employed, young and male. Penn’s courses account for 20 percent of Coursera’s enrollment. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Online Courses Attract Degree Holders, Survey Finds', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | Education', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Online Courses Attract Degree Holders, Survey Finds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Learning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Pennsylvania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Coursera Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T04:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tamar Lewin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tamar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lewin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/63399fc5-3b4c-5baf-b780-70b2796f6333', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63399fc5-3b4c-5baf-b780-70b2796f6333'}, {'abstract': 'The cleaning device figures out the size of your window mirror and then cleans the surface on its own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/21/technology/how-a-winbot-730-robotic-window-cleaner-works.html', 'snippet': 'The cleaning device figures out the size of your window mirror and then cleans the surface on its own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cleaning device figures out the size of your window mirror and then cleans the surface on its own.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/how-a-winbot-730-robotic-window-cleaner-works-1385006907496/how-a-winbot-730-robotic-window-cleaner-works-1385006907496