, {'abstract': 'Officials say the man arrested served four years in prison for his role as an accomplice in the shooting deaths of three police officers and a taxi driver in 1994.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/world/europe/suspect-held-in-shooting-at-a-paris-newspaper.html', 'snippet': 'Officials say the man arrested served four years in prison for his role as an accomplice in the shooting deaths of three police officers and a taxi driver in 1994.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — After a two-day manhunt, the French police arrested a man they believe was responsible for a shooting this week at a newspaper office in Paris and gunfire at a bank headquarters nearby, the authorities announced late Wednesday night.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Suspect Held in Shooting at a Paris Newspaper', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'France: Shooting Suspect Is Ex-Inmate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dekhar, Abdelhakim', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders and Attempted Murders', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T08:04:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Sayare', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sayare', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb70ac6a-d24c-5556-969f-9423055c22c7', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb70ac6a-d24c-5556-969f-9423055c22c7'}, {'abstract': 'Local governments in Shanghai and Changsha, the capital of Hunan Province, announced earlier this week that they had released all the people previously held at their “re-education through labor” camps.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/as-labor-camp-prisoners-are-released-questions-remain/', 'snippet': 'Local governments in Shanghai and Changsha, the capital of Hunan Province, announced earlier this week that they had released all the people previously held at their “re-education through labor” camps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Local governments in Shanghai and Changsha, the capital of Hunan Province, announced this week that they had released all detainees previously held at their “re-education through labor” camps. The news comes shortly after the central government declared its intention to abolish the labor-camp system – known in Chinese as laojiao – news that came in the report of the Third Plenum, the leadership meeting that wrapped up on Nov. 12.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'As Labor Camp Prisoners Are Released, Questions Remain', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forced Labor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Surveillance of Citizens by Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southern Weekend (Chinese Newspaper)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations Human Rights Council', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beijing (China)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guangdong Province (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T08:06:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_des