one-child policy may hurt some Chinese women by reviving patriarchal Confucian practices.', 'web_url': 'https://latitude.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/the-only-child-blues/', 'snippet': 'Relaxing the one-child policy may hurt some Chinese women by reviving patriarchal Confucian practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHANGHAI — News that the Chinese government would relax the one-child policy — one of its most sweeping, intrusive and defining — has been widely welcome.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Only-Child Blues', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Confucianism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Confucius', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T14:59:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clarissa Sebag-Montefiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clarissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sebag-Montefiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f9523b8-1d92-51ab-ace6-693c9a0f9cc3', 'word_count': 383, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f9523b8-1d92-51ab-ace6-693c9a0f9cc3'}, {'abstract': 'Responding to an article about joblessness itself as a deterrent to finding work, readers told their own stories of frustration, hopelessness and survival strategies.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/readers-react-to-unemployments-revolving-door/', 'snippet': 'Responding to an article about joblessness itself as a deterrent to finding work, readers told their own stories of frustration, hopelessness and survival strategies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When you lose your job, suddenly nothing feels secure. That was one of the most common themes among more than 700 comments on Annie Lowrey’s article “Caught in a Revolving Door of Unemployment” last weekend. Jenner Barrington-Ward, the subject of the article, found herself homeless after decades of employment. Two readers shared their own stories of homelessness. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Readers React to Unemployment’s Revolving Door', 'kicker': 'Economix', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Layoffs and Job Reductions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unemployment', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T15:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy R. Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2855260d-c691-5ba1-9c17-ed29b88fbe70', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2855260d-c691-5ba1-9c17-ed29b88fbe70'}, {'abstract': 'A Times critic admits to feeling envy in response to readers’ picks of the best actors they ever saw perform in William Shakespeare’s plays.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/20/theater/best-shakespeare-performances.html', 'snippet': 'A Times critic admits to feeling envy in response to readers’ picks of the best actors they ever saw perf