'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T18:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/57edacd2-a4b2-56d2-9b56-bce8e17f27f9', 'word_count': 131, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57edacd2-a4b2-56d2-9b56-bce8e17f27f9'}, {'abstract': 'Six months after Indiana beat the Knicks in the playoffs, it is obvious that the Pacers and their young star Paul George have taken a leap forward while New York has regressed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/sports/basketball/pacers-and-george-pass-the-knicks-on-their-way-up.html', 'snippet': 'Six months after Indiana beat the Knicks in the playoffs, it is obvious that the Pacers and their young star Paul George have taken a leap forward while New York has regressed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The crowd at Wednesday’s game between the Knicks and the Pacers at Madison Square Garden appeared to sense how much had changed since the teams met in the playoffs in May. Then, the Knicks were the higher seed, second in the East, and Carmelo Anthony was widely considered the best player in the series. Most of the players from that series remain on their teams, but six months after the Pacers bruised and bullied the Knicks on the way to a six-game series victory, the dynamic between the teams has irreversibly changed.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1490, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/sports/22dribble-span/22dribble-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pacers and George Pass Knicks on Their Way Up', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pacers and George Pass Knicks on Their Way Up', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mason, Beckley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indiana Pacers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George, Paul', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T18:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Beckley Mason', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Beckley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mason', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/811d14e7-a996-5415-bc8b-929ea1c69a43', 'word_count': 940, 'uri': 'nyt://article/811d14e7-a996-5415-bc8b-929ea1c69a43'}, {'abstract': 'In a city with a few electric vehicle charging ports, the BMW i3 is a perfectly reasonable and fun way to get around.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/automobiles/autoshow/a-drive-around-los-angeles-in-the-bmw-i3.html', 'snippet': 'In a city with a few electric vehicle charging ports, the BMW i3 is a perfectly reasonable and fun way to get around.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Depending on who you are, looking at the BMW i3 electric car will make you either love it or hate it. Its peculiar proportions and appearance, as with other odd-shape cars, seem to be polarizing. Something about it recalls the basic look of a Honda Element, but it is uniquely BMW and its fuel economy is much more impressive.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/automobiles/21BMWi3-1/21BMWi3-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/automobiles/21BMWi3-1/21BMWi3-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/automobiles/21BMWi3-1/21BMWi3-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1002, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty