appears-to-wind-down.html', 'snippet': 'The release from Belarussian custody of the director of the Russian potash fertilizer mining company Uralkali could lead to the return of a price-fixing cartel for potash fertilizer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MOSCOW — What was good news on Thursday for the chief executive of a Russian fertilizer company may be bad news for farmers around the world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Russian ‘Fertilizer War’ Appears to Wind Down', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': "'Fertilizer War' of Russia and Belarus Appears to Wind Down", 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potash', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fertilizer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Belarus', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'International Business', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew E. Kramer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Kramer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29828ac2-c340-5fb4-ad89-000fd3aa99ef', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29828ac2-c340-5fb4-ad89-000fd3aa99ef'}, {'abstract': 'Over two years, the IceCube Neutrino observatory in Antarctica detected 28 neutrinos from outside our solar system, the first detected since 1987.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/science/space/icy-observatory-detects-neutrinos-from-outside-our-solar-system.html', 'snippet': 'Over two years, the IceCube Neutrino observatory in Antarctica detected 28 neutrinos from outside our solar system, the first detected since 1987.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the bottom of the world, an observatory embedded in ice and designed to catch bountiful but elusive subatomic particles could give astronomers a brand-new look at the universe.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/science/22telescope-1/22telescope-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Icy Observatory Detects Neutrinos From Far, Far Away', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Icy Observatory Detects Neutrinos From Far, Far Away', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Space and Astronomy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Neutrinos', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANTARCTIC REGIONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Physics', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Science (Journal)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telescopes and Observatories', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Science', 'subsection_name': 'Space & Cosmos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kenneth Chang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/44cc7a86-3925-5093-b10f-0b8e947b3a09', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44cc7a86-3925-5093-b10f-0b8e947b3a09'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/the-gun-report-november-21-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The N.R.A. has sued\xa0San Francisco, Calif., claiming the city is violating citizens’ constitutional right to possess arms with a new ordinance that bans the possession of high-capacity gun magazines. The suit, brought on behalf of the San Francisco Veteran Police Officers Association and four individual gun owners, is in response to a measure expanding an existing ban on sales of large-capacity gun magazines. Starting Dec. 8, it gives owners of those magazines 90 days to turn them over to police.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 21, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f3efbf87-879c-534d-9c3c-4318ff78f892', 'word_count': 1443, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f3efbf87-879c-534d-9c3c-4318ff78f892'}, {'abstract': 'Vladimir Jurowski will conduct the Juilliard Orchestra at Alice Tully Hall, Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/arts/music/shostakovich-the-early-years.html', 'snippet': 'Vladimir Jurowski will conduct the Juilliard Orchestra at Alice Tully Hall, Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The maestro Vladimir Jurowski, 41, principal conductor of the London Philharmonic Orchestra, has been winning praise for his performance of Strauss’s “Die Frau Ohne Schatten” at the Met. But before the run ends (on Tuesday at 7:30 p.m.), Mr. Jurowski will conduct the Juilliard Orchestra at Alice Tully Hall, Lincoln Center. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Shostakovich, the Early Years', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Classical', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Shostakovich, The Early Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:04:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anthony Tommasini', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anthony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tommasini', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2403ee7-421f-5bcd-aa19-ec37547e4c96', 'word_count': 132, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2403ee7-421f-5bcd-aa19-ec37547e4c96'}, {'abstract': 'Dirk Bogarde has never been more sinister than in his role of Hugo Barrett, in the 1963 movie “The Servant.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/movies/reversals-of-fortune.html', 'snippet': 'Dirk Bogarde has never been more sinister than in his role of Hugo Barrett, in the 1963 movie “The Servant.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'With his insinuating heavy-lidded gaze and a contemptuous smirk, Dirk Bogarde has never been more sinister than in his role of Hugo Barrett, the manservant who takes over the life of Tony (James Fox), a young aristocrat, in the 1963 movie “The Servant.” The first of three collaborations between the director Joseph Losey and Harold Pinter, who adapted the screenplay from a novelette by Robin Maugham, “The Servant” is a high point of the Film Society of Lincoln Center’s 10-film series Comedies of Menace and Quiet Desperation, which focuses on movies written or adapted by Pinter. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Reversals of Fortune', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Film', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Reversals Of Fortune', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:04:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/227f2181-9cd9-5834-af37-e03b65cd841c', 'word_count': 142, 'uri': 'nyt://article/227f2181-9cd9-5834-af37-e03b65cd841c'}, {'abstract': 'The last of the nine black men falsely convicted of raping two white women in 1931 died years ago, but the case long hung over the state.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/us/with-last-3-pardons-alabama-hopes-to-put-infamous-scottsboro-boys-case-to-rest.html', 'snippet': 'The last of the nine black men falsely convicted of raping two white women in 1931 died years ago, but the case long hung over the state.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — More than 80 years after they were falsely accused and wrongly convicted in the rapes of a pair of white women in north Alabama, three black men received posthumous pardons on Thursday, essentially absolving the last of the “Scottsboro Boys” of criminal misconduct and closing one of the most notorious chapters of the South’s racial history.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 759}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 810, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1620, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22scottsboro/22scottsboro-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alabama Pardons 3 ‘Scottsboro Boys’ After 80 Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pardons for the Last ‘Scottsboro Boys’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'False Arrests, Convictions and Imprisonments', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blinder, Alan S', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scottsboro (Ala)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Patterson, Haywood', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weems, Charles', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wright, Andy', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:05:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/80746ce9-31fd-5f8d-9a6e-65e957644e92', 'word_count': 807, 'uri': 'nyt://article/80746ce9-31fd-5f8d-9a6e-65e957644e92'}, {'abstract': 'The Museum of Modern Art’s atrium will project a work by the British artist Isaac Julien, “Ten Thousand Waves.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/arts/design/remembering-a-tragedy.html', 'snippet': 'The Museum of Modern Art’s atrium will project a work by the British artist Isaac Julien, “Ten Thousand Waves.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Museum of Modern Art’s atrium has been home to any number of weird, wild and wacky goings-on. There was the time the performance artist Marina Abramovic sat there for 700 hours, and another when someone played a baby-grand piano from inside a hole that had been cut into it. There was also an installation of hazelnut pollen, and even a giant garage sale.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering a Tragedy', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Art', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remembering A Tragedy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Carol Vogel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Carol', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2117c94c-464c-560f-968c-735be923a3e0', 'word_count': 164, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2117c94c-464c-560f-968c-735be923a3e0'}, {'abstract': '“Surreal Graham,” presented by the Martha Graham Dance Company, sticks around for an added performance on Monday.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/arts/dance/sustaining-martha-graham.html', 'snippet': '“Surreal Graham,” presented by the Martha Graham Dance Company, sticks around for an added performance on Monday.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Performa 13, the monthlong festival of cross-disciplinary performance, officially wraps up this weekend. But at least one of its programs keeps on going: “Surreal Graham,” presented by the Martha Graham Dance Company, which sticks around for an added performance on Monday.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sustaining Martha Graham', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Dance', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sustaining Martha Graham', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Graham, Martha, Dance Co', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:10:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'By Siobhan Burke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Siobhan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/46ed379f-b866-5cbd-afa0-3032ec7b54b5', 'word_count': 159, 'uri': 'nyt://article/46ed379f-b866-5cbd-afa0-3032ec7b54b5'}, {'abstract': 'Last month, the Smithsonian Channel enlisted celebrities to help tell the deeper stories behind some pieces from its collection.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/arts/television/hands-on-journey-in-smithsonian.html', 'snippet': 'Last month, the Smithsonian Channel enlisted celebrities to help tell the deeper stories behind some pieces from its collection.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Perhaps the Smithsonian Institution has been feeling underappreciated lately. Sure, millions of people visit its museums each year, but they are seeing only a fraction of the material in its collections, and walking past a musty uniform or ancient airplane sometimes doesn’t convey the living history behind it. Last month, the Smithsonian Channel enlisted celebrities to help tell the deeper stories behind some pieces from its collection in the engaging three-part “Civil War 360,” and now ordinary museum visitors assume that role in “Seriously Amazing Objects,” which begins on Monday at 8 p.m. on the channel.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hands-On Journey in Smithsonian', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Television', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hands-On Journey In Smithsonian', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:12:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2854cb2e-a4e2-5974-bae1-9ce2db5ff4c8', 'word_count': 191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2854cb2e-a4e2-5974-bae1-9ce2db5ff4c8'}, {'abstract': 'Trixie Whitley’s not one for established formats', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/arts/music/turning-corners-guitar-in-hand.html', 'snippet': 'Trixie Whitley’s not one for established formats', 'lead_paragraph': 'Trixie Whitley could easily have done straightforward roots-rock on “Fourth Corner” (Strong Blood), the debut album she released in January. She has the pedigree, as the daughter of the bluesman Chris Whitley, and she has the voice, which holds smoke and sorrow, exhortation and ache. But she’s not one for established formats. Her mother is Belgian, and Ms. Whitley spent years in Europe, in theater and dance troupes, before settling in New York in her teens. She was a member of Black Dub, led by the producer Daniel Lanois, and her own songs move between confession and conundrum, with shades of Fiona Apple and Alicia Keys. For “Fourth Corner,” she collaborated with the keyboardist-composer Thomas Bartlett on songs that were orchestrated with string sections and gusts of guitar reverb and distortion. Onstage, with her electric guitar, her music can be cathartic. (7:30 p.m. Saturday, Le Poisson Rouge, 158 Bleecker Street, Greenwich Village, 212-505-3474, lepoissonrouge.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turning Corners, Guitar in Hand', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead | Pop', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turning Corners, Guitar in Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T19:13:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98996356-3754-54e2-9275-6e340a0f7f10', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98996356-3754-54e2-9275-6e340a0f7f10'}, {'abstract': 'Chart showing the proportion that have been used on high-level nominations and table of the nominees currently awaiting confirmation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/21/us/politics/senate-filibusters.html', 'snippet': 'Chart showing the proportion that have been used on high-level nominations and table of the nominees currently awaiting confirmation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chart showing the proportion that have been used on high-level nominations and table of the nominees currently awaiting confirmation.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'mul