count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/db1d2883-b7b8-5465-9f48-68690b8464c1'}, {'abstract': 'In “My Promised Land,” the journalist Ari Shavit reflects on the entirety of the Israeli experience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/books/review/my-promised-land-by-ari-shavit.html', 'snippet': 'In “My Promised Land,” the journalist Ari Shavit reflects on the entirety of the Israeli experience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Too much of the discourse on Israel is a doubting discourse. I do not mean that it is too critical: Sometimes it is, sometimes it isn’t. I mean that the state is too often judged for its viability or its validity, as if some fundamental acceptance of its reality is pending upon the resolution of its many problems with itself and with others. About the severity of those problems there is no question, and some of them broach primary issues of politics and morality; but Israel’s problems are too often combined and promoted into a Problem, which has the effect of emptying the Jewish state of its actuality and consigning it to a historical provisionality, a permanent condition of controversy, from which it can be released only by furnishing various justifications and explanations. ', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 358, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 358}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1224, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/books/review/Cover/Cover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of Israel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The State of Israel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'My Promised Land: The Triumph and Tragedy of Israel (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wieseltier, Leon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shavit, Ari', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Israel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jews and Judaism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zionism', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Israeli Settlements', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T20:33:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Leon Wieseltier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Leon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wieseltier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/73d52867-5eae-5024-bcfb-a756dd91896d', 'word_count': 1803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73d52867-5eae-5024-bcfb-a756dd91896d'}, {'abstract': 'Fed up with endless blockades by Republicans, a majority finally ends the filibuster on nominations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/opinion/democracy-returns-to-the-senate.html', 'snippet': 'Fed up with endless blockades by Republicans, a majority finally ends the filibuster on nominations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For five years, Senate Republicans have refused to allow confirmation votes on dozens of perfectly qualified candidates nominated by President Obama for government positions. They tried to nullify entire federal agencies by denying them leaders. They abused Senate rules past the point of tolerance or responsibility. And so they were left enraged and threatening revenge on Thursday when a majority did the only logical thing and stripped away their power to block the president’s nominees.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Democracy Returns to the Senate', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Democracy Returns to the Senate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Filibusters and Debate Curbs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reid, Harry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Courts and the Judiciary', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T20:41:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial B