mmercial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'There&#8217;s a Flag on the Commercial', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T20:50:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1bfc60c1-b5ae-5090-90b8-63ea309c3cc5', 'word_count': 204, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1bfc60c1-b5ae-5090-90b8-63ea309c3cc5'}, {'abstract': 'The marketers think they know the men who are watching pro football games, but at least one man doesn’t see himself when watching those commercials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/arts/television/sacked-by-the-media-blitz.html', 'snippet': 'The marketers think they know the men who are watching pro football games, but at least one man doesn’t see himself when watching those commercials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The most chilling words heard on any National Football League telecast are: “We’ll return right after these messages.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ADS_SPAN/24ADS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ADS_SPAN/24ADS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ADS_SPAN/24ADS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ADS_SPAN/24AD