rk Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Holiday Face', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Holiday Face', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T21:55:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4ed65f2-b7c7-55aa-9bfd-0319f5baf967', 'word_count': 869, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4ed65f2-b7c7-55aa-9bfd-0319f5baf967'}, {'abstract': 'The Brooklyn disco outfit Escort, known for its big, singalong choruses and even bigger onstage lineup, gets primitive in a new live video.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/listen-up-a-brooklyn-disco-orchestra-unleashes-its-inner-barbarian/', 'snippet': 'The Brooklyn disco outfit Escort, known for its big, singalong choruses and even bigger onstage lineup, gets primitive in a new live video.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Dance music played with live instruments has become really popular — it’s not just underground anymore,” says Eugene Cho, the keyboardist of the Brooklyn-based band Escort. Indeed, thanks to the surprise Top 40 success of Daft Punk’s “Get Lucky,” club grooves evoking the time before computer-made beats have reached mass consciousness anew. Escort, however, has been flying that flag for over half a decade. Founded by Cho and the guitarist Dan Balis, the band hails itself as “Brooklyn’s finest disco orchestra” — mixing mirror-ball rhythms and funky cowbell syncopation with club-ready choruses, as heard on the single “Barbarians,” from their forthcoming sophomore album, out next year. The song’s lush textures call to mind Studio 54 classics mixed with the legendary producer Trevor Horn’s work in the mid-1980s with Frankie Goes to Hollywood. “It’s not reasonable to expect everyone who listens to us to know the last 30 years of dance-music history,” Cho says. “We want what we do to translate broadly.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listen Up | A Brooklyn Disco Orchestra Unleashes Its Inner Barbarian', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'First Person: Rocku2019s True Love', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Escort (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T21:56:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By MATT DIEHL', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'DIEHL', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54c612a6-f769-59da-b94c-a133a930008b', 'word_count': 306, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54c612a6-f769-59da-b94c-a133a930008b'}, {'abstract': 'While it doesn’t own a Caravaggio, the National Gallery of Art is acquiring works by artists who painted in his style, including “The Concert,” a painting by Gerrit van Honthorst.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/arts/design/national-gallery-acquires-a-van-honthorst-masterwork.html', 'snippet': 'While it doesn’t own a Caravaggio, the National Gallery of Art is acquiring works by artists who painted in his style, including “The Concert,” a painting by Gerrit van Honthorst.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A MERRY DUTCH CONCERT, CAPTURED BY A MASTER', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/arts/22SUB4VOGEL_SPAN/SUB4VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/arts/22SUB4VOGEL_SPAN/SUB4VOGEL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo