ed economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the economy improves, the number of borrowers who are seriously behind on their mortgage payments continues to decline. The enhanced outlook is such that even those in delinquency are feeling more optimistic about their circumstances and homeownership in general.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 299, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 299}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 510, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1441, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/realestate/24mort-graphic/24mort-graphic-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Delinquency Rates on the Decline', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Delinquency Rates on the Decline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mortgages', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prevost, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreclosures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal National Mortgage Assn (Fannie Mae)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-21T22:32:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d14171d-812d-56fa-98cb-f0315aa5a2e3', 'word_count': 555, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d14171d-812d-56fa-98cb-f0315aa5a2e3'}, {'abstract': 'The departure of Sol Kumin underscores the transformation of SAC Capital Advisors to a symbol for corporate crime.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/21/as-sac-shrinks-its-operations-chief-departs/', 'snippet': 'The departure of Sol Kumin underscores the transformation of SAC Capital Advisors to a symbol for corporate crime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007, before the financial crisis and before federal authorities began listening to traders’ phone calls, the hedge fund SAC Capital Advisors was in aggressive expansion mode. And a charismatic young executive named Sol Kumin played an important role in its rise. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/21/business/dealbook/dbpix-sac/dbpix-sac-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/21/