N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T01:14:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felicia R. Lee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felicia', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Lee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11af3c08-a035-5081-b5bb-f78610f2e7e5', 'word_count': 1191, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11af3c08-a035-5081-b5bb-f78610f2e7e5'}, {'abstract': '“Zatoichi: The Blind Swordsman,” a box set from the Criterion Collection, assembles the 25 films starring Shintaro Katsu as a samurai.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/movies/homevideo/criterions-box-set-zatoichi-the-blind-swordsman.html', 'snippet': '“Zatoichi: The Blind Swordsman,” a box set from the Criterion Collection, assembles the 25 films starring Shintaro Katsu as a samurai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was never quite sure what to make of Zatoichi and his backhanded sword grip. Again and again, he would fight, taking down a platoon of opponents with such lightning speed that the slashes could not even be seen, and the victims would stand, stunned, for a few seconds before pitching over dead. Again and again, I wondered: How had he done it? And how could he have done it?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/arts/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN/24ZATOICHI1_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Master of Sightless Sword Play', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Master of Sightless Sword Play', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jamieson, Wendell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Criterion Collection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings and Downloads', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T01:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'subsection_name': 'DVD', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wendell Jamieson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wendell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jamieson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/08a9e086-b06d-584a-b360-fc736ae338b8', 'word_count': 1431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/08a9e086-b06d-584a-b360-fc736ae338b8'}, {'abstract': 'Of the 314 million Americans alive today, 26 percent were at least 5 years old when President John F. Kennedy was assassinated. A selection of them recalled the moment they heard the news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/us/kennedy-has-been-shot-memories-from-nov-22-1963.html', 'snippet': 'Of the 314 million Americans alive today, 26 percent were at least 5 years old when President John F. Kennedy was assassinated. A selection of them recalled the moment they heard the news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a moment we cannot forget. On the afternoon of Nov. 22, 1963, people were doing ordinary things: walking to classes, pumping gas or talking politics. For many of the 26 percent of Americans alive today who were at least 5 years old when they heard the news of President John F. Kennedy’s assassination, it was a time of outrage and grief. Those who were young schoolchildren tend to recall not so much the news itself, but its vivid effect on teachers or parents. Some adults sought refuge in a quiet pastime. And for a few, like me, the demands of work deferred the personal impact.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22memories-span/22memories-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22memories-span/22memories-span-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/us/22memories-span/22memories-span-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'im