cations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'City Councils', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T03:15:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Winnie Hu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Winnie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1500a7d6-31ac-58e0-b14f-cd355d52a007', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1500a7d6-31ac-58e0-b14f-cd355d52a007'}, {'abstract': 'After walking away a champion with the Ravens at the end of last season, safety Ed Reed’s two teams this season have yet to win a game with him in the lineup.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/sports/football/jets-reed-goes-from-ultimate-win-to-winless-season.html', 'snippet': 'After walking away a champion with the Ravens at the end of last season, safety Ed Reed’s two teams this season have yet to win a game with him in the lineup.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FLORHAM PARK, N.J. — Since Ed Reed walked off the Superdome turf last February, purple confetti clinging to his beard, every week has ended in darkly familiar fashion. The uniform has changed (twice). The results, through eight games he has played, have not. Reed is winless.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Jets’ Reed Goes From Ultimate Win to Winless Season', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Jets’ Reed Goes From Ultimate Win to Winless Season', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Baltimore Ravens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Jets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reed, Ed', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T03:16:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Zach Schonbrun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Zach', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schonbrun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c69dd442-53bb-5656-99e3-a23f7e8efa70', 'word_count': 682, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c69dd442-53bb-5656-99e3-a23f7e8efa70'}, {'abstract': 'For Bill Schermerhorn, creative director of Macy’s Parade and Entertainment Group, work at this time of year continues even on a day of rest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/nyregion/planning-for-the-arrival-of-cinderella.html', 'snippet': 'For Bill Schermerhorn, creative director of Macy’s Parade and Entertainment Group, work at this time of year continues even on a day of rest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you see a life-size dragon flying in the New York City sky on Thursday, chances are you’ve had either too much family time or sudden exposure to the work of Bill Schermerhorn. If it’s the former, take a deep breath and a bite of stuffing; if the latter, strap in: After Toothless the dragon adds its name to the list of balloons that have appeared in the Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade, there are still miles of floats, cheerleaders, dancers and marching bands to come, all choreographed and curated by Mr. Schermerhorn, the creative director of Macy’s Parade and Entertainment Group. “I’m the storyteller,” he said. Mr. Schermerhorn, 53, lives in Hell’s Kitchen with his partner, Dan Dutcher, a publicist.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/nyregion/24ROUTINE1_SPAN/24ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 