e thus-far-unregulated digital currency that has taken China, the United States and other countries by storm in recent months.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bitcoin Gets a Cautious Nod From China’s Central Bank', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bitcoin (Currency)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renminbi (Currency)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernanke, Ben S', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "People's Bank of China", 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T09:16:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Century', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Century', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81afcfda-eccc-5d97-9909-65f561eb3591', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81afcfda-eccc-5d97-9909-65f561eb3591'}, {'abstract': 'The blast in the industrial city of Qingdao erupted in a leaking crude oil pipeline operated by Sinopec, a major Chinese state oil refiner.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/pipeline-blast-kills-22-people-in-eastern-china/', 'snippet': 'The blast in the industrial city of Qingdao erupted in a leaking crude oil pipeline operated by Sinopec, a major Chinese state oil refiner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An explosion in a ruptured oil pipeline killed at least 35 people on Friday in Qingdao, a seaside city in eastern China, where the blast cracked apart streets, upended cars and sent a funnel of smoke into the air, according to Chinese news media reports and photos.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pipeline Blast Kills 35 in Eastern China', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China: Pipeline Blast Kills Dozens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Explosions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pipelines', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Sinopec Corp', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Xinhua', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qingdao (China)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T09:20:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9603943a-18ef-5928-8ca6-072e14899010', 'word_count': 379, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9603943a-18ef-5928-8ca6-072e14899010'}, {'abstract': 'Can you identify the simple predicate in the sentence from the article?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.b