g-chinas-violence/', 'snippet': '“A Touch of Sin,” the new film by the celebrated art house director Jia Zhangke, won a best screenplay award at Cannes in May. When it will be shown in China, however, is anybody’s guess.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Jia Zhangke screened his new movie, “A Touch of Sin,” for a small group of journalists in his office last August, he said the film would make a round of foreign film festivals in the autumn and then, if all went well, be released on Nov. 9 in China. Now, with winter approaching, there is still no indication that the film will be shown in Chinese theaters.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/world/22sino-jiazhangke/22sino-jiazhangke-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Release in Sight for Film Exploring China’s Violence', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drama Behind Film Awaits Climax', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cannes International Film Festival', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Three Gorges Dam (China)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Venice International Film Festival', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jia Zhang Ke', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jiang Wen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zhang Yimou', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Taiwan', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T09:48:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e6938be-5230-5ed1-936a-dc8537b678dd', 'word_count': 1116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e6938be-5230-5ed1-936a-dc8537b678dd'}, {'abstract': 'HBO begins a series about a dysfunctional geriatric rehab center.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/institutional-care-cue-the-laugh-track/', 'snippet': 'HBO begins a series about a dysfunctional geriatric rehab center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m sure the creators of “Getting On,” the HBO series that premieres Sunday night, see it as a blisteringly dark comedy about a dysfunctional geriatric rehab center, with characters and plot devices exaggerated for the sake of laughs.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Institutional Care: Cue the Laugh Track', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T10:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/33b4d41a-a495-50b1-8e59-17b4fce39e3b', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/33b4d41a-a495-50b1-8e59-17b4fce39e3b'}, {'abstract': 'Do you think the problem is that parents, teachers and society in general do not encourage girls to enter these fields? Or is it just not seen as “cool” for girls to excel in math and science?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/why-arent-more-girls-choosing-to-pursue-careers-in-math-and-science/', 'snippet': 'Do you think the problem is that parents, teachers and society in general do not encourage girls to enter these fields? Or is it just not seen as “cool” for girls to excel in math and science?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Natalie Angier wrote in September about the paradox of why girls who were equally competent and confident as boys in science and mathematics still chose not to enter the STEM fields — science, technology, engineering and math. The statistics are baffling. For example, women earned 37 percent of computer science degrees in 1985, yet only 18 percent in 2010. And only one-fifth of physics Ph.D.’s in this country are awarded to women. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Aren’t More Girls Choosing to Pursue Careers in Math and Science?', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T10:00:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88dc2ce6-6ac7-58a1-8aed-09ba2a8339b8', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88dc2ce6-6ac7-58a1-8aed-09ba2a8339b8'}, {'abstract': 'Gerard H. Gaskin’s photos of the vibrant, underground house ballroom scene, celebrated by mostly gay and transgender black and Latino men, have earned him recognition as a “Trinidadian Andy Warhol.”', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/being-seen-inside-an-unseen-world/', 'snippet': 'Gerard H. Gaskin’s photos of the vibrant, underground house ballroom scene, celebrated by mostly gay and transgender black and Latino men, have earned him recognition as a “Trinidadian Andy Warhol.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'A young man painted in blue fixes his eyes on the photographer before him. But before the portrait is made, he peeks in the mirror, retouches his lipstick and brushes away a few strands of white and blue hair from his face. He spent weeks preparing his wig and outfit — a shimmering handmade gown of plastic shower curtains and yellow buttons — all in hopes of taking home the title, and maybe some money, as “Butch Queen Bizarre.”', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Being Seen Inside an Unseen World', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flamboyance Immortalized', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parties (Social)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warhol, Andy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Trinidad and Tobago', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T10:00:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Whitney Richardson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Whitney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richardson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff56ed3e-c47f-58c8-b86f-e9cb2909e7f3', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff56ed3e-c47f-58c8-b86f-e9cb2909e7f3'}, {'abstract': 'A draft classified document states that, under specific circumstances, the American intelligence agency may spy on citizens of Britain without that country’s consent or knowledge.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/opinion/chappatte-nsa-memo-authorizes-us-spying-on-british-citizens.html', 'snippet': 'A draft classified document states that, under specific circumstances, the American intelligence agency may spy on citizens of Britain without that country’s consent or knowledge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A draft classified document states that, under specific circumstances, the American intelligence agency may spy on c