article/608c7c6d-c383-565c-92df-5d94fe243360'}, {'abstract': 'Starvation rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/magazine/is-it-ok-to-force-feed-prisoners.html', 'snippet': 'Starvation rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I believe medical professionals should act ethically. However, I’m not sure it’s unethical to force-feed prisoners on hunger strike. Setting aside the issues associated with incarceration (and Guantánamo Bay in particular), is it ethical to allow a prisoner to die of starvation, even if that is his/her choice? Or is it more ethical to force-feed them? Most suicides are, at least in part, caused by depression or other mental-health issues. I also realize that prisoners choosing starvation may be making a political statement, and it might be unethical to squelch their political speech. What do you think? SHELLEY MARKS, LOS ANGELES', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 467, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 934, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2014/02/02/magazine/ethicist/ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It O.K. to Force-Feed Prisoners?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is It O.K. to Force-Feed Prisoners?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hunger Strikes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klosterman, Chuck', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chuck Klosterman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chuck', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klosterman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/b627d16b-dde4-58cf-aefd-1f583ee8ba75', 'word_count': 522, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b627d16b-dde4-58cf-aefd-1f583ee8ba75'}, {'abstract': 'What happened when I “secreted” a ’90s supermodel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/magazine/desperately-seeking-christy.html', 'snippet': 'What happened when I “secreted” a ’90s supermodel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was 2007, and like anyone else with a yoga mat and a DVR set to record “Oprah,” my sister, Donna, and I were reading “The Secret,” the best-selling self-help book by Rhonda Byrne that espoused the cosmic “law of attraction.” Filled with the usual platitudes of the genre, it also held out this tantalizing promise: Whatever you desired — a better relationship, a fatter paycheck — you could draw into your life with the magnet of your mind. You just had to concentrate on what you wanted as if it were already on its way. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '62', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 257, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 348, 'width': 257, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24lives/24lives-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Desperately Seeking Christy', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Desperately Seeking Christy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Secret (Book)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klimkiewicz, Joann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrne, Rhonda', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turlington, Christy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:11:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joann Klimkiewicz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klimkiewicz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3cd2d9-fa8a-53a6-90f8-f318fa6f92d5', 'word_count': 772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da3cd2d9-fa8a-53a6-90f8-f318fa6f92d5'}, {'abstract': 'Readers respond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/magazine/the-11-10-2013-issue.html', 'snippet': 'Readers respond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE COACH WHO EXPLODED', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The 11.10.2013 Issue', 'kicker': 'Reply All | Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Coach Who Exploded', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:11:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5a8f15c-4044-5c41-bc90-cd648c472e06', 'word_count': 756, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5a8f15c-4044-5c41-bc90-cd648c472e06'}, {'abstract': 'Printed objects in the palm of your hand.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/magazine/who-made-that-3-d-printer.html', 'snippet': 'Printed objects in the palm of your hand.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the early 1980s, an engineer named Chuck Hull approached his boss with an idea: to build a machine that printed out objects you could hold in your hand. His manager discouraged him — after all, the company produced UV lamps, not “Star Trek” replicators. But eventually the two men reached a compromise: Hull would dedicate himself to the company’s lamps by day; at night he’d cobble together his dream machine.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/magazine/24wmt/mag-24WMT-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Made That 3-D Printer?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Made That? 3-D Printer', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': '3-D Printers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Pagan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}