klyn street, crashed into a parked car, jumped the curb and hit another vehicle. He turned, police said, sped the wrong way down a one-way street and mounted the curb again, this time pinning 9-year-old Lucian Merryweather under his 5,000-pound S.U.V. Lucian was killed instantly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/style/motherlode-lucien2/motherlode-lucien2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Could One Thoughtless Driver Take This Child?', 'kicker': 'Motherlode', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drunken and Reckless Driving', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Byrd, Anthony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Merryweather, Lucian', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Police Department (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:43:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hope Reeves', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hope', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reeves', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0c3866b-ab7e-597a-be2b-05200c7230ab', 'word_count': 790, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0c3866b-ab7e-597a-be2b-05200c7230ab'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Ari Shavit and Ann Patchett.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2013/11/22/books/review/24books_pod-blog.html', 'snippet': 'This week, Ari Shavit and Ann Patchett.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Ari Shavit and Ann Patchett.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside The New York Times Book Review: The Triumph and Tragedy of Israel', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Podcasts', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:46:30+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/68fa7b6e-8198-53a0-b46b-80835d92ecc2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/68fa7b6e-8198-53a0-b46b-80835d92ecc2'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/the-gun-report-november-22-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fifty years ago today, President John F. Kennedy was shot to death in Dallas, Tex. Though conspiracy theories abound, the Warren Commission found that Lee Harvey Oswald owned the rifle that was used to fire the shots from the sixth floor window of the Texas School Book Depository building. And Oswald procured that rifle through a mail-order ad in the February 1963 issue of the N.R.A.’s American Rifleman magazine.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 22, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:47:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/29c92db3-b1da-5649-ab84-4c7681192d75', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29c92db3-b1da-5649-ab84-4c7681192d75'}, {'abstract': 'From Coney Island to the Pacific Northwest, Los Angeles to Oklahoma, visiting a collection of places that formed notable chapters in the folk singer’s life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/travel/in-search-of-woody-guthries-america.html', 'snippet': 'From Coney Island to the Pacific Northwest, Los Angeles to Oklahoma, visiting a collection of places that formed notable chapters in the folk singer’s life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Pacific Northwest is one of my favorite spots in this world, and I’m one walker that’s stood way up and looked way down acrost aplenty of pretty sights in all their veiled and nakedest seasons. The Pacific Northwest has got mineral mountains. It’s got chemical deserts. It’s got rough run canyons. It’s got sawblade snowcaps. It’s got ridges of nine kinds of brown, hills out of six colors of green, ridges five shades of shadows, and stickers the eight tones of hell.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-guthrie-span/24-guthrie-span-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Search of Woody Guthrie’s America', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Land Is Your Land', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moon, Freda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Folk Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guthrie, Woody', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Northwestern States (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Oklahoma', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Santa Fe (NM)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T16:47:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Freda Moon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Freda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8b319a6-9383-53c6-936e-e213cc14d0e6', 'word_count': 3263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8b319a6-9383-53c6-936e-e213cc14d0e6'}, {'abstract': 'San Marino, a 24-square-mile country surrounded by Italy, may appear puzzling at times, but there are rewards to be found in trying to figure it out.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/travel/seeking-authenticity-in-italys-tiny-neighbor.html', 'snippet': 'San Marino, a 24-square-mile country surrounded by Italy, may appear puzzling at times, but there are rewards to be found in trying to figure it out.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The jagged peaks of the Apennines? Vertiginous. The shimmering Adriatic? Azure to turquoise. The hearty cuisine of Emilia-Romagna? As delicious as ever. It all might sound like an ideal Italian vacation. But if you’re enjoying the gorgeous scenery and a great sangiovese in the tiny Republic of San Marino, please don’t start talking about how much you love traveling in Italy.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/travel/24-next-span/24-next-span-t