’s riotous Performa commission, which runs for two more nights in Long Island City, Queens, is a chic meditation on the disappearance of the American frontier.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/22/after-hours-wild-west-zombies-walk-into-a-burlesque-show/', 'snippet': 'The artist Marian Vitale’s riotous Performa commission, which runs for two more nights in Long Island City, Queens, is a chic meditation on the disappearance of the American frontier.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several years, the artist Marianne Vitale has been making rugged sculptures from repurposed materials that walk a line between critique and chic. On one hand, her bridges, structures, train-track crossings and headstones serve as a mournful meditation on the disappearance of the old frontier America; on the other, they resemble the kinds of old-timey, artisanal home furnishings sold in hipster meccas like Brooklyn and Silver Lake.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Hours | Wild West Zombies Walk Into a Burlesque Show', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Performance Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vitale, Marianne', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T18:37:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4d49fcc6-c2f5-51cc-a2fb-58a4ac917662', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4d49fcc6-c2f5-51cc-a2fb-58a4ac917662'}, {'abstract': 'Ari Shavit discusses his new book, “My Promised Land: The Triumph and Tragedy of Israel.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nyti