makers get into the plug-in hybrid game, each one has a different approach. Audi’s offering works well and looks good.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Driving any car in the rush hour traffic that coats Los Angeles roads like a viscous layer of hair gel is a chore. You could have the fastest, fanciest, most cool looking car in the world, and you’d still be sitting in the same motoring morass as someone perched behind the wheel of a dented ’92 Toyota Corolla.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 302, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 302}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 515, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 521, 'width': 1036, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/22/automobiles/22AUDIA3-1/22AUDIA3-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Short Drive in the 2015 Audi A3 E-tron', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Los Angeles Auto Show', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Audi Division of Volkswagen AG', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T20:50:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Automobiles', 'subsection_name': 'Automobiles', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Preston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Preston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9f8995ad-3745-5a38-9667-6f7476732e54', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9f8995ad-3745-5a38-9667-6f7476732e54'}, {'abstract': 'A rare street-fashion vignette, often observed on Fifth Avenue in Midtown, is a group of strangers, attracted by one another’s highly individual style of dress.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/fashion/bill-cunningham-on-the-street-nothing-gold-can-stay.html', 'snippet': 'A rare street-fashion vignette, often observed on Fifth Avenue in Midtown, is a group of strangers, attracted by one another’s highly individual style of dress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A rare street-fashion vignette, often observed on Fifth Avenue in Midtown, is a group of strangers, attracted by one another’s highly individual style of dress, who pause on their way to work to inquire of their clothes. The tradition may vanish, as one member of the group is moving to California. At times, they spontaneously try on one another’s look. Last week, nature provided a backdrop only it could create. In Central Park, a “Brigadoon” mist settled over the lake, and cascades of willows framed the Bow Bridge. All over the city, the ginkgo tree proved once again as the leaves fell that Manhattan streets are indeed paved with gold.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bill Cunningham | Nothing Gold Can Stay', 'kicker': 'On the Street', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Nothing Gold Can Stay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T20:50:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Cunningham', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff6d24e7-d463-5cb6-9656-4ad15feac531', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff6d24e7-d463-5cb6-9656-4ad15feac531'}, {'abstract': 'With competition in high-end supermarkets heating up, there’s never been a better time to shop for the Thanksgiving meal. But which store offers the best deal?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/business/an-upscale-bounty-and-a-thankful-shopper.html', 'snippet': 'With competition in high-end supermarkets heating up, there’s never been a better time to shop for the Thanksgiving meal. But which store offers the best deal?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since opening its first store in Austin, Tex., in 1980, Whole Foods Market has transformed the way Americans shop for food and eat at home — at least those who live in mostly affluent urban areas. When a branch opened in my neighborhood — theretofore a culinary desert — I wandered wide-eyed through what seemed a paradise of offerings tended by an eager and informed staff.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/25/business/james-stewart/james-stewart-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'heigh