'snippet': 'In Long Island City, Queens, the longtime appraiser Michael Capo has opened Beaux-Arts Auction, with an eclectic inventory made up largely of finds from liquidated estates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After nearly 40 years as one of New York’s most revered generalist appraisers, Michael Capo has opened an auction house, Beaux-Arts Auction, in Long Island City, Queens, which hit the ground running in October with a first sale that brought in $250,000. The inventory is made up largely of finds from liquidated estates, ranging from antique furniture to contemporary art, making it a dream destination for interior designers and collectors. Capo founded Beaux-Arts, which sits in a sprawling 7,500-square-foot gallery, with his longtime friend Marc Lester, a Sotheby’s veteran who specializes in French and European furniture.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Art and Design Auction You Might Actually Be Able to Afford', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Auctions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-22T23:31:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Charles Curkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Charles', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Curkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d8c5685e-9d12-5a03-9413-96d7a4db70fe', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8c5685e-9d12-5a03-9413-96d7a4db70fe'}, {'abstract': 'Kareem Serageldin, who led a group at Credit Suisse that traded in mortgage-backed securities, was sentenced to two and a half years in prison on Friday for inflating the value of bonds as the housing market collapsed.', 'web_url': 'htt