evealed that Bob Baffert, a Hall of Fame trainer, had been giving every horse in his barn a thyroid hormone without ever checking to see if any of them had thyroid problems.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Despite the Evidence, Trainers Deny a Doping Problem', 'kicker': 'On Horse Racing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Despite the Evidence, Trainers Deny a Doping Problem', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Horse Racing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jockeys, Drivers and Trainers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baffert, Bob', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doping (Sports)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Veterinary Medicine', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T03:21:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Drape', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ef15a55f-c563-588d-8233-0e14412c7679', 'word_count': 831, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ef15a55f-c563-588d-8233-0e14412c7679'}, {'abstract': 'China is undergoing a surprising reverse migration: As millions leave to find work in the cities, some well-educated urban dwellers are relocating to small towns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/world/asia/urbanites-flee-chinas-smog-for-blue-skies.html', 'snippet': 'China is undergoing a surprising reverse migration: As millions leave to find work in the cities, some well-educated urban dwellers are relocating to small towns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALI, China — A typical morning for Lin Liya, a native of Shanghai transplanted to this ancient town 