, 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e6490ed-0334-5e36-9c61-48ab2b11a3c8', 'word_count': 782, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e6490ed-0334-5e36-9c61-48ab2b11a3c8'}, {'abstract': 'The Flyers, undefeated in their last six games, have figured out Coach Craig Berube’s aggressive system of forechecking and appear to have turned around a season that started poorly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/sports/hockey/flyers-rescue-season-behind-interim-coach-and-a-few-good-bounces.html', 'snippet': 'The Flyers, undefeated in their last six games, have figured out Coach Craig Berube’s aggressive system of forechecking and appear to have turned around a season that started poorly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHILADELPHIA — On Nov. 1, one month into the N.H.L. season, the Philadelphia Flyers lost to the Alex Ovechkin-less Washington Capitals, 7-0. They took nearly three times as many penalty minutes as shots, and goalie Ray Emery attracted criticism by leaving the crease to fight Washington’s Braden Holtby. The Flyers’ record fell to 3-9, and their star center Claude Giroux still had not scored a goal. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/sports/hockey/23flyers-1/23flyers-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/23/sports/hockey/23flyers-1/23flyers-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/23/sports/hockey/23flyers-1/23flyers-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'cre