e85-5a01-a897-ab4ff0641601'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) IDENTITY THIEF (2013) Melissa McCarthy stars as a crazed kewpie doll of a thief sometimes named Diana who wreaks havoc on a milquetoast, Sandy Patterson (Jason Bateman), after stealing his identity just as he lands a job insuring his upward mobility. After leaving his wife (Amanda Peet) and their kids in their meager apartment, Sandy heads toward Diana’s home in Florida to regain control over his life. But she’s not about to give up the spoils easily. “From the moment Diana comes on screen in ‘Identity Thief,’ sugar-talking Sandy out of his information while she’s slurping a soda, Ms. McCarthy owns the movie,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “The character may be drawn in broad strokes, but Ms. McCarthy slips between the saucy and the demonic with exquisite effortlessness, fluttering her lashes and flashing her dimples one minute, unleashing her inner Medusa the next.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Saturday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fb8e120-2d2e-56d8-afd1-d44d8e4cf6bd', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fb8e120-2d2e-56d8-afd1-d44d8e4cf6bd'}, {'abstract': 'The Chinese government warned that it claimed the right to possibly take military action against aircraft that enter a newly declared “air defense identification zone,” which covers sea and islands also claimed by Japan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/world/asia/china-warns-of-action-against-aircraft-over-disputed-seas.html', 'snippet': 'The Chinese government warned that it claimed the right to possibly take military action against aircraft that enter a newly declared “air defense identification zone,” which covers sea and islands also claimed by Japan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — The Chinese government on Saturday claimed the right to identify, monitor and possibly take military action against aircraft that enter a newly declared “air defense identification zone,” which covers sea and islands also claimed by Japan and threatens to escalate an already tense dispute over some of the maritime territory. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Claims Air Rights Over Disputed Islands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Claims Air Rights Over Disputed Islands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T08:22:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e755f5ca-3780-51b7-8cdc-10dda1cf0f8e', 'word_count': 656, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e755f5ca-3780-51b7-8cdc-10dda1cf0f8e'}, {'abstract': 'After announcing he would delay signing a deal he had agreed to, Hamid Karzai began a new quarrel with Americans, over a recent raid.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/world/asia/us-upset-by-karzais-claim-about-civilian-deaths.html', 'snippet': 'After announcing he would delay signing a deal he had agreed to, Hamid Karzai began a new quarrel with Americans, over a recent raid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — For the second time in less than a week, President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan has picked a high-profile fight with his American allies, in the midst of a grand council that he convened to support a long-term security agreement with the United States. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 502, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 502}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1713, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/24/world/sub-subafghanistan/sub-subafghanistan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Karzai Insists U.S. Forces Killed Civilians in a Raid ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Karzai Insists U.S. Forces Killed Civilians in a Raid', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T08:57:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9df95935-0858-591e-9aff-9caac54308e6', 'word_count': 1269, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9df95935-0858-591e-9aff-9caac54308e6'}, {'abstract': 'Sino American Global Entertainment, a partnership with IMG Artists in the United States and China Arts and Entertainment Group, aims to create new paths for performances and marketing in both countries.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/new-musical-partnership-in-china/', 'snippet': 'Sino American Global Entertainment, a partnership with IMG Artists in the United States and China Arts and Entertainment Group, aims to create new paths for performances and marketing in both countries.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the biggest, but least-tapped markets for classical music and dance — as both an importer and exporter — is China. So this week IMG Artists, a major representative of classical musicians in the West, announced a new partnership with the China Arts and Entertainment Group, a huge arts and entertainment company in China.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Musical Partnership in China', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IMG Worldwide', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T13:42:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cooper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cooper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/811a8d18-bfe0-5a2b-804c-6b0d8735ee6c', 'word_count': 271, 'uri': 'nyt://article/811a8d18-bfe0-5a2b-804c-6b0d8735ee6c'}, {'abstract': 'Perversity in Sweden.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/bubblephobia-and-monetary-policy/', 'snippet': 'Perversity in Sweden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How do you know that monetary policy is too loose? The textbook answer is that excessively expansionary monetary policy shows up in rising inflation; stable inflation means money is neither too loose nor too tight. This answer has, however, come under challenge from both sides. One side — the side I’m on, and I’m pretty sure the side Janet Yellen is on, says that at low inflation rates this rule breaks down: the Phillips curve isn’t vertical, even in the long run, at low inflation (perhaps thanks to downward nominal wage rigidity), so stable inflation at a low level is consistent with an economy operating well below potential.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bubblephobia and Monetary Policy', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T13:42:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69cbc104-a885-5cb4-a928-7dc3e91d4a31', 'word_count': 380, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69cbc104-a885-5cb4-a928-7dc3e91d4a31'}, {'abstract': 'Egypt cited “provocative” criticisms by Turkey, and Turkey announced reciprocal steps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/world/middleeast/diplomatic-ties-fraying-between-egypt-and-turkey.html', 'snippet': 'Egypt cited “provocative” criticisms by Turkey, and Turkey announced reciprocal steps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Egypt announced on Saturday that it was downgrading its diplomatic relations with Turkey and expelled the Turkish ambassador because of “provocative” criticisms of Cairo by Turkey’s prime minister, a spokesman for Egypt’s foreign minister said.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Expels Turkey’s Ambassador, Further Fraying Diplomatic Ties ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egypt Expels Turkey’s Ambassador, Further Fraying Diplomatic Ties', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cairo (Egypt)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahim, Kareem', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ANKARA (TURKEY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arsu, Sebnem', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Muslim Brotherhood (Egypt)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T13:53:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kareem Fahim and Sebnem Arsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kareem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fahim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sebnem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Arsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ff10e1-03d2-5c72-9fac-a66a1b570b74', 'word_count': 455, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ff10e1-03d2-5c72-9fac-a66a1b570b74'}, {'abstract': 'This week, Joe discusses the multitude of Obamacare glitches, which is also the subject of his column today.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/joe-on-wnycs-money-talking-nov-22-2013/', 'snippet': 'This week, Joe discusses the multitude of Obamacare glitches, which is also the subject of his column today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Healthcare.gov launched more than seven weeks ago and the program’s problems keep piling up, as hundreds of thousands of people received notifications that their current coverage is being cancelled. There are also concerns over the website’s security. Last week, President Obama announced a fix. This week on Money Talking, Joe Nocera and Rana Foroohar of Time magazine consider if these changes put the entire law at risk and what the uncertainty means for consumers and businesses. Plus, a look at the recent JPMorgan settlement, which forced the bank to shell out a record $13 billion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Joe on WNYC’s “Money Talking”: Nov. 22, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T14:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6512287a-f156-52e8-bdf6-3a57822e1483', 'word_count': 96, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6512287a-f156-52e8-bdf6-3a57822e1483'}, {'abstract': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/23/in-our-pages-november-23/', 'snippet': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': '1938: S.S. Vows ‘Fire and Sword’', 'source': 'The 