outdoors in a cold climate, reporters from The New York Times share their tales of meteorologic misery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/sports/big-games-in-the-great-unforgiving-outdoors.html', 'snippet': 'As New York prepares for the first Super Bowl to be played outdoors in a cold climate, reporters from The New York Times share their tales of meteorologic misery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some weather prognosticators are warning that the first outdoor Super Bowl in a winter environment could morph into the Snow Bowl. But conducting sporting events in extreme weather is nothing new. Reporters from The New York Times share their tales of meteorologic misery.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Big Games in the Great, Unforgiving Outdoors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Big Games in the Great, Unforgiving Outdoors', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vecsey, George', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kepner, Tyler', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T19:26:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By George Vecsey, Tyler Kepner, Harvey Araton, John Branch, Jeré Longman, Joe Drape and Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vecsey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Tyler', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kepner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Branch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}, {'firstname': 'Jeré', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Longman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 5}, {'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Drape', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 6}, {'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 7}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/71480c51-ef34-55eb-9b44-fcd2f7997a19', 'word_count': 3447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/71480c51-ef34-55eb-9b44-fcd2f7997a19'}, {'abstract': 'Banning the “n-word” is itself a double standard, ignoring the fact that context is everything.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/opinion/sunday/coates-in-defense-of-a-loaded-word.html', 'snippet': 'Banning the “n-word” is itself a double standard, ignoring the fact that context is everything.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MY father’s name is William Paul Coates. I, like my six brothers and sisters, have always addressed him as Dad. Strangers often call him Mr. Coates. His friends call him Paul. If a stranger or one of my father’s friends called him Dad, my father might have a conversation. When I was a child, relatives of my paternal grandmother would call my father Billy. Were I to ever call my father Billy, we would probably have a different conversation. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/06/08/opinion/TaNe