08 and 2009, Census Bureau figures show, the median size of a new home was smaller than it had been the previous year. It seemed that after more than a decade of swelling domiciles, the McMansion era was over. But that conclusion may have been premature. ', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'McMansions Are Making a Comeback', 'kicker': 'Datapoints', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'McMansions Are Making A Comeback', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Home Builders', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-23T21:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna Bernasek', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bernasek', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8e083a7d-8429-501e-b52d-9bc527d7f003', 'word_count': 245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8e083a7d-8429-501e-b52d-9bc527d7f003'}, {'abstract': 'In a new paper, two law professors warn that the rise of three-dimensional printing could set off lawsuits like those seen over music file-sharing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/business/beyond-3-d-printers-magic-possible-legal-wrangling.html', 'snippet': 'In a new paper, two law professors warn that the rise of three-dimensional printing could set off lawsuits like those seen over music file-sharing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When reports first appeared that computers could produce three-dimensional objects — from toys to auto parts to household items — it sounded like a page from a science fict