 None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b70a75a8-6eb5-572a-9b8c-9f8f86809493', 'word_count': 864, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b70a75a8-6eb5-572a-9b8c-9f8f86809493'}, {'abstract': '“Gori Tere Pyaar Mein,” a Hindi musical, concerns the divide between a playboy architect (Imran Khan) and an activist (Kareena Kapoor), and a construction project that unites them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/movies/gori-tere-pyaar-mein-starring-imran-khan.html', 'snippet': '“Gori Tere Pyaar Mein,” a Hindi musical, concerns the divide between a playboy architect (Imran Khan) and an activist (Kareena Kapoor), and a construction project that unites them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The star of the new Hindi musical romance “Gori Tere Pyaar Mein,” Imran Khan, uncannily resembles a combination of Vince Vaughn and Cary Grant in his portrayal of the self-centered playboy, Sriram. With his classically handsome yet rounded face and his cocksure swagger, Mr. Khan seems to meld those two actors physically. The character he plays, an architect who is reminiscing to his fiancée (Shraddha Kapoor) about a past romance with a feisty activist named Dia (Kareena Kapoor, no relation to Shraddha), is also like Grant at his most roguishly charming and Mr. Vaughn at his most frustratingly caddish. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Bridging Playboy and Activist', 'kicker': 'Movie Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bridging Playboy And Activist', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gori Tere Pyaar Mein (Movie)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-24T22:14:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Miriam Bale', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Miriam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bale', 'qu