'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c2fb6198-e1b6-5a71-a46f-f54fdd157f4b'}, {'abstract': 'The sign of things to come, with Kevin G. Der.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/start-of-a-bumper-sticker/', 'snippet': 'The sign of things to come, with Kevin G. Der.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONDAY’S PUZZLE — If you drive where I drive, you spend a lot of time sitting in bumper-to-bumper traffic, and the only decent reading material while you’re waiting to take your foot off the brake is often the rear bumper of the car ahead of you. That’s after you take note of the car owner’s family make up, which is prominently displayed on the window (Father sticker, mother sticker, various and sundry children and pets, etc.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Start of a Bumper Sticker', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bumper Stickers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-24T23:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26163848-331d-5cc5-928e-b43596e7e33a', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26163848-331d-5cc5-928e-b43596e7e33a'}, {'abstract': 'The facts and trivia magazine announced last week that Jessanne Collins, a former editor at Playgirl, was promoted to editor in chief.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/business/media/top-editor-at-mental-floss-has-some-spicy-credentials.html', 'snippet': 'The facts and trivia magazine announced last week that Jessanne Collins, a former editor at Playgirl, was promoted to editor in chief.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To the underpaid, well-educated magazine scribes hoping for a break in an industry with little growth opportunity, there is hope.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Top Editor at Mental Floss Has Some Spicy Credentials', 'kicker': 'Media Decoder', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Top Editor at Mental Floss Has Some Spicy Credentials', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haughney, Christine', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-24T23:03:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Haughney', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haughney', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8c216627-baee-5a5c-bd04-7772ec53d51d', 'word_count': 442, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8c216627-baee-5a5c-bd04-7772ec53d51d'}, {'abstract': 'The financial data and news company Bloomberg L.P. is three times as large as it was when Michael R. Bloomberg left to become mayor of New York City twelve years ago. As he prepares to leave office, the organization is at a crossroads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/11/24/business/Bloombergs-Empire.html', 'snippet': 'The financial data and news company Bloomberg L.P. is three times as large as it was when Michael R. Bloomberg left to become mayor of New York City twelve years ago. As he prepares to leave office, the organization is at a crossroads.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The financial data and news company Bloomberg L.P. is three times as large as it was when Michael R. Bloomberg left to b