et': 'The Thunder and the Spurs, who will play in Oklahoma City on Wednesday, are ranked in the top 10 in offensive and defensive efficiency.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every week, The New York Times chooses one essential game to watch, highlighting hot teams, winning and losing streaks, and statistical intrigue in the N.B.A.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'N.B.A. Game of the Week: Two of the West’s Best', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'N.B.A. Game of the Week: Two of the West’s Best', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Oklahoma City Thunder', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'San Antonio Spurs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-24T23:59:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonah Engel Bromwich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonah', 'middlename': 'Engel', 'lastname': 'Bromwich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0d8f7dc-f60b-5b93-99a4-13fbc55518ce', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0d8f7dc-f60b-5b93-99a4-13fbc55518ce'}, {'abstract': 'The Joyce Theater Foundation plans to announce on Monday that it will present the New York premiere of “Snow White” with choreography by Angelin Preljocaj.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/arts/dance/grimm-snow-white-coming-to-lincoln-center.html', 'snippet': 'The Joyce Theater Foundation plans to announce on Monday that it will present the New York premiere of “Snow White” with choreography by Angelin Preljocaj.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Joyce Theater Foundation plans to announce on Monday that it will present the New York premiere of “Snow White” with choreography by Angelin Preljocaj. Performed by Mr. Preljocaj’s French dance company, Ballet Preljocaj, and based on the Brothers Grimm fairy tale, not the 1937 animated Disney film, the production is scheduled for a six-performance run from April 23 to 27 at the David H. Koch Theater at Lincoln Center. Mr. Preljocaj recently choreographed a new work for the New York City Ballet and Ballet Preljocaj completed a run at the Brooklyn Academy of Music during its Next Wave Festival this month.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Grimm ‘Snow White’ Coming to Lincoln Center', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Grimm ‘Snow White’ Coming to Lincoln Center', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Ballet Preljocaj', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Preljocaj, Angelin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Joyce Theater Foundation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T00:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Dance', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Adam W. Kepler', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Kepler', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e81a9c6-a867-5f8f-940f-83b711c43ae5', 'word_count': 102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e81a9c6-a867-5f8f-940f-83b711c43ae5'}, {'abstract': 'John C. Malone, the chairman of Liberty Media, is working behind the scenes to gain control of Time Warner Cable, seeking a second act in an industry he once dominated.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/24/once-cables-king-malone-aims-to-regain-his-crown/', 'snippet': 'John C. Malone, the chairman of Liberty Media, is working behind the scenes to gain control of Time Warner Cable, seeking a second act in an industry he once dominated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John C. Malone made a fortune wiring American homes for cable television in the 1980s and 1990s. Known as the King of Cable, he sold TCI — once the country’s largest cable operator — to AT&T for $48 billion in 1999.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1315, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/cable-1/cable-1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once Cable