to the Cowboys on Sunday left the Giants on the verge of elimination from playoff contention. It was also a microcosm of their year so far.', 'lead_paragraph': 'EAST RUTHERFORD, N.J. — It was eerily quiet inside a frigid MetLife Stadium on Sunday evening as the clock wound down to what felt like two seconds left in a largely confounding and now deflated season. Most fans stood and no doubt prayed for a Giants miracle, or one of those trademark Cowboys debacles. Some headed toward the exits rather than watch Dallas’s Dan Bailey line up for a 35-yard field goal. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Illusion of Postseason Promise Heads for the Exits', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'An Illusion of Postseason Promise Heads for the Exits', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dallas Cowboys', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T04:02:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Harvey Araton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Harvey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Araton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/721c2112-6050-5e80-a6a1-8cd087e3708e', 'word_count': 917, 'uri': 'nyt://article/721c2112-6050-5e80-a6a1-8cd087e3708e'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Foster will play a disfigured woman on a journey to meet her father in the Roundabout Theater Company’s Broadway production of the 1997 musical “Violet.”', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/sutton-foster-to-star-in-roundabout-theater-revival-of-violet/', 'snippet': 'Ms. Foster will play a disfigured woman on a journey to meet her father in the Roundabout Theater Company’s Broadway production of the 1997 musical “Violet.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Roundabout Theater Company may end up competing against itself in the Tony Award race for best musical revival this spring. Roundabout announced on Sunday that it would team up with several commercial producers to mount a Broadway run of the 1997 musical “Violet,” with Sutton Foster, a two-time Tony Award winner, starring as a disfigured woman on a journey to meet a televangelist faith healer. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/theater/25foster/25foster-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 529, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/25/theater/25foster/25foster-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 529}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/theater/25foster/25foster-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 903, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/theater/25foster/25foster-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1806, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/theater/25foster/25foster-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/25/theater/25foster/25foster-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/t