ained/', 'snippet': 'As the United States deports record numbers of immigrants, John Moore looks at a newly opened detention center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Adelanto Detention Facility in California is designed like a federal prison, with cells, common areas and recreation centers. The 1,200-bed center keeps some detainees in “segregation cells,” for disciplinary reasons, and many of those are solitary confinement, where guards pass meals through openings in the bars.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An Immigrant’s Dream, Detained', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deferred Action for Childhood Arrivals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deportation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Illegal Immigration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'GEO Group Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Immigration and Customs Enforcement (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Guatemala', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T10:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ea244579-a252-5c44-859