ph': 'In my recent posts, I have told the story of how I started to explore my options for renewing my insurance this year. It’s been my habit in writing for this blog to try to convey useful information, derived from my experience as an ordinary small-business owner, in the form of narrative episodes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Seven Conclusions About Small-Business Health Insurance', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Part-Time Employment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Working Hours', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HealthCare.gov', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T12:00:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c57f1fe1-f02c-5f8b-9169-efdbbf512d65', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c57f1fe1-f02c-5f8b-9169-efdbbf512d65'}, {'abstract': 'The British bank principally owned by the government said that it had hired a law firm to examine its lending practices.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/government-report-blast-rbs-lending-practices/', 'snippet': 'The British bank principally owned by the government said that it had hired a law firm to examine its lending practices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Royal Bank of Scotland, the British bank principally owned by the government, said on Monday that it had hired a law firm to examine its lending practices after government reports criticized its operations, including claims that it pushed some business clients into serious financial difficulties.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 354}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1208, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/dealbook/dbpix-rbs/dbpix-rbs-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Lending Practices at R.B.S. Condemned in Two Reports', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Lending Practices at R.B.S. Condemned in Two Reports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cable, Vince', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Osborne, George', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal Bank of Scotland PLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T12:25:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julia Werdigier and Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Werdigier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f30894d-cd70-5388-b9e2-ce5b0ff12ee4', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f30894d-cd70-5388-b9e2-ce5b0ff12ee4'}, {'abstract': 'John C. Malone, once called the King of Cable, is back on the prowl in the industry he helped create. | While bitcoin draws mounting interest, dozens of digital alternatives are emerging. | The top lawyer at JPMorgan Chase has a bad taste in his mouth. | Apple is buying an Israeli start-up that makes motion-detection chips.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/morning-agenda-malone-aims-to-shake-up-cable-tv/', 'snippet': 'John C. Malone, once called the King of Cable, is back on the prowl in the industry he helped create. | While bitcoin draws mounting interest, dozens of digital alternatives are emerging. | The top lawyer at JPMorgan Chase has a bad taste in his m...', 'lead_paragraph': 'John C. Malone, whose success wiring American homes for cable television in the 1980s and 1990s earned him the nickname King of Cable, is back on the prowl in the industry he helped create, DealBook’s David Gelles reports. Mr. Malone, 72, now the chairman of Liberty Media, is working behind the scenes to gain control of Time Warner Cable, the country’s second-largest cable operator by subscribers, behind Comcast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Malone Aims to Shake Up Cable TV', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T12:59:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f655892f-98c9-52c4-8079-0da301e5e279', 'word_count': 1772, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f655892f-98c9-52c4-8079-0da301e5e279'}, {'abstract': 'Love Canal had bigger impacts on environmental policy than human health, followup studies show.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/revisiting-love-canal/', 'snippet': 'Love Canal had bigger impacts on environmental policy than human health, followup studies show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have a piece on the Booming blog of The Times looking back at the complicated environmental and political legacy of the Love Canal toxic waste site 35 years after state and federal officials declared an environmental emergency there. (Click on Google Maps to get the lay of the land.) My piece accompanies the latest video from Retro Report, a valuable new journalism project revisiting old stories to see which news elements held up, and which turned out to be unjustified. Here’s an excerpt and a link to the rest:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Revisiting Love Canal', 'kicker': 'Dot Earth', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Water Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ENVIRONMENT', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Niagara Falls (NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T13:27:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew C. Revkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Revkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2715774b-9f9f-56a2-af19-53211c2334d9', 'word_count': 463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2715774b-9f9f-56a2-af19-53211c2334d9'}, {'abstract': 'The Carlyle Group said on Monday that it had raised its sixth fund dedicated to buyouts in the United States – its first such fund since the dark days of 2008.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/carlyle-raises-13-billion-for-u-s-buyouts/', 'snippet': 'The Carlyle Group said on Monday that it had raised its sixth fund dedicated to buyouts in the United States – its first such fund since the dark days of 2008.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Carlyle Group has a new $13 billion war chest for leveraged buyouts in the United States.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dbpix-carlyle1/dbpix-carlyle1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 