lped Real Salt Lake eliminate the Portland Timbers and advance to Major League Soccer’s championship game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTLAND, Ore. — Real Salt Lake’s players and coaches climbed atop a small makeshift stage at midfield for a trophy celebration after dispatching the Portland Timbers in Sunday’s M.L.S. Western Conference final. A machine sprayed red confetti in the air.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1285, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/26mls/26mls-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sure-Footed Real Salt Lake Reaches M.L.S. Final', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Sure-Footed Real Salt Lake Reaches M.L.S. Final', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Salt Lake (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Soccer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Timbers (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T17:38:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32002dcf-a56c-5f47-8484-6d9dd0d247bd', 'word_count': 871, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32002dcf-a56c-5f47-8484-6d9dd0d247bd'}, {'abstract': 'Susan E. Rice told President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan to sign a security agreement or potentially face the complete pullout of American troops by the end of 2014, officials said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/world/asia/obamas-national-security-adviser-meets-with-karzai.html', 'snippet': 'Susan E. Rice told President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan to sign a security agreement or potentially face the complete pullout of American troops by the end of 2014, officials said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KABUL, Afghanistan — President Obama’s national security adviser, Susan E. Rice, told President Hamid Karzai of Afghanistan on Monday to stop his delay in signing a security agreement or potentially face the complete and final pullout of American troops by the end of 2014, according to American and Afghan officials.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Obama’s Visiting Security Adviser Tells Karzai to Sign Agreement', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Obama’s Visiting Security Adviser Tells Karzai to Sign Agreement', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rice, Susan E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T17:39:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a59816c4-2394-583d-af29-786498f9c94f', 'word_count': 1103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a59816c4-2394-583d-af29-786498f9c94f'}, {'abstract': '“High Hopes,” an album by Bruce Springsteen that includes studio recordings of songs that have been part of his stage set, is due out on Jan. 14.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/new-springsteen-album-coming-in-january/', 'snippet': '“High Hopes,” an album by Bruce Springsteen that includes studio recordings of songs that have been part of his stage set, is due out on Jan. 14.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The drill for rock stars usually goes like this: record an album’s worth of new material and release it, then take the songs on tour, recording the shows for what, these days, is the inevitable live album. Bruce Springsteen has been tinkering with that formula in recent months, making new studio recordings of songs that have been part of his stage set for ages but were never released on studio albums. The result, “High Hopes,” is due out on Columbia on Jan. 14. He announced the album on Twitter on Sunday evening.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Springsteen Album Coming in January', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Springsteen, Bruce', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'E Street Band', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T17:43:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/951fb2c9-a38f-5d07-ba1c-dc13f154bd48', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/951fb2c9-a38f-5d07-ba1c-dc13f154bd48'}, {'abstract': 'C. Douglas McMillon, a longtime company executive who is now president of Walmart International, will succeed Michael T. Duke, who has been Walmart’s chief since 2009, the company said.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/business/walmart-names-chief-of-international-unit-as-new-ceo.html', 'snippet': 'C. Douglas McMillon, a longtime company executive who is now president of Walmart International, will succeed Michael T. Duke, who has been Walmart’s chief since 2009, the company said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As Walmart enters a fiercely competitive holiday season while still hampered by sluggish sales, the company’s board announced on Monday that Michael T. Duke, its chief executive, would retire early next year and a longtime executive, C. Douglas McMillon, would replace him.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/25/business/25walmart/25walmart-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Succession at Walmart Puts an Insider at the Helm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Succession At Walmart Puts an Insider At the Helm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Walmart Stores Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duke, Michael T', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McMillon, C Douglas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T17:53:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d851f47e-3a46-51d0-93cb-436f1710272b', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d851f47e-3a46-51d0-93cb-436f1710272b'}, {'abstract': 'An investigator said deprivation of freedom and security, and the desire to feel protected, was pushing 2,000 to 3,000 people to leave Eritrea every month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/world/africa/government-abuse-drives-eritreans-to-flee-un-says.html', 'snippet': 'An investigator said deprivation of freedom and security, and the desire to feel protected, was pushing 2,000 to 3,000 people to leave Eritrea every month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GENEVA — Severe government abuse, not harsh living conditions, is driving thousands of Eritreans to flee their country every month and risk their lives trying, often by precarious means, to reach other countries, a United Nations investigator said Monday. Her assertion puts a spotlight on an exodus that resulted in tragedy last month when hundreds of migrants, many of them Eritreans, drowned as they tried to cross the Mediterranean to Italy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Government Abuse Drives Eritreans to Flee, U.N. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Eritrea: Migrants Fleeing Abuse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cumming-Bruce, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Eritrea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T17:59:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nick Cumming-Bruce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cumming-Bruce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9709afb-83fd-5b92-88a7-40172d471bdc', 'word_count': 431, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9709afb-83fd-5b92-88a7-40172d471bdc'}, {'abstract': 'Except to correct factual errors, The Times rarely changes or deletes published material.', 'web_url': 'https://publiceditor.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/why-a-times-photo-remains-online-after-criticism/', 'snippet': 'Except to correct factual errors, The Times rarely changes or deletes published material.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After I wrote last week about a photograph of a Palestinian mother, many readers and many other observers complained that – since two senior editors agreed it was not a good choice for dominant art with the story about an Israeli soldier’s death – it was wrong for The Times to not remove the photo online.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why a Times Photo Remains Online After Criticism', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor&#039;s Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T18:16:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margare