 in Wyoming and opposes same-sex marriage. Then Dick Cheney, the former vice president, and his wife jumped into the fray, defending “Liz’s many kindnesses.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Liz Cheney’s New Ad', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Same-Sex Marriage, Civil Unions and Domestic Partnerships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheney, Liz', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Wyoming', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T19:50:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0f7028cc-1d24-51ac-974a-6f6da3098321', 'word_count': 339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0f7028cc-1d24-51ac-974a-6f6da3098321'}, {'abstract': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'web_url': 'https://intransit.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/walkabout-medellin-reimagined-the-new-longest-flight-in-the-world/', 'snippet': 'A weekly capsule of travel news curated by our writers and editors.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Medellin, the city once known as the murder capital of the world and home to cartel boss Pablo Escobar, has undergone a decade-long campaign to soften its image and appeal to travelers. The urban renewal has not only cut down on crime, but led to several inventive strides in architecture, technology, fashion and, of course, night life. (Bloomberg)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Walkabout: Medellin, Reimagined; The New ‘Longest Flight in the World’', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Medellin (Colombia)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T19:52:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eb0af24e-f198-5975-83fd-11e3dcd87453', 'word_count': 140, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eb0af24e-f198-5975-83fd-11e3dcd87453'}, {'abstract': 'The Simon Wiesenthal Center, which runs the campaign, has passed information about four people to the authorities for further investigation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/world/europe/poster-campaign-generates-nazi-war-crime-tips.html', 'snippet': 'The Simon Wiesenthal Center, which runs the campaign, has passed information about four people to the authorities for further investigation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — A poster campaign by the Simon Wiesenthal Center intended to identify aging Germans who might have participated in Nazi crimes has yielded information about four people, including a woman who might have been a guard at Auschwitz, that has been passed to the authorities for further investigation, the group said Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 833, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/world/GERMANY/GERMANY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 833}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image