yt://interactive/34061951-5375-54ab-ae98-5a75cb0bcc58', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/34061951-5375-54ab-ae98-5a75cb0bcc58'}, {'abstract': 'Wayne Mills was fatally shot after a dispute in a Nashville bar early Saturday morning, the police said.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/country-singer-dies-after-nashville-bar-brawl/', 'snippet': 'Wayne Mills was fatally shot after a dispute in a Nashville bar early Saturday morning, the police said.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was an unusually rough weekend for country music. An after-hours bar brawl in Nashville on Saturday left the singer and guitarist Wayne Mills dead of a gunshot wound to the head. And members of Willie Nelson’s band, including his longtime drummer, Paul English, were injured when the band’s tour bus crashed into an overpass pillar on a highway near Sulphur Springs, Tex., also in the wee hours of Saturday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Country Singer Dies After Nashville Bar Brawl', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Country Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T20:28:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Allan Kozinn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Allan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kozinn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fe17c44-6156-590a-8644-f39565dcbb3e', 'word_count': 295, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fe17c44-6156-590a-8644-f39565dcbb3e'}, {'abstract': 'The autoworkers’ union probably needs Chrysler to be valued at $18 billion to make an initial public offering worthwhile, but recent price talk has fallen short of that.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/25/in-delay-of-chrysler-i-p-o-fiat-may-have-gained-upper-hand/', 'snippet': 'The autoworkers’ union probably needs Chrysler to be valued at $18 billion to make an initial public offering worthwhile, but recent price talk has fallen short of that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fiat may have slipped into the driver’s seat. An autoworkers’ fund that owns 41.5 percent of Chrysler has been pushing for an initial public offering of the company as part of talks with its Italian partner. Chrysler’s board has decided to delay the stock sale until next year, suggesting Fiat’s negotiating position has improved.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Delay of Chrysler I.P.O., Fiat May Have Gained Upper Hand', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marchionne, Sergio', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chrysler Group LLC', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Fiat SpA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Automobile Workers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-25T20:34:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Antony Currie', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Antony', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Currie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dcdcf18-418e-51b7-b91f-7534e5808afd', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dcdcf18-418e-51b7-b91f-7534e5808afd'}, {'abstract': 'Bill Bryson, the author of “One Summer: America, 1927,” talks about his “intense desire to go o