a market in central Baghdad killed 12 people, the police said. Earlier, a suicide bomber attacked a police checkpoint north of Baghdad, killing three police officers and two civilians. South of Baghdad, two militia members were killed by a roadside bomb. Another militia member was killed by a bomb attached to his car in Salahuddin Province, north of Baghdad, while a roadside bomb near a high school in the region killed a woman. In Baghdad, a bomb blew up a truck driver and gunmen killed a Ministry of Justice employee. More than 300 Iraqis have been killed this month in similar attacks. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Iraq: Attacks Kill at Least 23 People', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Middle East', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Iraq: Attacks Kill at Least 23 People', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Adnan, Duraid', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bombs and Explosives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T00:48:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Duraid Adnan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Duraid', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Adnan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/30c03308-83a9-5fab-8d57-caed0b5f7fee', 'word_count': 134, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30c03308-83a9-5fab-8d57-caed0b5f7fee'}, {'abstract': 'The Cowboys quarterback has the team in position to make the playoffs. But William C. Rhoden notes that history tells us Tony Romo will eventually disappoint Dallas fans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/vi