r suit in federal court on Monday, which comes about three months after the N.F.L. agreed to settle a similar case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/sports/hockey/retired-players-sue-nhl-over-head-injuries.html', 'snippet': 'The players, who were in the league in the 1970s, ’80s and ’90s, filed their suit in federal court on Monday, which comes about three months after the N.F.L. agreed to settle a similar case.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten former N.H.L. players sued the league Monday for negligence and fraud, saying the sport’s officials should have done more to address head injuries but instead celebrated a culture of speed and violence.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ten Former N.H.L. Players Sue League Over Head Injuries', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ten Former N.H.L. Players Sue League Over Head Injuries', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klein, Jeff Z', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Concussions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hockey, Ice', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Hockey League', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T00:51:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Hockey', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson and Jeff Z. Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': 'Z.', 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7738449d-5b4a-5f82-a634-30c4626607bf', 'word_count': 537, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7738449d-5b4a-5f82-a634-30c4626607bf'}, {'abstract': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia met with Pope Francis in the Vatican on Monday, and their first encounter was primarily focused on the Middle East.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/world/europe/the-vatican-putin-meets-the-pope.html', 'snippet': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia met with Pope Francis in the Vatican on Monday, and their first encounter was primarily focused on the Middle East.', 'lead_paragraph': ' President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia met with Pope Francis in the Vatican on Monday, and their first encounter was primarily focused on the Middle East. They emphasized “the need to bring an end to the violence” in Syria, ensuring humanitarian assistance to Syrians affected by the fighting while seeking ways to find a “peaceful solution to the conflict,” the Vatican said in a statement. They also touched on “the life of the Catholic community in Russia,” according to the Vatican, but the Holy See spokesman, the Rev. Federico Lombardi, said that the “ecumenical question” between the Roman Catholic and Orthodox Churches, whose relationship has been tense since the two churches divided nearly 1,000 years ago, was not discussed. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Vatican: Putin Meets the Pope', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Vatican: Putin Meets the Pope', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Putin, Vladimir V', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T00:53:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elisabetta Povoledo', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elisabetta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Povoledo', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f99de43-ca58-5879-826a-6ce6658997f9', 'word_count': 119, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f99de43-ca58-5879-826a-6ce6658997f9'}, {'abstract': 'This Op-Doc video explains why ordinary Americans should be concerned about online surveillance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/opinion/why-care-about-the-nsa.html', 'snippet': 'This Op-Doc video explains why ordinary Americans should be concerned about online surveillance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like many Americans and people around the world, I was deeply disturbed to hear the revelations of Edward Snowden about N.S.A. surveillance, which is an affront to the United States Bill of Rights. But as a filmmaker who has made a number of documentaries about technology and online activism, I can’t say that Snowden’s revelations came as a surprise. Some concerned citizens have long understood that powerful digital technologies can be abused to carve away at civil liberties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/opinion/video-opdoc-surveillance/video-opdoc-surveillance-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/opinion/video-opdoc-surveillance/video-opdoc-surveillance-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '