-general.html', 'snippet': 'Mark R. Herring, a Democrat, was certified by the State Board of Elections as Virginia’s next attorney general on Monday, but he may face a recount.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mark R. Herring, a Democrat, was certified by the State Board of Elections as Virginia’s next attorney general on Monday, but he may face a recount in a race he won by just 165 votes out of 2.2 million cast. Both Mr. Herring and his Republican opponent, Mark D. Obenshain, have formed transition committees. Mr. Obenshain, who has 10 days to request a recount, issued a statement calling the Nov. 5 vote “the closest statewide election in modern Virginia history.” He said the choice to press a recount “is not one to be made lightly.” Both sides have lawyers at the ready for a recount battle. There is a “nuclear option”: to contest the election, which would throw it into the state House of Delegates. Republicans hold a majority there. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Virginia: Democrat Certified as Attorney General', 'kicker': 'National Briefing | South', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Virginia: Democrat Certified as Attorney General', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Attorneys General', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriel, Trip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herring, Mark R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obenshain, Mark D', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Virginia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T01:19:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier'