Fox Sports carries Super Bowl XLVIII from MetLife Stadium, so will Fox Deportes, the Spanish-language network that is also part of 21st Century Fox. The Super Bowl has never before been televised in Spanish in the United States. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Super Bowl First: A U.S. Telecast With Spanish Announcers', 'kicker': 'N.F.L. Roundup', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Super Bowl First: A U.S. Telecast With Spanish Announcers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spanish Language', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Super Bowl', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T05:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Sandomir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sandomir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f38607fd-c0d3-584a-96a5-383c978bfdf8', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f38607fd-c0d3-584a-96a5-383c978bfdf8'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/arts/television/whats-on-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (FX) WANTED (2008) A meek cubicle drone (James McAvoy, above) is initiated into a secret society of assassins known as the Fraternity to avenge the murder of his father in this ultraviolent action-thriller directed by Timur Bekmambetov. Morgan Freeman plays the organization’s leader, and Angelina Jolie portrays an amoral if fashionably turned-out killer. “Mr. Bekmambetov, a Russian filmmaker who has earned a cult following with his razzly-dazzly thrillers ‘Day Watch’ and ‘Night Watch,’ certainly proves here that he knows how to use every blunt tool of the bullying trade: flashy effects, zippy cuts, simulated death, walls of sound, wheels of steel and, in between the bullets and blood, a hot mama to make the brother-to-brother, man-on-man action less worrisome,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times. “\xa0‘Wanted’ is a goof, then, and for a short stretch a pretty diverting one.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Tuesday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb942d5d-0089-56e5-adbf-59af3ea1f81c', 'word_count': 748, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb942d5d-0089-56e5-adbf-59af3ea1f81c'}, {'abstract': 'The Trail Blazers took an early 22-point lead and responded to every run from the Knicks, who were led by Carmelo Anthony’s 34 points and 15 rebounds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/sports/basketball/knicks-drop-sixth-straight-falling-in-portland.html', 'snippet': 'The Trail Blazers took an early 22-point lead and responded to every run from the Knicks, who were led by Carmelo Anthony’s 34 points and 15 rebounds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PORTLAND, Ore. — Before Monday night’s game, one of the television sets inside the visitors’ locker room at the Moda Center was tuned to an N.F.L. game. This did not please Amar’e Stoudemire, the veteran Knicks forward who was sprawled on the floor studying film of the Trail Blazers. He wanted the football turned off. Why was it even on?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 698}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 880, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1760, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/sports/knicks/knicks-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Knicks Drop Sixth Straight, Falling in Portland', 'kicker': 'Trail Blazers 102, Knicks 91', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Knicks Drop Sixth Straight, Falling in Portland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Portland Trail Blazers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T06:04:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc4d3bb-4b85-50c7-827c-90ed0668032c', 'word_count': 702, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc4d3bb-4b85-50c7-827c-90ed0668032c'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Jauhari spoke about how people’s perception about security has changed in the five years since the terror attacks in Mumbai.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/a-conversation-with-prabhat-jauhari-c-e-o-of-mumbai-private-security-firm/', 'snippet': 'Mr. Jauhari spoke about how people’s perception about security has changed in the five years since the terror attacks in Mumbai.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Prabhat Jauhari is the chief executive officer of Tops Air Rescue and Topsline Life Response Services, the first private emergency response service in Mumbai, which was started by Topsgrup in 2004. The Topsline crew, which is trained in rescue and evacuation operations, worked with the Mumbai police during the terror attacks of Nov. 26, 2008, to rescue over 150 people.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/world/asia/26-topsgrup-IndiaInk/26-topsgrup-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/world/asia/26-topsgrup-IndiaInk/26-topsgrup-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 593}}, {'rank