}, {'abstract': 'The proposal, 670 pages long, is part of an effort by Scottish authorities to answer many questions about the implications of a referendum next year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/world/europe/scotland-to-unveil-landmark-document-on-independence-from-britain.html', 'snippet': 'The proposal, 670 pages long, is part of an effort by Scottish authorities to answer many questions about the implications of a referendum next year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Behind in the opinion polls, Scottish Nationalists who are seeking independence from Britain in a referendum next year set out their wish list for a new nation on Tuesday, but made several assertions about their future relations with Britain and international partners that are sharply disputed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scots Propose Independence With Pounds and Passports', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scots Propose Independence With Pounds and Passports', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Scotland', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castle, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T09:59:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Castle and Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Castle', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/187ed412-5ffd-52aa-8436-1d9b82e70857', 'word_count': 673, 'uri': 'nyt://article/187ed412-5ffd-52aa-8436-1d9b82e70857'}, {'abstract': 'Running a global city is tough — and that’s a good thing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/magazine/why-mayors-cant-combat-income-inequality.html', 'snippet': 'Running a global city is tough — and that’s a good thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the not-yet-completed One57, a luxury residential tower off Central Park, the unsold floor-through apartments are going for $53 million and up. The penthouse sold for more than $90 million. One57 will be the tallest residence in the Western Hemisphere (until another luxury high-rise on Park Avenue is completed in 2015), and on a clear day, residents on the top floors should be able to just make out the South Bronx. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/mag-01Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/mag-01Economy-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/mag-01Economy-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/mag-01Economy-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1360, 'width': 2040, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/magazine/01economy/01economy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Mind the Gap', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mind the Gap', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Mayors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Davidson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Davidson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b4352c77-c98a-5ecc-9b43-e99cab0dfdc6', 'word_count': 1028, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b4352c77-c98a-5ecc-9b43-e99cab0dfdc6'}, {'abstract': 'Twin exhibitions throw together both scientific and fictitious depictions of space, from the 19th century to the present.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/the-final-frontier-in-photographs/', 'snippet': 'Twin exhibitions throw together both scientific and fictitious depictions of space, from the 19th century to the present.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There it is — the whole shebang. Or what’s left of the Big Bang, if you want to be precise and scientific about it. The trippy scene, all fall colors and gray splotches, was