nization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd154f6-f42e-5688-a363-d0101a7e4430', 'word_count': 314, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd154f6-f42e-5688-a363-d0101a7e4430'}, {'abstract': 'The Senate Special Committee on Aging has started a consumer hotline designed to help track scams targeting the elderly.', 'web_url': 'https://newoldage.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/a-new-way-to-report-fraud/', 'snippet': 'The Senate Special Committee on Aging has started a consumer hotline designed to help track scams targeting the elderly.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The letters arrive almost daily, on official-looking letterhead from a supposed charity, or from the J.M.D. Major Cash Disbursement Office. More blatantly, letters sometimes come from an outfit called Mountains of Money. They announce that the 85-year-old man to whom they’re addressed has won a prize — the amount seems to hover around $11,000 — and explain that to claim it, he has to fill out a form, often complete with a “verification code,” and send it in with a check for $6 or $7.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Way to Report Fraud', 'kicker': 'The New Old Age', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elder Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Frauds and Swindling', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paula Span', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paula', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Span', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9aa688e4-7c28-5762-83df-d400f8a694d8', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9aa688e4-7c28-5762-83df-d400f8a694d8'}, {'abstract': 'The mission was described as one of the most difficult to date for China’s space program.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/china-to-send-jade-rabbit-rover-to-the-moon/', 'snippet': 'The mission was described as one of the most difficult to date for China’s space program.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China will send an unmanned rover to the moon in early December, a spokesman for the Commission of Science, Technology, and Industry for National Defense said on Tuesday. The lunar probe will be called the Yutu, or Jade Rabbit, a name that comes from a Chinese myth about a white rabbit that lives on the moon and was selected in an online poll.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/world/26SINO-JADERABBIT01/26SINO-JADERABBIT01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 353, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/world/26SINO-JADERABBIT01/26SINO-JADERABBIT01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 353}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/world/26SINO-JADERABBIT01/26SINO-JADERABBIT01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/world/26SINO-JADERABBIT01/26SINO-JADERABBIT01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1204, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/world/26SINO-JADERABBIT01/26SINO-JADERABBIT01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/27/world/26SINO-JADERABBIT01/26SINO