ism', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carter, Ashton B', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Robert M', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rumsfeld, Donald H', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Defense Department', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T15:53:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By Thom Shanker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Thom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shanker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c72a2cd5-d6ef-57ae-8475-6748ff8172eb', 'word_count': 903, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c72a2cd5-d6ef-57ae-8475-6748ff8172eb'}, {'abstract': 'Bruce Arians, who was the A.P. coach of the year as the Colts’ interim coach last season, is only one reason the Arizona Cardinals are 7-4 and riding a four-game winning streak.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/sports/football/another-turnaround-by-arians-this-time-in-arizona.html', 'snippet': 'Bruce Arians, who was the A.P. coach of the year as the Colts’ interim coach last season, is only one reason the Arizona Cardinals are 7-4 and riding a four-game winning streak.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bruce Arians is doing it again. A year ago, he helped turn the Indianapolis Colts from the worst team in the N.F.L. to a playoff team. Hired as the team’s offensive coordinator, he was named the Associated Press coach of the year after Chuck Pagano, who was found to have leukemia, took a leave of absence. The Arizona Cardinals hired Arians as their head coach after firing Ken Whisenhunt, and Arians is again a viable candidate for the award.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/sports/27nflscore1/27nflscore1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Turnaround by Arians, This Time in Arizona', 'kicker': 'Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coach Takes His Magic To the Desert', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA CARDINALS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Arians, Bruce', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Indianapolis Colts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Palmer, Carson', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Campbell, Calais', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dansby, Karlos', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mathieu, Tyrann', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh Steelers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Floyd, Michael (1989- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T15:58:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chase Stuart', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chase', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stuart', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/261741ef-ceef-5fe7-9d74-ca5bc3130f7e', 'word_count': 898, 'uri': 'nyt://article/261741ef-ceef-5fe7-9d74-ca5bc3130f7e'}, {'abstract': 'A business owner says he realized this fall that if he spent time digging into his health insurance options, he might make a better choice. With luck, he hoped, he might even lower his costs.', 'web_url': 'https://boss.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/what-i-needed-to-understand-about-health-insurance/', 'snippet': 'A business owner says he realized this fall that if he spent time digging into his health insurance options, he might make a better choice. With luck, he hoped, he might even lower his costs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I have bought health insurance for my workers since 1994, and since then I’ve spent well over a million dollars paying premiums. I have always found it to be troubling that I was given sole authority to make the choice as to what kind of coverage we would offer, and to a certain extent, how much it would cost. Was I doing a good job? I never heard any complaints about the policies I chose, even when I moved us into an HMO in the late ’90s, when I made my workers contribute to their plan costs in 2005, and when rates skyrocketed in the years after that.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What I Needed to Understand About Health Insurance', 'kicker': 'You&#039;re the Boss', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insurance', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prices (Fares, Fees and Rates)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Small Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Downs, Paul', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paul Downs Cabinetmakers', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Entrepreneurship', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Downs', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d6baeee-2ef0-5cc1-8c5d-e196adcf703c', 'word_count': 1778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d6baeee-2ef0-5cc1-8c5d-e196adcf703c'}, {'abstract': 'Guest blogger Mari Kuraishi urges readers to fund smaller scale, on the ground relief efforts in the wake of Typhoon Haiyan in the Philippines.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/to-help-typhoon-survivors-go-local/', 'snippet': 'Guest blogger Mari Kuraishi urges readers to fund smaller scale, on the ground relief efforts in the wake of Typhoon Haiyan in the Philippines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two years ago I watched the footage of the earthquake and tsunami in Japan, willing myself not to start imagining what else was going on that I couldn’t see or read about. \xa0As a Japanese national living in the States, I was struck by the well-meaning experts who discouraged the public from donating to the relief efforts. \xa0Journalists questioned the logic of individuals giving to a wealthy country like Japan, and philanthropic advisors encouraged donors to give to organizations that could redirect funds to other more pressing needs outside of Japan after the initial relief effort. It was understandable, perhaps—the fog of disaster makes it hard to immediately know how much is “needed,” or what help is needed, even where.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'To Help Typhoon Survivors, Go Local', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T16:11:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mari Kuraishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mari', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kuraishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/baa5a007-6107-519e-995e-af82ff034193', 'word_count': 904, 'uri': 'nyt://article/baa5a007-6107-519e-995e-af82ff034193'}, {'abstract': 'The story of John Toffey, a Garden State soldier who won the Medal of Honor at Chattanooga.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/new-jerseys-mutinous-33rd/', 'snippet': 'The story of John Toffey, a Garden State soldier who won the Medal of Honor at Chattanooga.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Toffey was sick with fever. The Union lieutenant had been ill for days and not able to attend to his duties. An Army surgeon in Chattanooga, Tenn., examined the 19-year-old officer on the evening of Nov. 22, 1863, and handed him a permit to go into the hospital.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Jersey’s ‘Mutinous 33rd’', 'kicker': 'Disunion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civil War (US) (1861-65)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medal of Honor (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chattanooga (Tenn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T16:14:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronald S. Coddington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronald', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Coddington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b750924f-35cc-56c2-9728-932442fbe305', 'word_count': 1886, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b750924f-35cc-56c2-9728-932442fbe305'}, {'abstract': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/in-our-pages-november-27/', 'snippet': 'From The International Herald Tribune.', 'lead_paragraph': '1913: Oil Town Told to Surrender ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Our Pages: November 27', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War and Revolution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mexico', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T16:19:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d91c4c7-4f9f-5ea7-b32c-b8e608aee815', 'word_count': 211, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d91c4c7-4f9f-5ea7-b32c-b8e608aee815'}, {'abstract': 'Francis said women must play an increasingly important role in the church, but that letting women be priests was “not a question open to discussion.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/world/europe/in-major-document-pope-francis-present-his-vision.html', 'snippet': 'Francis said women must play an increasingly important role in the church, but that letting women be priests was “not a question open to discussion.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his first nine months as leader of one billion Roman Catholics, Pope Francis has parceled out glimpses of his vision for remaking the church — in homilies and news conferences, interviews and offhand remarks to visitors.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/world/POPE/POPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/world/POPE/POPE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/world/POPE/POPE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', '