neteen Hundred Sixties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hendrix, Jimi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Matthews, Dave', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Jeff', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Seal', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mellencamp, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T16:56:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Val Haller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Val', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06a68c4d-290d-545e-9c5e-730e6e08ed08', 'word_count': 305, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06a68c4d-290d-545e-9c5e-730e6e08ed08'}, {'abstract': 'For a dish rich in umami, you’ll need a wine that won’t wilt before it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/dining/a-well-aged-white-wine-to-cosset-miso-glazed-fish.html', 'snippet': 'For a dish rich in umami, you’ll need a wine that won’t wilt before it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is a dish rich in umami, and you need a wine that won’t wilt before it, preferably on the savory rather than fruity side. The ideal choice would be a well-aged white, like a 15-year-old grand cru Chablis, with just the right amount of richness and minerality to cosset the fish. Other options include a white Bordeaux from Pessac-Léognan or an older dry riesling with amplitude.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Well-Aged White Wine to Cosset Miso-Glazed Fish', 'kicker': 'And to Drink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Asimov, Eric', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T16:59:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Asimov', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Asimov', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1dcff8c-414a-5bad-bb9c-2970c8e8010b', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1dcff8c-414a-5bad-bb9c-2970c8e8010b'}, {'abstract': 'The publisher of the Grand Theft Auto game series agreed to buy Carl C. Icahn’s stake for $203.5 million. The sale also compelled the resignations of three board members he was allowed to appoint.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/take-two-interactive-software-buys-back-icahn-stake/', 'snippet': 'The publisher of the Grand Theft Auto game series agreed to buy Carl C. Icahn’s stake for $203.5 million. The sale also compelled the resignations of three board members he was allowed to appoint.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take-Two Interactive Software announced on Tuesday that it had bought back the stake held by Carl C. Icahn, compelling the resignations of three board members he was allowed to appoint.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/business/dbpix-icahn/dbpix-icahn-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/business/dbpix-icahn/dbpix-icahn-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/2