iginal': 'By Dwight Garner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dwight', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Garner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e1d277d4-d2cb-53f4-a8ad-070e024912c3', 'word_count': 1137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e1d277d4-d2cb-53f4-a8ad-070e024912c3'}, {'abstract': 'How did an $82,000-a-year tax inspector amass a fortune said to be about $8 million? Prosecutors offer an explanation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/world/americas/a-tale-of-love-taxes-and-bribery-entrances-brazil.html', 'snippet': 'How did an $82,000-a-year tax inspector amass a fortune said to be about $8 million? Prosecutors offer an explanation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — There were the boxes of Cuban cigars, which cost about $500 each at a shop in Vila Nova Conceição, one of the most exclusive districts of São Paulo, and the $2,260 bottles of Vega Sicilia Único, a legendary Spanish red. Throw in a Porsche Cayenne, speedboat jaunts to tropical islands and all-night soirees with high-end escorts, and what do you get?', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazil Is Entranced by a Tale of Love, Taxes and Bribery', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazil Is Entranced by a Tale Of Love, Taxes and Bribery', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bribery and Kickbacks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rio de Janeiro (Brazil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tax Evasion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sao Paulo (Brazil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T18:01:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/feab9662-c8d8-526b-a2be-2cef63be8344', 'word_count': 715, 'uri': 'nyt://article/feab9662-c8d8-526b-a2be-2cef63be8344'}, {'abstract': 'A break from fertility treatment is a chance to return to normal, but it’s hard to appreciate a phase of life you’re trying to leave behind.', 'web_url': 'https://parenting.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/taking-a-break-from-i-v-f/', 'snippet': 'A break from fertility treatment is a chance to return to normal, but it’s hard to appreciate a phase of life you’re trying to leave behind.', 'lead_paragraph': '“It’s all downhill from here.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/style/motherlode-bike-stroller/motherlode-bike-stroller-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/style/motherlode-bike-stroller/motherlode-bike-stroller-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/style/motherlode-bike-stroller/motherlode-bike-stroller-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/style/motherlode-bike-stroller/motherlode-bike-stroller-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1632, 'width': 1224, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':