gazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/now-screening-brought-to-you-by-kenneth-cole-an-inside-perspective-on-the-battle-against-aids/', 'snippet': 'The fashion designer produced the new HBO documentary “The Battle of AmfAR,” about Elizabeth Taylor and the physicist Mathilde Krim’s efforts to fight the disease by founding the global AIDS research nonprofit.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There is this pervasive sense out there that we have solved AIDS and that it’s not a crisis anymore,” says the designer Kenneth Cole, who is also chairman of the board of AmfAR, the Foundation for AIDS Research. “But AIDS is alive as it ever was. There are people living their lives recklessly and irresponsibly, and people need to understand that AIDS is still devastating, absent of a cure.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Now Screening | Brought to You by Kenneth Cole, an Inside Perspective on the Battle Against AIDS', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Now Screening: AmfAR Film', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cole, Kenneth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Taylor, Elizabeth (1932-2011)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T18:15:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Ortved', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ortved', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a163cc76-de5b-58f3-846d-d1f38c89885e', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a163cc76-de5b-58f3-846d-d1f38c89885e'}, {'abstract': 'In his first major piece of writing, Pope Francis called unfettered capitalism a “new tyranny.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/the-popes-take-on-capitalism/', 'snippet': 'In his first major piece of writing, Pope Francis called unfettered capitalism a “new tyranny.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the moment of his election, there have been signs that Pope Francis was going to be a very different sort of pontiff. It started with his decision to live in modest quarters instead of the palatial papal apartments, and continued with his tolerant comments about homosexuality and his complaint that the Roman Catholic Church had an unhealthy “obsession” with issues like abortion.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Pope’s Take on Capitalism', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dolan, Timothy M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Francis', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T18:16:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Rosenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenthal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b6ce38a-ab84-5e92-8414-1fe70b453f45', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b6ce38a-ab84-5e92-8414-1fe70b453f45'}, {'abstract': 'The typical result of these battles is a combination of the warring companies. The question is, who becomes the management and which set of shareholders, if any, receive a premium?', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/mens-wearhouse-dusts-off-the-pac-man-defense/', 'snippet': 'The typical result of these battles is a combination of the warring companies. The question is, who becomes the management and which set of shareholders, if any, receive a premium?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deal aficionados have a Thanksgiving present. Men’s Wearhouse has turned the tables on Jos. A. Bank Clothiers, offering to acquire the company, which had previously bid to acquire Men’s Wearhouse. What fun! ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/26/business/dealbook/dbpix-pacman/dbpix-pacman-thumbLa