ilian cuisine opened this spot in May, right next door to a restaurant that he has transformed over the past decade.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mocotó, José Oliveira de Almeida’s restaurant in the Vila Medeiros neighborhood of São Paulo, opened in 1974. Over the past decade, his son, Rodrigo Oliveira, has transformed the unassuming neighborhood restaurant and bar into one of the most famous in the country, making him one of the most recognizable faces in Brazilian cuisine. For years he has fought off offers to open another restaurant in the city’s wealthier southern districts. Instead, he opened Esquina Mocotó in May, right next door.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01-bites-span/01-bites-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01-bites-span/01-bites-span-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01-bites-span/01-bites-span-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01-bites-span/01-bites-span-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01-bites-span/01-bites-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01-bites-span/01-bites-span-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7