', 'word_count': 605, 'uri': 'nyt://article/486b2613-5540-5dfc-80f7-bccf6462f879'}, {'abstract': 'The Obama administration urged Iranian officials to help secure the release of a private investigator and former F.B.I. agent, Robert A. Levinson, who went missing in 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/an-unimaginable-milestone-for-an-american-hostage-in-iran/', 'snippet': 'The Obama administration urged Iranian officials to help secure the release of a private investigator and former F.B.I. agent, Robert A. Levinson, who went missing in 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the wake of its diplomatic success over Iran’s nuclear program, the Obama administration on Tuesday urged Iranian officials to help secure the release of a former F.B.I. agent who went missing in 2007 in Iran.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'An ‘Unimaginable Milestone’ for an American Hostage in Iran', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levinson, Robert A', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T20:06:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Barry Meier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Meier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a907fe41-a20a-5aef-93ea-35db3af8a6a0', 'word_count': 425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a907fe41-a20a-5aef-93ea-35db3af8a6a0'}, {'abstract': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'web_url': 'https://nocera.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/the-gun-report-november-26-2013/', 'snippet': 'A day in the life of armed America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Adam Lanza, the Newtown gunman, covered the windows in his room with black garbage bags. He changed his clothes multiple times a day and refused to eat unless his food was arranged in a special way on his plate. Though his bedroom was on the same floor as his mother’s in their Connecticut home, he only communicated with her by email, and he barred her from entering his room. He collected news clips about mass killings, including a couple from this newspaper. The only time he did bond with anyone else was when his mother took him shooting.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Gun Report: November 26, 2013', 'kicker': 'Joe Nocera', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T20:11:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Mascia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mascia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f716bdd-8f8d-51ee-9f12-6e6cddc89c33', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f716bdd-8f8d-51ee-9f12-6e6cddc89c33'}, {'abstract': 'The awards honoring more independent efforts in movies have some overlap with Oscar front-runners.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/12-years-a-slave-and-nebraska-lead-indie-spirit-awards/', 'snippet': 'The awards honoring more independent efforts in movies have some overlap with Oscar front-runners.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Film Independent Spirit Awards, which typically highlight non-blockbuster cinema, announced nominees on Tuesday. As usual, they include many films that are also on the path to the Academy Awards. The hopefuls for best feature include “12 Years a Slave,” “All Is Lost,” “Nebraska,” “Inside Llewyn Davis” and “Frances Ha.” ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 572, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1144, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/18/arts/18TWELVE_SPAN/18TWELVE_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘12 Years a Slave’ and ‘Nebraska’  Lead Indie Spirit Awards', 'kicker': 'ArtsBeat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indie Spirit Awards Announce Nominees', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blanchett, Cate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carruth, Shane'