, such pyrotechnics are extras best held in reserve and released sparingly. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27CALLAWAY/27CALLAWAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No Rain on Her Parade', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'No Rain On Her Parade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Callaway, Ann Hampton', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T22:16:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c43f68e-853a-5315-8999-c08763f3bfa0', 'word_count': 310, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c43f68e-853a-5315-8999-c08763f3bfa0'}, {'abstract': 'Demand at all of New York City’s food pantries and soup kitchens has spiked since federal food stamps were cut.', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/breadlines-return/', 'snippet': 'Demand at all of New York City’s food pantries and soup kitchens has spiked since federal food stamps were cut.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Great Recession was the worst downturn since the Great Depression. \xa0And yet, throughout the recent decline and today’s sluggish recovery, conditions have never seemed as bad as they were in the 1930s. Breadlines, for example, have not been commonplace.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Breadlines Return', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soup Kitchens', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Coalition Against Hunger', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-26T22:20:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teresa Tritch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teresa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tritch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ae0e2666-39b0-51e0-83c9-5560146d9272', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ae0e2666-39b0-51e0-83c9-5560146d9272'}, {'abstract': 'Juilliard String Quartet performed the New York Premiere of Jesse Jones’s “String Quartet No. 3” and works by Beethoven and Schubert at Lincoln Center.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/arts/music/juilliard-string-quartet-performs-at-alice-tully-hall.html', 'snippet': 'Juilliard String Quartet performed the New York Premiere of Jesse Jones’s “String Quartet No. 3” and works by Beethoven and Schubert at Lincoln Center.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Chemistry can be a fast process, but that seldom tends to be the case among musical ensembles, where the term also connotes the end result of that process: a state of grace formed among individuals bonded together as an aggregate. If at the start of a concert by the Juilliard String Quartet at Alice Tully Hall on Thursday night I was unsure that the vital transformation had occurred yet, by evening’s end I was convinced that it had begun in earnest.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/JUILLARD/JUILLARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/JUILLARD/JUILLARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/JUILLARD/JUILLARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/JUILLARD/JUILLARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 's