ruled that despite the contention of lawyers for Sulaiman Abu Ghaith, he had been read his rights before an F.B.I. interrogation and his statements had been voluntary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/nyregion/judge-says-statements-by-bin-ladens-son-in-law-can-be-used-in-terrorism-case.html', 'snippet': 'A judge ruled that despite the contention of lawyers for Sulaiman Abu Ghaith, he had been read his rights before an F.B.I. interrogation and his statements had been voluntary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A federal judge in Manhattan declined on Tuesday to suppress statements made to the authorities by a son-in-law of Osama bin Laden who is charged with conspiring to kill Americans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge Says Statements by Bin Laden’s Son-in-Law Can Be Used in Terrorism Case', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruling on Rights In Terrorism Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Miranda v Arizona (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abu Ghaith, Sulaiman', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T01:26:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14c0b1ca-0e49-5305-8159-b08191e13a34', 'word_count': 216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14c0b1ca-0e49-5305-8159-b08191e13a34'}, {'abstract': 'Wall Street has grown frustrated by low returns on other forms of debt and turned instead to riskier but more lucrative bets on ever-smaller companies.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/26/new-boom-in-subprime-loans-for-smaller-businesses/', 'snippet': 'Wall Street has grown frustrated by low returns on other forms of debt and turned instead to riskier but more lucrative bets on ever-smaller companies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A small, little-known company from Missouri borrows hundreds of millions of dollars from two of the biggest names in Wall Street finance. The loans are rated subprime. What’s more, they carry few of the standard protections seen in ordinary debt, making them particularly risky bets.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 574, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 574}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 979, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1958, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/business/CREDIT/CREDIT-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Boom in Subprime Loans, for Smaller Businesses', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Boom In Subprime Lending', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T01:26:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lynnley Browning', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lynnley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Browning', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa3bfd82-907e-50b9-a2e1-0ce37b37e695', 'word_count': 1329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa3bfd82-907e-50b9-a2e1-0ce37b37e695'}, {'abstract': 'The Supreme Court should protect women’s access to affordable contraception when it rules on two cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/opinion/another-challenge-to-the-health-care-law.html', 'snippet': 'The Supreme Court should protect women’s access to affordable contraception when it rules on two cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than a year after it upheld the constitutionality of the Affordable Care Act, the Supreme Court has set the stage for a showdown over the law’s requirement that employer health plans cover birth control. It agreed on Tuesday to hear two cases challenging the mandate, each brought by a secular, profit-making company seeking an exemption on religious grounds. They are among a slew of lawsuits seeking similar exemptions. Lower federal appellate courts have split on the question, creating a need for a decisive ruling from the Supreme Court that rejects the specious religious liberty claims.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Another Challenge to the Health Care Law', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Another Challenge to the Health Care Law', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corporations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T01:28:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/e922a36e-9470-593b-b2b5-491f440037d2', 'word_count': 413, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e922a36e-9470-593b-b2b5-491f440037d2'}, {'abstract': 'In the suit by 10 former N.H.L. players against the league for negligence and fraud, both sides will probably draw lessons from the N.F.L.’s concussion cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/sports/hockey/nfl-concussion-case-offers-clues-for-hockey-lawsuit.html', 'snippet': 'In the suit by 10 former N.H.L. players against the league for negligence and fraud, both sides will probably draw lessons from the N.F.L.’s concussion cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the N.F.L. agreed in August to pay $765 million to settle a lawsuit filed by thousands of retirees who said that the league had failed to disclose the dangers of repeated head trauma, it largely ended one legal challenge and invited others.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimed