for two to four inches of rain by Thursday morning, and sewer workers will be scooping out tons of street sludge from basins across New York City.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/nyregion/enjoy-the-parade-and-dont-forget-to-thank-your-friendly-sewer-workers.html', 'snippet': 'Forecasts are calling for two to four inches of rain by Thursday morning, and sewer workers will be scooping out tons of street sludge from basins across New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': 'By midmorning Tuesday, the sewer workers had taken apart five catch basins along Central Park West near the American Museum of Natural History. Then they scooped out street sludge that had been trapped in a kind of holding vault, where it had steeped for two or three years in about four feet of water. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Enjoy the Parade, and Don’t Forget to Thank Your Friendly Sewer Workers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Enjoy the Parade, and Don’t Forget to Thank Your Friendly Sewer Workers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dwyer, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sewers and Sewage', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rain', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Central Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T01:56:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Dwyer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2ab2