ctice is so widespread it has spawned a multibillion-dollar industry of private tutorial colleges that help students cram for highly competitive high-school and university entrance exams. Nearly 1.3 million children in Turkey are enrolled in more than 3,800 tutorial colleges.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Shadow Politics of Shadow Education', 'kicker': 'Latitude', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADMISSIONS STANDARDS', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gulen, Fethullah', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T12:42:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Finkel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finkel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d9159dc-4d68-5b3b-bab7-b739cf69c7d1', 'word_count': 497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d9159dc-4d68-5b3b-bab7-b739cf69c7d1'}, {'abstract': 'Elizabeth Shown Mills, a genealogist and historical writer, discusses hurdles in American frontier searches, identifying immigrant origins and other issues related to genealogy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/booming/advice-on-how-to-research-family-history-part-4.html', 'snippet': 'Elizabeth Shown Mills, a genealogist and historical writer, discusses hurdles in American frontier searches, identifying immigrant origins and other issues related to genealogy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here is the fourth and final set of answers from Elizabeth Shown Mills, a genealogist and historical writer who has been responding to readers’ questions about how to research family history using online sources, physical public records and the stories and DNA of living family members. Part one of her answers is here. Part 2 is here. Part 3 is here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/30/booming/30expertquery-booming-genealogy/30expertquery-booming-genealogy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/10/30/booming/30expertquery-booming-genealogy/30expertquery-booming-genealogy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/30/booming/30expertquery-booming-genealogy/30expertquery-booming-genealogy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/30/booming/30expertquery-booming-genealogy/30expertquery-booming-genealogy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 625, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/10/30/booming/30expertquery-booming-genealogy/30expertquery-booming-genealogy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/10/30/booming/30expertquery-booming-genealogy/30expertquery-booming-genealogy-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight':