to the top military command ended months of speculation about the successor to Gen. Ashfaq Parvez Kayani.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISLAMABAD, Pakistan — In the most crucial appointment of his new term, Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif on Wednesday chose a relative outsider, Lt. Gen. Raheel Sharif, to lead Pakistan’s powerful army.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 842, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 842}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 730, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1460, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/28pakistan/28pakistan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Flexing Autonomy, Pakistani Premier Picks Outsider to Lead Army', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Flexing Autonomy, Pakistani Premier Picks Outsider to Lead Army', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kayani, Ashfaq Parvez', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Taliban', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T13:08:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Salman Masood and Declan Walsh', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Declan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walsh', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a70f978-6ff1-5c42-bb9b-a8304e80bb26', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a70f978-6ff1-5c42-bb9b-a8304e80bb26'}, {'abstract': 'A loan package to a little-known company highlights a new credit boom taking shape. | Business development companies are suddenly hot, but they come with risks. | A former analyst at SAC Capital Advisors agreed to testify against his onetime boss in a bid to avoid jail time. | Men’s Wearhouse turned the tables on Jos. A. Bank.', 'web_url': 'https://dealbook.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/morning-agenda-a-new-credit-boom/', 'snippet': 'A loan package to a little-known company highlights a new credit boom taking shape. | Business development companies are suddenly hot, but they come with risks. | A former analyst at SAC Capital Advisors agreed to testify against his onetime boss ...', 'lead_paragraph': 'A $330 million loan package to a small, little-known company from Missouri highlights how a new credit boom is taking shape, five years after the bubble, Lynnley Browning reports in DealBook. The company, Learfield Communications, of Jefferson City, Mo., owns multimedia rights to more than four dozen college sports programs and made just under $40 million last year in a common measure of earnings. It borrowed the money from Deutsche Bank and GE Capital on Oct. 9. Though the loans were rated subprime, with few of the standard protections seen in ordinary debt, investors clamored to buy pieces of the loans, one of which pays annual interest of at least 8.75 percent.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Credit Boom', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T13:09:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By William Alden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/387acfb5-781a-5119-b88f-62b4a538c3d5', 'word_count': 2035, 'uri': 'nyt://article/387acfb5-781a-5119-b88f-62b4a538c3d5'}, {'abstract': 'Cylone Lehar, the second big storm in a week to threaten the state, is expected to make landfall late Thursday afternoon.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/andhra-pradesh-set-to-evacuate-250000-people-as-cyclone-lehar-nears-coast/', 'snippet': 'Cylone Lehar, the second big storm in a week to threaten the state, is expected to make landfall late Thursday afternoon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HYDERABAD, Andhra Pradesh – The National Disaster Management Authority is planning to begin evacuations of at least 250,000 people in Andhra Pradesh as early as We