for the busy shopper.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/fashion/shopping-for-fall-fashion-dont-fear-the-dark.html', 'snippet': 'Midnight blue is the coolest color for boots; Warby Parker’s Leith Clark eyewear; Jayne Min and Jennifer Fisher design jewelry; and an app for the busy shopper.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to boots this season, midnight blue is the coolest color. You can wear them pretty much interchangeably with your beloved black. Pair with bluejeans, various warm layers or, perhaps, a smart gray coat for a casually refined look. To dress up, slip them on with a black skirt (or even black leather pants) and a white blouse. The blue will prove unexpected and polished. Just dare to try.', 'print_section': 'E', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/fashion/28BROWSING1_SPAN-copy/28zBROWSING4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Shopping for Fall Fashion? Don’t Fear the Dark', 'kicker': 'Browsing', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Fear the Dark', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Warby Parker', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fisher, Jennifer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Min, Jayne', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Leith', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T16:27:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Erica M. Blumenthal', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Erica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/78715819-eb01-5dec-a0f8-71b102ee725e', 'word_count': 479, 'uri': 'nyt://article/78715819-eb01-5dec-a0f8-71b102ee725e'}, {'abstract': 'Frances McDormand takes to the intimate Fishman Space at the Brooklyn Academy of Music to portray Suzanne Bocanegra giving a lecture in “Bodycast.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/theater/youre-here-to-be-lectured.html', 'snippet': 'Frances McDormand takes to the intimate Fishman Space at the Brooklyn Academy of Music to portray Suzanne Bocanegra giving a lecture in “Bodycast.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the context of the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Next Wave Festival, which scours the globe for cutting-edge performances, the presence of an Oscar winner qualifies as exotica. But this week, Frances McDormand, who won Hollywood’s big prize for “Fargo,” takes to the intimate Fishman Space stage to portray Suzanne Bocanegra giving a lecture in “Bodycast.” Ms. Bocanegra’s works range across mediums: she paints, creates large-scale installations and orchestrates complex interdisciplinary events, often involving other artists. Paul Lazar, who directs “Bodycast,” portrayed Ms. Bocanegra giving a lecture in Ms. Bocanegra’s “When a Priest Marries a Witch,” to which “Bodycast” is a quasi-sequel. In the new piece, which includes guest appearances by the singer Theo Bleckmann and the dancer Emily Coates, Ms. Bocanegra reflects (in the person of Ms. McDormand) on evolving ideals of female beauty, among other topics, as refracted through her experience of wearing a body cast for two years in her teens to correct her scoliosis. (Opens Tuesday, Fisher Building, 321 Ashman Place, near Lafayette Avenue, Fort Greene; bam.org.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01GUIDE4/01GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01GUIDE4/01GUIDE4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01GUIDE4/01GUIDE4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 652, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'ur