6-04d25ca45895', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/9ae36ed7-8caa-5620-9196-04d25ca45895'}, {'abstract': 'The manuscript, said to date from 1974, includes 30 lines in Mr. Springsteen’s handwriting, neatly written in blue ink, but with second thoughts added in the margins and in the space above some of the lyrics.', 'web_url': 'https://artsbeat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/springsteens-handwritten-born-to-run-lyrics-head-to-auction/', 'snippet': 'The manuscript, said to date from 1974, includes 30 lines in Mr. Springsteen’s handwriting, neatly written in blue ink, but with second thoughts added in the margins and in the space above some of the lyrics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The lyrics to “Born to Run,” the evocative title track of Bruce Springsteen’s third album, from 1975, seem to roll off Mr. Springsteen’s tongue on the recording, a torrent of inspired urban car-culture imagery. But a page torn from a spiral-bound notebook that once belonged to Mr. Springsteen, which is currently up for auction at Sotheby’s, shows that it was a long road from Mr. Springsteen’s early thoughts about the song to its finished version.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27artsbeat-springsteen/27artsbeat-sprinsteen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27artsbeat-springsteen/27artsbeat-sprinsteen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 772}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27artsbeat-springsteen/27artsbeat-sprinsteen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 797, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/27/arts/27artsbeat-springsteen/27artsbeat-