ars because of a contract dispute with his former club, and whose case shined a light on the emirate’s labor laws, has been told he can return home.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 793}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 775, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1075, 'width': 813, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/28belounis/28belounis-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Qatar Lets Soccer Player Leave After Two Years', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Qatar Lets Soccer Player Leave After Two Years', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Cup 2022 (Soccer)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Montague, James', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Federation of Association Football (FIFA)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blatter, Sepp', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Qatar', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T17:43:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Montague', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Montague', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/05c0febd-01fc-5175-80b4-24af83f37c5c', 'word_count': 985, 'uri': 'nyt://article/05c0febd-01fc-5175-80b4-24af83f37c5c'}, {'abstract': 'On J.F.K., “Brave New World,” and the perils of seeking political solutions to cultural and moral stagnation.', 'web_url': 'https://douthat.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/the-perils-of-anti-decadence/', 'snippet': 'On J.F.K., “Brave New World,” and the perils of seeking political solutions to cultural and moral stagnation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My Sunday column tried to draw a serious point out of the coincidence of Aldous Huxley, C.S. Lewis and John F. Kennedy all entering the hereafter within a few hours of each other, portraying the resilience of the Kennedy mythos as, in part, a kind of secular/liberal rebellion against the same disenchanted utilitarian materialism that both Huxley and Lewis famously critiqued. This is a reason, I wrote, for even J.F.K. skeptics like myself to feel a little sympathy for the cult of Camelot\xa0— because it speaks to a deep and admirable human desire\xa0“for grace and beauty, for icons and heroes, for a high-stakes dimension to human affairs that a consumerist, materialist civilization can flatten and exclude.” The\xa0various things that J.F.K.’s admirers cite when they praise the man and his administration — the physical vigor and the soaring rhetoric, the patronage of high culture and the man-on-the-moon technological ambition, the Cuban Missile Crisis drama and the founding of the Peace Corps\xa0 — might not match up to a reality that was much more personally sleazy, culturally incurious and geopolitically reckless. But better a slightly bogus “vigah” than a society that deliberately cultivates what Lewis termed “men without chests.” Better a gap between self-sacrificial aspirations and grubbier realities than a society like Huxley’s “Brave New World” that excludes any dreams higher than comfort and consumption.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of Anti-Decadence', 'kicker': 'Ross Douthat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huxley, Aldous', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, John Fitzgerald', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewis, C S', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Peace Corps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T17:44:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ross Douthat', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ross', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Douthat', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fed4ed33-2858-5951-bc64-1e0a06a9299c', 'word_count': 1437, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fed4ed33-2858-5951-bc64-1e0a06a9299c'}, {'abstract': 'A paper written by two Israeli computer scientists linked a Bitcoin account to a transaction on Silk Road, an Internet black market. But the owner of that account, who is not the still-anonymous creator of Bitcoin, has come forward.', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/researchers-retract-report-that-linked-bitcoin-creator-and-silk-road/', 'snippet': 'A paper written by two Israeli computer scientists linked a Bitcoin account to a transaction on Silk Road, an Internet black market. But the owner of that account, who is not the still-anonymous creator of Bitcoin, has come forward.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two Israeli computer scientists who over the weekend published a paper describing a financial connection between the Bitcoin peer-to-peer transaction system and the operator of Silk Road, an Internet black market, have backed away from the claim after an independent security researcher took responsibility for the puzzling account that generated the transfer.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Researchers Retract Report That Linked Bitcoin Creator and Silk Road', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bitcoin (Currency)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Markets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dratel, Joshua L', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ron, Dorit', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shamir, Adi', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ulbricht, Ross William', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T17:45:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Markoff', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Markoff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None,