b09708'}, {'abstract': 'This month’s books include the reissue of a classic novel by John Rechy, stories by Laura van den Berg and a biography of Richard Pryor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/books/laura-van-den-bergs-isle-of-youth-and-more.html', 'snippet': 'This month’s books include the reissue of a classic novel by John Rechy, stories by Laura van den Berg and a biography of Richard Pryor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This month, fiction with grim edges, including a hustler’s lonely life, a possible assassination in Mexico City, women emotionally adrift and a murderer on the run. Also, a look at Richard Pryor’s career and a literary miscellany.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/newly2/newly2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 394, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/newly2/newly2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 394, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/newly2/newly2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/newly2/newly2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/newly2/newly2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Newly Released Books', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Newly Released', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van den Berg, Laura', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, Joe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver, Katherine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pryor, Richard', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rechy, John', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernal, Rafael', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Henry, David', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lynch, Paul', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nissley, Tom', 'rank': 17, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T19:17:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/524a404f-bbc9-596d-b45b-339c4c0385dc', 'word_count': 978, 'uri': 'nyt://article/524a404f-bbc9-596d-b45b-339c4c0385dc'}, {'abstract': 'Conor McPherson’s “The Night Alive” opens at the Atlantic Theater Company in a production he directed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/theater/conor-mcpherson-prepares-the-night-alive.html', 'snippet': 'Conor McPherson’s “The Night Alive” opens at the Atlantic Theater Company in a production he directed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 20 years, Conor McPherson ended most of his plays with a faint hope of salvation — for the lonely souls in “The Weir,” the therapist and patient in “Shining City,” and the Everyman alcoholic in “The Seafarer,” to name his three works that had critically acclaimed runs on Broadway. But his latest play, “The Night Alive,” tops them. Mr. McPherson, one of Ireland’s greatest living playwrights, has gone all in to render a powerful moment of redemption in the final scene — sure to be one of the most debated of the New York theater season, given that it leaves much room for interpretation. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/arts/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN/01MCPHERSON2_SPAN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hope Doesn’t Come Out of a Bottle', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hope Doesn’t C