{'abstract': 'The recently opened Sense Hotel brings a splash of contemporary luxury to the appealingly low-key metropolis of Sofia. Plus: four can’t-miss destinations while staying there.', 'web_url': 'https://tmagazine.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/accommodations-in-bulgarias-charming-old-world-capital-a-modern-oasis/', 'snippet': 'The recently opened Sense Hotel brings a splash of contemporary luxury to the appealingly low-key metropolis of Sofia. Plus: four can’t-miss destinations while staying there.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Until the beautifully designed 71-room Sense Hotel opened in June, luxury in Sofia, the handsome capital of Bulgaria, was often more defined by what the Balkan city doesn’t have than what it does — which is a lot of character and un-self-conscious charm. Despite a population of 1.2 million, the city has none of the stress-tinged, work-centric rhythms found in most European capitals, existing instead in a gentle post-Ottoman twilight, its leafy neighborhoods still full of small cafes, bars and taverns. The arrival of Starbucks hasn’t completely sidelined the local preference for Turkish coffee and the city’s old market — where kerchiefed farm wives sell their pickles in recycled jars and there is an abundant supply of the delicious cheese-filled phyllo pastries known as banitsa — is still busy, despite the big supermarkets opening on the outskirts of town.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Bulgaria’s Charming Old-World Capital, a Modern Oasis', 'kicker': 'T Magazine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T20:20:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Lobrano', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lobrano', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'orga