By Barbara Pollack', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Barbara', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pollack', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14440766-7f99-5f75-90a8-accd54bffade', 'word_count': 1223, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14440766-7f99-5f75-90a8-accd54bffade'}, {'abstract': 'One Direction’s new album has a blankness that perhaps is a strategy: Testing how little is needed to keep a pop phenomenon moving.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/arts/music/one-direction-releases-a-new-album-midnight-memories.html', 'snippet': 'One Direction’s new album has a blankness that perhaps is a strategy: Testing how little is needed to keep a pop phenomenon moving.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the current issue of Billboard, at the end of the cover feature on One Direction, there is a cooling mist of reality spritzed by, who else, Simon Cowell, the TV judge-impresario who helped Frankenstein this group into existence on the 2010 season of the British version of “The X Factor.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 327, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 327}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 558, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/arts/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION/SUB-28ONEDIRECTION-super