own river to explore. What falls there are, we know not; what rocks beset the channel, we know not; what walls ride over the river, we know not. Ah, well! we may conjecture many things.’’\u2009 — John Wesley Powell', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 743, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 929, 'width': 1280, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-grotzinger/28tp-grotzinger-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The World of Mars', 'kicker': 'Turning Points | Exploration', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mars (Planet)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Curiosity (Mars Rover)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Aeronautics and Space Administration', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T20:39:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Grotzinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Grotzinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Special Report', '_id': 'nyt://article/7d25e0e0-9fb3-5564-941c-3f392d3274d7', 'word_count': 1699, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7d25e0e0-9fb3-5564-941c-3f392d3274d7'}, {'abstract': 'I have experienced exile from both perspectives: that of those who leave, and of those who say goodbye. Both are terribly emotional and sobering.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/opinion/leaving-home-coming-home.html', 'snippet': 'I have experienced exile from both perspectives: that of those who leave, and of those who say goodbye. Both are terribly emotional and sobering.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Organizing one’s address book is always a thankless task. Every year, from my home in Havana, I attack the job of reviewing, page by page, all the names and data that make up my network of personal and professional relationships. Like a tapestry in which I am barely one strand, I review every thread that remains and each thread that was lost. And I find myself facing the alarming evidence of how many people I must subtract.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28TP-gottardo/28TP-gottardo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1134, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/1