1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Special Report', '_id': 'nyt://article/acaf62cb-e3dc-516e-94dc-77525b920b65', 'word_count': 1287, 'uri': 'nyt://article/acaf62cb-e3dc-516e-94dc-77525b920b65'}, {'abstract': 'How we manage the balance between conventional energy sources – oil, natural gas and coal – and renewables will shape our future.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/opinion/power-in-2030-the-roads-we-may-take.html', 'snippet': 'How we manage the balance between conventional energy sources – oil, natural gas and coal – and renewables will shape our future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There is no question that we are at a turning point in world energy. But then we are often at a turning point. Just as everybody gets comfortable with what they expect to happen, a big change comes along that undercuts existing assumptions. Just consider:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-yergin/28tp-yergin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 335, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-yergin/28tp-yergin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 335}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-yergin/28tp-yergin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 571, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-yergin/28tp-yergin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1143, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/opinion/28tp-yergin/28tp-yergin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thum