ime for the store’s opening party. They’ve still only stocked about two-thirds of their complete inventory, according to Stephen Godfroy, one of the owners.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Long Does It Take to Shelve 23,000 Albums?', 'kicker': 'The 6th Floor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Grant, John', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rough Trade NYC', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Williamsburg (Brooklyn, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T21:17:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Kellner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kellner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b67107d-c4a1-59aa-bcdf-f9ed4e2c34f1', 'word_count': 93, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b67107d-c4a1-59aa-bcdf-f9ed4e2c34f1'}, {'abstract': 'Acts of heroism abound in the Philippines after Typhoon Haiyan, often with a special emphasis on ensuring the survival of children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/world/asia/orphans-friends-and-neighbors-struggle-to-endure-in-typhoons-wake.html', 'snippet': 'Acts of heroism abound in the Philippines after Typhoon Haiyan, often with a special emphasis on ensuring the survival of children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TACLOBAN, the Philippines — Jomar Pascual stirred a steel pot full of instant noodles carefully in a typhoon-damaged former kindergarten building. He had already cooked rice. His three younger brothers and a younger sister, suddenly orphans like him, were hungry, and he began to feed them, spooning the pallid meal onto their green plastic plates.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source':