'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/10afb12e-1304-5d78-8323-91af0e6584fb', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/10afb12e-1304-5d78-8323-91af0e6584fb'}, {'abstract': 'When a “Make Love” Gap ad featuring a Sikh man was defaced, a photographer shared the image online and the company reached out to pinpoint its location. The ad was later removed.', 'web_url': 'https://thelede.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/a-defaced-gap-ad-goes-from-the-subway-to-the-web-to-its-demise/', 'snippet': 'When a “Make Love” Gap ad featuring a Sikh man was defaced, a photographer shared the image online and the company reached out to pinpoint its location. The ad was later removed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the New York City-based photographer Robert Gerhardt waited last Sunday for the No. 6 subway train to take him from the Bronx to Manhattan, he spotted a poster from Gap’s “Make Love” ad campaign. It featured a female model and a man wearing the distinctive turban of the Sikh religion. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Defaced Gap Ad Goes From the Subway to the Web to Its Demise', 'kicker': 'The Lede', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-27T22:02:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Blogs', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Hauser', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hauser', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/432e7eac-6808-569d-9e28-5e7ff5248ee7', 'word_count': 388, 'uri': 'nyt://article/432e7eac-6808-569d-9e28-5e7ff5248ee7'}, {'abstract': 'Great Wall Restaurant offers chicken feet and tripe among their more standard Sichuan and Cantonese fare, with dim sum on the weekends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/nyregion/a-review-of-great-wall-restaurant-in-new-haven.html', 'snippet': 'Great Wall Restaurant offers chicken feet and tripe among their more standard Sichuan and Cantonese fare, with dim sum on the weekends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A friend of mine advised caution when I told him I was visiting Great Wall Restaurant in New Haven, noting the tripe and chicken feet on the menu. In fact, both are delicious, but the restaurant also offers pages of less adventuresome options. ', 'print_section': 'CT', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01DINECT3/01DINECT3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 455, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01DINECT3/01DINECT3-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 455}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01DINECT3/01DINECT3-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 776, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01DINECT3/01DINECT3-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1552, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01DINECT3/01DINECT3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01DINECT3/01DINECT3-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/