tes this week, has thrown a broader spotlight on the control of international airspace, an issue that has created confusion, and danger, in other places affected by territorial disputes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Move Puts Airspace in Spotlight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Move Puts Airspace In Spotlight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'East China Sea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Senkaku Islands', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T02:28:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone and Matthew L. Wald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Wald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ab270fe7-ef76-5e33-9181-aa1427e9034c', 'word_count': 695, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ab270fe7-ef76-5e33-9181-aa1427e9034c'}, {'abstract': 'The Carbon Power Plant, the state’s oldest coal-fired power plant, is set to close by April 2015, a result of new stricter federal pollution regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2013/11/27/us/27COAL.html