he old dictatorship of Hosni Mubarak without Mr. Mubarak. In the name of crushing all resistance by the Muslim Brotherhood supporters of Mohamed Morsi, the democratically elected president ousted by the military in July, Egyptian authorities have now moved to ban most public protests and threaten those who take part in them with jail or heavy fines. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Silencing Dissent in Egypt', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Silencing Dissent in Egypt', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sisi, Abdul-Fattah el-', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T02:41:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/638692d7-edc0-5aa6-ace0-c9c8d1d88784', 'word_count': 509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/638692d7-edc0-5aa6-ace0-c9c8d1d88784'}, {'abstract': 'Doubling the number of people who get antiviral treatments by the end of 2016 would slow the epidemic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/opinion/more-money-to-treat-aids-abroad.html', 'snippet': 'Doubling the number of people who get antiviral treatments by the end of 2016 would slow the epidemic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At a time when partisan bickering has crippled Congress, it is encouraging to find agreement on the important issue of curbing the global AIDS epidemic. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'More Money to Treat AIDS Abroad', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'More Money to Treat AIDS Abroad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Coburn, Tom', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, Barbara', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T02:44:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/34ba1676-7262-553f-b9f6-4b9ea7236e53', 'word_count': 399, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34ba1676-7262-553f-b9f6-4b9ea7236e53'}, {'abstract': 'New York City officials should make a ban on foam containers and loose packaging happen as soon as possible.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/opinion/the-perils-of-polystyrene.html', 'snippet': 'New York City officials should make a ban on foam containers and loose packaging happen as soon as possible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Every year New York City residents throw away about 20,000 tons of plastic foam containers or, worse, the peanut-shaped packaging filler that sticks to anything in its path. Polystyrene foam is a plague on the environment. It is brittle. It breaks into pieces — sometimes very tiny pieces — that are devilishly hard to pick up. And there is no easy or cheap way to recycle it. New York City officials are considering a ban on foam containers and loose packaging. They should make it happen as soon as possible. Earlier this year the City Council speaker, Christine Quinn, made a pointed case for banning the substance. “It lives forever,” she said. “It’s worse than cockroaches.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Perils of Polystyrene', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Perils of Polystyrene', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Containers and Packaging', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T02:46:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/41f06d00-6336-57cf-9b32-872dadc64f92', 'word_count': 328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41f06d00-6336-57cf-9b32-872dadc64f92'}, {'abstract': 'Even though we rarely ask outright “what are you thankful for?” on Thanksgiving anymore, the question hovers over the holiday, awaiting an answer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/opinion/room-at-the-table.html', 'snippet': 'Even though we rarely ask outright “what are you thankful for?” on Thanksgiving anymore, the question hovers over the holiday, awaiting an answer.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There may be a stranger at dinner today — the friend of a friend, the brother of a daughter’s roommate, a business acquaintance stuck in town, someone who reminds us how expandable this close-knit holiday really is. And there will surely be someone missing for whom we keep a place set in our thoughts. On Thanksgiving Day, we sit down with the memory of everyone who has shared this holiday with us, and perhaps with an unexpected stranger, the person who helps us tell this one Thanksgiving apart from all the others.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Room at the Table', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Room at the Table', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T02:48:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/01f78034-3f15-59e4-bb77-9bed4de159f5', 'word_count': 362, 'uri': 'nyt://article/01f78034-3f15-59e4-bb77-9bed4de159f5'}, {'abstract': 'In Detroit, the tradition of football on Thanksgiving is deeply personal. The Lions have hosted the holiday games since 1934. But for the past decade, a new tradition has taken root: losing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/sports/football/for-lions-fans-a-bittersweet-thanksgiving-holiday.html', 'snippet': 'In Detroit, the tradition of football on Thanksgiving is deeply personal. The Lions have hosted the holiday games since 1934. But for the past decade, a new tradition has taken root: losing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DETROIT — On Thanksgiving Day, Darin Idyle will be tailgating in a church parking lot, as he has every Thanksgiving for about a decade. Tim Harry will be bonding in Ford Field’s stands with his teenage son. And M. G. Shapiro’s family knows that his overtime rule is in effect once again — a tie score means he will be late for Thanksgiving dinner.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/LIONS2/LIONS2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'During Lions Games, Giving Thanks While Gnashing Teeth', 'kicker': None, 'content_