_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Vitello', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vitello', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/928383df-9229-5078-ae37-b1bf48ffb4dd', 'word_count': 563, 'uri': 'nyt://article/928383df-9229-5078-ae37-b1bf48ffb4dd'}, {'abstract': 'A debut by Loren Muse Smith and the return of the nefarious Jeff Chen.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/27/cult-classic/', 'snippet': 'A debut by Loren Muse Smith and the return of the nefarious Jeff Chen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THURSDAY’S PUZZLE — This puzzle by Loren Muse Smith (who is making her New York Times debut today) and Jeff Chen is very clever. Even if you’re easily “squicked” out by SNAKES, you’re going to like this one. And there are two different ways to look at this answer, as it turns out. I’ll talk about how my noncaffeinated brain looked at it first.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Cult Classic', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T03:00:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/92190941-735e-5c90-81cf-7f7a8a360d15', 'word_count': 958, 'uri': 'nyt://article/92190941-735e-5c90-81cf-7f7a8a360d15'}, {'abstract': 'Competition between established French companies and outside mushroom pickers has brought with it darker undercurrents of hostility and discrimination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/world/europe/mystery-of-missing-mushrooms-leaves-french-blaming-roma.html', 'snippet': 'Competition between established French companies and outside mushroom pickers has brought with it darker undercurrents of hostility and discrimination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — Guy Sant is distressed about the sorry state of his mushroom business this year. Usually in the autumn, when the weather turns brisk and the leaves begin to fall, his pickers gather 60 tons of wild fungi to satisfy European consumers, he said. This fall, they found only 16 tons. “I lost so much this year, I may have to close,” he said bleakly.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/europe/28mushroom_1/28mushroom_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/world/europe/28mushroom_1/28mushroom_1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/europe/28mushroom_1/28mushroom_1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/europe/28mushroom_1/28mushroom_1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/europe/28mushroom_1/28mushroom_1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/