explanation:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Chinese-Pakistani Nuclear Deal', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chinese Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Energy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Nonproliferation Treaty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sharif, Nawaz', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Endowment for International Peace', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Energy Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'German Marshall Fund of the United States', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nuclear Suppliers Group', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Karachi (Pakistan)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T04:28:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chris Buckley', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Buckley', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47aa358c-ba06-5cf9-822f-8ccf8c5b193c', 'word_count': 920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47aa358c-ba06-5cf9-822f-8ccf8c5b193c'}, {'abstract': 'President Uhuru Kenyatta of Kenya and his deputy, William Ruto, have pleaded not guilty to charges that they were responsible for deadly violence after the 2007 elections.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/world/europe/the-hague-eased-rules-may-affect-trials-of-2-kenyans.html', 'snippet': 'President Uhuru Kenyatta of Kenya and his deputy, William Ruto, have pleaded not guilty to charges that they were responsible for deadly violence after the 2007 elections.', 'lead_paragraph': ' Member states of the International Criminal Court eased the trial rules on Wednesday in ways that could enable Kenya’s two top leaders, facing prosecution on charges that include crimes against humanity, to avoid personal appearances and even miss parts of the proceedings against them, news agencies reported. The changes, which apply to suspects who hold high office, had been strongly advocated by Kenya and other African members that have criticized what they call the court’s unfair focus on prosecuting African political figures. President Uhuru Kenyatta of Kenya and his deputy, William Ruto, have pleaded not guilty to charges that they were responsible for deadly violence after the 2007 elections. They have also asserted that the trials interfere with their ability to govern Kenya. Mr. Ruto’s trial has begun, and Mr. Kenyatta’s is scheduled to begin in February. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Hague: Eased Rules May Affect Trials of 2 Kenyans', 'kicker': 'World Briefing | Europe', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Hague: Eased Rules May Affect Trials of 2 Kenyans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Criminal Court', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ruto, William', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenyatta, Uhuru Muigai', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kenya', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T04:50:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/9222259f-5431-5c49-8b3a-59c42bba6177', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9222259f-5431-5c49-8b3a-59c42bba6177'}, {'abstract': 'Nineteenth-century wardrobe staples are enjoying a streamlined, contemporary renaissance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/t-magazine/victorian-style-makes-a-comeback.html', 'snippet': 'Nineteenth-century wardrobe staples are enjoying a streamlined, contemporary renaissance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Victorian aesthetic — high collars, leg-o-mutton sleeves, pearl trim — is having a renaissance. In the modern interpretation, minimalism is key and military references abound. Metallics are often paired with black so that they pop — as in the oversize brass buttons on a slim Balmain topcoat; the gold hardware on a simple Dolce & Gabbana bag and a Givenchy belt; and the trim around a dainty Phoebe Coleman lacquered pinkie ring. The ornate decoration of a simple Erdem skirt and round Monica Rich Kosann earrings are the essence of restrained elegance. Lace-up booties by Tabitha Simmons and a crown-shaped pendant necklace by Katie Mullally offer especially Anglophilic takes on the trend.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 778}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 790, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1167, 'width': 900, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/t-magazine/28market-barsamian/28market-barsamian-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Victorian Style Makes a Comeback', 'kicker': 'Market Report', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T05:00:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TCulture', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Barsamian', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barsamian', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bc3b4ba3-ec49-5cac-abac-d0f2a88eb850', 'word_count': 113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bc3b4ba3-ec49-5cac-abac-d0f2a88eb850'}, {'abstract': 'The police said they were investigating the deaths, including those of two women who were struck by a single vehicle as they crossed a street on Staten Island.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/nyregion/4-hit-and-killed-by-cars-in-new-york-city.html', 'snippet': 'The police said they were investigating the deaths, including those of two women who were struck by a single vehicle as they crossed a street on Staten Island.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Four people were hit by cars and killed across the city on Wednesday, including two women who were hit by a single vehicle while crossing the street on Staten Island, the police said. The circumstances of each of the crashes were still under investigation as of midnight on Thursday. No one was immediately charged with a crime.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '4 Hit and Killed by Cars in New York City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Fatalities)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Staten Island (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T05:37:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Schwirtz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwirtz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76982c5-26f1-57e2-a655-e1ec1ca3dec6', 'word_count': 221, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76982c5-26f1-57e2-a655-e1ec1ca3dec6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/arts/television/whats-on-thursday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 A.M. (NBC) MACY’S THANKSGIVING DAY PARADE Matt Lauer, Al Roker and Savannah Guthrie host this 87th installment of the parade, with appearances by the Big Apple Circus; Kristin Chenoweth; the Cherokee National Youth Choir; Cirque du Soleil, Gavin DeGraw; Brett Eldredge; Fall Out Boy; Jimmy Fallon; Kellie Pickler; the Roots with the cast of “Sesame Street”; Florida Georgia Line; Megan Hilty; Joan Jett and the Blackhearts; Sharon Jones and the Dap-Kings; Miss America 2014, Nina Davuluri; the retired N.F.L. players Bart Oates, Amani Toomer and Hines Ward; the retired N.H.L. players Cam Neely and Mike Richter; the Robertson family from “Duck Dynasty”; and the Radio City Rockettes. The casts of the Broadway shows “Matilda” and “Motown: The Musical” perform. So does Carrie Underwood, in her role as Maria in “The Sound of Music Live!,” next Thursday on NBC. Soaring above it all, weather permitting: Spider-Man; a 47-foot-tall balloon featuring portraits of characters from “The Wizard of Oz” and carrying the Wizard himself, in anticipation of the film’s 75th anniversary next year; Snoopy and Woodstock, in a 40th-anniversary tribute to “A Charlie Brown Thanksgiving”; and a spinning dreidel to celebrate Hanukkah.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on Thursday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Thursday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Schedule', '_id': 'nyt://article/d588ed48-27dc-528f-9c36-426890ead192', 'word_count': 723, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d588ed48-27dc-528f-9c36-426890ead192'}, {'abstract': 'I became the pastor to a nondenominational mission church to the homeless, and I quickly found out that if God had a vision for the place, I wasn’t privy to it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/booming/a-second-career-as-a-pastor-schooled-by-the-homeless.html', 'snippet': 'I became the pastor to a nondenominational mission church to the homeless, and I quickly found out that if God had a vision for the place, I wasn’t privy to it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The airplane that crashed had been heading to Greenville, S.C., where I was a reporter.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 487}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1663, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/booming/28mystory-booming-pastor2/28mystory-booming-pastor2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Second Career as a Pastor, Schooled by the Homeless', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ministers (Protestant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christians and Christianity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baby Boomers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robberies and Thefts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T06:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Booming', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Richardson-Moore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Richardson-Moore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f29d310-9e2e-5d73-a109-fe75a307f7fb', 'word_count': 1224, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f29d310-9e2e-5d73-a109-fe75a307f7fb'}, {'abstract': 'A butcher demonstrates how to carve a turkey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/dining/how-to-carve-a-turkey-for-thanksgiving.html', 'snippet': 'A butcher demonstrates how to carve a turkey.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2007, The Times asked Ray Venezia, a butcher and then the head of the meat department at Fairway Market, to demonstrate how to carve a Thanksgiving turkey.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Art of the Carve', 'kicker': 'Video', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T06:17:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32824f46-9072-50a1-814d-21e851d15794', 'word_count': 73, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32824f46-9072-50a1-814d-21e851d15794'}, {'abstract': 'Yao Ming is less than two years away from fulfilling his promise to his parents that he would go to college, a common but seldom realized dream for Chinese athletes.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/yao-ming-on-third-year-as-a-college-student/', 'snippet': 'Yao Ming is less than two years away from fulfilling his promise to his parents that he would go to college, a common but seldom realized dream for Chinese athletes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On class days, Yao Ming, the 7-foot-6 retired N.B.A. center, wakes up at the crack of dawn to beat the Shanghai traffic. Carrying a lunch prepared by his wife, Ye Li, a 6-foot-3 former player in China’s professional league, Mr. Yao drives more than an hour to Jiao Tong University, where he sits through his required courses in the economics and management department. According to one Chinese news report, Mr. Yao would prefer to live in the dorms with his 20-year-old classmates, a move that would save time and energy, “but the beds are too small.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Yao Ming on Third Year as a College Student', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emanuel, Rahm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Liu Yandong', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pippen, Scottie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yao Ming', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Bulls', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chinese Basketball Assn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Shanghai Sharks', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T06:17:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Century', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Century', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7388989e-f18f-5d62-943c-b2bc25cf20b1', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7388989e-f18f-5d62-943c-b2bc25cf20b1'}, {'abstract': 'In her resignation letter, Shoma Chaudhury defended her handling of a complaint by a staffer who had accused the editor in chief of sexual assault.', 'web_url': 'https://india.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/managing-editor-of-newsmagazine-resigns-amid-sexual-assault-controversy/', 'snippet': 'In her resignation letter, Shoma Chaudhury defended her handling of a complaint by a staffer who had accused the editor in chief of sexual assault.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW DELHI — The managing editor of the newsmagazine Tehelka, whose editor in chief has been charged in the sexual assault of a junior reporter, resigned Thursday morning in an email to the staff, citing the growing controversy over her handling of the initial complaint.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/asia/28-tehelka-IndiaInk/28-tehelka-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 415, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/world/asia/28-tehelka-IndiaInk/28-tehelka-IndiaInk-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 415}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/asia/28-tehelka-IndiaInk/28-tehelka-IndiaInk-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 709, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/asia/28-tehelka-IndiaInk/28-tehelka-IndiaInk-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1418, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/world/asia/28-tehelka-IndiaInk/28-tehelka-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/28/world/asia/28-tehelka-IndiaInk/28-tehelka-IndiaInk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non