, 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Corrections: November 28, 2013', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Corrections', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T07:59:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a83bfdd8-48f9-5cb2-9fa7-1271fbc5808c', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a83bfdd8-48f9-5cb2-9fa7-1271fbc5808c'}, {'abstract': 'A hamstring injury that sidelined the Clippers’ Chris Paul in the second half gave the Knicks a chance, but they squandered it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/sports/basketball/no-solutions-in-sight-knicks-lose-seventh-straight.html', 'snippet': 'A hamstring injury that sidelined the Clippers’ Chris Paul in the second half gave the Knicks a chance, but they squandered it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — J.\u2009R. Smith flew across the lane, the back of his untucked jersey flapping behind him. He was determined to do something Wednesday night to salvage the Knicks’ fourth-quarter hopes, and it came in the form of a flat-footed lob that the Clippers’ DeAndre Jordan batted away as soon as it left Smith’s hand.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/basketball/28knicks-img/28knicks-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/basketball/28knicks-img/28knicks-img-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/28/sports/basketball/28knicks-img/28knicks-img-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'le