, 'snippet': 'Some lawmakers support bans on food lines and loitering, because that’s easier than building affordable housing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You can call this post: Don’t Let Them Eat Cake. Or, Let Them Eat Cake Somewhere Else. Or Hide the Cake Altogether.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Insert Homeless Headline Here', 'kicker': 'Taking Note', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homeless Persons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nagourney, Adam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Coalition for the Homeless', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T14:23:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lawrence Downes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lawrence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Downes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/469360b9-0166-5626-ac4a-7ff8b7f41e5b', 'word_count': 453, 'uri': 'nyt://article/469360b9-0166-5626-ac4a-7ff8b7f41e5b'}, {'abstract': 'The invitation to the International Atomic Energy Agency came days after Tehran struck a landmark nuclear deal with world powers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/world/middleeast/iran-nuclear-inspections.html', 'snippet': 'The invitation to the International Atomic Energy Agency came days after Tehran struck a landmark nuclear deal with world powers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Days after Iran struck a landmark accord with world powers on its nuclear program, the International Atomic Energy Agency announced on Thursday that Tehran had invited its inspectors to visit a heavy-water production plant linked to the deal — the first tangible step since the agreement was concluded.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.N. Nuclear Inspectors Invited to Iranian Facility', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.N. Nuclear Inspectors Invited to Iranian Facility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Atomic Energy Agency', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Amano, Yukiya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T14:30:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Cowell', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cowell', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e38bdc47-a67a-50ca-88f6-9ed0f6778387', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e38bdc47-a67a-50ca-88f6-9ed0f6778387'}, {'abstract': 'Further delay in codifying limits on risk-taking by big banks will only weaken, not enhance, the prospect of effective regulation, an economist writes.', 'web_url': 'https://economix.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/getting-the-volcker-rule-done/', 'snippet': 'Further delay in codifying limits on risk-taking by big banks will only weaken, not enhance, the prospect of effective regulation, an economist writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Simon Johnson, former chief economist of the International Monetary Fund, is the Ronald A. Kurtz Professor of Entrepreneurship at the M.I.T. Sloan School of Management and co-author of “White House Burning: The Founding Fathers, Our National Debt, and Why It Matters to You.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Getting the Volcker Rule Done', '