 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'E.U. Eases Rules on Liquids on Planes', 'kicker': 'In Transit', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trending: E.U. Eases Rules on Liquids on Planes', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'European Union', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T15:00:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tanya Mohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tanya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2621f38d-b23c-5501-b246-51d90994ae75', 'word_count': 406, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2621f38d-b23c-5501-b246-51d90994ae75'}, {'abstract': 'In the United States, where unemployment remains stubbornly high, people are grateful that Amazon.com is hiring so many workers for its warehouses. In Europe, where the recession was worse, there is a different question: Are these jobs dehumanizing?', 'web_url': 'https://bits.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/28/europe-vs-amazon-anger-rising/', 'snippet': 'In the United States, where unemployment remains stubbornly high, people are grateful that Amazon.com is hiring so many workers for its warehouses. In Europe, where the recession was worse, there is a different question: Are these jobs dehumanizin...', 'lead_paragraph': 'On its home territory, Amazon.com is routinely hailed as a jobs machine. Thanks to its warehouse building spree, it is hiring tens of thousands of workers, plus many more for the holidays. President Obama, speaking at the retailer’s Chattanooga, Tenn., warehouse in July, called Amazon “a great example of what’s possible.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/business/amazon/amazon-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Europe vs. Amazon: Anger Rising', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recession and Depression', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM 