broadband provider that is expanding its presence in the Caribbean.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON – The French telecommunications company Orange has reached an agreement to sell its Dominican Republic operations to the Luxembourg cable and broadband provider Altice for $1.4 billion.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Orange to Sell Dominican Telecom Business', 'kicker': 'DealBook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Orange to Sell Dominican Telecom Operations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Altice SaRL', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Orange PLC', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dominican Republic', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'France', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Luxembourg', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T16:17:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chad Bray', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chad', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bray', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23ba6961-081a-5edf-99e2-a8dc260a6434', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23ba6961-081a-5edf-99e2-a8dc260a6434'}, {'abstract': 'Georgian Court, which this fall became a full-time coed institution, hopes the addition of men’s teams will expand awareness of the university beyond the campus gates.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/sports/once-for-women-only-georgian-court-looks-to-mens-teams-to-raise-profile.html', 'snippet': 'Georgian Court, which this fall became a full-time coed institution, hopes the addition of men’s teams will expand awareness of the university beyond the campus gates.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAKEWOOD, N.J. — Luka Zgonjanin arrived in the United States from Serbia in August, barely able to speak English. He had accepted a scholarship to play basketball at Georgian Court, a small liberal arts university on the outskirts of the Jersey Shore. A few months earlier, he had never heard of the college.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/sports/29georgianweb1/29georgianweb1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Once for Women Only, Georgian Court Looks to Men’s Teams to Raise Profile', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Strategy: Add Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'College Athletics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Berkman, Seth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Georgian Court University', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Roman Catholic Church', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lakewood (NJ)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jeffries, Rosemary', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball (College)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T16:19:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Seth Berkman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Seth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Berkman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/daa6987e-2afb-5ed1-b0c4-ce31e1ccc4cf', 'word_count': 1163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/daa6987e-2afb-5ed1-b0c4-ce31e1ccc4cf'}, {'abstract': 'Experience the past, present and future in this Chinese city, sampling everything from museums to street food to dancing in the park along the way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/travel/36-hours-in-shanghai.html', 'snippet': 'Experience the past, present and future in this Chinese city, sampling everything from museums to street food to dancing in the park along the way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What takes most cities eons to build, Shanghai can do overnight. Consider this: Just a decade ago, the city had four metro lines; now there are a dozen. The Jin Mao Tower was the tallest building in the neon-streaked financial center of Pudong; it has since been surpassed by the Shanghai World Financial Center and the nearly completed Shanghai Tower, which will be the second-tallest building in the world (after Dubai’s Burj Khalifa) when it’s finished next year. Still, what fascinates about this city is how little seems to have changed in the maze of lanes that have (thus far) eluded the bulldozer in the Old City or the former foreign concessions. Here, residents haggle over freshly caught fish in tiny markets or doze in lawn chairs on summer afternoons, ignoring the pounding jackhammers. Shanghai is remaking itself to become a “City of the Future,” but what’s so alluring is how much old-world character remains.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01HOURS_SPAN-sf/01HOURS_SPAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Shanghai', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '36 Hours: Shanghai', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bergman, Justin', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Shanghai (China)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T16:20:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Bergman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bergman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/593cf195-807d-5299-b355-00a0d727e88c', 'word_count': 1624, 'uri': 'nyt://article/593cf195-807d-5299-b355-00a0d727e88c'}, {'abstract': 'Nicosia is experiencing a renaissance with more and more venues catering to the artistic set.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/travel/in-cyprus-a-new-spirit-animates-the-capital.html', 'snippet': 'Nicosia is experiencing a renaissance with more and more venues catering to the artistic set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Europe’s last divided capital, Nicosia, Cyprus, is experiencing a renaissance with more and more venues catering to the artistic set. No longer wary of the demilitarized United Nations Buffer Zone that bisects the ancient walled city between the Greek Cypriot and Turkish Cypriot sides, young Nicosians have reclaimed their old town. Emboldened by falling real estate prices, arty cafes, boutiques celebrating homegrown fashion and buzzy restaurants have opened among the Venetian fortifications and Byzantine churches on the Greek side. While beachgoers have long flocked to the coasts, the rebirth of the inland capital is evidence of a historic city in transition.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFACING1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFACING1-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 503}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFACING1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 858, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFACING1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1716, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFACING1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFACING1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/travel/01SURFACING1/01SURFAC