 the chief executive and co-founder of DraftStreet, a daily online fantasy sports site, juggles work with family time on weekends.', 'lead_paragraph': '“What I do on a Sunday impacts what a lot of other people do on a Sunday,” said Brian Schwartz, the C.E.O. and co-founder of DraftStreet, a daily online fantasy sports site. Mr. Schwartz, who is 30 and lives on the Upper East Side of Manhattan with his wife, Jaime, their year-old daughter, Liv, and a pet puggle, Bascom, wasn’t being arrogant; he was being accurate. Since it started in 2010, DraftStreet has acquired more than 350,000 users, he said. Most of them visit the site on Sundays during football season, which tend — at least in part — to be workdays for Mr. Schwartz. The company has its Fantasy Football Championship on Dec. 15.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE4/01ROUTINE4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE4/01ROUTINE4-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE4/01ROUTINE4-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE4/01ROUTINE4-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1380, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/nyregion/01ROUTINE4/01ROUTINE4-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thu