unning through December at Café Carlyle, applies his gruff flair to standards.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/arts/music/steve-tyrell-performs-at-cafe-carlyle.html', 'snippet': 'Steve Tyrell’s show “Wordsmiths: Lyricists of the Great American Song,” running through December at Café Carlyle, applies his gruff flair to standards.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Aw, shucks, folks. That describes the attitude Steve Tyrell imparts to everything he sings. In his ninth holiday season show at Café Carlyle, “Wordsmiths: Lyricists of the Great American Song,” he brings an unwavering tone of genial bonhomie to standards by the Gershwins, Rodgers and Hart, Cole Porter and others. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A New Orleans-Inflected Style Puts Some Macho in the Standards’ Sweet Talk', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A New Orleans-Inflected Style Puts Some Macho in the Standards’ Sweet Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cafe Carlyle (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tyrell, Steve', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T22:07:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/54d7d67c-fbc3-53a7-bf92-5f29f239fa00', 'word_count': 286, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54d7d67c-fbc3-53a7-bf92-5f29f239fa00'}, {'abstract': 'Tanya Holt and Marcus Simeone brought chemistry to their show, “Quiet Storm,” at the Metropolitan Room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/arts/music/tanya-holt-and-marcus-simeone-at-the-metropolitan-room.html', 'snippet': 'Tanya Holt and Marcus Simeone brought chemistry to their show, “Quiet Storm,” at the Metropolitan Room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Congenial vocal chemistry is where you find it, and sometimes unlikely couples like Tanya Holt, a sultry pop-soul singer, and Marcus Simeone, a hyper-emotional tenor, who performed together at the Metropolitan Room on Saturday evening, have it. The title of their show, “Quiet Storm,” refers to the simmering romantic radio format first popularized in the mid-1970s. Adapted for cabaret, it embraces everything from Motown to “West Side Story” to Anita Baker. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Isn’t Like the Other, and That May be the Point', 'kicker': 'Music Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Isn’t Like the Other, And That May be the Point', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holt, Tanya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Simeone, Marcus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-28T22:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b5aef7e0-b2f7-59d3-9903-6184ae3deeef', 'word_count': 248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b5aef7e0-b2f7-59d3-9903-6184ae3deeef'}, {'abstract': 'The government has stepped away from an expected rejection of a proposed set of sweeping restrictions on cigarette packaging aimed at preventing smoking by young people.', 'web_url': 'https