reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94e62892-c4f1-5ff3-944c-421df411ec48', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94e62892-c4f1-5ff3-944c-421df411ec48'}, {'abstract': 'The legacy of the Fifth Avenue department store lives on as its founder prescribed a century ago, through a foundation that hands out grants.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/nyregion/b-altman-store-long-closed-still-makes-presence-felt.html', 'snippet': 'The legacy of the Fifth Avenue department store lives on as its founder prescribed a century ago, through a foundation that hands out grants.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There was a time when shoppers would crowd into B. Altman & Company on the Friday after Thanksgiving. That imposing Fifth Avenue department store still had a certain specialness as it aged gracefully, perhaps too gracefully — by the 1970s, it seemed almost fusty. And then, after a listless going-out-of-business sale that began on the day after Thanksgiving in 1989, it closed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/nyregion/29altman/29altman-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/29/nyregion/29altman/29altman-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/nyregion/29altman/29altman-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/29/nyregion/29altman/29altman-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy