e': 'subject', 'value': 'Dodd-Frank Wall Street Reform and Consumer Protection Act (2010)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Subprime Mortgage Crisis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bush, George W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dudley, William C', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kroszner, Randall S', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Deposit Insurance Corp', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Government Accountability Office', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T05:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Economy', 'byline': {'original': 'By Phillip Swagel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Phillip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Swagel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91c17c0d-4114-507d-b315-6ad7125d4d43', 'word_count': 1470, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91c17c0d-4114-507d-b315-6ad7125d4d43'}, {'abstract': 'The Spoleto Festival USA announced its 2014 lineup, which will feature 152 performances of opera, music, theater and dance from May 23 through June 8.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/arts/spoleto-festival-usa-announces-lineup.html', 'snippet': 'The Spoleto Festival USA announced its 2014 lineup, which will feature 152 performances of opera, music, theater and dance from May 23 through June 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Entering its 38th year, the Spoleto Festival USA announced its 2014 lineup, which will feature 152 performances of opera, music, theater and dance from May 23 through June 8. The festival, in Charleston, S.C., will include a new production of John Adams’s opera “El Niño.” Janacek’s “Kat’a Kabanova,” will be staged by Garry Hynes, above, who in 1998 became the first woman to win a Tony for directing, for her production of “The Beauty Queen of Leenane.” The festival will also feature the American premiere of the opera “Facing Goya,” by Michael Nyman, below, in a new version to be performed without amplification. The Spoleto Festival USA Orchestra, conducted by John Kennedy, will pair Beethoven’s Seventh symphony with Louis Andriessen’s “The Nine Symphonies of Beethoven” and Michael Gordon’s “Rewriting Beethoven’s Seventh Symphony.” The festival’s theatrical productions will include Joseph O’Connor’s adaptation of “My Cousin Rachel,” drawn from the Daphne du Maurier novel, in a production by the Gate Theater of Ireland, as well as the American premiere of Ravi Jain’s autobiographical play, “A Brimful of Asha,” and a multimedia work by Laurie Anderson called “The Language of the Future.” Dances will be performed by Hubbard Street Dance Chicago, Dorrance Dance, Keigwin & Company and Gregory Maqoma.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spoleto Festival USA Announces Lineup', 'kicker': 'Arts, Briefly', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spoleto Festival USA Announces Lineup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spoleto Festival USA', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Charleston (SC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Keigwin + Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gate Theater', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hubbard Street Dance Chicago', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T05:11:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'Compiled by Randy Kennedy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Randy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kennedy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Brief', '_id': 'nyt://article/cafb2651-aafa-5621-baad-5604fa40b0ed', 'word_count': 206, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cafb2651-aafa-5621-baad-5604fa40b0ed'}, {'abstract': 'A stretch of the Ohio Turnpike was shut down after a high-speed chase outside of Toledo that resulted in at least one death, according to local reports.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/us/ohio-turnpike-shut-down-after-high-speed-crash.html', 'snippet': 'A stretch of the Ohio Turnpike was shut down after a high-speed chase outside of Toledo that resulted in at least one death, according to local reports.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Ohio Turnpike was shut down near Fremont, the police said late Thursday, after what local reports described as a high-speed crash that may have left more than one person dead.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Ohio Turnpike Shut Down After High-Speed Crash', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Toledo (Ohio)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T05:52:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravi Somaiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Somaiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/32d9fdd0-8300-5a39-832d-f172e5f8e0fd', 'word_count': 127, 'uri': 'nyt://article/32d9fdd0-8300-5a39-832d-f172e5f8e0fd'}, {'abstract': 'Desperate for resources to fuel its fast-growing economy, China has become the world’s biggest importer of garbage: scrap paper, metals, wires and plastic. And while reprocessing discarded electronics and other goods can exact a toll on the environment, recycling can be less polluting than extracting the raw materials from mines, oil wells or forests.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/q-a-adam-minter-on-why-chinas-scrap-trade-helps-the-environment/', 'snippet': 'Desperate for resources to fuel its fast-growing economy, China has become the world’s biggest importer of garbage: scrap paper, metals, wires and plastic. And while reprocessing discarded electronics and other goods can exact a toll on the enviro...', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his new book “Junkyard Planet: Travels in the Billion-Dollar Trash Trade” (Bloomsbury Press), Adam Minter paints a Dickensian portrait of China’s massive garbage and recycling dumps. And then he tells us why they’re so vital to the environmental movement.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Q. & A.: Adam Minter on Why China’s Scrap Trade Helps the Environment', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hazardous and Toxic Substances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recycling of Waste Materials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ships and Shipping', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T05:58:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/970431a9-7505-57f7-b467-d7bd4d47d9d6', 'word_count': 1799, 'uri': 'nyt://article/970431a9-7505-57f7-b467-d7bd4d47d9d6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/arts/television/whats-on-friday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '9 P.M. (13) BARBRA STREISAND: BACK TO BROOKLYN In this “Great Performances” presentation, Ms. Streisand, above, sings with Il Volo, Chris Botti and her son, Jason Gould, at the Barclays Center in her first hometown concert since childhood. The two October 2012 performances from which this special was culled were “a sentimental homecoming and a royal act of noblesse oblige in which a show business monarch regaled the adoring subjects of her native province in a concert that was steeped in Brooklyn lore,” Stephen Holden wrote in The New York Times. “Appetite, yearning, curiosity — whatever you call it — is a quality embedded in Ms. Streisand’s voice. Like few singers of any age, she has the gift of conveying a primal human longing in a beautiful sound. She is hungry still.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s On Friday', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Friday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T06:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'o