d status symbol within China’s burgeoning class of business moguls and millionaires.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Eases Rules on the Coveted Pilot’s License', 'kicker': 'Sinosphere', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T08:05:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Century', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Century', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7c342f3-5546-543f-9ab6-a69037e283c3', 'word_count': 507, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7c342f3-5546-543f-9ab6-a69037e283c3'}, {'abstract': 'China’s cultural exchange program, the Confucius Institute, opens its first branch in the Mediterranean country, an old Communist ally from the 1960s and ’70s.', 'web_url': 'https://sinosphere.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/29/a-friendship-is-rekindled-with-albania/', 'snippet': 'China’s cultural exchange program, the Confucius Institute, opens its first branch in the Mediterranean country, an old Communist ally from the 1960s and ’70s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Educators, politicians and diplomats from China and Albania gathered last week to celebrate the opening of a new Confucius Institute at the University of Tirana, which welcomed the Chinese government-backed program whose mission is to promote Chinese language and culture abroad.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia':