Drone Strikes Strain U.S. Ties With Afghanistan and Pakistan', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Recent Drone Strikes Strain U.S. Ties With Afghanistan and Pakistan', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AFGHANISTAN', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pakistan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drones (Pilotless Planes)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khan, Imran', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Karzai, Hamid', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Afghanistan War (2001- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T15:13:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rod Nordland and Salman Masood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Salman', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Masood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/075d954d-911e-5b46-8e75-674b38e06495', 'word_count': 794, 'uri': 'nyt://article/075d954d-911e-5b46-8e75-674b38e06495'}, {'abstract': 'Anne Somerset reconsiders some of our most unflattering ideas about Britain’s Queen Anne.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/books/review/queen-anne-by-anne-somerset.html', 'snippet': 'Anne Somerset reconsiders some of our most unflattering ideas about Britain’s Queen Anne.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Britain’s Queen Anne (who reigned from 1702 to 1714) has not been treated kindly by historians. Consensus has it that “Brandy Nan” was obese and of limited intelligence, with a predilection for the bottle. More dangerously, she is supposed to have put herself under the thumb of domineering women favorites with political agendas: first the Whig partisan Sarah Churchill, Duchess of Marlborough, and subsequently the duchess’s upstart cousin Abigail Masham, a Tory sympathizer. (It is suggested from the surviving correspondence that Anne might have had lesbian leanings, though whether these were ever acted upon is unknown.) She is seldom given any credit for the great events of her reign, which included the 1707 Act of Union and the glorious victories over the armies of Louis XIV.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/books/review/1201-bks-ALLEN/1201-bks-ALLEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 992, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/books/review/1201-bks-ALLEN/1201-bks-ALLEN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 992}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/books/review/1201-bks-ALLEN/1201-bks-ALLEN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 620, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/books/review/1201-bks-ALLEN/1201-bks-ALLEN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1239, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/books/review/1201-bks-ALLEN/1201-bks-ALLEN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 