 in the search for viewers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Back in 1965, Linus stepped forward and calmed the chaos of “A Charlie Brown Christmas,” the classic animated special, by reciting verses from the Gospel of Luke about the birth of Jesus. “That’s what Christmas is all about, Charlie Brown,” he concluded.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 346, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 346}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 440, 'width': 762, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/30XMASTV/30XMASTV-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Single Mother Needs a Man: It Must Be Christmas on TV', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Single Mother Needs a Man: It Must Be Christmas on TV', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Christmas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hallmark Channel', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lifetime Television', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-29T22:37:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fb09e54c-35f6-581f-b672-9dc1fa769cb1', 'word_count': 1036, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fb09e54c-35f6-581f-b672-9dc1fa769cb1'}, {'abstract': '“The Pete Holmes Show,” hosted by a comedian known (by some) for his podcasts, favors timeless themes over the more usual topical humor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/arts/the-pete-holmes-show-late-nights-on-tbs.html', 'snippet': '“The Pete Holmes Show,” hosted by a comedian known (by some) for his podcasts, favors timeless themes over the more usual topical humor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pete Holmes was talking about his divorce on his new late-night talk show, and not for the first time. He had already told a guest, Allison Williams of HBO’s “Girls,” that his ex-wife cheated on him, but this time he took blame. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/sub-comedy/sub-comedy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/30/arts/sub-comedy/sub