'value': 'China', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T04:55:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Barboza', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barboza', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f9d991bb-e930-559d-b462-ff9a1ab6bfe4', 'word_count': 1340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f9d991bb-e930-559d-b462-ff9a1ab6bfe4'}, {'abstract': 'The Knicks lost for the eighth straight time as Carmelo Anthony returned to the city where he played his first seven-plus seasons and left under less-than-amicable circumstances.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/sports/basketball/back-in-denver-anthony-is-booed-as-knicks-lose.html', 'snippet': 'The Knicks lost for the eighth straight time as Carmelo Anthony returned to the city where he played his first seven-plus seasons and left under less-than-amicable circumstances.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DENVER — The fans at the Pepsi Center booed Carmelo Anthony during pregame introductions. They booed him when he brought the ball up the court. They booed nearly every move he made on Friday night, with the notable exception of his missed shots. The crowd loved those.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 475, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 475}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 811, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1621, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/11/30/sports/CITY-KNICKS/CITY-KNICKS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Back in Denver, Anthony Is Booed as Knicks Lose', 'kicker': 'Nuggets 97, Knicks 95', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Back in Denver, Anthony Is Booed as Knicks Lose', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Denver Nuggets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Knicks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T05:13:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Basketball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Cacciola', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cacciola', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5bc6ee31-0aa4-57a7-98a0-f5c1e2e930e6', 'word_count': 1005, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5bc6ee31-0aa4-57a7-98a0-f5c1e2e930e6'}, {'abstract': 'Television highlights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/arts/television/whats-on-saturday.html', 'snippet': 'Television highlights.', 'lead_paragraph': '8 P.M. (HBO) BEAUTIFUL CREATURES (2013) Ethan (Alden Ehrenreich), an almost-too-good-to-be-true high school boy despairing of his conservative South Carolina existence, meets his dream girl, Lena (Alice Englert), when her family of witches moves to town, and “it’s kind of like Romeo and Juliet, but, like you know, happier,” Manohla Dargis wrote in The New York Times about this “pop Southern Gothic amusement about teenage love and other powerful magic.” Lena has some spooky relatives, including her Uncle Macon (Jeremy Irons) and cousin Ridley (Emmy Rossum). Ethan comes with a nanny, Amma (Viola Davis, above left, with Ms. Englert and Mr. Ehrenreich). “\xa0‘Beautiful Creatures,’ its sweet young things and supernatural shenanigans have been marshaled to help fill the box office void left by the end of the ‘Harry Potter’ and ‘Twilight’ franchises,” Ms. Dargis said of this adaptation of Kami Garcia and Margaret Stohl’s book. “It’s a void that ‘The Hunger Games’ has already started to fill, partly by tapping into deeply American themes and giving them thrilling female form. ‘Beautiful Creatures’ has been spun from thinner material, despite its strong female characters, nods at the Civil War and a story that turns on good versus evil, a fight that — as in many young adult stories — is somewhat mirrored in the struggle between the high school herd and the individual. There’s not much new under the moon here, which makes what the writer and director Richard LaGravenese does with the story all the more notable.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'mai