53', 'word_count': 502, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a909f4b-8b53-581a-9975-84f8655d2253'}, {'abstract': 'A TV show’s name is not meant to be seen as an invitation to seek culinary success through bodily harm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/one-cooking-show-you-shouldnt-try-at-home.html', 'snippet': 'A TV show’s name is not meant to be seen as an invitation to seek culinary success through bodily harm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SOCIETY’S clamor for more cooking on television will be met this evening with the debut of a new show called “Cook Your Ass Off” — but do not be alarmed. The name is meant to be taken figuratively, program executives emphasize, and not as an invitation to seek culinary success through bodily harm.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'One Cooking Show You Shouldn’t Try at Home', 'kicker': 'Loose Ends', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Cooking Show You Shouldn’t Try at Home', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HLN', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T19:58:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Barry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/66860636-6956-532d-bf44-43738ddb48a4', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66860636-6956-532d-bf44-43738ddb48a4'}, {'abstract': 'The dead can’t retaliate. And I didn’t just write about my father’s life — I probed that life.', 'web_url': 'https://opinionator.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/when-writers-expose-the-dead/', 'snippet': 'The dead can’t retaliate. And I didn’t just write about my father’s life — I probed that life.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly after my father’s sudden death, a friend gave me C.S. Lewis’s “A Grief Observed.” I read it post-funeral, in the awkward days when visiting relatives have returned home, when you’re supposed to re-embrace work and routines. The book offered little comfort — it’s an often self-pitying look at Lewis’s “mad, midnight moments” following the loss of his wife. But one passage stood out. Lewis writes of tales he’s read, “in which the dead tell us that our mourning does them some kind of wrong. They beg us to stop it…It made the dead far more dead.”', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When Writers Expose the Dead', 'kicker': 'Draft', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'When Writers Expose the Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T20:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Budd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Budd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb440c3f-5292-5383-9883-13dffa4817ff', 'word_count': 1049, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb440c3f-5292-5383-9883-13dffa4817ff'}, {'abstract': 'How names are placed on lists of known or suspected terrorists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2013/12/01/sunday-review/into-the-government-funnel.html', 'snippet': 'How names are placed on lists of known or suspected terrorists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How names are placed on lists of known or suspected terrorists.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 463, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1272, 'width': 575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278/into-the-government-funnel-1385778174278-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Into the Government Funnel', 'kicker': 'NEWS ANALYSIS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T20:01:52+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Sunday Review', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/29f2f0eb-ab5c-5d5b-a1c6-01ca746975e2', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/29f2f0eb-ab5c-5d5b-a1c6-01ca746975e2'}, {'abstract': 'After almost eight years, a case involving terrorist watch lists is going to court.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/sunday-review/who-is-watching-the-watch-lists.html', 'snippet': 'After almost eight years, a case involving terrorist watch lists is going to court.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GOVERNMENTS wade into treacherous waters when they compile lists of people who might cause their countries harm. As fears about Japanese-Americans and Communists have demonstrated in the past, predictions about individual behavior are often inaccurate, the motivations for list-making aren’t always noble and concerns about threats are frequently overblown.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Is Watching the Watch Lists?', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who Is Watching the Watch Lists?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stellin, Susan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Airport Security', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ibrahim, Rahinah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernstein, Anya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T20:01:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Susan Stellin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Susan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stellin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/aaadc9a1-c990-5084-92a9-bc4520e82cee', 'word_count': 984, 'uri': 'nyt://article/aaadc9a1-c990-5084-92a9-bc4520e82cee'}, {'abstract': 'In the United States, we do not track how many sperm donors there are, how often they donate, or how many children are born from the donations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/the-unregulated-sperm-industry.html', 'snippet': 'In the United States, we do not track how many sperm donors there are, how often they donate, or how many children are born from the donations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NEW HAVEN — THE new movie “Delivery Man” stars Vince Vaughn as a former sperm donor who finds out that he has more than 500 children. Is this a Hollywood exaggeration or a possible outcome? Truth is, no one knows. In the United States, we do not track how many sperm donors there are, how often they donate, or how many children are born from the donations. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/01SPERM/01SPERM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 250, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/01SPERM/01SPERM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 250}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/01SPERM/01SPERM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/sunday-review/01SPERM/01SPERM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 854, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank'