eek’s elections, has rejected the official results and called on her supporters to march in the streets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TEGUCIGALPA, Honduras — Xiomara Castro, the left-wing presidential candidate in last week’s elections, has rejected the official results and called on her supporters to march in the streets, adding new uncertainty to the country’s already polarized politics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Honduras Election Results Challenged', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Honduras Election Results Challenged', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Honduras', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Castro, Xiomara', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hernandez, Juan Orlando', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T20:15:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Phillips and Elisabeth Malkin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Phillips', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elisabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Malkin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cfbb241b-8ea7-50c6-a309-3602d1d1a951', 'word_count': 439, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cfbb241b-8ea7-50c6-a309-3602d1d1a951'}, {'abstract': 'Photographing the forms and functions of gigantic new technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/machine-age.html', 'snippet': 'Photographing the forms and functions of gigantic new technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Form and function have always fascinated me. I thoroughly enjoy being in grand spaces; I like feeling the magnitude of a dam looming over me, or the crackling of electricity everywhere about me. For 40 years I have tried to capture these forms, to convert them into images that bespeak their power and strength.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/opinion/sunday/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS/01exposures-ss-slide-N6JS-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Machine Age', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Machine Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T20:21:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Steele', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Steele', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c27a643b-6c89-5a07-be73-75cf8e5af384', 'word_count': 184, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c27a643b-6c89-5a07-be73-75cf8e5af384'}, {'abstract': 'Nature may be red in tooth and claw, but she is utterly ruthless when it comes to genitalia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/sunday-review/the-shocking-sex-secrets-of-insects.html', 'snippet': 'Nature may be red in tooth and claw, but she is utterly ruthless when it comes to genitalia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PROSTITUTION is supposedly the oldest profession, which means that sex itself must be one of the oldest behaviors, a conclusion underscored by the recent discovery of two bugs fossilized as they coupled 165 million years ago. Simply being ancient doesn’t make a sex act interesting, but this one was noteworthy in part because behavior is generally so ephemeral, leaving none of the preserved remains we rely upon to tell us about how early forms of life ate, or ran, or saw the world. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'ima