l to halt Iran’s nuclear program.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sunday Breakfast Menu, Dec. 1', 'kicker': 'The Caucus', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T22:54:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jada F. Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jada', 'middlename': 'F.', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2de4b0cb-c20d-5180-9908-b57b055dc3b6', 'word_count': 381, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2de4b0cb-c20d-5180-9908-b57b055dc3b6'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s how to apply for my annual win-a-trip contest.', 'web_url': 'https://kristof.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/win-a-trip-in-2014/', 'snippet': 'Here’s how to apply for my annual win-a-trip contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My latest column, my annual gift-giving guide, also announces my next win-a-trip contest, an annual event in which I take a university student with me on a reporting trip to the developing world. The aim is to generate interest in global poverty both with the contest and with the blogging and videos that the winner will contribute to the New York Times website. I started the contest in 2006 and we’ve had some great trips over the years. For some of the winners, it has been life-changing, and HBO did a documentary called “Reporter” based on my 2007 trip; it’s on Amazon if you want to see what you’re getting yourself in for.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Win a Trip in 2014!', 'kicker': 'Nicholas Kristof', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T22:58:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Kristof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kristof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b66990e-1eb3-53b9-9c62-18b32dcc6e25', 'word_count': 520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b66990e-1eb3-53b9-9c62-18b32dcc6e25'}, {'abstract': 'Alan DerKazarian returns, and then splits.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2013/11/30/two-halves-in-one/', 'snippet': 'Alan DerKazarian returns, and then splits.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SUNDAY’S PUZZLE — I know this is wrong, and probably way too undignified for a New York Times blog, but I couldn’t help headbanging along to this solve. I might have even stopped briefly to play some air guitar. Not only do we have a fun theme with a critical word hidden inside the black squares and a grid that is split in two, but we have a hardcore soundtrack playing in the background as we solve.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Halves in One', 'kicker': 'Wordplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crossword Puzzles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2013-11-30T23:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Deb Amlen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e91e47c0-f95d-51bf-bb3d-244bbd7ede8b', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e91e47c0-f95d-51bf-bb3d-244bbd7ede8b'}, {'abstract': 'With the new prosperity, soaring crime rates have come to places in Montana and North Dakota, straining law enforcement resources and shattering the sense of safety.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2013/12/01/us/as-oil-floods-plains-towns-crime-pours-in.html', 'snippet': 'With the new prosperity, soaring crime rates have come to places in Montana and North Dakota, straining law enforcement resources and shattering the sense of safety.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SIDNEY, Mont. — One cold morning last year, a math teacher jogging through her hometown in eastern Montana was abducted, strangled and buried in a shallow grave. Charged in her death were two drifters from Colorado, drawn to the region by the allure of easy money in the oil fields.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/us/oilfield/oilfield-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2013/12/01/us/oilfield/oilfield-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/us/oilfield/oilfield-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 736, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2013/12/01/us/oilfield/oilfield-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1473, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Oil Floods Plains Towns, Crime Pours In', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'As Oil Floods Plains Towns, Crime Pours In', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crime and Criminals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Dakota', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 